Cambodian yellow bananas exported to Chinese market are gaining strong support from the Chinese people
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Li An, Economic and Trade Advisor at the Embassy of the People's Republic of China, on July 24, 2019, confirmed that Cambodia's yellow bananas exported to the Chinese market are receiving Has strong support from the Chinese people.
Li An, Economic and Trade Adviser at the Chinese Embassy, made the remarks during a courtesy call on Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Veng Sakhon after completing his mission in Cambodia and introducing him. Wu Guoquan, who will replace him.
The above meeting was held at the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries on Wednesday afternoon, 08 Roch Khe Asat Chhnang Kor Eksak. 2563 is July 24, 2019.
Minister Veng Sakhon sent a message of thanks to the Chinese people and government for their support for Cambodia's development, and especially through the one-way belt policy of the Chinese government. To build important transport infrastructure, trade between the two countries.
He added that the Chinese government has decided to increase the quota on Cambodian rice imports to the Chinese market to 400,000 tons and recently allowed Cambodia to export yellow bananas directly to the Chinese market.
The Minister also requested the Chinese side to cooperate with the Ministry and all relevant parties to review and promote the export of corn products from Cambodia.
The Minister hopes and believes that through solidarity, friendship and comprehensive cooperation between the people and the Royal Government of the two countries, Cambodia will get many more benefits to build and develop the country.
Mr. Li An expressed his gratitude for the Minister's time to allow him and his team to meet now, and especially for the excellent cooperation provided by the Minister and his colleagues during his mission. In the past.
Li An also praised the export of yellow bananas to the Chinese market and confirmed that it is receiving strong support from the Chinese people.
He said that in addition to studying the legal procedures and techniques to export mangoes to the Chinese market, the two sides have been actively negotiating and hope to be able to start exporting those agricultural products soon. Coming soon. For dragon fruit, pepper and saliva, we are preparing technical documents and negotiating.
Li An hopes and believes that this cooperation will be further enhanced and strengthened during the tenure of Wu Guoquan and his colleagues, with the Chinese side supporting and continuing to support the Ministry for the Development of the Agricultural Sector in Cambodia. Stay away from drugs! Nationwide drug crackdown for July 24: 30 cases cracked, 49 arrested
