(Siem Reap): The APSARA Authority on July 24, 2019 held a groundbreaking ceremony for a concrete bridge and sluice gate in Nokor Krao village, Kork Chak commune, Siem Reap city, with the expectation that it will facilitate the living and Growing crops for more than 300 families in Nokor Krao village.
The groundbreaking ceremony for a new bridge and sluice gate in Nokor Krao village was held near the construction site of a bridge and sluice gate in Nokor Krao village, Kork Chak commune. The concrete bridge, which is the new contract of the APSARA Authority, gives the villagers of Angkor now 31 meters long, 3.5 meters wide and 4 meters high built on O Khlot. The sluice gate is 10 meters long and 3.5 meters wide at the dry river outlet.
Phoeun Sokhim, Deputy Director of the Water Management Department of the APSARA Authority, said that in 2013, Nokor Krao villagers were flooded due to heavy rains because there was no proper sluice construction at that time. Seeing such hardships in 2014, the APSARA Authority restored and built some irrigation systems in the area, and since then there have been no more floods.
Mr. Yit Chanda, Deputy Director General of APSARA Authority, recalled some of the work of APSARA Authority in the conservation and development of Angkor resort, as well as the core work to improve the lives of Angkor residents, such as the construction of sluice gates, bridges, roads and restoration. Other irrigation systems, etc.
With the achievements that APSARA Authority is building for the people of Nokor Krao now, the Deputy Director General expressed the expectation that it will serve a wide range of benefits to local people, especially to avoid any risks arising from Flooding during the rainy season, as well as helping to hold water for growing crops here. Kouchol offers lucky 20 Honda Dream motorcycles to customers
