Malaysian Embassy Announces Campaign for Official Launch of Malaysia Visitors Year 2020
The official inauguration of the logo for Malaysia Tourism Year 2020 took place on July 22, 2019 at Kuala Lumpur International Airport, Malaysia. This is according to the press release of the Malaysian Tourism Council Office of the Malaysian Embassy in Phnom Penh on July 24, 2019, which was received by Fresh News.
The logo is a combination of Malaysian identities, such as animals, tassels and flag colors, which represent the rich diversity of cultures, traditions and biodiversity of plants.
By 2020, the ministry has launched a campaign to attract 30 million international tourists to Malaysia and generate 100 billion ringgit ($ 25 billion) in revenue, focusing on ecotourism and culture. .
In addition, a 5 million ringgit fund called GAMELAN Malaysia was set up to provide financial support to the private tourism industry, which organizes marketing activities in Malaysia as a business and entertainment destination. In addition, the government has opened 13 more ports for entry visas in an effort to facilitate the arrival of Chinese, Indian and other international tourists.
