Sangkat Choam Chao 2 Authority, Khan Por Sen Chey Repairs Damaged Concrete Road
(Phnom Penh): Sangkat Choam Chao 2 Authority, led by Sangkat Chief Va Sarang, put a machine down a 30-meter-long concrete road that was completely damaged, making it impossible for people to travel to fill a new concrete floor. To be as clean as before and for people to travel easily and safely again.
The damaged road is located in Prey Lvea village, Sangkat Choam Chao 2, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, and was demolished by the authorities at 4 pm on July 24, 2019.
Mr. Va Sarang said that the concrete road was built by pouring concrete with bamboo bones during 2006, and as of 2019, the road is 13 years old.
The construction at that time did not use steel bones, but used bamboo bones, 2,400 meters long and 6 meters wide, and connected from Veng Sreng Road at Chrey Kong village to Prey Sandek village, Prey Lvea village and Prey Speu village, Choam Chao 2 commune, but it did not Damaged 2,400 meters, only 30 meters damaged, making it impossible for people to move around.
The commune chief said that the damage caused the villagers great distress. Because of this, he could not remain silent, he also led the force to put the machine down to the broken point to pour new concrete floor to complete the repair to improve the difficulties of the people who use this road.
