Foreign Ministry Spokesman: Cambodia's Visa Restrictions Exaggerated by Radio Free Asia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Cambodia's Visa Restrictions on Foreigners Are Exaggerated by RFA Let the general public be confused. This is the assertion of Mr. Ket Sophan, spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation.
A spokesman for the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs gave an interview to the media after talks between Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, and Maria Sargren, outgoing Swedish Ambassador to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. This morning, July 24, 2019.
The Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs' immediate response came after Radio Free Asia on July 23, 2019, reported that Samdech Techo Hun Sen was behind the deployment of six European officials. In the blacklist that does not provide visas.
Ket Sophan, spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia, said that for the issuance of the Ministry's instructions to its representative offices in other countries, Cambodia does not limit, do not grant or restrict "visas" to any foreigner. No one, but RFA published completely exaggerated information.
However, according to Ket Sophan, an independent, sovereign country has the right to refuse and has the right to enforce the law to restrict any foreigner or group that enters their country for any reason. It will affect the security and order of the country.
