Ratanakkiri Provincial Authority Continues to Disseminate the 4th Anti-Drug Campaign
(Ratanakkiri): The fourth anti-drug plan for 2019 has been disseminated by the Ratanakkiri Provincial Authority to young people, students, the Armed Forces and all government officials in Ratanakkiri.
The dissemination of the 4th Anti-Drug Plan 2019 was organized by the Provincial Drug Control Committee at the Samdech Techo Hun Sen Theater this morning, July 24, 2019 under the chairmanship of Mr. Thong Savun, Provincial Governor. Ratanakkiri will be attended by young people, students, government officials, the three armed forces and more than 300 people.
Mr. Lon Sopheap, Director of the Secretariat for Combating Drugs and Deputy Governor, said that the plan for the fourth anti-drug campaign has been set by the Royal Government for one year, starting from December 31, 2019.
Ratanakkiri provincial governor Thong Savun, chairman of the provincial drug control commission, has put in place a plan to prevent, crack down and fight illegal drugs. He said that the drug problem is an issue that must be prevented together because drugs lead to the destruction of society and hinder the development of the country.
The provincial governor added that students, youth, civil servants, including the armed forces of all kinds must stay away from drugs and must join together in cracking down on the influx of traffic, trafficking and illegal use of drugs for society, villages, communes and districts. And a drug-free society.
There is now information related to the African swine fever, or ASF, pandemic in China, Vietnam, which has severely affected pig farmers. What should all consumers know about African swine fever?
On July 24, 2019, a company that specializes in raising pigs called CPF came out to explain to the people. By understanding the symptoms and signs of the disease, you also become a part of preventing it from spreading and causing damage.
ASF is a viral disease in pigs that originated in Africa and spread to Europe last year, to China and to Vietnam this year. This disease causes the pigs to die suddenly, so we consider it a disease that causes great loss to pig farmers.
At the moment, Cambodia is very surprised by swine flu! All public and private institutions and breeders' associations have joined hands to fully support the prevention of this disease by organizing seminars to educate pig farmers across the country by inviting specialists in the field. Presentation and knowledge, as well as constant monitoring of the situation.
At this point, the company explained that the disease is not transmitted to humans. Do not be afraid of this disease, because the virus is transmitted only to pigs, not infecting or transmitting to humans. You can still eat pork normally just by cooking it properly. For the method of choosing to buy pork should be purchased from a place that is clean and reliable.
Have you ever seen some pictures or video clips shared on social media? In fact, diseases caused by unhygienic eating often infect various germs, especially bacteria that are present during production or when stored improperly, causing food spoilage and improper cooking. Hygienic, including uncooked cooking. As a eater, how can you contribute to improving this situation?
The disease is not transmitted to humans and you can still eat pork without worry, but to reduce the risk of spreading the disease, you should stop importing or consuming foods of unknown origin or from a group of countries that have Risks, and in addition, you should dispose of food waste properly.
