On that occasion, Minister Veng Sakhon praised the Republic of Belarus for providing quality and efficient agricultural machinery to Cambodian farmers.
The Minister also pointed out that in the current situation in the agricultural sector, Cambodia has evolved from the use of traction by cattle to the use of machinery more than 97%, which is a priority mechanism to promote the modernization of agriculture and machinery. Agricultural trade of the Ministry's agricultural development strategy.
He said that the development of the use of machinery in the agricultural sector has greatly increased competition between companies that produce machinery and require the introduction of new technologies.
The minister stressed that the Belarusian side should examine the possibility of supplying high-tech machinery for harvesting and post-harvest to increase convenience, efficiency and competitiveness for farmers.
The Minister hoped and believed that the cooperation between the two countries would not only focus on the supply of agricultural machinery to Cambodia, requesting the Belarusian side to examine the possibility of trade, investment in processing and export of Cambodian agricultural products. Foreign.
In response, Mr. Svidersky agreed and supported the Minister's statement, stating that the third meeting of the Joint Committee on Trade and Economic Cooperation between Cambodia and Belarus will be held on 25-26. In Siem Reap, there will be many opportunities and benefits for both countries to strengthen and expand cooperation in the expected areas, especially in the field of agriculture.
Regarding the processing of agricultural products, Mr. Svidersky also informed that he invited and welcomed the Minister to lead a delegation of professional and private sector officials to visit, exchange experiences and learn more about management, development, production chain and product processing. Agriculture in the Republic of Belarus soon.
Please be informed that the main results obtained from this morning's meeting include:
First, to cooperate in researching the needs of machinery and new technology between the Ministry and officials of manufacturers and suppliers of machinery from the Republic of Belarus to meet the needs and markets of Cambodia.
Second, to expand cooperation between the two countries through official visits to exchange experiences and learn more about the production chain and processing of agricultural products, as well as management, development and reforestation.
Third, agree to establish a mechanism to promote Cambodian rubber trade to the Republic of Belarus.
Fourth, the two sides agreed to organize and participate in the upcoming agricultural machinery exhibition.
