Koh Kong Provincial Referral Hospital and Khlong Yai District Hospital provide free treatment for gastrointestinal diseases
(Koh Kong): Gastric or peptic ulcer: It affects almost all people in the gastrointestinal tract. On July 23, 2019, people in the province received free medical check-ups and treatment from a team of doctors from Bangkok, Thailand under the collaboration between Koh Kong Provincial Referral Hospital and Khlong Yai District Hospital.
This is the first time that people living in Koh Kong province receive treatment and treatment of gastroenteritis without having to pay a fee from a team of doctors from Thailand, while observing a large number of people with gastrointestinal problems. And need a lot of money to treat.
Dr. Hay Layson, Director of Koh Kong Provincial Referral Hospital, said that through modern medical technology and skilled doctors can provide better examination and treatment of gastrointestinal diseases to the people under the cooperation of the department to the parties. Thailand.
The director of the provincial referral hospital said that in case of a virus suspected to be cancer of the stomach or intestines, the doctors will continue to test at Thammasat hospital after knowing the diagnosis and send back to the provincial referral hospital to provide Therapeutic drugs. This treatment does not examine and treat gastrointestinal diseases, Thai doctors will select 100 patients for 2 days, from 23 to 24 July 2019.
According to Dr. Hay Layson, gastrointestinal disorders are caused by a virus that disguises the face, misuse of dietary fiber and self-inflammation, which needs to be treated in a timely manner to avoid worsening symptoms. Cancer.
Ms. Wongwanwatna added that she was happy that the health's humanitarian mission was aimed at improving public welfare as they suffered from chronic stomach and intestinal problems. If there is another opportunity, she will ask for work from other Thai doctors to come and check and treat the people of Koh Kong again.
