Phnom Penh plans to host the General Assembly of the International Association of Mayors in French in early December 2019
(Phnom Penh): Phnom Penh is planning to host the General Assembly of the International Association of Mayors in French in early December 2019, focusing on urban development and people's livelihood.
Phnom Penh Governor Khuong Sreng confirmed that the Phnom Penh Capital Administration is ready to host the General Assembly of the International Association of Mayors in French from December 3 to 5, which will be Members join more than 100 cities to discuss and share experiences of sustainable urban development.
Mr. Khuong Sreng, at the meeting of the organizing committee of the General Assembly of the International Association of Mayors in the French Language on the afternoon of July 23, said that the organization of this General Assembly is the pride of Cambodia in the international arena to be able to welcome the delegation as Many countries came to the meeting in Phnom Penh, Cambodia, and presented the full peace factor to the international community.
"For this work, we have prepared for the permission of the head of the Royal Government and informed the relevant ministries, the Council of Ministers, as well as three other provinces, including Siem Reap, Battambang and Kampot, which are also French-speaking cities, so we can do this work," he said. "We have prepared a lot and our main task is to receive guests from other cities, to arrange security and order, and this guest travels to Siem Reap, where we have to organize hospitality."
Mr. Nuon Pharath, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, said that the International Association of French Mayors, which is planned to be held in Phnom Penh, focused on the 40th anniversary, the 40th anniversary of the establishment of the International Association of French Mayors and the 40th anniversary. The year of the liberation of Phnom Penh from the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime.
"By defining this topic, it shows what the wonders of Phnom Penh start from the ghost town and become the city with the highest economic growth today," he said.
