The Kantha Bopha Hospital Foundation's announcement, obtained by Fresh News on July 24, states that since its inception and official launch on April 11, 2018, the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia Receive large donations from government officials, the armed forces, private companies, organizations, associations and people across the country, as well as people living in other countries.
At the same time, the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia observed fundraising activities in various forms, including concerts, product sales and fundraising, in order to raise funds to donate to Kantha Bopha Hospital directly or through the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia.
On behalf of the guardians of the children and on behalf of the hospital itself, the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia would like to express our deep gratitude to all the benefactors and donations that these are the best charitable gestures to contribute to the sustainability of the hospital. The five Kantha Bopha locations are in Phnom Penh and Siem Reap.
Kantha Bopha Hospital Foundation emphasizes that "However, the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia also observed some activities operating in an inappropriate and irregular manner, which may be opportunistic and do not serve the interests of the hospital as a whole. The Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia would like to call for an immediate end to these irregular activities, otherwise the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia will cooperate with the competent authorities to take legal action.
For fundraising activities that are truly willing to serve the interests of Kantha Bopha Hospital, the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia encourages direct collaboration with the Secretariat of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia, located at the Ministry of Economy and Finance or by telephone. : 061 701 111 or 096 701 1111.
The Secretariat of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia is pleased to provide full cooperation to all stakeholders and to authorize the use of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia logo as well as other logos in the conduct of legal activities.
Authorities demolish a fence post of a general who encroached on the land of Wat Kork Panchan, Srah Preah Tonle in Por Sen Chey district
(Phnom Penh): Po Sen Chey district authorities, led by Deputy District Governor Pang Lida, went down to remove and demolish a post that residents claimed was ordered by a general to plant and throw stones to encroach on the Preah Tonle pond. The land of Wat Kork Panchan is more than 3 hectares in Choam Chao 2 village, Sangkat Choam Chao 2, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
In fact, on the evening of July 23, 2019, the authorities of Po Sen Chey district went down to remove and demolish the pillars and arrested two men suspected of being part of the group that encroached on the pagoda land to interrogate him. Any general in command behind that back.
Residents of Choam Chao 2 village said that the construction of a post to take Preah Tonle land has only recently taken place, with a group of elderly men with radios in their hands carrying cement poles to plant around the pond. Preah Tonle and then spray blue paint. After planting the poles, a group of about 10 people always drank and guarded the poles without anyone removing them.
Residents added that when people went to inquire about planting poles to take the pagoda land, the casters and guards told the villagers that their boss should come down and cast their ballots because the land belonged to their boss. That wears three stars, so people do not remove this pole, be careful.
Around this case, Venerable Seng Thong, the chief abbot of Kork Panchan pagoda, once said that he knew that someone had come to set up a pagoda to take the land at Wat Preah Tonle, but he had already reported to the local authorities. He also said that the pagoda land is still pagoda land and no one can buy, sell or take ownership of it.
It should be reminded that on November 7, 2005, 36,656 square meters of Preah Tonle pond land was registered by Mr. Chhay Rithisen, former director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Phnom Penh. Banchan is located in Choam Chao Village, Sangkat Choam Chao, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
During 2016, the land of Srah Preah Tonle was once stolen by a group of crooks, but was prevented by the people and complained in time. At that time, a group of corrupt people stole and sold the land next to Kok Panchan Primary School, which belonged to a pagoda measuring 7 meters by 100 meters.
Residents of Sangkat Choam Chao 2 said that the case of Wat Kork confirmed that the Tonle Sap pond is under the action of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court because the villagers have filed a lawsuit to protect and dissolve the Wat Kork Commission because they suspect that the pagoda land can Merchants can buy because there is a conspiracy from people who have the authority to do things in the pagoda.
Residents in Romeas Hek district, Svay Rieng province, are still afraid of African swine fever, and pig traders are still selling poorly
(Svay Rieng): Vendors selling pork in Kampong Trach market, Romeas Hek district, Svay Rieng province, said that people were afraid to eat pork, but only two pigs could not be sold for two days.
Vendors said that the reason for not daring to eat pork for fear of contracting African swine fever, affecting the health of the family and fear of transmitting the virus to their pigs is raising a family, which leads to loss of money, affecting the livelihood of the family, despite the Ministry of Agriculture and Forestry Hunting and fishing claim that African swine fever is contagious, but not to humans.
Most people and government officials stop eating pork by eating chicken, beef and fish, making the pork business lose capital to sell pork. Especially in Kampong Trach market, Kampong Trach village, Kampong Trach commune, Romeas Hek district, hundreds of families and government officials have stopped buying pork to eat.
It should be noted that more than 10 pork stalls were closed and one stall selling only two pigs for two days was thrown into the Kampong Trach River. The reason is that traders continue to import Vietnamese pigs through some corridors in Romeas Hek district, Svay Rieng province.
On Tuesday, Russian and Chinese military planes led the first joint patrol operation in the Asia-Pacific region, after which South Korea accused Russia of encroaching on its airspace and Japan. Russian and South Korean military planes have breached their airspace over the waters of an archipelago controlled by South Korea, but Japan is also claiming ownership.
However, at a press conference on Wednesday, Chinese Defense Ministry spokesman Wu Qian dismissed the allegations made by the Seoul government, saying that "during the patrol, Russia and China respected "Strictly abide by international laws and standards without flying into the airspace of any country."
(Phnom Penh): The construction of 209 "Borey Kimthy" apartments in Kakap village, Sangkat Kakap 2, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, was found by the authorities to be illegal.
After that, Mr. Pang Lida, Deputy Governor of Por Senchey District, led the Khan Office with the participation of Khan Land Officer and Chief of Khan Environment Office to inspect and suspend construction activities at 9:30 am on July 24. 2019 and sent a letter to the owner of the Borey who is abroad to order the right to be able to continue construction.
Mr. Pang Lida said that the construction of the Borey "Kim Thi" has 209 flats, which are under construction without a proper permit, and now some flats are almost 100 percent completed, while others are under construction. Achieved about 70 to 80 percent. The temporary suspension of construction activities now due to the suspicion that this Borey is under construction without permission because the authorities never knew before.
The Deputy Governor confirmed that after receiving information from the people, he also led a joint committee to inspect and ask information from the owner of the Borey to find other relevant documents, especially business law and construction law.
However, in this case, Mr. Sok Sambath, Borey representative, confirmed that his company actually had a building permit for 150 flats from the governor of Por Senchey district on April 1, 2016.
