(Kampong Chhnang): Sre Ampil Waterfall is a new eco-tourism resort located in Kdol Sen Chey commune, Teuk Phos district, Kampong Chhnang province, from Kampong Chhnang provincial town to Sre Ampil natural waterfall, just over 50 kilometers away.
Upon arrival in Kdol Sen Chey commune, the people and the authorities were very welcoming, each of them really understood the value of tourism, which can help improve their lives to another level.
Walking a little closer to the river, you will see the water flowing through the rocks incessantly, this attraction does not allow tourists to skip swimming and not only have a place to swim. If you travel along the river, you will find a diving spot.
Kdol Sen Chey commune chief Moeung Visal Sok said that the community is currently focusing on the development of the Sre Ampil resort to welcome the presence of tourists who are expected to increase in the future. Ahead.
Excursions along the river under the shade of lush trees ensure that visitors will fade away and return with a refreshing fun with the natural beauty of the eastern part of the Reserve. Nature of the Oral Mountains.
Apart from the natural area, which is a unique tourist treasure, the Sre Ampil waterfall area also leaves historical sites from the Khmer Rouge era and traces the legends of the people of the district, such as Koh Ta Preng, Dan Preah Bat, etc. .
Currently, there are not many tourists from other provinces to visit Sre Ampil Waterfall Resort, but it is not that the road to get there is not difficult to travel because this resort is newly established and has not been prepared. Some are still good, but there are still local tourists to visit gradually, and there are also tourists to camp there.
The main purpose of establishing the community and the Sre Ampil waterfall resort is to create tourism services provided by the community itself, which enables them to earn extra income from this sector.
In particular, it has diverted from deforestation, wildlife hunting and crime in protected areas, leading to the destruction of natural resources in the region. On the other hand, if the community works together to protect the forest, wildlife and natural resources to survive, this area will receive more attention from tourists and increase the number of recreational activities, the community will also earn income. Too much.
