(Phnom Penh): Mr. Dy Vichea and Ms. Hun Mana have decided to donate $ 20,000 per year for 5 years to the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia to support the activities of the five Kantha Bopha Hospitals in Phnom Penh and Siem Reap for Help treat Cambodian children. This was confirmed by Mr. Nong Piseth, Deputy Director of the Secretariat of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia to Fresh News on July 24.
Mr. Nong Piseth stated, "The Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia would like to express our deepest gratitude for the generosity of His Excellency Dy Vichea and Lok Chumteav Hun Mana, who on the occasion of the 11th Anniversary of the Cambodian Youth Movement A.157. $ 20,000 / year for the next 5 years to the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia. "This is the most precious spirit we can never forget."
Please be informed that the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia is an official fund established by the Royal Government of Cambodia under the initiative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who are currently both the Founder and Honorary President of the Foundation. This fund was established for the purpose of mobilizing charitable funds to support the operation of the five Kantha Bopha Hospitals in Phnom Penh and Siem Reap.
For more information, please contact the Secretary of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia, located at the Ministry of Economy and Finance, or by phone: 061 70 1111 and 096 701 1111.
