Siem Reap Armed Forces Arrest 13 Suspects and 1 kg of Drugs to Court
(Siem Reap): The Siem Reap Provincial Gendarmerie, in cooperation with the Sot Nikum District Gendarmerie, led by Lt. Col. Tha Dalux, Provincial Gendarmerie Commander, conducted a large-scale operation to crack down on drug offenses in Sot Nikum District. Detained 13 suspects and 1 kg of drug exhibits and sent them to the Provincial Gendarmerie Headquarters for questioning and to build a case to be sent to the provincial court for legal action.
The operation to crack down on a large drug trafficking group was carried out under the direction of Brigadier General Por Vannith, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie, and was coordinated by Mr. Keut Van Reth, Prosecutor of the Siem Reap Provincial Court. On the night of July 19, 2019, it was located in Ta Nhek village, Ta Nhek commune, Sot Nikum district, Siem Reap province.
After the interrogation, the police brought in a drug dealer named Pen Thea to cooperate in cracking down on another gangster. Phnom Penh seized another 300 grams of ice drugs, two mobile phones and some appliances.
The 13 suspects and more than 1 kg of drug exhibits and samurai swords, as well as mobile phones and smoking equipment were sent to the provincial court by the Provincial Gendarmerie on the afternoon of July 23, 2019 for legal action. Legal way.
