21 Cambodian Muslims go on pilgrimage to Saudi Arabia with the help of the Cambodian Good Sources Association
(Phnom Penh): Twenty-one Cambodian Muslims on the evening of July 23, 2019 at the Phnom Penh International Airport left for the Hajj in Saudi Arabia with the help of the Good Sources Association of Cambodia. Mr. Sos Mohamad, Advisor to Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister of the Ministry of Interior and President of the Good Sources Association of Cambodia, paid a courtesy call on the Cambodian Muslims today.
On that occasion, Mr. Sos Mohamad thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, for facilitating all forms of Islam to comply with the rules of Islam.
Mr. Sos Mohamad confirmed that 2019 is the third year of the Hajj project of the Good Sources Association of Cambodia. In the first year, 2017, the association supported 9 staff, the second year (2018) sent 24 staff. This is the third year that 20 staff members have been sent to Hajj in Saudi Arabia.
The Good Sources Association of Cambodia is a national association with many charitable projects. Currently, the association feeds 3,575 orphans, providing three meals a day while staying in dormitories, schools, education and medical check-ups.
The association runs 32 self-built schools, 120 mosques, five ponds and 300 wells and toilets. At the same time, the association also built a hospital in Prek Anchanh commune, Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province.
