Minister of Women's Affairs Urges JICA to Continue Cooperation on Economic Empowerment for Women in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs, on July 23, 2019 requested the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) to further strengthen cooperation on the project on gender mainstreaming for economic empowerment of women. In Cambodia.
This was confirmed by Ms. Chan Sory, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, to the media after the courtesy call and discussion of the mission of the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) headquarters with Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi at the Ministry of Women's Affairs. In the afternoon of July 23, 2019.
Ms. Chan Sory stated that during the meeting, Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs, told JICA to further strengthen cooperation on the project on gender mainstreaming for women's economic empowerment in Cambodia.
Ms. Chan Sory added that at the same time, Minister Ing Kantha Phavi also requested the JICA side to monitor more in order to do more and must continue to cooperate on this work even more.
According to the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, the project is currently available in five provinces: Kampong Cham, Kampong Thom, Tbong Khmum, Kampong Chhnang and Siem Reap. In that work to increase the capacity of tourism in Siem Reap and agriculture in Kampong Chhnang.
She said that this is the main work of the Gender Mainstreaming Project in the economic work to increase women's empowerment, to have additional income in the family, to increase the family budget and reduce the gender gap in the province. Those.
It should be noted that the Ministry of Women's Affairs and the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) have a long history of cooperation since the early 1990s. Since 2003, two technical cooperation projects to strengthen gender mainstreaming mechanisms at the national and sub-national levels have been implemented for 10 years.
(Phnom Penh): At least 900 high standard restaurants in Cambodia have applied for the "Clean Restaurant Contest" organized by the Ministry of Tourism in the near future. This is according to the report of the Ministry of Tourism.
The contest "Clean Restaurant: No Trash under the Table" can be successful based on the participation of the private sector, business owners, restaurants, cafes, tourists and all citizens through the use of Green passport booklets that can evaluate restaurants, canteens. Which he ate by asking the business owner of the restaurant, restaurant, tourism, stamp to confirm that it is clean on its booklet.
Please note that every end of the year, the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia always organizes a summary of restaurants with the most stamped restaurants will win.
The "Clean Restaurant: No Garbage Restaurant Under the Table" ranking rating, which includes 2 basic indicators, 5 detailed indicators and 13 criteria:
* Indicators on the management of garbage at the table: In order for business owners to prepare bins for all meals and have staff to collect garbage that guests throw the wrong bins and remind guests about the impact. Of disposal of waste by using wipes instead of paper.
Key indicators on clean public toilets: In order to clean the bathroom regularly when there are many guests and there is a separate bathroom for men and women and there is no bad smell.
