Cambodia-Vietnam Ministry of National Defense Continues Border Information Exchange Cooperation to Crack Down on Crimes
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia and the Ministry of National Defense of Vietnam will continue to work together to exchange information to ensure security and order along the border and timely crackdown on various crimes along the border. This is according to General Neang Phat.
The presentation on strengthening cooperation in cracking down on border crime was made during a meeting between General Neang Phat, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of National Defense, and Lieutenant General Nguyen Chi Vinh, Deputy Minister of Defense, at the Ministry of Defense. This afternoon, July 23, 2019.
General Neang Phat stated that the two sides will build a border of peace and good cooperation, continue to cooperate in excavating the remains of Vietnamese volunteer soldiers who were sacrificed in Cambodia during the civil war in Cambodia.
In addition, the General said that the two Ministries of National Defense will continue to jointly implement and take effective measures to prevent the enemy's strategy of dividing the peace and solidarity between Cambodia and Vietnam. The armies of the two countries must be the core force to ensure stability, cooperation and development in all fields, prevent any inactive activities that lead to the disintegration of peace and the disintegration of the two armies.
