Mr. Pech Sophoan: The new Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province will lead the province successfully with the participation of government officials and people from all walks of life.
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Pech Sophoan, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, expressed his belief that Mr. Kouch Chamroeun will lead Preah Sihanouk Province to more success, but at the same time requires the participation of officials Government officials and citizens of all walks of life.
Mr. Pech Sophoan's speech was made this morning, July 23, 2019, during the graduation ceremony with Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province at the graduation ceremony of students of Sihanoukville Polytechnic Institute at the hotel. Independent.
Mr. Pech Sophoan also expressed his appreciation to Mr. Kouch Chamroeun for his ability to lead Sihanoukville to success and prosperity, but in order to be successful, it is necessary to have the support of government officials, people and youth. The new Governor of Sihanoukville will be able to lead the administrative reform towards further progress, despite the many complex challenges ahead.
The leader of the Ministry of Labor added that Sihanoukville is currently developing rapidly and almost unexpectedly, and he considers that this progress is the fruit of peace under the leadership of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen. He stressed that peace is the most important factor that gives us the opportunity to develop the country.
At the same time, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun emphasized that all the work can not be achieved without the participation, so it is necessary to involve all relevant parties to manage the growing waste in Sihanoukville. Up this better.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun called on the people as well as the youth to participate in improving the sanitary environment in Sihanoukville, especially the problem of garbage. He said that currently Sihanoukville is a significant increase in waste, and the increase in the amount of waste is due to the growth of people and human consumption.
For good waste management, the governor recommended three points, including:
* First, urge local authorities and relevant officials to make clear plans to work with waste collection companies. * Second: Garbage collection companies must strengthen their capacity and equip themselves with the necessary equipment to ensure timely garbage collection. Time. * Third: Ask citizens who use garbage to pack and organize properly so that garbage collectors can easily collect.
At the same time, both Mr. Pich Sophoan and Mr. Kouch Chamroeun commended all the teachers and academic staff who participated in the skills training for young people so that they have the opportunity to get a job at the same time. The job market in Sihanoukville is in demand while it is developing rapidly. Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign on July 23: More than 1,180 illegal vehicles found and more than 414 fined
