(Phnom Penh): In order to promote the education of young Cambodian students, on July 23, 2019, True Vision Cambodia International School sent 20 more of its primary school students to study in Singapore. One week to attend the study exchange and sign a memorandum of understanding.
According to Seng Bona, the founder and director general of True Vision Cambodia International School, in order to have a high salary and success in life, young people must have real knowledge, clear skills, honesty and high patience by working from the heart. Ethical ‍‍.
In fact, schools often send students to study exchanges in developed countries and economies to enable them to acquire more new knowledge and build human resources in Cambodia through the acquisition of external knowledge. Fill in the knowledge inside, which in part helps to develop the nation to progress continuously.
True Vision Cambodia International School is open from Kindergarten to 12th grade and upcoming university level.
The main goal of True Vision Cambodia International School is to provide students with a broader perspective on the world, to explore a diverse system of study abroad, especially to make our students see the best of both worlds. Of living and working abroad, and in the near future, the school is also preparing to send its students to study abroad.
According to Khim Sokheng, the guardian of the students, sending students to exchange experiences abroad is opening a vision for Cambodian boys and girls to gain new knowledge because children are the heirs of bamboo. Getting a good education in the country as well as gaining experience abroad with a more advanced education system is a good thing.
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Thong Sam Ath, Under Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, this morning, July 24, 2019, led a delegation to visit 141 police students at the National Police Vocational Training Course at the National Police School, Zone 2, Kampong Cham Province. Know well-being, study, training, accommodation and eating.
After listening to the report of Major General Rath Chamroeun, the principal of the school, Mr. Thong Sam Ath said that this training course is a history for people who have turned from civilian to police students and will become a police force. Full National Police Force after the successful completion of this course.
He emphasized that the Royal Government, under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has continued to set out reform policies in all areas, including the armed forces of all kinds. The Royal Government is highly committed to ensuring peace, political, economic, social, security and security of villages, communes, and sangkats, which are the foundation of the nation's development in all areas and provide opportunities for people to live in peace.
On this occasion, Mr. Thong Sam Ath also made some recommendations as follows:
* First, the National Police School of the region: must monitor the teaching of teachers and evaluate the study in accordance with the internal regulations and punish students who do wrong without understanding.
* Second: For children who are police students: must pay attention to study, both inside and outside the classroom, must be present at all times of study and training, respect all the rules stated in the internal regulations, must adhere to the concept of learning To know, not to finish.
When returning to work, you must behave as a qualified police officer, have good morals, be responsible for your work, and be honest so that the management can give you confidence.
In addition, the delegation also brought 50 small boxes of noodles, 5 sticks of fish sauce, 5 sticks of soy sauce and some money to support the school, school officials and police students.
