Minister of Public Works: In 2021, Cambodia plans to build another bridge across the Mekong River in Kratie province, more than 1,700 meters long (Video inside) (Kratie): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, confirmed that Cambodia will request a concessional loan from the Chinese government. In the future, to build another bridge across the Mekong River in Kratie province with a total length of 1761 meters.
The Minister of Public Works confirmed this to the media as he led a team to inspect the construction site of the Mekong River bridge in Kratie province on July 23, 2019.
Mr. Sun Chanthol confirmed that after this review, he will prepare a proposal in 2020 and construction may take place in 2021. He claimed that the bridge will make it easier for people to travel from Stung Treng to Kampong Thom, which saves more time and money.
