Mr. Vongsey Visoth led a delegation to study in China under the Master Plan for Integrated Transportation in Cambodia.
The working group of the Supreme National Economic Council, with technical assistance from the Chinese government, has been working on a master plan for a transportation system that will determine (1) the infrastructure needs to support development in Cambodia and (2) methods and prioritization. And the management of public investment projects, including projects implementing the Public-Private Partnership (PPP) mechanism, which covers transportation, roads, waterways, airways and railways.
The master plan for the transportation system is in line with the policy of the Royal Government, especially the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 to achieve a transport system that is highly interconnected and competitive with neighboring countries. To support the long-term economic development, connect the major economic poles in the country and accelerate economic integration into the region and the world.
A vibrant transportation system will help Cambodia increase its export capacity, promote economic diversification and attract investment and all kinds of business activities. This master plan is also an important achievement goal set in the Industrial Sector Development Policy 2015-2025.
At the same time, this master plan can improve the quality of investment planning to have a clear concept from all angles and can be properly prioritized, taking into account all aspects of technical, social, environmental and financial, including cost recovery plans. Additional arrangements have been made for financing and institutional capacity development to ensure sustainable development.
After the study visit, Mr. Vongsey Visoth, representing the Royal Government of Cambodia, will also sign three exchange letters with representatives of the Chinese government.
Executive Director of the Cambodian Tourism Federation calls on people to return to growing coffee as the coffee sector grows
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Lou Meng, Executive Director of the Cambodian Tourism Federation, called on people to return to growing coffee as the coffee sector is growing rapidly in Cambodia and will continue to grow for the next 30 years.
This statement was made by the Executive Director of the Tourism Federation of Cambodia on the occasion of participating in the program "Official Announcement of the National Coffee Competition in Cambodia" organized in collaboration with the Ministry of Tourism, Restaurant Association of Cambodia, Tourism Federation of Cambodia. , Coffee Institute and Coffee Company.
The program "Official announcement of the National Coffee Competition in Cambodia" was held on the morning of July 23, 2019 with the participation of Mr. Mean Vandeth, Director of the Vocational Training Department of the Ministry of Tourism, Mr. Lou Meng, President of the Federation Cambodia Tourism, Ms. Hak Lina, President of the Cambodian Restaurant Association, Mr. Chong Hok Sun, President of the Coffee Institute.
Please be informed that under the cooperation of the Ministries of Tourism, the Cambodian Restaurant Association, the Cambodian Tourism Federation, the Coffee Institute and the Coffee Company organized the launch of the 2019 National Coffee Competition in Cambodia.
He added, "Therefore, I would like to urge people who have plantations or those who want to invest to invest in coffee crops, because now coffee in Cambodia is famous, coffee in Mondulkiri, Ratanakiri or neighboring provinces. "This is all good land to invest in coffee and get better results."
Mr. Lou Meng said that coffee is predicted that from now until the next 30 years, it is still important all over the world, and Cambodian coffee tastes different from coffee imported from other countries. Especially for those who want to invest should start growing from now on, because coffee is very expensive in the future.
In addition, Mr. Mean Vandeth, a representative of the Ministry of Tourism, encouraged and encouraged more investment in the coffee sector. He explained the promotion of the coffee sector in Cambodia, saying that as the tourism sector grows, more and more tourists come, which leads to the establishment of hotels, hotels, and other restaurants, and when there are more hotels and restaurants in demand. More coffee the same.
He said that when there is a high demand, the production of farmers is the same. On behalf of the Ministry of Tourism, we would like to encourage the tourism industry, hotels and restaurants to declare their support for the coffee industry.
With this overwhelming demand for coffee, Cambodia always organizes the national coffee brewing competition in Cambodia every year. In fact, on July 23, 2019, in collaboration with the Ministry of Tourism, the Cambodian Restaurant Association, the Cambodian Tourism Federation, the Coffee Institute and the Coffee Company, organized the launch of the 2019 National Coffee Competition in Cambodia.
The National Coffee Maker Competition in Cambodia has four main objectives of the National Coffee Maker Competition, including:
1: Provide a platform for all sectors of the coffee industry to share information and jointly promote the use of coffee and coffee business. 2: Raise awareness and promote the coffee industry in Cambodia. 3: Present the coffee industry at national and international forums. 4. Encourage the younger generation as well as improve coffee making skills throughout the country.
Chong Hok Sun, President of the Coffin Institute, said that the national coffee making competition in Cambodia has been held since 2010 until now for nine years. Nationwide national coffee brewing competitions are held annually, with many coffee brewing professionals demonstrating their excellent brewing talents and inspiring new innovations to the coffee industry.
He added that this year, Cambodia has 30 applicants and all are Cambodians and do not require them to participate as a shop owner or business owner, but allowed to participate freely.
