Senior Minister Kun Kim Chairs a Disaster Preparedness and Rescue Meeting at 70th Brigade Command
(Phnom Penh): General Kun Kim, Senior Minister in charge of Special Missions and First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, this morning, July 23, 2019, chaired a meeting on disaster prevention and rescue work. Organized by Lt. Gen. Mao Sophan, Deputy Commander of the Army and Commander of the 70th Division.
Speaking on the occasion, Lt. Gen. Mao Sophan confirmed that the 711 Emergency and Fire Brigade of the 70th Brigade was established in March 2009 under the cooperation between the Division and the Japanese Medical Rescue Organization (JPR). Of Kobe, Japan in order to strengthen disaster relief capacity.
According to General Mao Sophan, in the past, the emergency forces and fire brigade of the 70th Brigade issued a total of 1,701 rescue interventions, of which 1,668 were rescued and participated in the operation. Search and rescue victims in the collapse of a seven-story building in Sihanoukville.
After watching the demonstration of traffic and fire rescue exercises and listening to the experience of search and rescue in the collapse of the seven-story building, Senior Minister Kun Kim expressed his appreciation and appreciation to the 70th Brigade and all soldiers. Classes that take care of both physical and mental strength, try to explore, cooperate well and respond in a timely manner in disaster relief in accordance with the principles of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
