Ratanakkiri Provincial Governor Urges Citizens and Civil Servants to Participate in Preserving the National Achievement by Not Dumping Garbage in Drainage and Violating Public Roads
(Ron Kiri): The Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, Mr. Thong Savun, urged the people and government officials in the units to take care of the national achievement by not throwing garbage in the sewers on the streets and not violating the public sidewalks. Because environmental sanitation is the duty of every citizen.
The urging of the provincial governor on the occasion of presiding over the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the DBST asphalt road, drainage and gardening on Street 50 and Street 46 in Boeung Kanseng Sangkat, Banlung City on the morning of the 23rd. This July 2019.
The above ceremony was also attended by Mr. Sok Horm, Provincial Councilor, Mrs. Deputy Governor, Deputy Director of the Department, student unit, hundreds of people.
Mr. Thong Savun confirmed that this road is an achievement under the initiative of Elder Bou Thong, the founder of Banlung, although he is currently receiving medical treatment, but he always thinks and sends condolences to the people in Ratanakkiri.
He said that in particular, Elder Bou Thong always advised local authorities at all levels to continue to develop Ratanakkiri province to develop in all areas, in fact, Road 50, which will build the pavement is his own initiative is to promote The beauty of the provincial town and the commute of the people are easy.
At the same time, he confirmed that after the completion of Road 50, it will be named "General Bou Thong Street" in return for the gratitude of Elder Bou Thong, who had sacrificed his precious life to join the national liberation movement. The motherland of Cambodia came out of the flames of war in the past and is the founder of Banlung today.
In addition, the provincial governor also requested the provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, which is the recipient of the project, to repair and build this road with good quality in accordance with the existing layout and technical standards.
Please note that section 50, which will be constructed of DBST type rubber flooring, is from the corner of No. 23 to Street 78A with a total length of 950 meters and a width of 18.2 meters, including a 0.8-meter-wide American sidewalk with a total size. 18,329 square meters. There are concrete embankments, corridors on both sides of the road and a 540-meter-long garden in the middle of the road.
Ratanakkiri Cam Control Officer Continues to Inspect Goods at Banlung Market, Bor Keo Market and O'Yadao, Found Some Outdated Products and Confiscated
(Rattanakiri): Officials of CamControl Rattanakiri Branch this morning, July 23, 2019, in cooperation with the Department of Commerce and local authorities, inspected the quality of pre-packaged goods at Banlung Market, Bor Keo Market and O'Yadao Market. Ratanakkiri province found more than 300 kg of expired products confiscated and burned.
Ratanakkiri Provincial Cam Control Officer said that during the inspection operation of the goods displayed at Banlung Market, Bor Keo Market and O'Yadao, the team found a total of 323.8 kilograms of expired and damaged goods. Make notes, confiscate, burn and destroy.
Ratanakkiri CamControl officials also called on all traders and vendors to be careful and pay attention before traveling, distributing, selling and buying food safely without affecting the health of consumers.
In a Q&A at a press conference posted on the Chinese Foreign Ministry's website on July 23, 2019, Geng Shuang was questioned: US media yesterday reported that China will be allowed to Using Cambodian naval bases under a secret agreement between the two countries? What do you think about this?
A Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman responded: "As far as I know, the Cambodian side has denied such publication. As a neighbor, China and Cambodia have been involved in cooperation throughout the country. Our cooperation is open, transparent, equitable and mutually beneficial. "We hope that such a story will not be exaggerated."
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, announced on Fresh News that the dissemination of information about Cambodia secretly signing with China using military bases was the worst fabrication against Cambodia. "This is the worst fabrication against Cambodia," he said. "Such a thing does not happen because foreign military bases are against the Cambodian constitution."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen clearly stated, "Why does Cambodia need a Chinese military presence on its territory?" We have never had any discussions with the Chinese leaders, let alone the signing of the agreement. "It is enough to stop using fake information about the presence of Chinese troops on Cambodian territory to oppose us."
Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly urges the national working group to help local people to meet their needs in a timely manner
(Kampong Cham): Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly, Permanent Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Central Working Group for Kampong Cham Province, urged all national working groups to unite between the Council and the Unity Command. The Armed Forces to build, develop and serve the needs of the people at the grassroots level.
Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly made this statement on the morning of July 23, 2019, when he presided over the launch of the National Working Group to Monitor and Support the Implementation of the Fourth Rectangular Political and Tactical Program. Of the Royal Government of Cambodia at Kampong Cham Provincial Hall.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol installs weighing station on Street 62 in Preah Vihear province
(Preah Vihear): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, decided to set up an additional weighing station on National Road 62 at the border of Preah Vihear and Kampong Thom provinces to prevent overcrowding. The decision to install a truck weighing station in Preah Vihear province was made during a meeting with officials of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear province this morning, July 23, 2019.
During the meeting, Mr. Sam Leang Try, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, raised concerns about overweight transportation in Preah Vihear Province. Especially on National Road 62, which is a challenge leading to this road being damaged.
Mr. Samleang Try requested Senior Minister Sun Chanthol to install another weighing station on National Road 62 at the border of Preah Vihear and Kampong Thom provinces to prevent overcrowding.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol agreed to this proposal and also instructed Mr. Seng Chhuon, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, who is responsible for the weighing station and the overweight work, to arrange the installation of the weighing station.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also advised to pay attention to the overweight. The minister said the overcrowding had severely damaged the road. He also used the formula to show that a truck overweight 10 tons is equivalent to 10,000 cars traveling on the road, and if a truck overweight 30 tons is equivalent to about 810,000 cars. Vehicles drive on that road.
