The Minister of Agriculture ordered the General Department of Agriculture to send agricultural machinery and rice seeds to help restore rice cultivation to agricultural communities in Tbeng commune, Kampong Thom province.
In the first phase, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries released 29 tons of rumduol rice seeds within the Cambodian food reserve system to distribute to more than 300 families for rehabilitation on 290 hectares.
The plowed rice is now a light, non-seasonal rice that is in the early stages, stunted and has a lot of weeds that can not be saved, even if it rains or there is a pumping water.
