(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance on July 23, 2019 launched a program to increase awareness of the use and implementation of information systems for public financial management (FMIS).
Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the FMIS Project Management Team, on behalf of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy, led a program to raise awareness on the implementation of the FMIS system.
Dr. Hean Sahip said that raising awareness on the implementation of FMIS directly on financial and budgetary operations has two main objectives:
1: In order for 17 ministries and institutions and budget units to fully transfer their rights, find out more about FMIS through the live demonstrations of officials who have been using FMIS in the relevant ministries and relevant departments of the Ministry of Economy and Finance. Stuff.
2. To encourage ministries and institutions to be prepared to consider the changes that will take place in 2020 and to provide a clear foundation and lead to a reduction in some of the implementation procedures and to prepare for the integration into the FMIS system. , Continue to eliminate work procedures and paperwork outside of FMIS completely in the future.
Dr. Hean Sahip praised the launch of this process as a symbol of great progress towards the use of FMIS as a unique system and as an important tool in directly supporting the implementation of key programs of The Public Financial Management Reform Program will contribute to the transformation of Cambodia into a digital government in the financial sector in line with the "Fourth Industrial Revolution".
