Man Arrested for Forging Army Uniform and Exaggerating Information of Ratanakkiri Provincial Governor
(Ratanakkiri): Police in Banlung City, Ratanakkiri Province, arrested a man in connection with a case of public defamation, forging an army uniform and using drugs.
According to the Banlung City Police report, the suspect was arrested on July 22, 2019 in O'Kandil Village, Boeung Kanseng Commune, Banlung City, Ratanakkiri Province. The suspect is Tham Kimleang, 27 years old, a carpenter, currently residing in O'Kandil Village, Sangkat Boeung Kanseng, Banlung City, Ratanakkiri Province.
Banlung police said the arrest was made because he posted a message on his Facebook page exaggerating the news of the change of governor of Ratanakkiri and that he was wearing an illegal army uniform.
The suspect is currently being held in custody at the Banlung City Police Inspectorate for further investigation.
Sanitary and phytosanitary certification (Phyto) is an essential document for the export of agricultural products such as fresh fruits, fresh vegetables, fresh plants, fish, live animals and other products required by the importing country.
The certificate states that the export product does not contain any pests or diseases that can damage the crop. Importers are responsible for compliance with sanitary and phytosanitary conditions.
He added that at this time, for the application for sanitation and phytosanitary certification can be done online through the same national gate.
