Please read the full text of the sub-decree below: University of Battambang organizes a two-day workshop to disseminate higher education education improvement projects
(Battambang): The University of Battambang this morning, July 23, 2019, has been organizing a workshop to disseminate the launch of the Higher Education Improvement Project for the University of Battambang under the funding of the World Bank and the Ministry of Education and Youth. And sports.
The workshop was held at Khemara Hotel, Battambang 1, Battambang City, chaired by Ms. Seang Em Totim, Rector of the University of Battambang and Chair of the Higher Education Improvement Project for the University of Battambang.
The workshop lasted for 2 days, from 23 to 24 July 2019, with the participation of relevant departments and institutions in Battambang and surrounding provinces, as well as representatives of NGOs, high schools in Battambang and project staff. More than 100 people.
Please be informed that the World Bank has recently provided US $ 90 million in financing and US $ 2.5 million in contributions from the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. To launch a project to improve education in five public higher education institutions in Cambodia.
The University of Battambang, a potential university in the Northwest Zone, was selected by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports to implement this project with a funding of 5 million US dollars. The project has a duration of 6 years, which started in July 2018 and will be completed in June 2024.
The purpose of this Higher Education Improvement Project is to improve the quality of higher education and research, mainly in the fields of science (STEM), agriculture, and support sectors, in which the goal is to implement This project is a higher education institution. This higher education improvement project focuses on:
* Enhancing teaching and learning capacity * Improving research in science (STEM) and agriculture * Strengthening governance in various fields and project management
We would like to thank the Royal Government of Cambodia for its dedicated attention, especially to the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the World Bank, for financing investment in education in Cambodia and to producing quality human resources for the country's development. To be equal on the international stage.
