The meeting was also attended by leaders and senior officials in the Ministry of Public Works and Transport.
With such questions, Mr. Sun Chanthol reminded his officials to pay attention to the construction of roads in the province as well as national roads.
Mr. Sun Chanthol announced his position that from now on, the Ministry only needs roads that have been built for a long time, that is, the Ministry will stop accepting any roads that are not of good quality.
The minister also recommended a thorough inspection of each road before signing the receipt from the construction company so as not to be criticized by the people. Mr. Sun Chanthol continued to inspect National Road No. 64 and talk with officials of Preah Vihear Provincial Public Works Department
(Preah Vihear): On the morning of Tuesday, July 7, 2019, which is the second day of the inspection of the quality of roads that have been built and are under construction, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol The Ministry of Public Works and Transport, along with other ministry leaders, continued their journey from Siem Reap to the north, inspecting the newly constructed National Road 64.
Currently, this road facilitates the movement of people from Siem Reap to Preah Vihear and also facilitates the people on both sides of the road in both Siem Reap and Preah Vihear for the transportation of their agricultural products to Marketing.
In addition to inspecting National Road 64, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also met with officials of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province. Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, was also present at the meeting.
In this conversation, the Senior Minister reminded the officials of the Public Works Department of Preah Vihear Province to work hard to serve the people who have trusted to vote for the Cambodian People's Party, support Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister of Cambodia. Senior Minister Sun Chanthol reminded Samdech Techo Hun Sen to the officials of the Public Works Department that the officials are honest servants of the people, not the bosses of the people.
The Minister also mentioned the story of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's pumpkin seeds distributed to officials. Citing the story of the pumpkin official, he wants the officials in the public department to be honest, not to lie and hurt others.
Regarding the provision of services, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol reminded his staff to be transparent and fast and to find ways to accelerate the provision of public services related to public works and transportation. He said, for example, that the Ministry of Public Works has opened two driver's license and exchange licenses at Aeon Mall, making it easier for people to come and receive services.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also instructed the officials of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province to pay attention to some other issues, such as repairing damaged roads, educating people to obey traffic laws, continue to prevent overweight transportation, and continue to crack down on vehicle processing. Wrong technical characteristics and so on.
The Minister of Public Works and Transport also mentioned the construction of the road. Regarding the construction of this road, the Senior Minister asked the officials to pay attention to check the quality, if the construction is not of good quality and not in accordance with the agreement, it will not be accepted.
It should be noted that the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province has a total of 99 civil servants, including 47 civil servants, 13 women, and 52 contracted officers, 12 women, divided into 8 offices and 1 unit.
Mr. Samleang Try, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport, said that some of the achievements that the Department has achieved in the past related to the repair and maintenance of roads in the province and the provision of public services.
According to Mr. Samleang Try, the Department of Public Works and Transport has registered 556 motorcycles, 119 cars and 6 garages. Inspected the technical characteristics of 4 tricycles, 944 vehicles, 3 semi-trailers, issued transportation licenses for 361 vehicles, 6 semi-trailers.
The department has licensed 19 garages and 1 branch of a passenger transport company. Conducted 6 online driving test exams and issued 130 driving licenses, as well as exchanged and renewed a total of 117 driver's licenses.
The Department has disseminated road safety information 13 times, provided 386 helmets and some documents, and sent professional officers to inspect 2,289 vehicles with technical defects.
The Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province is also committed to continue to do his job better to meet the needs of the people in both urban and rural areas or remote areas.
