Ministry of Water Resources: From today to July 29, the rain will be good to moderate and more scattered, while thunder, lightning and gusts will be lighter than before!
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a notification on the weather situation in Cambodia from today to July 29, 2019, stating that the rain will continue to be good to moderate to heavy and scattered. While thunder, lightning and gusts of wind are milder.
The Ministry of Water Resources confirmed that the pressure valley, which used to be in the upper part of Cambodia, has now moved down amid the southwest monsoon and has been moderately influential. By July 29, the weather will be positive again:
1. Upper provinces will receive good to moderate rainfall. 2: Provinces and capitals in the lower central lowlands will receive light to moderate rainfall. 3. Coastal provinces will receive light to moderate rainfall.
The ministry said thunderstorms and gusts of wind were also milder.
