Today, police checked 5,174 motorcyclists, forcing 2,767 to wear helmets
(Phnom Penh): The General Commission of the National Police has launched a campaign to promote helmet wearing nationwide for a full month, and for July 22, 2019, the traffic police force inspected 5,174 motorcyclists in That forced 2,767 people, or 53 percent, to wear helmets. This is according to the report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department, which was obtained by Fresh News.
Please be informed that General Santibandit Neth Savoeun, the National Police Commissioner, has issued an order for the traffic police throughout the country to start taking measures to promote the wearing of helmets to all motorcyclists and tricycle drivers.
