(Preah Vihear): For food safety as well as the health of the people, CamControl Preah Vihear Branch on July 22, 2019, in cooperation with the Department of Commerce and local authorities, inspected the quality of packaged goods at home shops in the village. Saang, Saang commune, Chey Sen district, Preah Vihear province, as a result, 9 products were found out of date and confiscated and burned.
According to the Preah Vihear branch of CamControl, during the inspection operation, the team found nine expired and damaged goods, including: Saang village, Saang commune, Chey Sen district, Preah Vihear province.
Taking the opportunity, the team also distributed posters and disseminated to traders, sellers and consumers to understand the consequences of eating out of date and not using and adding banned chemicals. In food.
