(Banteay Meanchey): Speaking from Banteay Meanchey province on the occasion of continuing to inspect the construction of National Road No. 5 from Battambang to Serei Sophorn, Banteay Meanchey Province, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that Cambodia will build a national road No. 10. Further, connecting Samlot district, Battambang province to Koh Kong province with a length of 193 kilometers.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, during a visit to National Road No. 5 on the afternoon of July 22, 2019, claimed that the budget for the construction of a new national road is a concessional loan from China worth about 183 million US dollars. The official opening of the construction site will coincide with the inauguration of National Road 55, possibly during the end of 2019.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said, "Apart from the official inauguration, the construction site of Road 10 from Samlot down to Veal Veng to Koh Kong will be opened." "Route 10 also received a concessional loan from China, and today, as far as I know, the Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance traveled to China to discuss the loan."
However, for the exact time of these two programs, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol has not been able to confirm yet, only revealing that it will be held under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech decided to set the date. Inauguration of National Road 55 and construction of National Road 10.
