(Kratie): A dolphin weighing more than 100 kg died due to fishing nets on July 22, 2019 in a protected area in Kakot village, Sambok commune, Chit Borey district, Kratie province.
The bodies of the dolphins were stored in a refrigerator at the WWF Kratie provincial office for autopsy, a joint research team with the Fisheries Administration and WWF initially concluded that the dolphins had died. Because it is trapped in a net because there is a net in its tail, and that male dolphin weighs 104 kilograms.
The Global Fund for the Conservation of Natural Resources says the dead dolphin has been identified as the fifth dolphin to be found dead since January 2019 and the number of baby dolphins born during The same number is nine.
