Mr. Sok Lou urges the municipal authorities and all relevant professional officials to put out the fire and not to sit and smoke
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Sok Lou urged the municipal authorities and all relevant officials to put out the fire, do not sit and blow the smoke.
He said this at the monthly meeting of the Unified Administrative Command on July 22, 2019, with the participation of the Deputy Governor, heads of departments around the province, municipal authorities and nearly 100 relevant officials.
After mentioning some of the challenges related to crime as well as challenges in the past, Mr. Sok Lou said that all crimes that occurred in Kampong Thom must be prevented and cracked down immediately. In particular, it is necessary to inspect all handicrafts that are close to the conservation area, and the municipal and district authorities must regularly crack down on all crimes that actually occur in their localities.
He said to put out the fire, not to sit and blow the smoke, to manage the forest in their area well, especially the community forest must be strictly monitored by a committee to monitor the forest in that area regularly Anyone involved in the crime must withdraw immediately so as not to be punished according to the law.
He said that all arrests, if any, to intervene should be recorded to investigate those who intervene in various crimes to be in line with the principles of the Prince, which mentioned the five approaches. Participate in correcting any mistakes and operating any officials involved in the crime, focusing on the law.
Finally, he urged all officials to pay attention to crack down on all crimes that occur in Kampong Thom, such as forest crime, fishing offenses, drug problems and traffic accidents.
