JERUSALEM (Reuters) - Israeli troops on Monday began destroying homes and buildings near a military barricade on the outskirts of Jerusalem, ignoring Palestinian protests and international condemnation. This was released by Reuters on Monday afternoon, July 22, 2019.
According to Reuters, machinery and hundreds of Israeli officers and police were dispatched to the Palestinian village of Sur Baher on the eastern outskirts of Jerusalem. The village was occupied by Israel in the 1967 war, and Palestinians have expressed protest and concern that such acts of vandalism could spread to other Palestinian villages near the Israeli military post.
In addition, according to the community leader of the village of Sur Baher, the Israeli army evacuated the Palestinians and started planting explosives on the houses or buildings they wanted to destroy from 2:00 am on Monday. So far, despite opposition from international activists.
The Israeli Supreme Court ruled in June that the infrastructure in the village of Sur Baher violated construction restrictions and required Palestinians to evacuate the buildings before the day. Last Friday.
