The construction of this road project started on May 4, 2015 under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, and so far the company has completed 100% of the construction, using a construction period of 42 months.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized that the inspection of National Road 55 aims to check the remaining shortcomings.
During the inspection, Mr. Sun Chanthol instructed the construction company and the technical inspection company to review the installation of warning lights instead of signs at strong corners so that people traveling on this road can easily see and have High caution.
The senior minister also recommended building walls on the slopes to prevent landslides and stones, collecting floating stones on the road to avoid accidents due to the fact that the road on the hillside is very flexible.
The Minister also examined some technical issues related to the construction to encourage the construction contractors to adjust the technical specifications properly to make this road strong and durable before requesting the policy from the Royal Government in Official launch.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized that National Road No. 55 is an important economic artery for connecting internal integration as well as facilitating people's travel easily and quickly and contributing to the transformation of potential areas. Agriculture, especially in remote areas bordering Cambodia and Thailand, which can be easily connected to the town.
He added that the road would improve connectivity between Cambodia and neighboring countries, facilitate cross-border trade, investment and promote tourism and agricultural development.
"There are hopeful roads, good roads, bringing tourists, investors and transportation, which is a driving force for job creation and national economic growth, poverty reduction in line with the policy," he said. Of the Royal Government under the wise leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, after the improvement of some remaining issues, he will submit a request for principles and respectfully invite Samdech Techo Hun Sen to officially inaugurate this road in the near future.
General Neth Savoeun Takes Action to Crack Down on Drugs on Cambodia-Vietnam Border
(Phnom Penh): General Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police, this morning, July 22, 2019, set out measures to strengthen the crackdown on drug crimes along the Cambodia-Vietnam border as both sides Already determined to join together to crack down on this crime together.
During a meeting to disseminate the plan of the Ministry of Interior on the campaign to prevent and suppress drug crimes along the Cambodian-Vietnamese border this morning, General Dr. Neth Savoeun affirmed that the drug problem is a global concern that requires both authorities All must work together to crack down, otherwise it will be even more dangerous for the world.
In response to these concerns, General Neth Savoeun has put forward a number of necessary measures that all authorities must be involved in, including:
* First: Outreach: This work should be divided into two related public forums and explanations of local people standing at the border, which is the responsibility of the provincial governor to continue to guide the sub-national authorities to understand the activities. The catastrophe of drugs and the tricks of criminals.
In addition, it is necessary to explain to law enforcement officials to increase special vigilance at border checkpoints, customs and immigration officials to increase inspections and to continue to cooperate with law enforcement along the border for more information. Finding drugs is not a coincidence, be informed and be suspicious.
At the same time, the border police force must continue to be educated to understand the law, the tricks, the actions of drug criminals, the effects caused by drugs and to stay away from drugs, that is, law enforcement officers must not stay After this crime.
* Second: Strengthen law enforcement: The BLO Border Liaison Office must increase its relationship with the BLO and educate officials to understand the importance of drug prevention and other illegal activities. The officers of the Border Patrol to be patrolled must explain, warn and be responsible for discipline and state law.
Separately, the provincial police commissioner must manage the relationship with the Vietnamese provincial commissioner by setting a meeting time, setting a notification time and opening an address for communication 24 hours a day, 24 hours a day. Be on time.
In relation to the Anti-Drug Department, which is responsible for the General Commission of the National Police and the Ministry of Interior, to cooperate with the two countries and to establish a 24-hour communication working group to handle the situation, collect information and put in place control measures to crack down on drug offenses. Addicted. In addition, a unified team must be formed to search for subpoenas.
Along with the implementation of this measure, General Neth Savoeun also strongly expressed his belief that all Cambodian authorities involved and jointly carry out this work with Vietnamese authorities to effectively eliminate drugs, improve security and order in the region. Better borders. Promote reading! Three groups of monks take more than 1,000 books and keep them at Barach Primary School, Mesang District, Prey Veng Province
