Cambodia hopes that the United States will implement the Treaty of Amity and Cooperation with ASEAN without interfering in the internal affairs of other countries
The United States, under the administration of Barack Obama, signed an agreement with ASEAN 10 years ago, pledging not to interfere in the internal affairs of any country.
July 22, 2019 marks the 10th anniversary of the US-ASEAN Agreement, and on this occasion, Cambodia expressed its hope that the United States will fully respect and implement the Treaty of Amity and Cooperation with ASEAN without interfering in its internal affairs. Of other countries.
Phay Siphan, a spokesman for the Royal Government of Cambodia, recalled the agreement. He said the United States is committed to implementing the principle of non-interference in the internal affairs of each nation of ASEAN as a whole, as well as directly with ASEAN member countries. At the same time, President Donald Trump from the Republican Party also affirmed that foreign policy does not interfere in the internal affairs of other countries.
"My note is that the two parties' governments have the same principles," he said. I sincerely hope that the United States, both the executive and the legislature, as a civilized state institution of the United States, will demonstrate certainty in the implementation of treaties of friendship and cooperation in the rule of law and be a role model for nations. "In the world together against interference in the internal affairs of each nation."
