Senior Minister Kun Kim Chairs a Meeting to Review the Performance of Prey Veng Provincial Disaster Management Committee
(Prey Veng): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Deputy Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, this morning, July 22, 2019, chaired a meeting to review the work of the Prey Veng Provincial Committee for Disaster Management and disseminate precautionary measures and response time. There was a disaster.
The meeting was held at the Red Cross branch office in Prey Veng province with the participation of Mr. Chea Somethy, Provincial Governor and 339 civil servants from relevant departments, institutions, armed forces, partner organizations and municipal, district, commune and sangkat authorities throughout the province.
According to Mr. Chea Somethy's report, Prey Veng is a province that is vulnerable to the Mekong River floods and is prone to strong winds. In the first six months of the year, strong winds caused damage to 996 houses and drought Affected 14,715 hectares of transplanted rice.
He added that the province's ability to respond was limited, so the province requested timely intervention from the National Committee for Disaster Management, chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, so that the province could respond in a timely manner. And effective.
At the same time, the meeting also listened to the presentations of the departments under the National Committee for Disaster Management (NCDC) on information, disaster preparedness and response measures.
After sending greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kattipritthbandit to the members of the meeting, Senior Minister Kun Kim praised the efforts of the Provincial Disaster Management Committee, which has worked hard and planned. Clear details of disaster response management.
