Defense Spokesman: US media fabrication of Chinese military bases in Cambodia intends to undermine Cambodian security and peace in the region (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Cambodian Defense Ministry Spokesman Gen. Chhum Socheat The US media fabrication of foreign military bases in Cambodia appears to be intended to undermine security and peace in Cambodia and the region.
General Chhum Socheat confirmed to Fresh News: "It is outrageous that the US media has arbitrarily fabricated crazy news about foreign military bases on Cambodian territory and been defiled by their media. Others seem to be intent on undermining security and peace in Cambodia and in the region. ”
Mr. Chhum Socheat stated that he could not accept such fabrications and claimed that "the Ministry of Defense has never had any secret agreement for the Chinese army to use Cambodian territory as a base. "You should stop using fake information about the presence of Chinese troops on Cambodian territory to continue to oppose Cambodia."
In connection with the accusation of Cambodia about this foreign military base, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, also announced on Fresh News that the dissemination of information about Cambodia secretly signing with China using military bases is a fabrication. Worst against Cambodia.
Regarding this foreign military base, Cambodia has repeatedly stated its position that the Royal Government of Cambodia does not allow foreign military bases on Cambodian territory. The Cambodian Constitution also does not allow the establishment of foreign military bases on its territory, nor does it send Cambodian troops abroad, except for missions with the United Nations. This is according to General Chhum Socheat.
