Mr. Oknha Leang Khun added that Chip Mong has always been proud to contribute with the Royal Government in the rehabilitation and construction of road infrastructure as a contribution to national economic development through the Royal Government's policy to reduce Poverty for local people. Minister of Health: Cambodia Nutrition Project for Mothers, Babies and Children in 5 years will focus on 7 provinces in need
(Phnom Penh): Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, said that the Cambodian Nutrition Project for Mothers, Babies and Children in the five years (2019-2024) will focus on seven provinces that are experiencing severe malnutrition. They are among the 25 provinces.
This statement was made by Minister Mam Bun Heng on the occasion of the official announcement on the implementation of Cambodian nutrition, which was held at Sofitel Phuket Tra Phnom Penh this morning, July 22, 2019.
Minister Mam Bunheng continued, "In response to our Royal Government's policy to improve the provision of effective maternal, infant and child health and nutrition services to pregnant women, midwives and children under 2 years of age." "The Ministry of Health will continue to work hard to do this."
In addition, during the five-year Cambodia Nutrition Initiative, a total of $ 53 million was raised from the national budget and contributed by the World Bank, the Global Fund for Women, Children and Youth, the German Development Bank and the Australian Government.
Minister Mam Bunheng continued, "This project will promote the provision of effective maternal, infant and child health services and nutrition to pregnant women, obstetricians and children under 2 years of age and health facilities and in the community, focusing on "Seven provinces: Mondulkiri, Ratanakiri, Kratie, Stung Treng, Preah Vihear, Kampong Chhnang and Koh Kong."
This Cambodian nutrition project will reduce the gap between rich and poor, between urban and rural areas, and improve access to universal health services. This project complements and coincides with the implementation of the Health Equity Fund, the implementation of the current Health Quality and Equity Improvement Project.
In addition, health workers at local health facilities where the project will be implemented will receive additional clinical training to provide services at hospitals, health centers, as well as provide health care services and counseling in Pregnancy, maternal nutrition, postpartum care, infant / child rearing, monitoring the growth of young children through the provision of health services in remote rural communities.
In addition, from June 1, 2019, the Royal Government of Cambodia has also introduced a cash support program for pregnant women and children under 2 years of age who have an equity card or priority card to help poor families. Receive a full 1,000 days of care.
