Currently, the gambling addicts and the confiscated exhibits have been sent to the Por Sen Chey District Inspectorate for legal action.
The congratulatory performance was made on the occasion of the courtesy call of Mrs. Maria SaGren and the farewell speech of Samdech Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, on the morning of July 22, 2019.
The Ambassador informed the National Assembly President that Sweden has contributed to the development of Cambodia in many areas, including the promotion of human rights, democracy, education, community development, adaptation to climate change and gender equality.
During her three-year diplomatic mission in Cambodia, she was overjoyed to see the friendship, cooperation and cooperation between the two countries flourishing in trade, diplomacy and culture.
Samdech Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, stated that Samdech believes that the years of her diplomatic mission in Cambodia have actually seen the continuous development of Cambodia, including the real situation in Cambodia, which is contrary to the outside voice for the benefit. That political interest.
He said that through the CEDA Development Agency, Sweden has played an important role in contributing to the development of Cambodia. For more than 5 years, CEDA has provided development assistance in various fields in the amount of more than 100 million US dollars. Samdech considers Sweden an important development partner of Cambodia.
The President of the National Assembly hopes that no matter where Maria Saren completes her diplomatic mission from Cambodia to take on a new mission, she will maintain good relations with Cambodia and continue to encourage and encourage investors and tourists to visit Cambodia. .
