Khmer Civilization Expert: Did the adoption of the US House of Representatives pass the bill on Cambodian democracy reflect the will of the Cambodian people?
Because Cambodia is a sovereign state, it is not possible for a country's parliament to make laws. If so, the actions of the US House of Representatives, which recently passed the Law on Democratic Kampuchea, are no different from the US Congress producing laws to control Cambodia, nor is it different from the "US Congress dominating the Cambodian Congress." That too.
Mr. Rath Sandab continued that, therefore, for the act of the US House of Representatives, which made the law in violation of Cambodian sovereignty, the US Congress is no longer the US Congress, it is the Cambodian Parliament or the World Congress, because a country's parliament is not Can make a law to order a country to do this or do that.
In conclusion, Mr. Rath Sandab considered that if the proposal for the law on democracy in Cambodia, which recently passed the US House of Representatives, this law is not different from one of the strangest laws in the world, because in terms of sovereign states. Can a country not form a parliament to accuse a country of being democratic or not?
On the other hand, the actions of the US House of Representatives are also contrary to the principles of the United Nations, because the UN Charter does not allow one state to interfere in the sovereignty of another. If so, the proposed Cambodian Democratic Law, which was recently passed by the US House of Representatives, is a law that could only embarrass the United States on the international stage, because in this world, democracy has no standards.
