Not less than 500 tons of all kinds of fish in Stung Treng province were rescued from illegal fishing in 5 months
(Stung Treng): From May 1, 2019 until today, Stung Treng Fisheries Administration District has launched a large-scale and permanent campaign during the closed fishing season to protect all species of fish from fishing with floating nets and fishing gear. Violation of fisheries laws aimed at protecting the mother fish has the opportunity to travel safely to spawn to continue the sustainability of fishery resources to future generations.
The campaign was attended by fisheries officers from Stung Treng City and Thala Borivat District, Stung Treng River Dolphin Conservation and 30 Community Fisheries Committees.
According to the district chief, evaluating the five-month campaign during the closed fishing season, we are able to save at least 500 tons of all kinds of fish, and natural fish stocks will gradually improve if we continue the campaign. This is 3-5 years in a row.
Please note that this campaign is fully supported by all levels of leadership in the province, the armed forces, local authorities, especially the community and most of the fishermen. Finally, the district chief urged all fishermen to participate in the protection and use of our rare fishery resources to be stable in the future.
