Currently, the vehicles have been sent to the Office of Land Traffic of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police for further instruction on the procedures. Non-aligned countries condemn violations of independence, sovereignty of their member countries
(Phnom Penh): Non-aligned countries have issued a statement condemning the violation of the independence and sovereignty of their member countries.
The condemnation was made at a ministerial meeting of the Coordinating Office of the Non-Aligned Movement (CoB-NAM) in Caracas, Venezuela on July 20-21, 2019.
In this meeting, the Cambodian side was represented by Mr. Ouch Borith, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation.
At the meeting, several delegations issued statements criticizing unilateralism and condemning unilateral coercive measures and violations of the independence and sovereignty of member states of the Non-Aligned Movement.
The Non-Aligned Statement comes as the Law on Democracy in Cambodia was unanimously approved by the US House of Representatives on July 15, 2019. The law was enacted with the aim of punishing Cambodian officials and restoring democracy after the US House of Representatives argued that the democratic process in Cambodia had slowed down.
The Non-Aligned Meeting also approved the Declaration of Caracas on the Ministerial Meeting of the Coordinating Office of the Non-Aligned Movement, the Political Statement of Caracas and the Petition of Gratitude and Solidarity with the People and Government. Republic of Venezuela. The meeting also expressed support for the political statement of the Committee of Ministers of the Non-Aligned Movement on the Palestinian issue.
The meeting also discussed the organization of the 18th Non-Aligned Movement Summit to be held on October 21-26, 2019 in Baku, Republic of Azerbaijan.
In the Cambodian statement, Mr. Ouch Borith highlighted the following points:
* The world is facing cases where some countries are forcing other countries to adopt self-governing standards, expressing their desire to elect leaders, the government of other countries decides the legitimacy of a country or the government of a country clinging to a role. Represent the people and evaluate other countries according to their standards on the basis of their national interests and geopolitical interests.
* In 2018, Cambodia held free, fair and peaceful general elections with the participation of 20 parties and a turnout of 83.02%, which is a high rate compared to some countries that have practiced democracy. A long time ago.
* Despite its many efforts and achievements, Cambodia has never been praised by a group of countries or institutions that adhere to the same standard in their thinking, "regime change".
On the occasion of the meeting, Mr. Ouch Borith also had a bilateral meeting with Mr. Reuben Daryo Molina, Deputy Minister for Foreign Affairs of the Middle East and Oceania of the Venezuelan Ministry of Foreign Affairs. Both sides expressed their desire to strengthen friendly relations and fruitful cooperation between the two countries for the benefit of both nations. Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh Meets Japanese Deputy Defense Minister
