Solve the problem of drought! Minister Veng Sakhon Instructs the General Department of Agriculture and the Department of Agriculture to Prepare Rice Seed Reserves for Distribution to Farmers in Severely Affected Areas
(Siem Reap): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and his colleagues, on Sunday morning, July 21, 2019, inspected the drought situation. In Veal village, Darun commune, Sot Nikum district, Siem Reap province.
According to the report of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, as of July 19, transplanting work across the province has reached more than 141 thousand hectares, equivalent to 75.77% of the plan of more than 186 thousand hectares. Due to the prolonged hot and dry weather, rice fields in Kralanh, Srey Snom, Puok and Sot Nikum districts were affected by a total of nearly 5,000 hectares.
More than 170 hectares of Sotnikum district are facing water shortages, but a few days ago the area received light rain, causing some seedlings to regenerate, and hopefully in the next few days it will continue to rain.
On that occasion, Minister Veng Sakhon also instructed the General Department of Agriculture and the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to prepare spare seeds for distribution to farmers, especially in the worst affected areas.
The Minister further stated that the Department must visit all affected areas to find solutions to farmers in a timely and effective manner, such as providing fuel for pumping water in case of water sources and seeds if needed. Restore.
In the morning of the same day, the Minister and his colleagues also came to inspect the drought in Po village, Tram Khla village, Ta Ream village and Russey Cheas village, Tbeng commune, Kampong Svay district, which is located next to Samdech Techo Hun Sen canal that connects the pool on September 30. Overall, technically, the 50-day-old tuber is in the early stages of puberty and flowering, although it does not produce good water.
At the same time, Minister Veng Sakhon instructed the General Department of Agriculture, Department of Agricultural Engineering, in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to intervene, plow the rice and prepare enough seeds to distribute to farmers waiting for the rain to start sowing. New.
