(Phnom Penh): The trial of Lay Vann: Former Governor of Takeo Province, Lay Narith, former Deputy Commissioner of Takeo Province and his accomplices on suspicion of murder of Chev Sovathana will be brought to trial on July 22. 2019 tomorrow.
This trial has reached the conclusion stage after the court has spent a lot of time questioning the suspects, witnesses and plaintiffs. Phnom Penh Municipal Court officials told Fresh News this morning, July 21, 2019, that tomorrow's hearing will be chaired by Mr. Horm Mengse, Deputy President of the Trial Chamber and President of the Trial Chamber.
Please be reminded that on May 24, 2018, the prison guards brought the convicts Lay Vann, former Governor of Takeo Province, Lay Narith, former Deputy Commissioner of Takeo Province and his accomplices for further questioning. According to the content of this trial, the court will continue to question the forensic experts of the police of the Criminal Department of the Ministry of Interior, and in this case also led by Mr. Horm Mengse.
During the trial of the victim, Chev Sovathana, the mistress of Lay Vannak, the former governor of Takeo province, on the morning of March 22, 2019, the court questioned three forensic witnesses who were officials in Takeo province. .
Through the cross-examination of the three forensic officers, including: Mr. Meas Ten, Deputy Chief of Technical Office of Takeo Provincial Police, Mr. Aun Noeun, Chief of Technical Section of Takeo Provincial Police and Dr. Chhou Chhuon, Director of Provincial Referral Hospital. Takeo to confirm the truth about the report and the record of examining the bodies of the victims at the time of the incident.
All three witnesses testified in defense of their report that after they examined the scene, examined the condition of the victim's body, examined the evidence (warrants) left by the victim and listened to your answers. Serve the victim named Chan Ry, a professional officer, including Mr. Chiv Chandara, Prosecutor of the Takeo Provincial Prosecutor's Office to hear the autopsy results, confirmed that the victim hanged himself.
The victim, Chev Sovathana, was found hanged in her bedroom in a large rented house rented by Mr. Lay Vannak in Phsar Ta Kor village, Rokar commune, Daun Keo city, Takeo province on the evening of the 26th. January 2018 ago.
The murder case was immediately concluded by the authorities as a suicide because of a love crisis, but after an investigation, the competent authorities of the Criminal Department of the Ministry of Interior found that the above case was not a suicide, that is, a murder with someone. Order and prepare to kill the victim. After opening an investigation, the competent authorities arrested the four accused and sent them to court for legal action.
