(Phnom Penh): General Chhum Socheat, spokesman for the Ministry of National Defense, claimed on July 20, 2019 that the announcement that "the Cambodian military court, partisanship, familyism is an exaggeration beyond reality." He denied that the Cambodian military tribunal was not partisan as published.
Mr. Chhum Socheat confirmed this on his Facebook page: "As a spokesperson for the Ministry of National Defense, I would like to reiterate to the media and the public that the Cambodian military court does not have a partisan or familial issue as published. No charges. "The Cambodian military tribunal operates independently and always provides justice for all soldiers."
However, a spokesman for the Ministry of National Defense confirmed that the Ministry welcomes constructive criticism and accepts all information for review before submitting a report to higher levels, and the army is always waiting to implement all of Samdech's orders. Pichey Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Defense.
It should be noted that the statement made by the spokesman of the Ministry of National Defense came after Radio Free Asia reported that the Cambodian military court was a corrupt and family-oriented institution under the leadership of Lt. Gen. Nay Thol.
Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign, July 20: 979 illegal vehicles found and 650 fined
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for July 20, 2019, the traffic police force inspected 3,502 vehicles, found 979 vehicles violating the law (71% motorcycles), 329 education vehicles and fined 650 units, according to the official report of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 1,289 helmets and goggles were inspected on July 20, 68 education helmets and 478 helmets were fined.
