The Ministry of Interior instructs homeowners across the country to report the presence of foreigners staying at their locations (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, has issued a directive to homeowners or occupants. All over the country report the presence of foreigners who come to stay at their locations.
The competent ministry claimed that after issuing instructions on the provision of information related to the residence of foreigners in the past, it has found that many owners or occupants of all types of housing have followed the instructions consciously. Urgent and high responsibility, but some homeowners or occupants still do not understand the obligations and properly comply with the rules and regulations.
In order to strengthen the implementation of the Immigration Law to increase the effective management of the presence of foreigners, ensure the protection of security, public order and social safety, as well as the personal safety of all foreigners staying in Cambodia, the Ministry of Interior would like to make the following recommendations. Under:
1. The owner or occupier of all types of houses must report the presence of foreigners who have come to stay in their location to the local commune / sangkat administrative police station through a sample report or information technology system for managing the presence of foreigners. Prepared by the General Department of Immigration for no more than 24 hours.
In case the owner or occupier of all types of housing is a foreigner, he / she must report the presence of himself / herself and the foreign member in charge within no more than 24 hours.
2. The content of the report must clarify the length of stay, the length of stay and the incidents on foreigners so that the competent force has appropriate measures in a timely manner.
3. Any owner or occupier who does not report the presence of a foreigner in accordance with the laws and regulations shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the Immigration Law and other laws of the Kingdom. Cambodia.
4. The Capital-Provincial Police Commission shall provide sample reports and application forms for the use of information technology systems for the management of foreign presence prepared by the General Department of Immigration to the owners or occupants of all types of houses for daily reporting and summary. Report sent to the General Department of Immigration.
5. The Capital-Provincial Police Commission shall report to the Ministry of Interior through the General Department of Immigration on the deaths, disappearances and incidents of foreigners and be responsible for inspecting foreigners who have settled or have just arrived. Settled in the territory under its jurisdiction.
6: The General Department of Immigration shall prepare a plan to implement and disseminate guidance to the owners or occupants of all types of housing, the Capital-Provincial Police Commission, relevant authorities and the public and assign professional officers to inspect the implementation of this instruction and to summarize and report to the Ministry. Interior to have guiding principles.
7. The Ministry of Interior calls on the public, civil servants at all levels, and all competent forces to contribute to providing information and reporting to the relevant authorities about the presence of foreigners staying in their localities.
