Workshop on Beer and Beverage Production Technology Arrives in Kampot Province
(Kampot): Khmer Breweries' Beer and Beverage Technology Training Workshop has arrived in Kampot. This workshop was held on July 19, 2019 after being successfully held in Phnom Penh and some provinces.
The workshop was held at Mittapheap Restaurant in Kampot with the participation of about 300 distributors of Khmer Breweries in the province.
Ms. Kong Kosal, Marketing Director of Khmer Breweries, said that she was very pleased that the training on Khmer Breweries Beer and Beverage Technology was conducted smoothly and successfully, starting from Phnom Penh. Kampong Speu, Koh Kong, Kampong Som, Takeo and now arrive in Kampot and continue to other provinces throughout Cambodia.
"The thing that brings the biggest smiles is that by evaluating each region where the workshops have been held so far, our participants almost 100% understand the process of brewing beer and the ingredients," she said. "We use it to produce Cambodian beer with the best taste and quality in line with international standards, along with other beverages such as energy drinks, ice cream, juices, and Cambodian pure water."
Mr. Chea Sophoan, a distributor of Khmer Breweries, also stated, "I am very happy to be invited to this event because it is a good time to meet with the same beverage vendors and even find out how "We also produce standard quality beer and beverages."
He added that he really liked this program because it was fun and won extra prizes from the company. He hopes that the company will hold this program next year. Authorities and water resources officials continue to build the Mekong River bank to prevent landslides and help improve the beauty of Kratie province.
(Kratie): Seeing the potential of tourism in Kratie province, it is growing and attracting more and more national and international tourists from year to year, and to enhance the attractiveness of the province's environmental beauty. Kratie Provincial Administration, in collaboration with the Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, has begun construction on the Mekong River.
Heng Rath Molida, Director of the Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, confirmed on July 20, 2019 that the Kratie Provincial Administration has continued to build the Mekong River bank to prevent landslides. Damage to public property such as: roads, buildings and Korki trees along the river.
Kratie Provincial Administration has confirmed that the provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology is organizing and is constructing a 230-meter-long Mekong River embankment in front of the Provincial Health Department in front of the Diamond City Entertainment Club. Of Kratie Provincial Hall.
The director of the department added that Kratie province is geographically adjacent to the Mekong River, so Kratie Provincial Hall has built the Mekong River bank from 2006 to 2019 to reach a length of more than 23,000 meters.
He added that the construction of the riverbank is not only a strong protection against landslides, but also an important corner of the province's tourism, which is aesthetically attractive to national and international tourists. Also.
According to the official, the construction of this river bank will definitely provide important benefits to the province, including:
* First: Prevent landslides, riverbanks, protect infrastructure, roads and buildings along the river * Second: After construction, it is a tourist area, every day in the morning and evening, people and International guests often sit and play and take pictures at sunset and admire the scenery of Koh Trong in front of the provincial town.
