Authorities crack down on a Chinese business venue in Daun Penh district without proper permission
(Phnom Penh): A joint police force with the participation of relevant institutions inspected and cracked down on a Chinese business location along Norodom Blvd. in Chaktomuk Sangkat, Daun Penh District, Phnom Penh. Large packages of goods and some bottled water are used for business without proper rules.
The operation took place on the evening of July 19, 2019, led by Mr. Sok Penh Vuth, Daun Penh District Governor, and was attended by the Director of the Phnom Penh Inter-sectoral Office, the Head of the Phnom Penh OWSO and representatives of the Phnom Penh Department of Commerce, Camcontrol Branch.
After inspecting, the team decided as follows: The business owner must dismantle the trademark within 5 days and must go to register the business properly and apply for a location permit before launching the business.
