More than 40,000 hectares of early-season rain-fed rice in Pursat and Battambang provinces are facing water shortages, the Minister of Agriculture inspected the actual situation of drought
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on July 20, 2019, inspected the drought situation in Ta Lok commune, Talo Sen Chey district and Romlech commune, Bakan district.
After inspecting the actual situation of the drought in Bor Chres village, Ta Lok commune, Talo Sen Chey district, Minister Veng Sakhon hopes that the Royal Government will plan to expand irrigation to this area in the coming years.
The Minister helped solve the problem immediately by donating 400 liters of oil for pumping water as much as possible to save seedlings.
The Minister advised the General Department of Agriculture to cooperate with the Department to monitor the situation on a regular basis and should also study the possibility of replacing some crops that use less water, and farmers should also prepare seeds for re-sowing after sufficient water to ensure food security. In the coming year.
