Col. Sok Min said that with the order of Brigadier General Thao Yen, Provincial Gendarmerie Commander and with the coordination of Mr. Raborandi, Deputy Prosecutor of Ratanakkiri Provincial Court, the means of transporting illegal timber were burned at the site. Above.
The ceremony was also attended by senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, President of the National Scout Association of Cambodia, senior leaders of the Cambodian Red Cross, Chairman of the International Committee of the Red Cross in Cambodia, The program coordinator of the Federation of Cambodia, as well as the leaders of the Cambodian Red Cross from various branches, distinguished guests and many other Red Cross youth.
CRC Youth Phnom Penh Branch was established in 2004 with about 860 Red Cross youths (399 women). In 2019, the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Phnom Penh expanded to 3,000 new youth members from 27 target high schools, which currently has a total of approximately 4,042 Cambodian Red Cross branches (2,050 females). The Cambodian Red Cross Youth in Phnom Penh Branch has been actively involved in humanitarian causes.
According to the Governor of Phnom Penh, in the past year, the Cambodian Red Cross Youth of Phnom Penh Branch of 27 educational institutions conducted educational campaigns on traffic safety, participated in providing first aid skills training, rescued students and citizens and participated in Campaigns to encourage blood donation.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit also emphasized that the organization of the Cambodian Red Cross Youth on this occasion is another testament to the efforts to strengthen the youth and is the best opportunity to declare the right to The young people of the Cambodian Red Cross deserve to be qualified human resources of the Cambodian Red Cross and the International Red Cross-Red Crescent Movement now and in the future.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen also expressed his pride in the work results and implementation direction of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Phnom Penh with the hope that the branch will continue to pay more attention to the work of the Red Cross Youth. To become stronger and stronger so that the youth can be the current and future force of the Cambodian Red Cross and the nation.
In the context of the Cambodian Red Cross, the youth are "agents of positive attitude change in the community", Samdech Kittipritthbandit, President of the Cambodian Red Cross also shared seven recommendations for the CRC youth to participate more widely and Act more effectively in providing humanitarian services to help victims and vulnerable in a timely manner in all walks of life across the country. The seven recommendations include:
First, to jointly continue to strengthen and expand the CRC youth force according to the actual capabilities of each branch by strengthening the capacity of youth, providing opportunities, autonomy, management, work activities, vocational training to participate in disaster preparedness activities, outreach Laws on road traffic, blood donation, environmental clean-up and tree planting to create a better environment for society.
Second, we must continue to strengthen the activities of educating friends and helping friends in all CRC youth clubs by supporting students who have difficulty in studying and living daily in schools and universities. Effectively contribute to the provision of knowledge on first aid, hygiene and health, prevention of communicable diseases in the community, and help disseminate emergency health education in the 25 branches of the capital-province.
Third, to jointly continue to strengthen the existing CRC youth management mechanism through the provision of ID cards to youth and to strengthen national and international cooperation through study visits, exchange of experiences, workshops, youth forums and sessions. Training to ensure harmonization and strengthen friendship and solidarity among young people in the national, regional and international framework.
Fourth, to continue to provide continuous training to young people, including the continued dissemination of the guidelines of the Cambodian Red Cross to be effective and comprehensive to facilitate the implementation of humanitarian activities in all walks of life across the country.
Fifth, we must continue to pay more attention, especially to encourage young people to participate as a volunteer force to ensure the progress and sustainability of young humanitarian forces for taking turns in community service activities in all capitals and provinces. .
Sixth, to continue to strengthen solidarity, friendship and mutual assistance with youth organizations and youth networks in all generations, without underestimating others and sectarian divisions that could lead to disunity among the youth of the Cross. Cambodian Red.
Seventh, all CRC youths must have a high sense of responsibility when performing their duties, you must link your existing knowledge to the practice and study of new skills just acquired for you. Can help victims and vulnerable people in the community in a timely and effective manner.
