The hotel owner adheres to the principle of recruiting 25-30% of the total number of deaf youths working in his hotel.
Mr. Yeung Sarath, Director of GNZ Hotel, said that there are good reasons why his company hires deaf employees and they are paid from $ 150 to $ 350 depending on their skills and workload. .
He also stated that all of the deaf employees automatically have an 8% stake after joining the company, and the company is also donating an additional 2% for social work related to helping. To the deaf and dumb.
He said that many people are wondering how the company works with the Deaf Kingdom? In fact, deaf staff are just like ordinary people, they just lack the ability to speak or hear, but they can write and they also have a special ability to fill that gap, such as honesty, intelligence. Be agile and try to be patient.
He added that for the future, the company has a policy to recruit about 150 deaf people to work in the company.
Ms. Chon Chamroeun, a deaf woman who works as a restaurant manager for GNZ Hotel, expressed her pleasure and warmth that the company has hired a deaf man.
She added that they have learned both general knowledge and some have also learned skills and foreign languages, and some can read, write and use sign language in up to two or three languages, especially English. And providing employment opportunities for the deaf has really contributed greatly to the promotion of the rights of people with disabilities and has improved their lives, families and socio-economic development.
