Siem Reap Governor: Lifelong learning is an important topic for education
(Siem Reap): Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap, said that in the 21st century, lifelong learning is an important topic for education in response to changes in the needs of the labor market.
Mr. Tea Seiha made this statement on July 19, 2019, when he presided over the closing ceremony of the training course for the 39th generation of 12 12 + 2 primary school teachers who came. 154 from Siem Reap and 45 from Oddar Meanchey from Siem Reap Teacher Training College.
The Siem Reap provincial governor said that for this reason, the Royal Government of the sixth mandate, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister, has pushed for a new stage of development through the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. All images and policies will focus on five components: virtue, equity, environment, lifelong learning and education for all.
In response to the Royal Government's priority policies and national development and the strategic plan of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, he on behalf of the Provincial Board of Governors fully supported all activities of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports, in particular. Provincial pedagogical and vocational schools are important educational institutions for training primary school teachers.
In addition, Mr. Tea Seiha expressed his belief that all educators, teachers, especially young people, all students must pay attention to the development of professional knowledge, professional practice, vocational education and ethics. Bio for the qualifications and education staff of the regional countries and for the benefit of the children.
He stated that the Royal Government, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Outstanding Guide, has set the National Development Strategic Plan 2019-2023 in the sixth mandate, which is a continuation of the achievements of the Strategic Plan 2013-2018. To accomplish important tasks include:
First, evaluate the overall results and the main challenges that arise in the implementation of the National Strategic Development Plan 2013-2018 in the fifth mandate.
Second, determine the policy measures of all relevant ministries and institutions in order to implement the priority policies of the Royal Government and the sustainable development goals of Cambodia to stabilize economic growth, reduce poverty and improve the living standards of the people. And to achieve the status of a high middle income country by 2030 and a developed country by 2050.
