Mr. Van Puthipol informed the workshop that the purpose of today's workshop is to disseminate the provisions related to tax incentives to agricultural enterprises such as:
1: The preference for value added tax is the burden of the state
For importing and supplying some goods such as all kinds of fertilizers, all kinds of crops, livestock, medicine, animal feed and feed additives, all kinds of animals, machinery and agricultural equipment.
2: VAT exemption on the supply of unprocessed agricultural products
Provides value-added tax exemption on the supply of unprocessed agricultural products, such as roots, tubers, bark, fruits or seeds of agricultural crops grown, even if they have not been milled or broken. Is processed into other products. Unprocessed agricultural products also include grains, including rice.
3: Incentive tax, value added tax, income tax exemption, minimum tax, withholding tax
A: Value Added Tax is the burden of the state
Enterprises that supply goods or services to local production, supply or export enterprises, rice, corn, soybeans, pepper, cassava, cashew nuts and rubber, value-added tax shall be borne by the state from March 2019 to the end of 2023 and will be Allow tax credits on inputs related to this supply.
B: Temporary suspension of income tax exemption payment
Enterprises, local suppliers or exporters of rice, corn, soybeans, pepper, cassava, cashew nuts and rubber are temporarily suspended from paying monthly income tax exemption for 5 years from January 2019 until By the end of 2023.
C: Minimum tax exemption for domestic producers, exporters or exporters of rice, corn, soybeans, pepper, cassava, cashew nuts and rubber are exempted from the minimum tax from 2019 to 2023 in case of proper accounting in accordance with the law. And provisions in force.
D- Exemption from obligation to deduct tax on service payment
Enterprises, producers, suppliers or exporters of rice, corn, soybeans, pepper, cassava, cashew nuts and rubber are exempt from the obligation to deduct tax on payment for the provision of services by non-self-declared individuals from March 2019 to the end of 2023.
* Apply for the value-added tax certificate of the state from the General Department of Taxation, which is valid once a year. Accounting in accordance with the laws and regulations in force and declaring the payment of other taxes in force on a regular basis.
4: Income tax exemption for small and medium enterprises in priority sectors (agriculture)
Small and medium enterprises in priority sectors for agricultural or agro-industrial products shall receive the following income tax incentives:
* 3 years from the date of registration or update from October 2018 onwards * 5 years from the date of registration or update from October 2018 onwards, which meets any of the following conditions: - Use local raw materials for 60 days or more or - Increase the number of additional employees by at least 20% or - Located in a small and medium enterprise concentration area.
