Public forum between the people of Speu (A) commune, Ba Phnom district and the national working group helped solve some local problems
(Prey Veng): On the morning of July 19, 2019, the National Working Group for Ba Phnom District, in cooperation with the provincial administration and local authorities, organized a public forum in Speu (A) commune with representatives of almost all the people. About 1,000 people from 10 villages participated.
The main theme of this gathering focused on two main issues related to public order in accordance with the policy of safe villages and communes and the provision of public services to serve the lives of the people.
After emphasizing the importance of public forums aimed at promoting the successful implementation of the Rectangular Political Program and Strategy, Mr. Prum Sokha, Working Group Chair, highlighted the continuous progress of the society in peace, stability, democracy and the rule of law. The leadership of the Royal Government, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Next, the people's representatives raised some suggestions to solve some problems that are happening at the local level, including:
* Regarding public order, the people clearly see the determinants of security, safety and stability at the local level, starting from their active participation with the competent authorities in complying with the proper laws in force.
* Regarding the efficiency of providing public services, the requests of the people gathered around issues such as:
Rehabilitation of Po Lok canal to serve agriculture; Continuation of electricity connection to the remaining two villages (East Spear and South Kali)
Accelerating the provision of documents, family books and ID cards, resolving minor disputes of neighbors, etc.
Clarifications of working groups and representatives of relevant competent authorities, including representatives of private businesses, responded to and answered almost all the requests of the people and the remaining issues were recorded for further action in accordance with the appropriate procedures.
