(Phnom Penh): General Kun Kim, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Missions, expressed his deepest shock and regret after receiving the news of the death of Lt. Gen. Ul Navy, Deputy Chief of Joint Staff and Commander of the Air Defense Command. Which is a brave close ally in defending territorial integrity during the recent border dispute with Thailand.
In a condolence message to Roeung Sophany, wife and family of Lt. Gen. Ul Navy, received by Fresh News on July 19, 2019, Senior Minister Kun Kim highlighted the death of Lt. Gen. Ul Navy. Ul Navy is the loss of a wonderful husband, father and grandfather.
Kun Kim recalled that Lt. Gen. Ul Navy had taken care of the work of strengthening the base by sacrificing a lot of personal resources to help the base, and his heroism was indescribable.
Senior Minister Kun Kim emphasized that the death of Lt. Gen. Ul Navy left a heroic example for the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces in general and for the armed forces on the Cambodian-Thai border in particular.
Kun Kim said he and the entire army would remember Ul Navy's heroic example. "We will always remember your heroism. On behalf of myself, as the former First Deputy Chairman of the Cambodia-Thailand Border Command, once again I share my condolences with her and her family and pray for the late Lt. Gen. Ul Navy. "Stay healthy, don't be lazy."
