Case 1: A man driving a fast car violated the traffic light and hit a CAMRY car, then overturned and hit the metal railing and road number plate, causing severe damage, but fortunately no one was injured. The incident happened at more than 1 am on July 19, 2019, located along the corner of Monivong Street and Street 310, Sangkat Boeung Keng Kang III, Khan Chamkar Mon, Phnom Penh.
Suddenly, the side of the PRIUS car got out of the car and fled from the scene. After the incident, the local police arrived at the scene and contacted the traffic police to measure the two vehicles and store them at the Phnom Penh Road Traffic Office to wait for a legal settlement later. .
Case 2: A man drove a PRIUS car as fast as it flew and hit a house, causing the car to break its wheels and cause severe damage, but fortunately, the accident did not cause any injuries. The accident happened at 3:30 pm on July 19, 2019, located along Street 598 near the Indra Tevy High School traffic light, Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Sen Sok, Phnom Penh.
Preah Sihanouk Province: Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, Mr. Cheam Him, Chairman of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Council and Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, presided over the facilitation ceremony on July 19. And the new Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Sihanouk Province.
The ceremony was held at Sihanoukville Provincial Hall with the participation of officials from relevant departments and units in Sihanoukville in large numbers.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun praised the efforts of Mr. Nop Heng, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Sihanoukville Province in the past, to work hard to achieve the development of infrastructure such as roads, traffic safety, roads. Water, drainage system management, drainage and drainage well.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun said that in recent years, Sihanoukville has received a lot of development from foreign investors, especially Chinese investors, making the province grow rapidly in all areas. Progress has spawned the birth of people from various provinces and cities to work and do business according to their skills and abilities.
According to Sihanoukville, Sihanoukville has nine special economic zones, five of which are in operation, with a total of 210 factories, 1,037 handicrafts and other businesses absorbing labor. About 81,475 people, of which about 50 percent are women.
He said that at present, Chinese investors are the number one investors in business, industry, trade, transportation, construction and tourism. At the same time, Sihanoukville Autonomous Port has grown significantly and is playing a role in the storage, transfer and transportation of container goods in and out of the country about 73%.
