(Kampong Cham): Police in Kampong Cham province have launched a series of operations to detain 10 suspects in connection with drug cases in Kampong Cham and Stung Trang districts.
Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Em Kosal said that the operation was carried out in accordance with the Royal Government's plan to fight against illegal drugs for the fourth time and the order of the National Police General Gen. Neth Savoeun. There are measures to suppress drug activity.
In fact, on July 18, 2019 in Kampong Cham City and Stung Trang District, after receiving information from the people, the Commissioner assigned the Anti-Drug Office in cooperation with Kampong Cham City and Stung Trang District, led by Lieutenant Colonel Chiv Seng Ros, Director of the Anti-Drug Bureau. Drugs used open administrative rules and incitement rules to crack down on cases of storing, trafficking and illegal use of drugs in 2 cases, arrested 10 suspects.
