Kampong Cham CamControl Officers Continued to Inspect Goods at Stung Trang Market, Found Some Products Over
(Kampong Cham): For food safety and health of the people, Kampong Cham Provincial CamControl Officer on July 18, 2019, in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Commerce, inspected food items at Stung Trang Market in Boeung Deng Village, Prey Kak Commune, Stung Trang District, Kampong Cham Province.
Mr. Sean Sinath, Head of CamControl Kampong Cham Branch, said that the purpose of the inspection was to prevent the traffic of defective goods, counterfeit labels, expiration dates and the presence of banned chemicals that could affect people's health.
During the inspection, CamControl officers confiscated 167 out-of-date items, such as: 167 finished LB cakes, 3 bottles of VC brand chili sauce, and 3 bottles of B-smart orange juice. On that occasion, the team introduced traders and vendors to better understand food safety and hygiene of the fair.
On the same day, CamControl branch officials instructed other traders to understand and follow the law on quality control, safety of products and services to avoid affecting the health of people will be able to face the law.
