Health Minister Asks Chinese Ministry of Economy to Expand Preah Sihanouk Provincial Hospital
(Phnom Penh): Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, said that the Economic Adviser of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia will take his request to the Ministry of Economy of China to help expand the hospital in Sihanoukville. Sihanoukville is more populated and a fast-growing place.
Prof. Mam Bunheng confirmed this to the media on the afternoon of July 18, 2019, when he received a courtesy call from Mr. Li An, Economic Adviser of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia. Office of the Ministry of Health.
On the occasion of courtesy and farewell, Professor Mam Bunheng also expressed his deep appreciation to Mr. Ly An for his hard work in helping the health sector in Cambodia, which has many projects. Joint operations include the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital Preah Kosomak, which has been building Tbong Khmum Hospital, and is building 40 mobile ambulances to continue operations to help patients.
