The S-400 is capable of launching 72 missiles and hitting 36 targets at the same time, capable of shooting down fighter jets at a maximum range of 400 km and missiles at a range of more than 61 km at an altitude of 27 km. But the missile system has never been tested in real life or in any war.
In fact, before deciding to buy the S-400 from Russia, Turkey also negotiated the purchase of missile systems from NATO member states such as France, Italy and the United States, as well as China, to strengthen its territorial defense capabilities. The talks were fruitless as several cities in southern Turkey were hit by a series of missiles or rockets fired from Syria during 2016.
But what made Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan decide to buy the S-400 was because the coup overthrew him that same year. At the time, insurgents were using US F-16 and F-4 fighter jets to fly over Ankara and Istanbul, where they fired on the Turkish parliament and presidential palace, and even Erdogan himself was killed. The attack, too.
In 2017, Turkey signed a $ 2.5 billion deal to buy the S-400 from Russia, and some experts see the purchase as a political decision just as Turkey wants to show the United States and Europe independence. And the sovereignty of its air defense strategy only.
Some experts say the purchase of the S-400 was due to Erdogan's view that to protect himself from another coup, Russian weapons and especially missiles were the best defense measures, while the United States and Europe. Seems to ignore him, who is also one of the strongest leaders in the region.
In addition, following the leak of unofficial information, a small number of experts claim that the purchase of S-400 is a project of Turkey and the United States, with both NATO member countries wanting to dismantle Russian technology to study. Investigate weaknesses and develop a new weapon that can only destroy the missile system.
