Anthropologist Explains the Importance of Alcohol Used in Interaction with Humans and Its Benefits
Prof. Chulan presented some evidence that wine as a means of attachment to this deity is available to both foreigners and Cambodians, especially ethnic minorities in Kampong Speu, Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri provinces about the use of alcohol in the living. Important offerings in ceremonies such as: In Japan, Shinto religion, an ancient religion that is revered by Japanese emperors, is often kept in shrines and given to priests.
In Christianity, wine is considered a sacred wine, like the blood of Christ. Therefore, those Christians always drink wine on special occasions, just as they are connected to God and incarnate.
For the Por / Sui minority in Kampong Speu, therefore, wine is the most important and revered item and is also used in some ceremonies, such as the minorities in Mondulkiri and Ratanakkiri. But in some cases, during the New Year, people hug the jars of wine and there are people who grab them like rugby and bring them to the ceremony happily.
For the Cambodian people in the area of Sambor Prei Kuk temple, at the end of each rice cycle, people gather at home to collect wine and have a happy ceremony, while some even carry a small bottle of wine with incense, candles and cakes to take Go to your grandfather. During the sacrament, they pour wine on the elders, talk to the wine and drink wine together to connect with the gods and fulfill the request of the beggars.
In addition, they also see the presence of wine used to treat diseases by offering sacrifices during the Memot feast, putting wine on the village to live and offering to Preah Pisnouka, along with musicians so that the gods can remove the poison to bless the owner The sick figure was healed and the band was playing in a way that did not disrupt the program. In addition, Cambodian society also needs alcohol used in weddings to grow old until the funeral.
