More than 600 hectares of rain-fed farmers affected by drought have been rescued, but more than 3,000 hectares have not yet been intervened.
(Prey Veng): Rainy season rice of farmers in two districts in Sithor Kandal and Kamchay Mear districts of Prey Veng province is experiencing drought, and among the rice affected by the drought, professional officials have gradually intervened to help.
In which, the team of Prey Veng Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology brought 2 65-pump water pumps to pump 620 hectares of rain-fed rice in Prey Deum Thnong commune, Sithor Kandal district, Prey Veng province. Pumps from Prek Romlech are placed in the main canal and then the farmers continue to pump water into the fields.
While the rain-fed rice of farmers in Kamchay Mear district is experiencing the same drought, there has been no intervention to help lack the source of water to irrigate the rice. Regarding this issue, Mr. Soeung Socheat, Governor of Kamchay Mear District and Deputy District Governor, as well as the relevant specialized offices, commune chief, commune chief Cheach, post chief inspected the farmers' rice, but no response has been taken yet.
Farmers say that nearly 3,000 hectares of rain-fed paddy fields are suffering from drought and that they have been asked by the authorities to request emergency intervention from the Prey Veng Provincial Department of Agriculture and the Department of Resources. Water in Prey Veng province soon.
