US Congress approves resolution banning Donald Trump from selling arms to Arab countries
WASHINGTON: Democrat-controlled US Congress has approved three resolutions to prevent the administration of US President Donald Trump from selling arms to Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates without congressional scrutiny or approval. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Thursday, July 18, 2019.
The above three resolutions, including two resolutions, were adopted this Wednesday by a vote of 238 to 190, while a third by a vote of 237 to 190. The vote also comes in response to Donald Trump, who announced in May the urgency and need to sell more than $ 8.1 billion worth of weapons to US allies. Middle East to counter the threat from Iran.
In June, the Republican-controlled Senate also passed a resolution banning the Donald Trump administration's arms sales. But the White House has stated that Trump will veto the decision.
