A survey released Wednesday by Pulse Asia after it took place from June 24 to 30 showed that 85 percent of Filipinos were interviewed. Across the country, about 1,200 people over the age of 18 have expressed support for Duterte's leadership style, and 85 percent of Filipinos continue to have high confidence in the 75-year-old leader. Also.
Duterte came to power in June 2016 with a commitment to cracking down on corruption and enforcing law and order throughout the Philippines by launching a crackdown on criminals and terrorists. The president of the Philippines generally holds only one term. Duterte's term ends in 2022.
The poll is a testament to the fact that while other countries condemn Duterte's leadership style, especially on human rights issues and the Philippine leader's crackdown on drugs. However, most people living directly in the Philippines still support and believe in Duterte.
