With the influx of Chinese investors and people coming to work in Sihanoukville, a group of Chinese people wrote and produced a new song entitled "If there is no dream, why should I come to Kampong Som The meaning of this song is about the hard work life of Chinese workers in Sihanoukville.
The content of this song explains why they want to fulfill their dreams, so they are willing to leave their homeland to travel to Cambodia, even though they are tired and miss their family, they are willing to endure the pain.
The following is the meaning of a Chinese song translated into Khmer:
* Everyone wants to seize the opportunity to create their own brilliance, but there are winners and losers.
Every time I imagine the eyes of parents who are waiting for their children to try to wipe the tears dry and then continue to work hard.
* No dream, why come to Kampong Som to give up everything, strive to move forward with courage
* No dreams, why come to Kampong Som, believe in yourself that there is great power
* No dream, why come to Kampong Som to strive for success
