This morning, the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit held a press conference on "Measures to Prevent Forest Crimes"
(Phnom Penh): At 9:30 am on July 18, 2019, the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit will hold a press conference on "Measures to Prevent Forest Crimes" on the ground floor of the meeting hall of the Office of the Council of Ministers.
According to a statement from the Government Spokesperson's Unit, which was received by Fresh News, the conference aims to address the concerns of the people who are focusing on effective measures. Of forest crime prevention such as:
* Legal aspects and measures to prevent forest crime
Effectiveness of past law enforcement and measures
During the meeting, Mr. Chan Chhun Sing said that Cambodia is a country with high potential to export goods to Singapore, but exports by Cambodia to Singapore are still small.
However, he still has high hopes of strengthening trade cooperation between Cambodia and Singapore, with goods such as vegetables, fruits, fish, meat and seafood all in high demand in Singapore. In addition, Cambodia also has high potential to import construction equipment such as cement, sand and in the future can supply clean water and energy.
The Cambodian Minister of Commerce agreed with the Singaporean Minister's statement that the strengthening of this cooperation is in line with the vision of the ASEAN leaders in promoting more trade in ASEAN.
As for export products, the Minister also introduced such as Kampot pepper, Kampong Speu palm sugar and Koh Trung grapefruit, which are all geographically identified products, especially Kampot pepper, which is the best and most expensive pepper. In addition, the Minister also introduced more mango and rice products and invited Singaporean companies to learn more about Cambodia's potential products.
Six more timber trucks were raided in Sesan district, Stung Treng province, the vehicles were burned and cut to pieces on the spot
