Cambodia has every right to defend its sovereignty and independence, protected by international law and norms, as enshrined in the UN Charter. Non-interference, mutual respect and equal sovereignty are the core principles of international relations. We all in Cambodia understand that there is nothing more precious than freedom and independence. All Cambodians have never thought that self-determination came easily.
