Director General of the Cambodia Securities Exchange: 7 listed companies raised a total of more than 130 million dollars to raise capital!
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hong So Hour, General Director of the Cambodia Securities Exchange, on July 17, 2019, confirmed that the Cambodia Securities Exchange currently has seven listed companies and has raised a total capital of more than $ 130 million. America in raising capital.
This confirmation was made during the official launch of the special benefit package from Canadia Bank Plc. For companies listed on the Cambodia Securities Exchange. The ceremony was held at the Cambodia Securities Exchange on the evening of July 17, 2019.
Mr. Hong Sohour stated, "In terms of raising capital, our seven listed companies have raised a total capital of more than 130 million US dollars, of which five companies have registered shares with a total capital raising of "80 million US dollars and two other companies have registered bonds, raising about 50 million US dollars."
The Director General of the Cambodia Securities Exchange added that the Cambodia Securities Exchange will also have more companies ready to issue securities this year and next. He claimed that this marked a good start and a stable market growth.
Mr. Hong Sohour also said that trading in the Cambodian stock market has recently become more active and attractive, with the average daily trading volume of the stock exchange has increased to more than 180,000 shares or 560,000 shares. Dollars per day for the second quarter of 2019. The number of investors in the stock market has also increased to more than 21,000.
Mr. Sou Socheat, Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, said that this special benefit package will be provided to companies listed on the Cambodia Securities Exchange, as well as employees who have been working in these listed companies are a positive sign for the securities sector. And the banking sector. Therefore, he strongly hopes that the two sectors will continue to cooperate as a whole and favor each other.
According to Raymond Siegon, CEO of Canadia Bank Plc., Canadia Bank has developed a special package that combines attractive benefits and terms as well as competitive interest rates for all listed companies.
As one of the largest local banks, he strongly believes in supporting the customer economy, which means that Canadia Bank wants to provide banking services to its subsidiaries as well as their employees.
Emphasize that the provision of this special benefit package is expected to contribute to facilitating the company's cash management. In addition, this special benefit package will also be available to listed subsidiaries as well as full-time employees of these companies.
2,000 tons of organic rice of farmers in Preah Vihear province signed by a local company to be exported to the European Union
(Preah Vihear): Organic rice of farmers in Preah Vihear province, which is the largest producer of rice, has received 2,000 tons of organic rice from 11 farming communities in Preah Vihear province. For the 2019-2020 season for export to the European Union.
Mr. Peng Trida said that rice in Preah Vihear province is more expensive than other provinces by partnering to supply organic rice within the agricultural framework under the contract with the company, in the past, rice in Preah Vihear province has always been the lowest in the range. 30 to 40 riel per kilo because at that time there were no partner companies to buy yet.
Mr. Kong Pheach also said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has always considered the issue of agricultural markets for farmers so that farmers have a better life, as today in the framework of contract farming is very beneficial for all parties, while farmers are not worried. No more lack of market because the market has reached the homes of farmers.
Mr. Kong Pheach added that the prices of most agricultural products were set by traders and were not as clear or guaranteed as agricultural contracts, as the companies that ordered them had contracts to supply them directly to the international market. Having this agricultural contract makes it difficult for traders to shake up the market as much as they want. Minister Mam Bunheng: Nursing Science Conference 2019 Contributes to Strengthening Cambodia's Health System
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, said that the organization of the 2019 Nursing Science Conference, which is held for two and a half days at the University of Health Sciences (CIS) is a contribution to strengthening the country's health system. Cambodia.
Professor Mam Bunheng said that under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Cambodia has made progress in all areas. The health sector has also achieved significant success.
The Minister expressed his appreciation to the University of Health Sciences, EWHA University of the Republic of Korea and the Cambodian Nurses Association for organizing this important conference.
In addition, the professor stated that "Today's conference contributes to the Ministry of Health to further strengthen the capacity of professors, nursing professionals and students in the field of nursing science, expand the value of the profession and help the health system in Cambodia. To be more prosperous and better.
He thanked EWHA University of the Republic of Korea and KOICA for their cooperation over the University of Health Sciences for the past 5 years.
Prof. Saphon Vattanak, Rector of the Royal University of Phnom Penh, outlined the main purpose of the conference to share new knowledge on the results of research in nursing science, share good experiences related to training and practice in nursing science and practice. Provide opportunities to strengthen the capacity of students and teachers with a career in nursing.
She stressed that the partnership between Ewha Womans University and the University of Health Sciences represents the cooperation between Korea and Cambodia, and we believe that this partnership provides an opportunity for both countries to grow. Joint face on health care in Cambodia.
Mr. Nakyoung Oh, Ambassador of the Republic of Korea to Cambodia, hopes that the Nursing Science Conference will be an important opportunity in strengthening the capacity of healthcare professionals for the Cambodian people.
