APSARA Authority is restoring the drainage system in Angkor Wat to facilitate the flow of water during the rainy season
(Siem Reap): The team of Water Management Department of APSARA Authority has been restoring the drainage system in Angkor Wat to facilitate the flow of water before the rainy season arrives, while the restoration has been completed in the southern and eastern parts. The team is continuing to work on the north side.
During the dry season, the drainage system in the Angkor Wat temple area has fallen leaves, causing condensation and blocking the flow of water during the rainy season. That is why the team of APSARA Authority restored the remains.
