Cambodian National Assembly requests US Congress to reconsider passing sanctions on Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia expresses its deepest condolences to the US House of Representatives for approving the draft law on "Democracy". In Cambodia 2019 "on July 16, 2019 ago.
In a statement issued by the spokesperson of the National Assembly, which was received by Fresh News on July 17, 2019, the approval of the draft law was considered to be contrary to the efforts of Cambodia and the United States. Take in promoting all-round partnerships based on common interests and mutual respect.
The statement said that despite the unjust pressure and unilateral sanctions from the United States, the Royal Government of Cambodia has sincerely chosen a positive approach in order to continue cooperation with the United States. In all areas.
A spokesman for the Cambodian National Assembly called on the US Congress to seriously reconsider taking an unjust bias towards Cambodia, which is committed to practicing its democracy.
The Speaker of the National Assembly also fully supported the statement of the Spokesman of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on July 16, 2019 yesterday in response to the decision of the US House of Representatives.
Although the law was passed by the National Assembly, it will have to wait for another decision from the upper house before being sent to the president for review and implementation.
Cambodian monk receives "Golden Stupa for the Support and Preservation of Buddhism" from the King of Thailand
(Phnom Penh): Preacher Dr. Khy Sovanratana, Vice Chancellor in charge of Buddhist management at Sihanoukville University, received the "Golden Stupa for the Support and Preservation of Buddhism" Awarded by His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej. The 10th Ream of Thailand.
The award ceremony was held on July 17, 2019 by General Chalit Pokphasok, Commander of the Royal Thai Air Force, Supreme Adviser to the King and Representative of His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej of the Kingdom of Thailand.
After receiving the award of "Golden Stupa", the preacher Dr. Khy Sovanratana had a decree expressing his happiness to receive this prestigious award.
He added that as a Cambodian monk, receiving a prestigious award from the King of Thailand was not only a great honor and pride for him, but also for Cambodian and Cambodian monks. .
Thailand has just organized the evaluation and selection of the best person to receive the "Golden Stupa" award, and this is the first year to present 103 dignitaries, mostly monks and Thai families with outstanding achievements. Dominant. Of the 103, only seven were from Cambodia, Vietnam, Laos, Sri Lanka, Singapore and Burma, Indonesia.
Overall, the outstanding individuals who received this award were evaluated and selected by a committee set up by Thailand, which was selected with the utmost care and precision. In addition, the outstanding individual must have relevant knowledge in six areas, including management, religion, education, counseling, Buddhism, public benefit, and public relief.
Preacher Dr. Khy Sovanratana is one of the senior intellectuals in contributing to the promotion of Buddhism in Cambodia and also a member of the Senior Sangha Abroad.
Preacher Dr. Khy Sovanratana always had good relations and communication with foreign monks during his invitations to attend events and as a speaker in all those countries, often sacrificing almost his life. Strive to promote and participate in the promotion of Buddhism and strive to study and study in Cambodia, Sri Lanka and India.
