The F-35's famous features can disguise itself from radar, but this disguise has not been leaked because it is a secret. The aircraft is also equipped with 360-degree cameras that capture both night and day images, as well as advanced weapons, including missiles, grenades, intelligence systems and electromagnetic systems.
The U.S. military has more than 200 F-35 stealth fighter jets as its largest operator. Other countries that have bought and are ordering the F-35 include Japan, South Korea, Australia, Singapore, Turkey, Italy, the United Kingdom and Israel.
Countries participating in the development of the aircraft with the United States include Britain, Italy, the Netherlands, Turkey, Canada, Australia, Denmark, Norway, Israel, Japan and South Korea. Britain and Japan are the largest buyers of F-35s, but only the United States and Israel have used them in military operations, especially in the Syrian war.
The F-35 was launched in 2001 and first flew in 2006 and was officially launched in 2015 after the US Marine Corps announced that it was ready for combat.
The F-35 is the best aircraft in the world, but it is not perfect until it has no problems. In fact, a Pentagon report released in 2016 found that the F-35 had a bizarre problem, as it used fuel to cool some parts of the aircraft, but usually in some weather conditions. It must be kept below freezing before pumping into the aircraft.
