Vendors and noodle sellers in Svay Rieng use alternative meats to cook pork after African swine fever outbreak
(Svay Rieng): African swine fever Although not affecting people, some people and traders in Svay Rieng province have turned to other meats for cooking as African swine fever has spread in Kralokor district. Svay Chrum, Svay Rieng Province.
The rice seller said that in the beginning, he used to buy 10 to 15 kilograms of fried pork every day, but now, with the presence of African swine fever, the sale of rice noodles Decreased gradually until he decided to stop selling pork.
She added that if the disease calmed down and customers came, he would dare to sell, otherwise there would be no buyers.
Similarly, traders who sell beef and pork at the market say that in the past they sold a decent amount of pork per day can sell 100 kg to more than 100 kg, but this time due to the outbreak. The African swine fever came and he sold only 10 kilograms of meat.
It should be noted that African swine fever, which causes the death of pigs, is very contagious to other pigs and causes both pigs to die without a cure, but according to the announcement of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. Africa does not infect humans, only pigs.
