Bolton made the remarks in connection with a bill drafted by two U.S. senators aimed at strengthening US President Donald Trump's executive order in May on blacklisting Chinese technology company Huawei.
Mr Bolton alleged that Huawei was under the control of the Beijing government, which could pose a high risk if allowed to do business with US companies. Therefore, the security adviser thinks that the United States should permanently cut off this Chinese technology company from the US market.
The United States and China are still embroiled in a trade war, with competition for 5G network services between the two countries, while China currently has Huawei as the world's leader in the latest technology. The latter. Seeing that it seems to be losing to China, Washington has been trying to put pressure on Huawei to exit its European and European markets.
The United States has also called on allies or other countries to end ties with Huawei over 5G connectivity, citing US allegations that Huawei is the world's top 5G telecommunications company. That is unsafe because it could be used by Beijing for intelligence, but no concrete evidence has been found as alleged by the United States.
(Preah Sihanouk): General Dr. Mao Ha Vannal, Minister in Charge of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation and Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Working Group on Land Impact Assessment in the Sihanoukville International Airport Development Project, on July 16, 2019, chaired an emergency meeting. On security arrangements for all types of aircraft operations at Sihanoukville International Airport.
