Senior Minister Kun Kim tells officials in Tbong Khmum province to be ready to help people affected by natural disasters
(Tbong Khmum): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, on Wednesday, July 17, 2019, chaired a meeting to review the work of the Tbong Khmum Provincial Disaster Management Committee and set out some measures to Prepare to solve various problems caused by natural disasters in the province.
During the meeting, Mr. Kun Kim reminded that Tbong Khmum province is also a province bordering the Mekong River, and this rainy season is also a time when people are vulnerable to floods. The Senior Minister reminded Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province and Chairman of the Provincial Disaster Management Committee, as well as relevant officials in the province, the police force to be ready to help evacuate people in the event of floods.
Mr. Kun Kim stated, "In order to be ready for prevention and timely response, the province must make detailed preparations in detail, including the provision of safe havens, facilities, equipment, and reserve forces for intervention with pre-training and care." Training human resources to rescue victims and so on.
However, Senior Minister Kun Kim praised the Provincial Disaster Management Committee for its commitment and response to disaster preparedness and response.
According to the report, Mr. Cheam Chansophorn, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, pointed out that in the first six months of 2019, strong winds, lightning, fire, drowning and other epidemics affected the property and killed a total of 7 people in the province, outbreaks African swine fever killed 47 pigs and dengue fever increased by 1,983 cases.
