Net Pheaktra, secretary of state and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, told Fresh News that the illegal waste originated from the United States and Canada, weighing up to 1,600 tonnes and was ready for shipment. Back.
The spokesman said: "According to preliminary data obtained from the investigation authorities, the 83 containers of plastic waste, which are prohibited goods, were confiscated at the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, originating from the United States and Canada. About 1600 tons. Authorities have been working to repatriate the company and fine the importing company in accordance with the law.
"The specialized police force has been continuing to investigate further to find out the real reason that led to the import of this plastic waste, which is a prohibited commodity to Cambodia. Authorities are also investigating companies that smuggle in plastic waste to take action in accordance with the law, "said Pheaktra, an active spokesman for the Ministry of Environment.
The crackdown on the import of plastic waste from abroad into Cambodia now confirms strict enforcement of prohibited laws and hazardous waste. The timely crackdown on banned plastic waste also demonstrates the close cooperation between the Ministry of Environment and relevant institutions, including the General Department of Customs and Excise and the Autonomous Port, to prevent prohibited goods from entering Cambodia.
The Royal Government of Cambodia will continue to implement strict legal measures against the smuggling of all types of prohibited goods. The Royal Government of Cambodia does not allow the import of plastic waste for recycling in Cambodia. Cambodia is not a dumping ground for outdated technology, and Cambodia has always opposed the import of plastic waste and motor oil for recycling in Cambodia.
Please be informed that on the afternoon of July 16, 2019, the Ministry of Environment and the General Department of Customs and Excise of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and relevant institutions decided to remove all the containers for inspection in Sihanoukville Port after Suspicious of the goods in the container.
Ministry of Labor begins discussions on raising wages for garment workers for 2020
(Phnom Penh): Discussions on raising the minimum wage for textile, garment and footwear workers in Cambodia for 2020 began this July and will continue until October. This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, which was received by Fresh News on July 17, 2019.
According to the announcement, the discussion on the minimum wage for 2020 is as follows:
* Set July 2019 as the start of the internal minimum wage discussion of each party. * Set August 2019 as the start of the tripartite minimum wage discussion * Set the October 2019 opening date. Meeting of the National Minimum Wage Council to achieve the minimum wage in the textile, garment and footwear sector for 2020 * Set January 1, 2020 as the effective date of the minimum wage.
According to the Ministry of Labor, all parties must apply social criteria (household status, inflation rate and cost of living) and economic criteria (productivity, national competitiveness, labor market status and sector profit margins). ) As well as the poverty line as a basis for discussing the minimum wage in Cambodia.
All parties should focus on scientific data and research in accordance with the seven criteria set out in Article 5 of the Minimum Wage Law as a basis for internal coordination and a common position.
