According to the Global Fund for the Conservation of Natural Resources (WWF), an organization that assists in the Mekong Dolphin Conservation Project, a newborn baby dolphin was recently found by the WWF-'s research team. Cambodia is found in Kampi Dolphin Canyon in Kampi village, Sambok commune, Chit Borey district, Kratie province.
He added that the new baby dolphin was the sixth baby dolphin to be recorded in 2019.
He added that there were only more than 70 dolphins in 2017, but by 2019 there were more than 90 dolphins and more than 30 children under the age of five, according to WWF officials. Excluding large dolphins, new baby dolphins were recently born in 2019, confirming joint efforts to conserve the Mekong River dolphins in Cambodia.
This result is a reflection of the excellent cooperation in conservation work between WWF-Cambodia and conservation partners such as local authorities, fund owners, community partners, the general public, and especially the Fisheries Administration of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Ministry of Environment and the Ministry of Tourism. Kratie Provincial Authority.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng: Illegal intruders along the border must be evicted (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, reminded the police force to take strict control of foreigners and High responsibility. Samdech Krala Hom stressed that there must be immediate measures to deport foreigners from Cambodia illegally entering Cambodia.
Remarks by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng on the occasion of presiding over a meeting to disseminate the results of the work on the confiscation of irregular Cambodian administrative documents used by foreigners and the receipt of applications for alienation, immigration and permanent residence permit in This July 17, 2019.
During the ceremony, Samdech Krala Hom said that the management of foreigners in Cambodia is an important task that must be taken care of, not to leave foreigners outside the law can cause chaos and uncontrollability. Has had a negative impact on security, order and social security, national development programs and human rights.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also stressed that the law enforcement forces to prevent foreigners from entering Cambodia illegally. Samdech Krala Hom stated that foreigners who come illegally must be deported because it is an international principle.
"The Capital, Provincial, Police, District, Municipal, Khan and Police Offices of the Commune / Sangkat Administration must take care to manage foreigners responsibly and take immediate measures to deport them from Cambodia." "Stay illegally to prevent recurring situations." This was confirmed by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng in front of the senior leadership of the National Police Force.
In addition to warning to take action against foreigners who enter Cambodia illegally, in this morning's ceremony, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng instructed the Cambodian police force to strictly control immigrants in Cambodia by following legal measures. That Cambodia has.
According to the results of the confiscation of irregular Cambodian administrative documents held by foreigners and the receipt of the application for declaration of alien immigration and permanent residence permit, which was implemented for 2 years and 6 months, it was found that the immigrants in Cambodia There are 11 nationalities, 49,603 families, equal to 182,673 people, 82,488 women. Of these, 125,893 were aged 18 and over, 54,882 were women.
Due to the secrecy of the barracks, some people think that the US government actually has information about aliens and UFOs that they try to hide from the general public. It has been around for decades, and now there is a resurgence.
Of the number of foreigners who did not have their Cambodian administrative documents confiscated, who did not apply for citizenship, and who did not apply for permanent residence permits, 50,000 Vietnamese returned to their home countries. However, some figures were duplicated and about 15,000 were deported and died in prison and other causes.
General Kiet Chantharith, Director General of the General Department of Immigration, emphasized at the ceremony that the process of confiscating Cambodian administrative documents was irregular, and that the application for immigration and permanent residency was a great success and a matter of national pride. The Royal Government, and especially for the Ministry of Interior, has overcome many major challenges and has achieved good results.
General Kiet Chantharith emphasized that the results of this work are significant because it will end the chronic problems related to the settlement of foreigners in Cambodia and as a basis for the management of foreigners in the future. Preventing new intruders from staying illegally in Cambodia.
Mr. Kirth Chantharith added that this result will also reduce the baseless criticism from unscrupulous people, both inside and outside the country, who always take this issue for political gain, as well as exaggerate to intimidate the people. Prevent inactive activities related to the illegal issuance of Cambodian administrative documents to foreigners and contribute to increase the national budget revenue by fulfilling the obligations of foreigners residing in Cambodia.
According to Mr. Kirth Chantharith, this result also contributes to the implementation of international conventions and conventions on human rights and to prevent cross-border crime in order to protect national security and social order.
In this morning's ceremony, although the work (confiscation of irregular Cambodian administrative documents held by foreigners and permission to apply for alien registration, immigration and application for permanent residence) was completed, General Kiet Chantharith also presented the direction of the General Department of Immigration. The direction of the work includes:
In order to continue to implement the above work direction to get better results, General Kiet Chantharith also proposed to amend the Law on Immigration and amend the relevant standards, as well as to cancel the Census and Management Committee for Foreigners, Ministry of Interior and the Capital. Provinces after completing all administrative tasks.
