APSARA Authority urges people to stop any activities that affect the values of Angkor (Video inside) (Siem Reap): Angkor is a sacred place where Cambodians often worship and practice their religious beliefs. Its highest. At the same time, the temple of Angkor, the soul of the Khmer nation, is considered by historians and archaeologists to represent the universe.
Currently, the APSARA Authority, as well as the public, has observed that a small number of people do not value the temple of Angkor as meaning above, that is, sitting on the grass on the cliffs of Angkor Wat, Angkor Wat on other temples. To drink alcohol, turn on the loudspeakers, have fun, and leave behind trash that harms the sanctuary, aesthetics, the environment, and general order.
These acts have been gradually losing the wonder, the place of worship of Angkor, and also making foreign tourists lose faith in this wonderful land as they imagined before visiting.
The participation of our compatriots in enhancing the value and preservation of the Angkor temple environment through indirect activities by not eating or drinking alcohol on the grass and not littering around the Angkor temple complex, especially in accordance with the Angkor Code of Conduct It is a tribute to the work of our ancestors and a large part of it has already been conserved.
In this regard, APSARA Authority would like to ask the people to stop any activities that affect the values of the Angkor resort and participate in preserving the heritage of our ancestors, especially our Angkor temples. May the temple of Angkor remain a wonder forever.
