(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, has made it clear that one of the main priorities of the Royal Government among the key priorities of the medium-term public financial framework is to continue to focus on Pay attention to improving the lives of all types of civil servants to be better and better.
The Deputy Prime Minister added that for 2020 and the next medium term, the minimum (minimum) total monthly salary of each civil servant and members of the Armed Forces will be projected to increase by an average of 7% per year. With continued priority on the implementation of social protection policies in both the social security system and the social assistance system.
The Deputy Prime Minister made the remarks while addressing a workshop on understanding the development of macroeconomic and public financial policy frameworks for the preparation of the draft financial law for 2020 at the Palace. National Assembly, July 15, 2019.
