(Phnom Penh): Cambodian tricycle riders who are using Grab to receive travel bookings are satisfied with many of the new features in the program, they have confirmed that those special features It will help make their work more efficient and increase their ability to earn a living.
Grab, one of Southeast Asia's leading technology companies, is launching a number of new features since launching in Cambodia in 2017 to provide better access to Drivers and passengers.
Many travelers have applauded Grab's recent offer that makes travel through the program the cheapest and most rewarding experience by saving points, exchanging discounts and Promote a wide range of products at many of Cambodia's leading stores and businesses.
Drivers can also get a lot of encouragement through this program, but what makes many drivers more satisfied are the special features that make their work more efficient.
The most popular new feature among the new features that allows drivers to spend the most valuable time on the road is the "Pax No Show", which will automatically pay the driver comfort if the passenger Those who booked their vehicle did not arrive at the waiting area five minutes after the driver arrived.
"I like these special features and hope that the company will keep creating more useful features like this," Kiri added.
Another new feature of Grab, the "Heatmap" feature, is a map display feature that allows drivers to see different areas of the city from a busy location, so they can access it. Take advantage of high-demand venues such as venues for concerts or sporting events that can accommodate a large number of passengers.
Grab states that a key part of its mission is to use technology to generate revenue opportunities for its driving partners, as well as to make transportation services more affordable for Cambodians.
Preah Vihear Youth Volunteers Donate Blood to 16th January Referral Hospital to Save Patients' Lives
(Preah Vihear): Many young people of Preah Vihear province on the morning of July 16, 2019 volunteered to donate blood to the 16th of January Referral Hospital, which is facing anemia to save your life. Disease.
On this occasion, Dr. Kuong Lo informed that the transfusion of blood from the blood of the volunteers to the hospital is safer for patients than the blood that is exchanged immediately or the blood bought in the country. Global as well as regional countries. About 90% of the patients who receive blood transfusions come from free blood donation, especially in Cambodia, which is lower than other countries in the region.
He said that the blood donation of young people in the province now really contributes to social work to reduce maternal mortality because the causes of maternal mortality during pregnancy and postpartum are. Postpartum hemorrhage In addition, as dengue cases are on the rise, hospitals need more blood to treat patients, especially children.
Mr. Kuong Lo also stated that a one-time donation of 300 ml of blood does not affect health, and this blood donation can be given to men every three months and women can donate blood every four months.
Separately, Mr. Yong Kim Hean said that today, 28 members of the CPPCC volunteered to donate blood to the 16th January Referral Hospital to save patients' lives.
At the same time, Mr. Yong Kim Hean also thanked all the members of the Provincial CPPCC who volunteered to donate blood to the Referral Hospital on 16 January at this time, and he would like to appeal to our youth. All volunteered to donate blood to save the victims.
