Football match to help Angkor Hospital for Children to reach the final match this weekend
(Siem Reap): After nearly two months of competition, the football match to help Angkor Hospital for Children to reach the semi-finals on Saturday, July 20, 2019 this weekend. The final match will be held on Sunday afternoon, July 21, 2019.
Please note that the humanitarian football match to raise funds to help Angkor Hospital for Children has been organized by a group of workers and businesses in the tourism sector in Siem Reap. The competition started on June 1, 2019, raising more than US $ 10,000 to support Angkor Hospital for Children, a free hospital in Siem Reap.
Chheang Phalla, a representative of the Humanitarian Awards Committee, said that the football tournament to raise funds for humanitarian activities has been established for four years, starting in 2019. Mr. Phalla said that this match program was created by the staff and tourism business who love to play football in Siem Reap, not professional football players.
Mr. Chheang Phalla stated that for the first two years, the competition was held in a format and raised funds to help schools in need and in remote areas. In the last two years, he returned to help Angkor Hospital.
This year's charity football tournament has 14 teams competing, which is more than in previous years.
Please be informed that Angkor Hospital for Children is a charity hospital providing free medical services and was established in 1999. In the last 20 years, the hospital has treated more than 2 million children. The hospital treats between 500 and 600 children a day at a cost of about $ 6.5 million.
Nearly 90 percent of these funds are from foreign philanthropists, and more than 10 percent are from local philanthropists and the government.
