Cambodia Establishes Commission to Implement Action Plan for Prevention and Response to Violence against Children
(Phnom Penh): Ministries, state institutions and NGOs have jointly set up a steering committee to implement the action plan to prevent and respond to violence against children. The committee is chaired by Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, and has many members who are professional officers of the Ministry of Social Affairs, as well as many NGOs.
For the establishment of this commission, Mr. Vong Soth, as the chairman, said that it is necessary to require the participation of all ministries, institutions, national and international organizations and all relevant partners to address violence, discrimination and child abuse. Improving existing national standards, including the United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child.
Mr. Vong Soth stated that violence against children is an intolerable activity in any form because it affects the development of children, morality, society, dignity and human resource development in the future.
Mr. Touch Channy said that the committee has 22 members, 15 from ministries and institutions and 7 from representatives of organizations working with children. The committee has three technical working groups: the Working Group for the Awareness and Prevention of Violence against Children, the Service and Law Enforcement Working Group, and the Working Group on Legal Standards, Monitoring and Reporting.
