(Kratie): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, reminded the authorities in Kratie to be highly prepared to deal with and rescue people in the province. Which can face various dangers due to natural factors such as storms, tornadoes and floods in this rainy season.
The warning of the Senior Minister was made during the meeting to review, indicate and guide the disaster management work in 2019 to the disaster management officer in Kratie province on the morning of July 16, 2019. The ceremony was attended by Mr. Vathon, Governor of Kratie Province, relevant officials from various departments, the Armed Forces and development partners in the province.
During the meeting, Mr. Vathorn said that the National Committee for Disaster Management in the province is updating the contingency plan in Kratie province in 2019. This plan will be published in the near future and will meet with the National Committee for Disaster Management in municipalities, districts, communes, sangkats, strengthen its mechanisms on a regular basis and update disaster preparedness plans at the local and community levels.
He added that the province has set up a disaster management mechanism by strengthening the armed forces, civil servants, Red Cross youth, Red Cross volunteers, emergency teams, the Union Youth Union, the Peace Youth Union, the A157 youth group and the Scouts. Etc. to be ready to participate in rescue and response to possible emergencies.
Senior Minister Kun Kim praised and appreciated the officials and the armed forces in the province who were ready to rescue the people. The Senior Minister also praised the officials and the Armed Forces of Kratie Province, who have always cooperated well and responded in a timely manner in the event of a disaster.
However, the first vice-chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management continues to urge leaders, officials and the armed forces to be adequately prepared, such as safe havens for evacuation during floods. Establish a network to receive and provide information for the rescue of victims as well as the provision of food for victims.
"There must be the highest level of attention in this rescue," Kun Kim said. Disasters do not tell us in advance, we must be prepared to help the people in time. "Like during a flood, you have to find a safe place to help evacuate them to a safe place so that their lives are not endangered."
