The Law on Democracy in Cambodia was unanimously approved by the US House of Representatives on Monday, July 15, 2019. This law was made by them with the aim of punishing Cambodian officials and restoring democracy after them on the grounds that the democratic process in Cambodia had slowed down.
For Phay Siphan, the law drafted by the US House of Representatives is politically motivated and against the political will of the Cambodian people to elect their leaders legally through a peaceful and democratic election process.
In response, Phay Siphan also called on the US legislature and government to reconsider their position on Cambodia for the benefit of maintaining good relations and mutual benefits. For the people and governments of both countries.
Phay Siphan hoped that the US Senate as well as the President of the United States, the executive branch, would pay close attention to the good relations and international cooperation that our two nations have been striving to maintain. The mutual benefit is absolute.
