Vendors in Grand Chompouvan Market, 200 stalls erupted in protest again after they asked the market manager to help reduce the price of stalls, but to no avail
Vendors ask the governor of Por Senchey district to help find a solution for them. The protest again took place on July 14, 2019, located in Sangkat Choam Chao 3, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
They added that the president of the market had talked with the vendors at 40% for the first three months, if the vendors did not work, the market will continue to discuss renting stalls.
However, the vendors made two or three requests to meet, and the market manager said that the president of the market had not returned yet and that the market manager had taken a three-day notice to close the stalls. If a trader closes a stall and does not come to sell and refuses to pay 40% of the market price, the scrap metal will be removed from the stall and all traders will have to remove the stall and pay $ 500.
Vendors do not understand the manager and the president of the market? They really want to sell in this market, but the market does not keep the words that he said to the traders before the traders came to sell in this market.
In the past, they protested two or three times and did not see the market director come out to solve the problem, and they also continued to protest in front of Choam Chao III to ask the commune chief to help find a solution, but the commune chief did not seem to take Pay attention to the traders at all, instead of saying, "Wait and see the market manager from abroad, where do the people get their business and livelihood?"
Finally, the vendors would like to request the district governor Por Sen Chey to help find justice and solve this problem so that they can continue to sell in this market.
