But the 35-year-old opposition leader has failed to oust current Venezuelan President Nicolas Maduro, and some experts see this because Russia, especially China, remains a backbone. Maduro's big.
* Why is Maduro Venezuela important to China?
While Beijing is an indispensable economic and political partner for Caracas, the first American nation is also of paramount importance to China. China regards oil-rich Venezuela as a trading partner and strategic ally to compete politically and economically with the United States.
In fact, through Chinese investment in recent years, Venezuela has become an important component in the future of China's economic growth and energy security. From 2000 to 2018, China's direct trade volume reached more than $ 6 billion, while loans, especially in the oil sector, provided more than $ 60 billion by China to Venezuela.
Despite some economic losses, China continues to support Maduro's government so far. The official reason behind this support is that the Chinese government does not want to interfere in the internal affairs of other countries, but it does not mean that China is willing to let its economy lose.
For unofficial reasons, Beijing sided with Maduro because he believed Caracas could help it compete economically and politically with the United States in Latin America.
Juan Guaido has promised to protect China's interests as well as give China better financial concessions in Venezuela than the government of Nicolas Maduro if Beijing stops supporting Maduro. The Ministry of Water Resources confirms the water level situation at various hydrological stations on July 16!
