(Phnom Penh): Mr. Loy Virak, one of the outstanding Cambodian teachers, was selected by the Samdech Chao Fah Makhakri Prize of Thailand to be awarded 10,000 USD as a teacher who brought change to the lives of students in Cambodia.
At a ceremony to exchange the work experience of Master Mak Ha Chakri on the afternoon of July 15, 2019 at the Thai Embassy in Cambodia, the Foundation Committee of the award said that this award is an international award to honor. To outstanding teachers at the basic education level of 11 ASEAN countries and Timor-Leste.
The committee added that the selection is based on the principle of quality of education, based on the quality of teachers, the quality of teachers has an impact on the construction of quality human resources.
"Because this award is also to enhance the reputation of Samdech Preah Reach Kanitha, Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn, who has a great wisdom and great merit in the field of education, both inside and outside the country." This is a further emphasis of the Fund Committee of the Grand Master McHugry Award.
The Prince Chao Makha Chakri Award Foundation cooperates with the General Secretariat of the Teachers' Council of the Ministry of Education, the Education Equity Fund, the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and other relevant agencies of Thailand. The award was first announced on October 2, 2015 and is selected every two years.
The selection of teachers for the third Prince Chao Makha Chakri Award 2019, the teachers who received the award from the selection of the Ministry of Education in ASEAN and Timor-Leste 11 countries are qualified teachers. Qualified as a teacher who brings change to the lives of students and has the merit of one person per country in the field of education.
