Senior Minister Ly Thuch: The project to give love to children under the initiative of Samdech Techo and Chinese leaders is very important for Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of July 15, 2019, Senior Minister Ly Thuch received a delegation from Yunnan Heart Hospital of the People's Republic of China to pay a courtesy call and say goodbye after completing a medical examination mission for Cambodian children.
The above team of doctors led by Dr. Malin Khun, Director of Yunnan Cardiology Hospital, completed a 10-day mission in Cambodia from July 5 to 15, 2019 to examine the health of Cambodian children. Especially looking for children with congenital open heart disease.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, expressed his deep gratitude to the team of doctors who provided free open heart examination and surgery to the people, especially Cambodian children.
The Senior Minister added that this is a contribution to the Royal Government of Cambodia in reducing open heart disease mortality and reducing poverty in Cambodia. Children who have undergone surgery will be the messengers to Cambodia, signaling the steel ties between Cambodia and its great friend China.
At the same time, the Senior Minister requested that doctors continue to provide support and surgery for open heart disease and provide training for cardiologists to help ease the burden on the government and people with heart disease who need treatment. .
