(Siem Reap): Residents of Preah Dak village, Preah Dak commune, Banteay Srei district, Siem Reap province, hold a prayer service for rain as the rainy season approaches but there is no rain to provide enough rain for farmers to harvest. Good and pray for happiness to the villagers, which is an ancient tradition of Angkor people.
This prayer ceremony was held on July 14, 2019 in front of the East Mebon Temple, and the villagers cooked rice for the monks and prepared offerings for the water lords who kept in this village, which was attended by the people. A lot of people.
Mrs. Him Prem, 61 years old, the leader of the rain prayer ceremony, said that every year until the month of Asat, set a day in this month when there is no rain or little rain, all the villagers. Gathered together and raised money with generous force to cook food for the monks and prepare the equipment for the sacrifice and supply the needs of the whole program.
She said that the rain prayer ceremony is held every year, never misses, whether there is rain or not, and in addition to the villagers of Preah Dak, there are other villagers to participate and cook for the monks on the occasion. This includes Sen Pren, the landlord, the owner of the temple.
After the completion of the Buddhist rituals, up to nine relics are included, but the most special is the relics at the eastern Mebon temple, the corrupt relics, to visit and ask for rain for the relics to eat. Food, etc.
