Li An, Economic and Trade Advisor of the Embassy of the People's Republic of China in Cambodia, said: "We are pleased to see that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has continued to increase his investment in education. "And with remarkable results, I believe the future of education in Cambodia will be better."
He also said that Huawei's "Seeds for the Future" program is a public welfare program that has helped Cambodia develop its young ICT talent and the potential of the program is growing every year. This year is the fourth year and the top 10 students selected will be the seed representing the participating countries.
"Traveling thousands of miles to see the world and build new friendships is a unique value of a program, as one Chinese proverb says," Reading 10,000 books is like doing something. Travel tens of thousands of miles and make friends from all over the world. ”
