(Phnom Penh): The specialized force of the Criminal Police Department of the General Commission of the National Police launched an operation to crack down on the theft of a missing car in Sangkat Kbal Koh, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh last night, July 8, 2019.
The operation was ordered by General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, Lt. Gen. In Bora, Deputy Commissioner General for Judicial Police Central Planning, and led by Lt. Gen. Neng Chuor, Director of the Criminal Police Department. Department.
Colonel Kheng Meng Chheang, Director of the Office of Minor Offenses, said this morning, July 15, 2019, that after receiving the order, his office immediately launched a series of investigations until the relevant targets were identified and reached. Arrested on the afternoon of July 13, 2019.
He confirmed that the suspect was apprehended in Kbal Koh commune, Chbar Ampov district and sent to the specialized office for further interrogation and confiscated the car he stole, which was hidden in a house in Prek commune. Tradition of Leuk Dek district, Kandal province.
Lieutenant Colonel Kheng Meng Chheang confirmed that in addition to confiscating the car he stole, the police also confiscated a K54 handgun and seven bullets from the suspect. The suspect, 30-year-old Tey Sopheak, confessed to stealing the car and using a firearm illegally.
After the interrogation, the suspect was sent to court by the Criminal Police Department for legal punishment on July 15, 2019, and the car was returned to the victim.
