(Phnom Penh): As loans in Cambodia are increasing year by year, the Association of Cambodian Banks, in collaboration with the Cambodian Microfinance Association, this morning, July 15, 2019, organized a workshop on the process of Lending aims to further strengthen and expand the scope of the banking and financial sector to compete and curb challenges and reduce debt risk.
The workshop was also attended by relevant institutions, the Cambodian Credit Bureau, the Cambodian Banking Association, the Cambodian Microfinance Association and many other stakeholders.
Mr. Dich Sochol, Representative of the Board of Directors of the Association of Banks in Cambodia, said that reducing challenges such as debt, debt consolidation, customers and the general community requires increased cooperation and sharing of good development. As well as common challenges.
He added that in conclusion, for this workshop on lending principles, it is important to highlight the lending issues, including the form of credit risk and non-lending risk. Original.
Mr. Kea Boran, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Microfinance Association of Cambodia, stated that the purpose of today's workshop is related to the lending process, and loans always play an important role and are the first and foremost knife: customers take the right loan and Proper lending is good for the borrower, but secondly, if the borrower does not use it properly and is unable to repay it, the lender will have a hard time.
He said that in the first five months of 2019, loans continued to increase by more than 10 percent, and if this growth continues until the end of the year, it is possible that the end of this year will increase forever. Up to 20 to 30 percent, similar to 2018 ago.
He said that most of the loans are in the agricultural sector and loans for purchases, and in the last two years, there has been a sharp increase in home loans, while the real estate sector is currently booming. Well.
