On this occasion, the Commissioner urged all police officers to follow the five-point approach of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, including: 1: Mirror, 2: Bath, 3: Brush, 4th: Treatment and 5th: Surgery (officials must serve the people).
Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin also clarified the contents of the 10 guidelines of the Ministry of Interior, which clearly set out the roles and responsibilities of the National Police Force, the use of force, the use of weapons and the means appropriate to the tasks assigned by the higher level. Given the discipline, the troops must dress appropriately, the forces must cut their hair short, be ethical and speak appropriately.
