(Phnom Penh): Colonel Hour Meng Wang, Police Inspector of Sen Sok District, said that the police force of Kok Khleang Ka Administration Post at 12 o'clock on July 14, 2019 arrested a suspect after seizing a mobile phone. On Street 1928 in Trapeang Svay Village, Sangkat Kork Khleang, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh.
The victim in the shock was named Samnang Puthearin, an 18-year-old female resident of Vimean Trung Village, Sangkat Kraing Thnong, Khan Sen Sok.
Inspector Hour Meng Wang added that before the incident, the victim was riding a motorcycle alone on the road 1928. At the scene, suddenly a suspect riding a motorcycle near the victim and shocked. Taking the mobile phone from the victim, causing both motorcycles to fall, the patrol force immediately saw the incident, arrested the suspect and interrogated him at the Sen Sok District Police Inspectorate, and the victim filed a complaint against the suspect.
The suspect is currently being held at the Sen Sok police station to be sent to court for sentencing.
