(Phnom Penh): According to the clear encouragement of the Minister of Tourism, Mr. Thong Khon, in the study to develop the master plan for tourism development in Siem Reap, the area around Angkor, Phnom Kulen, Tonle Sap Lake and the surrounding area must be developed into tourism products. Recently to attract more tourists to visit Siem Reap, but this development must also take into account the conservation, sustainability and high responsibility.
Considerations for the recent development of tourism products have been actively promoted by the Minister, and were reiterated at a consultative workshop on master planning for tourism development in Siem Reap this weekend.
He said that Siem Reap-Angkor is getting a lot of attention from international tourists, with the number of tourists increasing every year, for example, in 2018, about 5 million tourists visited Siem Reap. Angkor as a whole, among which there are about 2.5 million international tourists.
However, this growth may slow down if Cambodia refuses to develop new tourism products as an additional attraction because some tourists are not sure to visit only Angkor and other temples in the Angkor heritage area, that is They definitely need to travel to other places not far from Angkor.
Seeing the trend of tourists like this, Minister Thong Khon strives to promote the development and expansion of new tourism products for this sacred land, in which he saw the potential of Phnom Kulen National Park. Tonle Sap Lake and the area around Angkor.
In studying the master plan for tourism development in Siem Reap, the Minister also urged the working group to study the organization of new tourist sites in the above locations.
Regarding the study visit to those areas, Mr. Nep Samuth, Director General of Tourism Industry Management of the Ministry of Tourism, said that the experts of the Inter-Ministerial Commission have visited those areas, especially Phnom Kulen and Tonle Sap, for direct questioning. With citizens and get some information.
He said that according to the survey of experts, in addition to visiting the Angkor area, tourists also like to visit the Phnom Kulen National Park and the Tonle Sap Lake, so it means that the surrounding areas have a lot of potential. Very culturally and historically.
In addition to the potential for cultural and historical tourism, Phnom Kulen National Park and the Tonle Sap Lake area can also be developed into more attractive ecotourism and agro-tourism areas, he said.
According to Nep Samuth, the study on the master plan will be completed in stages and will be completed by early 2020. This master plan will be implemented from 2020-2035.
Mr. Tith Chantha, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Tourism, also said that in order to study the master plan for tourism development in Siem Reap, the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to establish an inter-ministerial commission to implement not only the tourism sector, but also Many other related fields.
