Mr. Khuong Sreng: The activities of the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Phnom Penh have the same goal: to solve the difficult problems of the people
(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh and the President of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, confirmed that the activities of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Phnom Penh have only one goal: to solve the difficult problems of the people, especially the poor and vulnerable. The elderly, people living with HIV and the poor, regardless of political affiliation, religion, caste, or color.
This confirmation by Mr. Khuong Sreng was made this morning, July 15, 2019, during a meeting and distribution of gifts to 863 poor families from 10 communities and 18 villages in Sangkat Koul Roka, Khan Prek Pnov.
Phnom Penh Governor Khuon Sreng said that this was not the first time that the Red Cross had distributed humanitarian donations, nor was it the last time it would continue to do so.
He said that although this is a small gift, but this gift can help share some of your suffering and not let any people die because there is no food.
The Governor of Phnom Penh said that all the donations of the Red Cross came from the support of various philanthropists to the branch of the Cambodian Red Cross in Phnom Penh. These activities, the art of sharing among our Cambodian people, really mean a lot and very deep.
On that occasion, Kork Roka Sangkat Chief said that 863 poor families from 10 communities and 18 villages in Kork Roka Sangkat, Prek Pnov District received donations from the Cambodian Red Cross today. Exactly.
He said that all these poor people, they are construction workers, AIDS, the elderly, widows and people living with HIV.
In particular, timely intervention for various disasters that have occurred in Cambodia, as well as in Phnom Penh, such as fires, hurricanes, droughts, riverbanks and traffic accidents, etc., in line with the slogan "Where there is suffering Difficulty there is the mission of the Cambodian Red Cross.
This is the third time that the Capital Red Cross Branch, Mr. Khuong Sreng, has brought the Red Cross donations to the people here to alleviate their hardships. This activity shows the efforts of the authorities at all levels to solve the difficulties of the people who are in need.
Mr. Khuong Sreng stated that the Red Cross is an organization that does not receive funding from the Royal Government or any other organization, but from philanthropists who have donated their resources to support humanitarian activities regardless of party affiliation, political affiliation or religion. The important thing is that where there are difficulties, there is always the Red Cross.
