Top Global Researchers Share Experiences on Genocide Prevention
(Phnom Penh): Nearly 500 senior researchers from around the world have gathered in Phnom Penh to share their research and work experience on "reconsideration of genocide prevention".
The genocide in Cambodia is one of the many topics of genocide to be discussed, such as in Sierra Leone, Rwanda.
This year, as Cambodia is chosen as the venue for the International Conference on the Prevention of Genocide, it marks the 40th anniversary of the fall of the Khmer Rouge regime, which massacred more than 3 million Cambodians during Of their rule from 1975 to 1979.
"In the past, Cambodia has become an important lesson to share with the world about post-genocide recovery, and we want to engage in a global dialogue on preventing this terrible crisis," he added. "
The recent sentencing of former Khmer Rouge leaders by the Khmer Rouge tribunal is a significant contribution to the global commitment to curbing genocide and other atrocities.
The four-day conference, July 14-17, 2019, will be held at AUPP University, the only educational institution in Cambodia to offer a degree accredited by a partner American university.
Fifty Cambodian senior researchers are ready to present their research and share their experiences with all international senior researchers.
