(Phnom Penh): From now on, the competent force of the Ministry of Interior will cooperate with relevant institutions to inspect and take strict legal action against any restaurant or restaurant that does not have food hygiene standards for citizens and tourists by implementing First in Phnom Penh and continue to work across the country. This is according to Lt. Gen. Chea Bunthol, Deputy Director of the Judicial Police Department of the Ministry of Interior.
The warning was made by Lt. Gen. Chea Bunthol at the opening ceremony of the Food Hygiene Training on July 13, 2019, with the participation of Mr. Ley Sopheap, Executive Director of the Federation of Cambodian Investors and Mr. Ngy Mean Heng, Director of Phnom Penh Health Department.
On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Chea Bunthol said that from now on, the authorities will take strict legal action against any restaurant or restaurant that does not have food hygiene standards, because the lack of hygiene standards will affect the health of the people. Causes various invisible diseases, especially can affect life.
"From now on, if the joint forces inspect the food, it will be unsafe and unhygienic, they will have strict measures," he said.
The Lt. Gen. appealed to all restaurant owners to participate in food hygiene training for everyone to raise awareness about hygiene and to implement it well for the benefit of the nation and its people. All together.
Mr. Ngy Mean Heng said that food hygiene is an important issue related to public health. On the other hand, food hygiene knowledge, if you have a lot of understanding, is not useless because it can help protect the health of your family.
The director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Health Department confirmed that chronic illness caused by food poisoning has two points: immediate food poisoning and chronic food poisoning.
At the same time, Dr. Ley Sopheap said that food safety and hygiene is an important thing that can not be missed if one day there is a slight mistake can lead to harm to life or may occur. Chronic diseases as well. He also called on restaurant owners, cafeterias and food and beverage service providers to pay close attention to food hygiene issues.
