Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh Recommends 9 Points to the Gendarmerie to Prevent Challenges (Video inside) (Tbong Khmum): Speaking from Tbong Khmum Province at the Commemoration of the 26th Anniversary of the Establishment of the Gendarmerie Institution Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Defense, recommended nine key points as a vision and prevent the challenges of the military police.
The recommendations of Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh given in the ceremony on the morning of July 14, 2019 include:
* Second, care must be taken to continue to deepen the reform, including the structure, roles, duties, human resource development, capacity building, improve the quality of work responsibly, in response to the needs of the army. The Royal Gendarmerie to be effective.
* Third: Continue to strive to improve the efficiency and quality of public services, because it is the main mission to improve the lives of the people. To transform the Royal Gendarmerie into a force that provides effective services, to serve the people better, with the spirit of service, sharpness, loyalty, service providers, respect and professional ethics.
* Fourth: To strengthen the work of building strength effectively by purifying the newly recruited components and eliminating those who do not comply with professional regulations, and to manage the existing force to ensure that the work is assigned, even if the number is not yet. Sufficient quantities as needed.
* Sixth, to maintain the existing construction and pay attention to the construction of the Tbong Khmum Provincial Gendarmerie Command and in other provinces in a technical manner to ensure quality and long-term use. Continue to build the headquarters building that is being built in the provinces and has not been built and promote the construction of the actual shooting range of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to be ready in time to host the upcoming ASEAN Games.
* Seventh: Continue to strengthen forces to be the core of operations to maintain safety, security, public order, continue to participate in the suppression of all crimes, participate in humanitarian work, social work and disaster relief.
* Eighth: To strengthen the effective inspection mechanism in accordance with the roles and responsibilities assigned by the Royal Government as a force to provide legal authority with many advantages and to manage the work of public administration and take strict legal measures to prevent There is corruption or abuse of power by the public authorities against the people.
* 9th: Participate in drafting laws and regulations because the military is a direct servant to the people to get the reality of the daily life of the people and the desires of the people.
