(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Veng Sakhon, announced that he has decided to send specialized officers, including diagnostic equipment, to the swine flu outbreak area in order to diagnose swine fever as soon as possible. To sell pigs to the people.
Please be reminded that recently, after the outbreak of swine fever in Cambodia, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries issued a directive to temporarily suspend the raising, sale and transportation of pigs and raw products. Birth of all types of pigs in African swine fever outbreaks in order to prevent the spread of the disease to other areas.
Following such a decision, some pig farmers are concerned about measures to curb the pig trade in the area, making it impossible for their pigs to trade and affect their daily lives. .
After the concerns of such people, only on the afternoon of July 13, 2019, Mr. Veng Sakhon decided to introduce new measures by sending veterinary officers, including equipment for immediate analysis, inspection and sampling. Pig blood was analyzed at the site of the outbreak to detect the African swine fever virus.
Mr. Veng Sakhon called on pig farmers to remain calm, patient, understanding and provide better cooperation to the Ministry of Veterinary Officials in carrying out this task to achieve better results.
Currently, African swine fever has occurred in five provinces of Cambodia, including Ratanakkiri, Tbong Khmum, Svay Rieng, Takeo and Kandal. A total of more than 2,000 pigs have been killed and maimed by the African swine fever.
