Phnom Penh Governor and Mrs. Vesa Candle Parade to All 150 Pagodas in Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng and Ms. Chea Sina, accompanied by officials under the supervision of Phnom Penh Capital Hall and 14 district governors, brought gifts of candles, food and suffixes to the monks who remember the rain. 150 pagodas throughout Phnom Penh to support and make it easier for monks this rainy season.
The Rainy Day Parade was organized in a very generous and transparent manner in the temple of Wat Neak Voan, Sangkat Boeung Kak II, Khan Toul Kork on the afternoon of July 13, 2019 with the participation of Buddhist monks. A lot of people.
Mr. Khuong Sreng stated that the Phnom Penh Capital Administration organizes this Vesa Candle Parade to all pagodas throughout Phnom Penh every year in the traditional way of Buddhism.
Taking the opportunity, he said that under the leadership of the Royal Government, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has made the field of Buddhism and the empire grow together, especially the Buddhists have a prosperous life to participate in the construction of pagodas. Well developed.
He added that all these valuable achievements came from the efforts and sacrifices of all in the spirit of high responsibility, upholding the interests of the nation and the people of the Royal Government with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister.
He called on the people and all Buddhists to continue to support the Cambodian People's Party and participate in maintaining peace, stability and achievements of our nation for the people to live in peace.
In that, the Governor also gave gifts to 50 grandmothers, each receiving 20,000 Riels and a piece of white cloth, 95 students staying in the pagoda, 1 ton of rice and 20,000 Riels each.
Please note that the Vesa ceremony is an important festival in Buddhism, an important time for monks and nuns to learn the Dharma and discipline consistently according to the Buddha's teachings for 3 months starting from 01 Roach Khe Asat to the 15th day of the month of Assoch.
