(Tbong Khmum): Pig farmers in Ou Raing Ov district, Tbong Khmum province, expressed their happiness after the Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Veng Sakhon, issued an emergency rule in response to his request by sending officials and equipment. Diagnosing African swine fever paves the way for their pig trade.
Residents affected by African swine fever in Ou Raing Ov district, through Fresh News, thanked Veng Sakhon for introducing measures to address pig trade in Ou Raing Ov district.
With gratitude, local people in Ou Raing Ov also expressed confidence that Minister Veng Sakhon will send professional officers as well as equipment to their districts as soon as possible to check and diagnose African swine fever as soon as possible. The way they traded pigs quickly reduced losses.
In Ou Raing Ov district, Tbong Khmum province, there are about 848 families raising pigs. There are more than 9,000 pigs that raise both offspring and meat. To date, swine fever has killed many pigs. Apart from the deaths of their surviving pigs, they were not allowed to be sold because the ministry feared the pig trade in the area would spread to other areas.
The pig farmers have urged the ministry to take appropriate measures to sell the pigs to reduce losses.
On the afternoon of July 13, 2019, the Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Veng Sakhon, decided to send specialized officers, including diagnostic equipment, to the swine flu outbreak area in order to diagnose swine fever. Quickly facilitate the sale of pigs to the people.
The Minister stated that if the results of the analysis of pig blood samples did not show the presence of African swine fever, the Ministry would allow the sale of pigs from the African swine fever epidemic area to enable the people to earn income. In order to pay for the expenses that have been raised in the past.
