(Tbong Khmum): As the Vesa Festival is coming soon, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, and Lok Chumteav brought Preah Vossa candles and gifts to the monks at 12 pagodas. 8 pagodas are located in Ponhea Krek district, Tbong Khmum province, 2 pagodas in Kamchay Mea and Romeas Hek districts, Prey Veng province.
The ceremony of offering alms and giving alms was held according to the Buddhist path at Wat Kiri Sovannaram (called Wat Thkov), located in Anlong Chrey village, Kak commune, Ponhea Krek district, Tbong Khmum province, on the morning of Saturday, 12 Corrected on July 13, 2019.
The three-month Vesa festival will arrive on the 1st day of the month of Asat until the 15th day of the month of Assoch. Entering Preah Vossa is a precept that the Samma Samputa commanded for monks and apostles to practice by remembering Preah Vossa in the pagoda to study the Dharma Discipline and follow the Buddha's precepts.
In support of the monks, during these three months, the Buddhists always bring gifts such as rice, candles, incense, oil, saffron, chivor, skirts, sadak and other materials to the monks at the pagoda.
Every year, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, a Buddhist, brings alms and candles to the monks at the pagodas along the traditional path. Samdech said that because the country is peaceful, the organization of religious ceremonies, not only in Buddhism, has been very solemn and happy according to the beliefs of the people.
