Wellington: An international collaboration led by a group of New Zealand scientists has revealed for the first time the secrets of 500 species of fish that can be transgender. For decades. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Friday, July 12, 2019.
According to the new research, there are definitely some signs that affect the genes of these transgender fish. Observations of a species of blue-headed fish living in coral reefs in the Caribbean have yielded impressive results. The most powerful male blue-headed fish always protects its females, which are yellow in color. If the male dies then the largest female will be transformed into a male within 10 days.
The female changes its behavior in just a few minutes, and its color changes in a matter of hours. The female reproductive organs will turn into male reproductive organs and within 10 days they will be able to produce sperm.
"This research is important for understanding how genes are altered during the evolution of all animals, including humans, and to understand how the environment can affect the transgender process," the researchers said. Incredible like this.
