Speaking to Fresh News on the afternoon of July 12, 2019, Mr. Bun Barang stated that "Cambodia will be short of salt supply of about 50,000 tons because currently produced only 30,000 tons of salt, which 30,000 tons can not Supply on the market. "But the 50,000 tonnes are not sure to be imported at all, depending on the actual situation, just that 50,000 tonnes of salt is lacking in supply."
He added that the community does not know exactly how to import until the decision of the board can only be imported if not decided on the community can not import.
"The problem that makes salt still unproductive is because the weather in Kampot province has a lot of rain. If you think about the past three years, the weather is not favorable, that is, the rain does not stop, so the salt production is not and required. "To have imports to supply the market."
He added that the import of salt from China does not affect the production of domestic salt, because this import, we compare, considering in advance how much salt is not enough to import. When the Cambodian salt is produced, we will suspend the import, just to confirm that the shortage of salt is 50,000 tons, with 100,000 tons of salt needed per year to supply the market.
He said that the community does not affect the salt production of farmers, as the import of salt is just a supplement.
He has stated that importing salt from abroad is not a good option for Cambodia, as the ministry is working hard to reduce its dependence on the climate on salt production.
Please note that this is the third year that Cambodia faces a shortage of salt, in 2008 Cambodia experienced this problem once. In particular, in 2016, Cambodia produced 140,000 tons of salt, which is more than the demand.
In general, the supply is only 100,000 tons, but for 2017-2018, salt production decreased due to climatic factors, and this year, Cambodia continues to lack salt and must import salt from other countries.
