ACLEDA-Jardin Foundation for Education Provides a New School Building for Students and Teachers in Pong Commune, Chong Kal District, Oddar Meanchey Province
The new school building was officially inaugurated on the morning of July 12, 2019 in the presence of Deputy Governor of Oddar Meanchey Khin Nhean, Dr. In Channy, President and CEO of ACLEDA Bank Plc. And the Board of Directors. ACLEDA-Jardin Foundation for Education and other relevant local authorities.
Peter Benin, Founder and Vice Chairman of the Board of Trustees of the organization, said that the school building will provide a permanent education that will increase the number of children enrolled in basic education at at least 200 in Kok Sangke Primary School. People.
He hopes that this school building, in addition to providing education to the children and students of the people in this area, it will also help build and expand the quality of life for parents and students in this community have better human resources. Caring and social sustainability.
According to Dr. In Channy, the ACLEDA-Jardin Foundation for Education was established by connecting the two companies and working together to help children have equal access to basic education. He said that this organization operates with the consent of the authorities in the field of special education, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, which in the first stage is to build school buildings.
The scope of this organization's humanitarian activities extends to the whole of Cambodia, but the first step is to focus on remote, impoverished areas in the provinces of Oddar Meanchey, Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri and Preah Vihear. The organization also plans to support and build school buildings in several primary schools each year in areas within its target geography, according to the fund's resources.
According to Dr. In Channy, ACLEDA-Jardin Foundation for Education has been supporting and constructing two primary school buildings in accordance with the plan of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, one in Oddar Meanchey province, which is now inaugurated. The other has five rooms with toilets in Ratanakiri that can accommodate more than 100 students.
Mr. Khin Nhean expressed his deep gratitude to ACLEDA-Jardin Foundation for supporting the education and construction of a school building at Kork Sangke Primary School with 5 classrooms and toilets, as well as adequate school facilities and toilet facilities. 2 rooms for students in Chongkal district, comfortable for this generation and the next generation to study for their better future.
Mr. Khin Nhean also considered the ACLEDA-Jardin Foundation's humanitarian activities for education as a confirmation of its active contribution to humanitarian work and human resource development, which is the most valuable asset in the development of the society. The Royal Government's rectangular strategy, especially the education quality reform strategy of the Ministry of Education.
