(Koh Kong): CamControl Branch, Koh Kong Province, on July 12, 2019, cooperated with the Trade Officer of the Municipal Authority to inspect all the goods that the vendors put up for sale in the houses and at the markets in the Royal City of Khemarak Phoumin, Koh Kong Province. Focus on goods, beverages, cakes, pastries that are past the date of manufacture.
Mr. Sam Chentra, Deputy Chief of CamControl Branch in Koh Kong Province, said that the operation was based on the Law on Quality Management, Safety of Products and Services and Trade Facilitation through Risk Management. General Exterior of food to labels, packaging, dates, cans, rotten cans.
He said that the quality and compliance check by conducting a preliminary analysis of the product using a test kit to find banned chemicals such as porcine and formalin, etc. In case of doubt, the sample should be sent to the laboratory of the General. Camcontrol to identify risks as well.
He added that as a result, CamControl officers inspected the goods, drinks, foodstuffs of the vendors in the houses and markets in the Royal City of Cambodia and found some pastries, expired food and confiscated. Take it to the office and wait for it to be burned.
During the inspection, the vendors were educated to know how to look at all items before selling them, and if any items are about to expire, do not buy or sell them, it may affect the health of buyers. Take to eat.
He appealed to all importers to import only those products that are highly compliant, free of chemicals and have the correct packaging, have a specific date to contribute to the protection of the interests of consumers, both health and economy, and CamControl officials. Advertise to traders in the market and at home to explain the features before buying to use or eat.
