Finally, Kim Jong Un must be nominated as the head of state to compete with the world's top leaders
The new constitution, which was amended at a plenary session of North Korea's Supreme People's Assembly in April, stipulates that Kim Jong Un, chairman of the State Committee, has the same role as the "supreme leader." Namely, representing North Korea as the head of state. The role of North Korean head of state before the constitutional amendment was that of the chairman of North Korea's Supreme People's Assembly, Choe Ryong Hae.
According to North Korean media, the removal of Kim Jong Un as head of state could help North Korea restore diplomatic relations with other countries. In addition, the appointment will give Kim an equal role in summits with other leaders, such as US President Donald Trump, Chinese President Xi Jinping or Russian President Vladimir Putin. .
