Phay Siphan, the minister accompanying the prime minister and spokesman for the government, said the draft law had been approved without amendment.
He added that the draft law on "consumer protection" will complement the relevant laws and regulations on consumer protection, including the Civil Code.
The draft law on "consumer protection" will provide protection for consumers' interests from traders and unfair practices in commercial activities. The law also protects the rights and interests of consumers, supporting a competitive market for both price and quality of goods and services.
According to Phay Siphan, the law applies to individuals who do business, whether for-profit or non-profit, including the sale of goods or services or real estate rights to consumers in Cambodia. Unless there are separate provisions stating otherwise.
This draft law is also reviewed by the expert representatives of the Ministry of Justice on the articles in each chapter, especially Chapter 7, Chapter 8, Chapter 9, Chapter 10, related to procedures and provisions to ensure consistency with other applicable laws of the Ministry of Justice. Kingdom of Cambodia.
Today, many countries around the world, including nine ASEAN countries, are implementing consumer protection laws. This draft law is designed not only to protect consumers from fraud and misconduct. It also stipulates the information to be provided to consumers and allows regulators to prepare regulations on information standards that traders must comply with.
