What do the Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan focus on?
(Siem Reap): The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to establish an inter-ministerial commission to prepare a master plan for the development of tourism in Siem Reap, with the Ministry of Tourism as the leading body and composed of relevant ministries, institutions, authorities, Siem Reap Provincial Administration, partners and the world. Toulouse High School in France, which specializes in academic planning.
The inter-ministerial committee has been studying some areas gradually, but in order to be a beacon for the successful planning of the master plan, the Ministry of Tourism has organized the first consultative workshop on the organization. Siem Reap Tourism Master Plan at Sokhalay Angkor Hotel, closed on July 11, 2019.
In this workshop, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, outlined some basic approaches and recommendations by Fresh News already mentioned in the previous article, and for this article, we will highlight the main points in Study that master plan.
According to Minister Thong Khon, the study process on the Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan focuses on work in the province, in the country and abroad, including:
* First: Study on creating new tourism products beyond what is already in the Angkor Wat area to attract tourists to visit and stay in Siem Reap for a long time and cost.
* Second: Study on the development and expansion of infrastructure systems such as the construction of expressways, high-speed railways, road widening, construction of a new, larger international airport to connect Siem Reap with Phnom Penh, Siem Reap with the coast. The sea of Siem Reap with the northeast, Siem Reap with the border as well as Siem Reap with the international.
* Third: Study on the organization and management of clean and green environment in Siem Reap and Angkor to provide freshness to tourists who visit Siem Reap, promote the promotion of good points from the province. Siem Reap is like Cambodia. In addition, there are studies on waste management, waste, decoration, aesthetics in the province and the area, study on gardening and so on.
* Fourth: Study on the decoration of the road to be beautiful.
* Fifth: Study the mechanism of management of this famous tourist site to improve, because without management, the study will be empty.
Apart from this, there are also studies on foreign factors such as tourism market study, tourist trends, market growth, market demand, study on tourist facilitation.
Of course, Angkor is now famous all over the world, but Cambodia needs to be further developed, that is, apply conservation in the Angkor area and further development in the surrounding area in a sustainable and responsible manner. To affect the heritage of ancestors, such as temples, culture, traditions and customs of the people.
The minister said that the study project on the master plan will be completed and implemented from the beginning of 2020 until 2035.
"These efforts are also in line with Cambodia's vision to receive about 10 million international tourists by 2025 and about 15 million by 2030," Thong Khon said. The owner of "Lim Phorn Pure Water" enterprise in Kampong Thom province claims that his business is legal and decided to sue the officials for arbitrary crackdown in court
