Kandal Governor Inspects and Inquiries of Pig Farmers Affected by African Swine Fever in Their Backyards
(Kandal): Following the outbreak of African swine fever in Kraing Yov commune, Saang district, Kandal province, on July 11, 2019, Dr. Mao Phirun, Governor of Kandal Province, led a team to visit people who are raising pigs. Infected with African swine fever in the backyard and advised people to be careful when buying pork to eat.
It should be noted that as of 11 a.m. on July 11, 2019, an African swine fever outbreak occurred in Kraing Yov commune, Saang district, Kandal province, killing more than 500 pigs.
Experts say the outbreak was caused by a pig trader who had contracted African swine fever from neighboring countries into the Cambodian market, and consumers bought meat to eat and transmitted the disease to his pigs at home. Infected, the disease dies one after another.
After the outbreak of African swine fever, Dr. Mao Phirun visited and visited the people who own the affected pigs to the location or back of the house. These days, Mr. Nhim Vandin, the governor of Saang district, and the professional officers of the relevant departments around Kandal Provincial Hall have sprayed pesticides and prevented germs in some pig farms.
