Phay Siphan, the minister accompanying the prime minister and spokesman for the government, said the draft national strategy had been approved without amendment.
Mr. Phay Siphan said that the draft National Strategic Law on "Financial Environment 2019-2025" was prepared in accordance with the vision of the "Rectangular Strategy" Phase 4 of the Royal Government, which gives priority to the development policy. Sectors will identify practical measures as a priority in order to promote economic growth and social development.
This draft National Strategy is a national policy framework based on the Financial Sector Development Strategy 2016-2025, which has a comprehensive and clear action plan and supports effective implementation to achieve an existing financial system. Stability, efficiency and diversification of environmentally friendly financial markets.
Focusing on expanding the financial environment is a global trend not only in Cambodia, but many countries in the world and major international institutions are also prioritizing this agenda. An efficient and effective financial sector provides the potential to improve people's livelihoods, boost economic activity and improve social benefits and private sector innovation.
The "National Strategy for the Financial Environment 2019-2025" is expected to contribute to the financial environment through the development of financial services strategies and business models that provide better value to low-income people and contribute to economic growth. And social welfare, as well as promoting closer cooperation between all stakeholders, including development partners and the private sector.
Mr. Phay Siphan emphasized that the approval of the draft "National Strategy for the Financial Environment 2019-2025" is also to meet the financing requirements with the Asian Development Bank.
