Minister Thong Khon makes important recommendations to be a beacon in studying the master plan for tourism development in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, provided a number of key approaches and recommendations to be a beacon in the study of Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan, especially for the smooth planning and implementation of this master plan. Succeeded.
On that occasion, Minister Thong Khon said that the master plan is strategically important to support the development of Cambodia's tourism sector, especially to support the achievement of the vision of receiving 11 million tourists in 2025, 15 million people. In 2030 and 20 million in 2035, of which nearly 50% will visit Siem Reap because Siem Reap is Cambodia's main tourist destination.
He said that Siem Reap needs to strengthen its qualifications to seize the opportunities available in the international market and be ready for new challenges such as the slowdown in global economic growth caused by trade wars. Of superpowers.
Therefore, this master plan should be prepared based on two basic approaches, including:
First, sustainable management of both tangible and intangible heritage assets with superior values.
Second, responsible development and environment that takes into account the economic and social benefits for local people. Therefore, all the topics discussed yesterday are intertwined. Requires the participation, thinking, implementation and responsibility of all stakeholders.
In order for the master plan to run smoothly and successfully, Minister Thong Khon outlined the following key recommendations:
First, request the institution and all stakeholders to continue to provide information to the Secretariat and experts as requested, as well as to provide advice as needed so that international experts can study, understand and analyze in all aspects.
Second, call for the participation of the private sector to revive, because successful development is absolutely necessary to cooperate with the private sector, which is a direct service provider and a guest to Siem Reap.
Third, although the master plan has a long-term vision until 2035, some strategic plans and plans need to be implemented soon to respond to the current situation. Therefore, both experts and stakeholders must consider together to decide on this master plan as a plan that can be implemented in stages after receiving approval from the Royal Government in February 2020.
Sixth, consider diversifying tourism products by continuing to organize Phnom Kulen National Park and Tonle Sap area as ecotourism destinations, organizing tourism, food, rural tourism and agro-tourism connected to the temple area, so consider Zoning Areas developed by type of tourism product.
According to Mr. Nep Samuth, Director General of Tourism Industry at the Ministry of Tourism, the study on the master plan will be completed in stages and will be completed by early 2020. It will be implemented from 2020-2035 and there will be further study, preparation and implementation.
ABA Obtained Permission to List Bonds on the Cambodia Securities Exchange
Speaking at a recent seminar, Mr. Hong So Hour, General Director of the Cambodia Securities Exchange, stated that “The Cambodia Securities Exchange has just decided to grant permission to register the sale of corporate bonds of Vattanac Asia Bank Limited (Bank). "ABA) Therefore, soon investors who are interested in ABA Bank bonds will be able to register to buy bonds in the IPO phase."
Mr. Sou Socheat, Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, considered the entry of ABA Bank into the stock market as a positive sign of the securities market that the company can get more capital to expand its business operations rather than seek foreign funding.
He added that at the end of July, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia will have a meeting to decide on the entry of ABA securities market, and ABA is expected to open trading in mid-August 2019.
Please be informed that the Cambodia Securities Exchange has been operating for about 7 years and this market is constantly evolving. There are currently a total of seven listed companies, five of which are listed on the Cambodia Securities Exchange, while the other two are listed on corporate bonds.
It should be reminded that ABA Bank, a member of the National Bank of Canada, in early June 2019 received approval from the National Bank of Cambodia to organize the issuance of its corporate bonds (CSX) on the Cambodia Securities Exchange (CSX). It plans to issue 100 billion riel worth of bonds, equivalent to about $ 25 million.
