Cambodia Securities Exchange organizes first investment seminar for Chinese investors in Cambodia and launches Chinese language on mobile trading system
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodia Securities Exchange (CSX) in collaboration with the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and the General Department of Immigration has organized the first investment seminar for Chinese investors in Cambodia under the theme "Opportunity". Of Securities Investment in Cambodia "on July 9, 2019 at the Cambodia Securities Exchange.
The seminar attracted a large number of Chinese people, most of whom were entrepreneurs, senior executives of companies and investors.
Based on the success of previous seminars abroad, especially in Shenzhen, China in April, which attracted a lot of interest from Chinese investors on the Cambodia Securities Exchange, it also organized this local seminar. For potential Chinese investors who are in Cambodia to learn more about securities investment opportunities in Cambodia.
During the workshop, the speakers presented the mission and development strategy of the Stock Exchange of Cambodia, as well as provided investors with important information, including the types of investment products available in the market, information about listed companies, laws and regulations for trading. Tax and non-tax incentives, conditions and procedures for the initial public offering and guidelines for listing on the CSX.
During the workshop, the CSX also announced the launch of a new Chinese language function on the existing MTS mobile trading system in addition to the existing Khmer and English languages to facilitate Chinese investors in Using the MTS system. In addition, the workshop also provided a venue for participants and securities firms to meet and discuss securities procurement procedures and securities brokerage services.
