5: Draft Law on the Approval of the National Strategic Development Plan 2019-2023.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra: Youth Forum on Environment 2019 as a mechanism to train more human resources
(Phnom Penh): Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment, Mr. Neth Pheaktra, said that the Youth Forum on Environment 2019 will be a mechanism to cultivate human resources among young people in addition to disseminating and mainstreaming environmental awareness among the public.
Mr. Net Pheaktra made this statement on July 11, 2019, when he opened the "Youth Forum on Environmental Dialogue 2019" with the participation of female candidates. From 16 high schools in Phnom Penh to educate the public about the environment and natural resources.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that this is the 39th time that the Ministry of Environment has organized a youth forum to discuss this environment, and this year the Ministry of Environment, with the Department of Environmental Education of the General Department of Environmental Knowledge and Information as the facilitator. This forum is for undergraduate students, while in the past this forum was only attended by young people from universities or higher education institutions.
In this regard, the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment has directed the candidates to study environmental issues in connection with recent developments in the world, especially the Fourth Industrial Revolution, as well as in connection with technological and scientific discoveries.
The Secretary of State stated that the young people participating in the 2019 Environmental Forum will strive to study and gain knowledge, not only to compete for victory, but also to explain to the public about environmental protection. Managing natural resources, biodiversity conservation and sustainable development, especially contributing to changing human habits and attitudes for environmental and natural resource causes.
At the same time, Mr. Neth Pheaktra thanked the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports for providing good cooperation with the Ministry of Environment in the framework of human resource training, saying: "The Ministry of Environment has worked closely with the Ministry of Education and Youth. "And sports work together for a common purpose: human resources for the environment, the environment for human resources."
