(Tbong Khmum): Pigs in Ou Raing Ov district affected by swine fever die every day, causing great concern to pig owners, as remedial measures are still seen as slow. .
On July 10, 2019, in Soy village, Mean commune, Ou Raing Ov district, Tbong Khmum province, protests erupted for the intervention of the relevant authorities and officials. The villagers who raised pigs affected by swine fever have asked to sell live pigs and provide financial support for dead pigs.
Protesters added that if they were not allowed to sell their pigs, there would be no bank debt.
In Ou Raing Ov district, Tbong Khmum province, there are about 848 families raising pigs. There are more than 9,000 pigs that raise both offspring and meat. To date, swine fever has killed 337 pigs and left 67 sick.
Residents have expressed concern that they will suffer even more if no effective and timely solution is found, as they see that the authorities' response measures and relevant officials have not yet responded.
