(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ngy Mean Heng, Director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Health Department, appealed to people all over the country that if there is a high fever, do not take heat medicine, please hurry to the public hospital and health center immediately to avoid Danger to life by dengue fever.
This statement by Dr. Ngy Mean Heng on the occasion of inviting drug dealers in pharmacies to participate in a meeting to promote the prevention of dengue fever on the afternoon of July 10, 2019 at the Health Department in Phnom Penh.
Dr. Ngy Mean Heng also continued, "In order to participate in protecting the health and life of our people, we would like to join all vigilance in this cycle of dengue outbreaks, especially in the rainy season. "Up to 40 degrees and more than 2 days, please bring your child to the hospital immediately, especially to government hospitals and health centers that our doctors are ready to rescue."
In addition, the director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Department stated, "It is strictly forbidden to buy medicine at a pharmacy or to a private clinic that does not specialize in treating dengue fever." "Pharmacists in all pharmacies do not sell drugs to him and help tell buyers to consult with doctors at public hospitals and health centers to help protect the lives of our citizens."
