(Phnom Penh): The spokesperson of the Royal Government, led by Mr. Phay Siphan, this morning, Thursday, July 11, 2019, held a press conference on "Swine Plague Outbreak". The purpose of this conference is to explain the concerns of the people who are focusing on swine flu with the actions and measures of the Royal Government to control the situation and prevent the spread of the disease.
The conference will cover the general situation of swine fever in Cambodia, its impact in the past, as well as measures to prevent and control the spread of the disease. Speakers who will be invited are: 1: Representative of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries 2: Representative of the Ministry of Health
Please note that African swine fever has continued to spread and erupt in two more provinces of Cambodia, Svay Rieng and Takeo. So far, four provinces in Cambodia have had outbreaks of this deadly African swine fever: Ratanakkiri, Tbong Khmum, Svay Rieng and Takeo.
African swine fever is not contagious to humans, but it is a deadly disease that spreads from region to region, causing up to 100% disease and death in pigs, which can cause great harm to you. Raise pigs.
The outbreak of African swine fever has raised concerns as reports of 183 dead pigs spread from Mean commune to Ampil Tapok commune, with 58 dead pigs in Preah commune. The item contains 62 dead pigs. The other four communes of this district also have dead pigs.
Forty-six families have asked the relevant authorities to help solve the problems that people are experiencing as soon as possible and said that the outbreak is not serious because it has killed many of their pigs. Head and have already lost a lot of money.
During the outbreak of African swine fever, the Ou Raing Ov District Assistance Team, led by Mr. Eang Sophalleth and the team, in collaboration with agricultural officials, educated the people and introduced measures to prevent and prevent the spread of African swine fever. The disease aims to eradicate local viruses to resume business.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth informed the farmers that the active response, both professionally and as a team, is motivated by being a member of the same family who is always in harmony with the community. Our nation. Consideration of public health: is an important factor that is the main issue and priority.
He also informed the pig farmers that the movement of pigs from this area could cause an epidemic, leading to a series of losses in other areas. At the same time, he urged experts to continue to monitor and recommend measures to prevent and prevent the spread of the disease in order to eliminate local viruses to resume business.
Responding to the concerns of pig farmers, he called for better cooperation in veterinary measures to control the disease throughout the commune and to participate in the implementation of measures as instructed by experts and immediately report cases of sick animals and Died to make sure the area announces the eradication of the disease.
He emphasized that business people should pay attention to solve problems for the common good and think collectively as the main factor.
