Do the crimes and activities that affect the security and order by the Chinese in Cambodia reach an uncontrollable level, as the concerns of the Cambodian people?
In an interview with Fresh News, General Kirth Chantharith, Director General of the General Department of Immigration of the Ministry of Interior, said that about 250,000 Chinese in Cambodia are currently staying long-term to invest and work. Other.
Compared to other foreigners, about 60 percent of Chinese are staying in Cambodia. Of the 250,000, nearly 100,000 are in Phnom Penh and more than 110,000 in Sihanoukville. In addition, in Kandal, Svay Rieng and Banteay Meanchey.
General Kirth Chantharith acknowledged that the Chinese nationals living in Cambodia were indeed hiding, engaging in illegal activities and undermining security and order in Cambodia. But compared to all the Chinese in Cambodia, the number of perpetrators and activities that affect the security and order is small.
"It simply came to our notice then. But the number is not large compared to the Chinese presence, which compares with the presence of 2 million Chinese tourists, the number of crimes committed by the Chinese will not be much. "Compared to the number of common crimes, as far as I know from the data we have from the National Police, compared to the Chinese crime is not much." Mr. Kirth Chantharith emphasized.
The Director General of the General Department of Immigration added, "I would like to note this issue. Naturally, no matter how many races there are, there is never any good or pure, even in our family in any community, there are always bad people and bad people. Thus, the Chinese who came to stay temporarily in our country more than 200,000 people can not be good at all. "But I just assess that most of the criminal activities he commits are with his own people."
Mr. Kirth Chantharith also said that crimes committed by Chinese people do not affect the Cambodian people, and most of those crimes are related to mutual debt, which is a daily business. Of them and drinking problems.
Responding to concerns that Chinese crime and insecurity are out of control, General Kirth Chantharith asserted that there was nothing to worry about, that the Cambodian authorities were competent enough to control it. All these problems, and if there is a crime, the Cambodian authorities must crack down, there is no exception.
General Kirth Chantharith also outlined a number of measures to prevent Chinese crimes. He claimed that the Ministry of Interior has close cooperation with China's Ministry of Public Security, and every year the Ministry plans to take action to prevent and crack down on these crimes.
According to Mr. Kirth Chantharith, under the cooperation between the Ministry of Interior of Cambodia and the Ministry of Security of China, as well as the tightening of law enforcement in Cambodia, the crime and actions affect the security of public order. China in Cambodia is also declining.
Mr. Kirth Chantharith said that in 2018, Cambodia deported more than 900 Chinese people back to their countries of origin. But for the first five months of 2019, only 165 Chinese were deported from Cambodia. The general also said that in the last two to three years, Cambodia has expelled about 2,000 Chinese from Cambodia. Have to say no to drugs! Nationwide anti-drug campaign July 10: 30 cases cracked, 65 arrested
