(Takeo): Mr. Tan Sophannara, Delegate of the Royal Government of Cambodia in charge of the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and relevant authorities in Takeo Province this morning, July 10, 2019, visited the outbreak area. African pig farm in Ampil village, Ponley commune, Angkor Borey district, Takeo province.
Speaking at the ceremony, Mr. Tan Sophannara said that in the area that came to declare an outbreak of African swine fever, all traffic in pigs was banned, as well as the movement of pigs from this area. A 10-kilometer radius to other areas avoids the spread of African swine fever to other areas.
