(Siem Reap): The Minister of Tourism of Cambodia, Mr. Thong Khon, requested all ASEAN member countries to make efforts to develop new tourism products and expand as many direct flights as possible to attract more tourists. As well as to address some of the challenges.
This call is no different from what this busy minister always urges all stakeholders in Cambodia to participate in promoting cooperation in the development of national tourism, he always encourages the development of new tourism products. And attracts direct flight connections from destination countries often.
At the opening ceremony of the ASEAN NTOs, Minister Thong Khon highlighted a number of challenges that ASEAN member countries need to work together to address, including the promotion of intra-ASEAN tourism. Achieve an average growth rate of 4% per year and encourage tourists to travel on their own, especially cross-border travel.
Because ASEAN is rich in natural resources, intangible culture, which is conducive to the development of tourism in the region to become a unique product and provide exciting memories to tourists, so Mr. Thong Khon urged. Water to ASEAN member countries need to create more new tourism products to attract more and more tourists.
The Cambodian Minister of Tourism also thanked the Philippines and Indonesia for connecting direct flights to Cambodia, which contributed to boosting the flow of tourists from each other.
According to the report, throughout 2018, the whole ASEAN region received about 135 million tourists, an increase of 7.6%.
According to Mr. Try Chhiv, Director of the Department of International and ASEAN Cooperation of the Ministry of Tourism, the ASEAN NTOs focus on tourism development in the ASEAN region, including reviewing the work implemented since 2016 and setting work directions. By 2025.
In addition, there is the promotion of cooperation within the framework of ASEAN and development projects that contribute to the development of the entire ASEAN region, as well as the tourism sector in Cambodia through the exchange of experience and the implementation of ASEAN quality standards, including the training of human resources in accordance with the program. ASEAN standard training.
July 10 is the day of remembrance of the inclusion of the temples of Preah Vihear and Sambor Prei Kuk in Cambodia as a World Heritage Site (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): July 10, 2019 is the day of remembrance of the inclusion of the temples of Preah Vihear and Sambor Prei Kuk in Cambodia The temples of Preah Vihear and Sambor Prei Kuk in Cambodia are World Heritage Sites, which the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, officially announces today every year.
Today marks the 11th and 2nd anniversary of the inclusion of the Temple of Preah Vihear and the Sambor Prei Kuk site in the World Heritage List.
The Cambodian Temple of Preah Vihear was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List at the 32nd Session of the United Nations General Assembly in Quebec City, Canada on July 7, 2008.
Sambor Prei Kuk was inscribed on the World Heritage List at the 41st Summit of the World Heritage Committee, held on July 2-12, 2017, with 193 member countries and 21 standing committees. Decided to include "Sambor Prei Kuk Temple" as a World Heritage Site at 9:40 pm (Cambodian time) on July 8, 2017 in Cracovie, Poland.
* History of Sambor Prei Kuk
