Chipmung Industries Receives 50 Civil Engineering Students
(Phnom Penh): Chip Mong Industries has received 50 students studying civil construction at Paragon University to visit the Chip Mong Ready-Mixed Concrete Plant and learn about the latest technology from Italy and the use of objects. Excellent quality raw materials in factory production.
Lim Meng Heang, a second-year civil engineering student at Paragon University, said after visiting the factory that the students came to see the factory of Chip Mong Industries to see first-hand the concrete mixing process. Accurate to the standard as well as the production line of the whole factory.
The second-year student stated, "Watching live concrete production is very important because at school we only learned the theory, but here we have seen it." In addition, students know, know and see the management structure in the factory and working life in the construction sector.
Kob Phalla, president of the concrete plant and laboratory manager of Chip Mong Industries, said the purpose of the paragon's civil engineering students at the concrete plant was to demonstrate the company's technology, technology and production chain. Factory.
"We demonstrate standard technology and factory order, student products from pre-production, post-production and post-production processes such as stone testing, sand testing, cement and concrete mixing," he said.
