(Phnom Penh): The bail application of the accused Hem Vann Soeun was rejected by the Court of Appeal in connection with the crime of falsifying public documents and encroaching on people's land in Kampong Tralach district, Kampong Chhnang province, while the Court of Appeal held a hearing this morning. This July 10, 2019.
It should be noted that the instigator accused in the case of forging public documents to encroach on the land of 34 families, known as Hem Vansoeun, resides at 10, Street 366, Sangkat Toul Svay Prey I, Khan Chamkarmon, a former land officer in Phnom Penh. A former adviser to the senior leadership, he was arrested on a warrant and is being held for questioning by a Phnom Penh Municipal Court judge.
Separately, the arrest of a woman named Yin Dara Phuong, according to the conviction of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court issued on July 23, 2015, which convicted Yin Dara Phuong, female, residing at No. 153E, Group 9, Khleang Saing Village, Sangkat Russey Keo, Khan Russey Keo, for forging public documents, committed in Leach village, Orussey commune, Kampong Tralach district, Kampong Chhnang province, sentenced to 5 years in prison.
Later, the landowners complained to the authorities to get their land back. Suddenly, Hem Vansoeun and Yin Dara Phuong came out and claimed that the land above belonged to them and had 26 hectares of legal title. Back.
At that time, Hem Vansoeun, an existing cadastral officer and one of the leading advisers in the National Assembly, used his skills and influence to intimidate the people and local officials to testify and prepare documents to mix the land. The above became its legal land by claiming to have bought it from Yin Dara Phuong, who inherited it from her husband, Silemeng, through a proper court ruling.
An acquaintance claimed that the mastermind in forging documents to encroach on 26 hectares of people's land, equivalent to 34 families, was named Hem Vansoeun. As for Yin Dara Phuong, he was just a conspirator for profit.
Now, when the authorities arrest Yin Dara Phuong, everything will be clear when Yin Dara Phuong gives an answer in court. Construction contractor and landlord in Banlung dispute over $ 90,000 debt, court to resolve on July 22
(Ratanakkiri): A construction contractor and the owner of an apartment in Banlung City, Ratanakkiri Province, had a dispute over a construction contract, with the contractor accusing the apartment owner of nearly $ 90,000, but the apartment owner replied that he could not. No breach of contract.
Due to the non-settlement, the construction contractor has applied to the court and on July 22, 2019, the court will resolve.
