Mr. Las Woody said that he and Mr. Taing Ny had a disagreement, that is, not paying nearly $ 90,000 in labor, leading him to lack money to pay workers and buy materials for construction needs.
He also asked for a protection order (suspension of construction), waiting for the apartment project owner to pay first. In relation to the above case, Mr. Mao Sary, the lawyer representing Mr. Taing Ny, also said that this was a civil matter, so each party argued.
(Phnom Penh): Major General Khov Ly, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Chhnang Province, ordered to investigate and crack down on fishing offenses in the conservation lot area at the point of wearing mats in the territory of Kampong Preah Koki commune, Boribo district, and called on the people and fishing community in The area cooperates to provide information.
