Is Iran refining uranium to build nuclear weapons or to negotiate with the United States? (Video inside) (Tehran): In response to US sanctions as well as European inactivity, Iran has decided to increase uranium enrichment to the 3.67 percent limit set under the 2015 Iran Nuclear Agreement.
On Monday, Iran refined its uranium to 4.5 percent and is considering increasing it to 20 percent. In addition, Tehran also refined 300 kilograms of low-enriched uranium last week.
Is Iran stepping up uranium enrichment to make nuclear weapons, or is it just trying to force Europe or the United States to return to the negotiating table?
What can Iran do with 20% uranium enrichment?
A 4.5 percent uranium enrichment is sufficient to meet Iran's energy needs. A spokesman for the Iranian Nuclear Agency added that Iran had previously had only one nuclear power plant in Bushehr and relied heavily on fuel imports from Russia.
Therefore, he understands that in the current situation, Iran just wants to tell Europe and the United States that if it is still forced or there is no solution, Tehran has no choice but to restart the old uranium enrichment reactor.
* European reaction
Britain and Germany have warned Iran to stop any activities that violate the nuclear deal, while French President Emmanuel Macron has agreed to hold talks with Iran, but also warned of the consequences if the city Tehran continues to enrich uranium.
In addition to refining uranium enrichment, Iran has warned Europe that it will reduce or cancel its commitments in the nuclear deal every 60 days if it fails to salvage the nuclear deal. The United States has withdrawn unilaterally and is imposing sanctions on Iran.
