National Bank of Cambodia and Central Bank of Korea jointly share experiences on interbank market development
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia and the Central Bank of Korea on July 9, 2019 organized a joint workshop on "Knowledge Partnership" to share experiences and research on the chair. Development of the interbank market in Cambodia.
Ms. Neav Chanthana thanked the Central Bank of Korea for providing an opportunity for the National Bank of Cambodia to share their experiences.
She said that this program is an important step forward and research of the National Bank on the development of the banking and financial sector of Cambodia.
She added that the topic to be explored this year is the development of the interbank market. The purpose of this research is to assess the current state of the interbank market in Cambodia and to find additional ways to develop and use liquidity in the banking system effectively.
Ms. Chea Serey also said that this is the fourth year that the National Bank and the Bank of Korea have cooperated, and from year to year, the two partner banks have discussed different topics. . For this year, both sides raised topics related to the development of the interbank market.
She added that in general, both sides study to find out what we should do to develop the interbank market in Cambodia to be more efficient and smoother. In the past, the National Bank of Cambodia has tried to develop the interbank market, but it has not improved, so the NBC wants to do more research to find out what else needs to be done to make this work. Smoothly.
She stated that the goals of this research are many, including wanting to find out about new tools that should be available, to find out and make sure that banking institutions enter the interbank market more than before, and that the study lasts for 4 months. Starting from today. Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign, July 9: More than 1,000 illegal vehicles found and more than 1,000 fined
