According to the report, 2,780 helmets and goggles were inspected on July 9, 195 education helmets and 399 glasses were fined.
APSARA Authority is repairing the dilapidated Tonle Snguot temple
So far, the temple structure and other structures of the temple have been severely damaged and now the APSARA Authority is in the process of repairing with a plan to repair about 2 years.
According to Chea Sarith, an archaeologist with the Department of Temple Preservation in Angkor Park and Preventive Archeology, who is in charge of the temple's restoration project, the Tonle Sap temple was severely damaged by two main factors: rain because the temple had no roof. Leading water into the foundation makes the foundation of the temple very weak and collapses.
On the other hand, the tree is the backbone of the temple and also the destroyer of the temple because it grows on the temple and takes root in the foundation, causing the stone of the temple structure to move out of its original condition, so that some of the stones slip and some of the tree roots. Pull apart.
Mr. Sarith said that due to the deteriorating situation, in 2005, the Apsara Authority worked around the temple to prevent collapse. It is not until 2019 that the team will be able to restore and restore the temple structure, as well as raise the value of the ancestral heritage, which is an important architecture of the hospital of Jayavarman VII to improve the appearance. Back.
As for the process of repairing the Tonle Snguot temple, the archaeologist claims that it is very difficult and complicated because the foundation of the temple made of laterite is completely damaged and can not support the stability of the temple made of sandstone.
Therefore, this work requires a long time, experts and clear techniques, divided into two stages:
First, dismantle all the temples from the top to the foundation and collect the stone, register the stone, number the stone, quote the plan of the temple and excavate 4 places to study the condition of the foundation before repairing.
The second is to reorganize according to the original technical standards, the original form, with a detailed study of the foundation, walls and roof, as well as to study the scattering of stones, collect, prepare, test and put back to the original location during the repair.
It should be noted that the temple or the dry river hospital in 2017 was excavated by archaeologists of the APSARA Authority, found a gate almost 2 meters high, Buddha statues, many statues, door pieces and living scars. Of many people in the past.
The temple has never been renovated before, only French experts came to clean and cut down the trees growing on the temple in 1930 and excavated the southeast corner and around the temple to remove the debris on the roof. Temple and collect the rocks that fall from the top, leave it in one place and compile only some documents.
