The owner of the car was arrested and taken to court by Battambang City Police.
(Battambang): Battambang police arrested a man to court this morning, July 9, 2019, after he drove a car and hit a victim, causing serious injuries after he was angry with The victim threw stones at the windshield of his car, causing it to explode. This incident happened on the night of July 7, 2019 at the point of Street 1 on the river in Kampong Krabei village, Sangkat Svay Por, Battambang city, Battambang province.
The inspector confirmed that before the incident, the victim was riding a motorbike, when he arrived at the scene, he threw stones at the suspect's car window, causing it to explode, so the suspect became very angry and drove the car, causing serious injuries. Once.
Currently, the car and motorbike of the victim were dragged by the Battambang City Police Force and kept at the Municipal Police Inspectorate, while the victim was taken to the provincial hospital. As for the perpetrators, the authorities have built a case and sent it to the provincial court for legal action. King urges local authorities to take care of wedding garden for newlyweds and plant trees as souvenirs
(Kratie): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, urges local authorities to take care of the wedding garden established by the Forestry Administration. Everyone in towns, districts, cities, communes, sangkats, villages, for newlyweds to get married and plant trees as a souvenir.
The King of Cambodia said this on the occasion of his presidency to celebrate the Royal "Tree Day" in Sre Treng village, Kbal Damrey commune, Sambo district, Kratie province this morning, July 9, 2019.
The King said, "Care should be taken to arrange for the newlyweds to plant a tree as a souvenir in the wedding garden established by the Forestry Administration for everyone in the town, district and city." Commune, commune, village.
During the Royal "Tree Day" ceremony, King Norodom Sihamoni also said that the Cambodian people really understand that forests are a great natural resource for human and animal life on our planet. Forests have contributed to maintaining natural balance and contributing to economic, social, cultural, tourism development, research, and protection of wetlands, biodiversity protection systems, and so on.
The king said that the loss of all kinds of forests could lead to floods, strong winds and lightning, and droughts, which have depleted water reserves for human and animal needs, leading to the loss of animal income. Forests, fish resources of all kinds and can cause desertification and deterioration of soil quality.
At the same time, His Majesty the King appealed to the monks, local authorities and compatriots all over the country to plant all kinds of trees to provide shade for human and animal habitats, construction trees to increase the fertility of agricultural land to reduce consumption. Natural wood also helps withstand wind force, contractions and climate change.
Sitting on a red copper urn, Chum Kosal, a metal sculptor in Po Touch village, Kampong Luong commune, described how he had been making metal sculptures since 1988, but in 1996 he was also a sculptor. Suspended for a while due to low income and he went to work.
The tall sculptor said that in the past, people did not like metal sculptures more than this flag, but now he observed that there are people who like to think carefully about the purchase order to use a lot.
The 45-year-old flag-maker said that being a metal sculptor, the flag-maker had to be patient and meticulous in order to achieve a satisfactory product.
According to Chum Kosal, the sale of this metal sculpture depends on the weight of the copper and the carving more or less on the metal products. The metal sculptures he used to make include pumpkins, pumpkins, wedding accessories, jewelry, jars, trophies, animal figures, utensils and more.
As both a sculptor and a sculptor, Chum Kosal said that for the fancy designs on the metal products, customers often prefer the Reamker storyline, the transport of wealth, the sea of milk, the royal chariot, the war of angels and giants. Or Khmer style flower arrangement.
Some of the metal products his family sells in his own house, some he sells to traders at Toul Tompong Market in Phnom Penh, and some to traders in Siem Reap until they buy wholesale. In Thailand, such as Long Klue Market. Family life is also more comfortable when the metal sculpture products are in demand from day to day.
Although the demand for metal sculptures has been constant, in Kampong Luong commune, there is a decrease in the number of sculptors due to the migration to work in Phnom Penh or in other provinces.
Mr. Chum Kosal said that in his metal sculpture, in addition to his siblings and children, he also has three children. The famous Cambodian metal sculptor was also hired by the Lao government to make a huge copper trophy for about three months, which is located at the Pakse roundabout in Champasak province.
As an apprentice from Kien Svay district, Mr. Meng Hak has been working as a metal sculptor for more than two years. For the past two years, he has not been able to carve on metal in the kiln, as he can only help with basic work.
Mr. Hak really loves and wants to continue to preserve this ancestral heritage because these products are the work of the people from the hands of the builders of Angkor. To support his family, Meng Hak thought that when he learned a lot of skills he could do on his own, he wanted to open a small craft in his hometown in combination with other occupations.
The owner of a metal sculpture shop and a metal sculptor in Kampong Luong commune also complained about the competition of this metal sculpture product with neighboring countries, as their products are made in large quantities and the price is lower than metal sculpture products. Khmer handicrafts are very far away, which is the reason for competition in the market.
Although Cambodian metal sculptures are not as expensive as those made in neighboring countries, Meng Hak, a young metal sculptor, called on the people to support the sculptures. Metal, which is a real Khmer work, to encourage more craftsmen to continue to preserve the heritage of this ancestor.
Mr. Chum Kosal appealed to the people as well as customers to increase the promotion of this ancient Khmer metal sculpture to revive, because not only help the family life of the sculptor to have the strength to continue this career. But it is also a continuation of the Khmer ancestral heritage, which leaves the next generation to continue to survive for a long time to come.
The King's Meditation, the most revered deed, took place this morning, July 9, 2019, on the occasion of His Majesty's celebration of the "Tree Day" ceremony in Sre Treng village, Kbal Damrey commune, Sambo district. Kratie.
Your Majesty, I would like to dedicate this plant day ceremony in the hearts of all our compatriots and become a tradition of unity, planting all kinds of trees together, preserving and protecting our precious forest resources and wildlife. To last forever.
It should be noted that the Tree Day was established during the Sangkum Reastr Niyum era under the royal wisdom and royal leadership of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk since the fifties, with the participation of the people throughout the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Tree Day is celebrated every year by the Royal Government to inspire people everywhere to participate in planting trees, protecting forests, flooding forests, and all kinds of biodiversity in the spirit of loving forests and natural resources, which is a valuable heritage, especially for sustainability. The lives of all of us, as well as the mammals on the planet and the glorious future of future generations.
