Germany continues to assist Cambodia in the field of textiles and garments for another 2 years through a memorandum between the Ministry of Labor and GIZ
(Phnom Penh): The German organization GIZ has agreed to continue to assist the Royal Government of Cambodia in the field of textiles and garments for another two years, valid from April 1, 2019 to March 31, 2021 through the signing of a memorandum. Memorandum of Understanding with the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on the Implementation of the Asia Textile and Garment Sustainability Project (GIZ, FABRIC) in Cambodia.
GIZ Country Director for Cambodia said that GIZ expressed its appreciation for the cooperation in providing assistance to make the project more successful.
Both sides expressed their appreciation for this cooperation and pledged to continue this work on the project to achieve success in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia as well as the strategic plan of the Ministry of Labor.
Please note that this memorandum will cost 6 million euros, which will be used for Bangladesh, Cambodia, China, Myanmar, Pakistan and Vietnam.
The purposes of this Memorandum include:
* Support public and private institutions to exchange information, dialogue and cooperation at the regional, national and enterprise levels to strengthen compliance with social and labor standards as enshrined in Cambodian labor law and international conventions provided by Cambodia. Ratify and improve gender equality in the workplace.
* Provide financial and technical support from GIZ, FABRIC project to the Ministry of Labor to strengthen the labor inspection system in Cambodia to be more capable, transparent, effective and gain the trust of all stakeholders.
