(Preah Sihanouk): Immediately after the complaint, the Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, ordered the professional officers of the local authority and relevant authorities to arrest the machinery that was clearing the land in Otres commune, Stung Hav district, Preah Sihanouk province. And allow the relevant parties to resolve the issue based on the documents they have.
The action by the provincial authorities came after more than 10 families in Village 5, Stung Hav district, accused a woman named Him Sovannary, also known as "Chumteav", by using a bulldozer to hit a fence. Boundaries and their land ownership on July 08, 2019.
Speaking to Fresh News, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun confirmed that after the incident, he ordered the district governor, police commissioner and military commander to send forces to intervene immediately to temporarily prevent the machine to solve the explosion. Violence happens by any means.
The provincial governor also told environmental and agricultural officials to visit the scene, whether the land is owned by the state or private to facilitate settlement together.
So far, however, both parties, both citizens and the accused women, have been required to bring their respective documents to the table for legal settlement as to who actually owns the property and who violated it. .
As of this morning, July 9, 2019, clearing activities have been temporarily suspended pending a settlement.
Residents Ly Sour and Khoy Ngov Kheng said they had been buying and occupying the 4 hectares of land since 2007 with the knowledge of local authorities and proper documents. .
Residents said that after he bought the land, he built a fence, planted crops and raised livestock there. Suddenly, Ms. Him Sovannary used a machine gun to destroy his fence and rafters, and there were still nearly 10 other families who were also abused by this woman.
