This morning, the King presided over the Royal "Tree Day" ceremony in Kratie province
(Kratie): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, on the morning of July 9, 2019, celebrated the Royal "Tree Day" in Sre Treng Village, Kbal Commune. Domrei, Sambo district, Kratie province.
The Royal Ceremony was also attended and attended by Samdech, Ladies and Gentlemen, who are the President, Vice President and Members of the Senate, National Assembly and Heads, as well as members of the Royal Government, as well as the presence of His Majesty the Prince, Ladies and Gentlemen, Ambassador Ambassadors, distinguished national and international guests, and some compatriots living near the area.
His Majesty the King appealed to the authorities at all levels to make efforts to plant more trees in public squares to shade the people and called on the local community to participate in managing, maintaining, protecting and planting forests that can provide many benefits. To develop the socio-economy and to support the livelihood of our people.
It should be noted that the Tree Day was established during the Sangkum Reastr Niyum era under the royal wisdom and noble leadership of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk since the 50s, with the participation of the people throughout the Kingdom of Cambodia.
It should be informed that the Tree Day is celebrated by the Royal Government every year to inspire people everywhere to participate in planting trees, protecting and protecting forests, flooded forests, and all kinds of biodiversity in the spirit of loving the forest and natural resources, which are especially valuable heritage. To support the lives of all of us, as well as all the mammals on the planet and the glorious future of future generations.
