A large statue found in Preah Ko temple
The statue was spotted by residents of Ovulok village, Bakong commune, Prasat Bakong district, digging to fill the backyard.
Mr. Thai Mech, who saw the statue, said that in the past he used to dig a little bit of land here and there in the basin near Preah Ko temple to fill the water tank behind his house.
Mr. Mich said that at first he did not think it was a statue, but looking at the rock, he was suspicious and then continued to dig to find out that it was a statue and stopped the activity and reported to the heritage police to take measures to save. In a safe place.
Lieutenant-Colonel Uon Yang, a heritage police officer at Rolous Park, said that after receiving the information, he immediately asked to suspend his activities, waiting for him to come down to inspect the site and report to the relevant authorities.
He confirmed that in the past, people have encountered various statues like this many times and reported to the authorities regularly, which is an example to follow.
He called on the people as well as the public to find any archeological remains anywhere, handing them over or reporting to the authorities.
Please note that the statue found is not complete, because the hair on both hands and both knees to the knee was lost and handed over to the Apsara Authority to be stored at the Norodom Museum. Sihanouk-Angkor, with the participation of representatives of the Heritage Protection Police, Prasat Bakong District Administration Post, Department of Culture and Fine Arts of Siem Reap Province.
