The Senior Minister also outlined the procedures and system for registering a unique 8-digit personal identification number and public bidding using the Industrial Revolution 4.0 technology with digital payments with partner institutions. In order to bring services closer to the people, reduce complicated procedures, reduce time, eliminate informal expenses.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol welcomed these US companies to establish and continue good cooperation with the Ministry to contribute to the development of Cambodia to another level.
Members of the delegation also presented their participation and action plans in the areas of transport infrastructure, traffic safety and information technology related to the public and transport sectors, as well as volunteering to participate in responsible activities. Be socially capable of investing (CSR) as well.
(Phnom Penh): Recently, Cambodia has been facing African swine fever infections from Vietnam, including in Ratanakiri, Tbong Khmum, Svay Rieng and Takeo provinces.
To prevent the spread of the disease, Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, called on provincial governors and authorities on the Cambodia-Vietnam border to tighten restrictions on the influx of pigs from Vietnam.
Speaking on Fresh News' "Weekly Special Guest" program, Mr. Veng Sakhon added, "With this appeal, I hope that the Governor of the Provincial Board of Governors will strengthen this cooperation for the benefit of Cambodia's economy. "Especially the family economy that wants to raise pigs in Cambodia so that it does not affect his family's economy."
He added that Cambodia does not yet have the resources to compensate for the slaughter of pigs, if people face problems and lose their capital, this is an important point that makes raising pigs can not respond. The needs of the market.
He added that at present, only 80-81 percent of the pigs are raised through suppliers, which requires Cambodia to import more than 10 percent of the pigs to supplement the supply to the Cambodian market.
Mr. Veng Sakhon added that people should not worry about the problem of African swine fever, because this disease does not cause infection to people. But the disease kills pigs, causing losses to breeders.
Mr. Veng Sakhon said that African swine fever is not contagious to humans, but if people eat infected pigs, it is not healthy and will infect livestock. Statues of RUPP intellectuals and two leaders were erected for the younger generation and students to know and appreciate
