(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government Spokesperson Unit, led by Mr. Phay Siphan, will hold a press conference on "Swine Plague Outbreak" to be held on the morning of July 11, 2019 at the meeting hall of the Office of the Commission. Minister.
According to a statement from the Royal Government Spokesperson's Office, the conference aims to address the concerns of the people who are focusing on swine fever with the government's actions and measures in Managing the condition and preventing the spread of the disease.
The conference will cover the general situation of swine fever in Cambodia, its impact in the past, as well as prevention and control measures. Speakers who will be invited are: 1: Representative of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries 2: Representative of the Ministry of Health
Please note that African swine fever has continued to spread and erupt in two more provinces of Cambodia, Svay Rieng and Takeo. As of July 08, 2019, four provinces of Cambodia have had outbreaks of this deadly African swine fever: Ratanakkiri, Tbong Khmum, Svay Rieng and Takeo.
Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Destroyed 232 Recycled Motorcycles and Motorbikes in Violation of Traffic Laws
(Banteay Meanchey): On July 8, 2019, Major General Ace Cam, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, smashed and destroyed 232 recycled motorcycle cement pipes, which his police force cracked down on and confiscated from gangs driving loudly. Disrupts people's lives and affects public order on the streets.
According to the direct order of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General At Cam, the provincial traffic police force, as well as the nine district and municipal police inspectorates, always prevent and crack down on motorbikes that are not technically correct. The cement of the car is not up to technical standards and the processing of the laser light is not technical and so on.
Lt. Gen. Ace Cam urged the police force to continue to curb the use of all types of vehicles that are not technically processed, causing harm to public order, because the use of motorcycles to repair cement pipes (brand) and the use of cement pipes ( Bren) On the streets, people have complained to him directly about the disruption of their lives and called for restraint.
The General Commissioner called on the young people who use cement pipes (motorcycles) to stop to respect the road traffic law, maintain public order and keep their own lives and the lives of others.
Speaking in an interview with Fresh News, Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that joining the International Bamboo and Rattan Network Cambodia will benefit many benefits.
Mr. Veng Sakhon said that when Cambodia became a member of the International Network of Bamboo and Rattan, the benefits that Cambodia received include:
First, find out about the evolution of bamboo cultivation, what are the benefits to trade in the region or respond to the world market. Second: Capacity building of our officials involved in bamboo cultivation, especially the Forestry Administration. Third, the cultivation of bamboo brings significant benefits to the care of Cambodia's green environment, which is sustainable.
The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, with the Forestry Administration in charge, has begun implementing the Law on "Establishment of the International Network for Bamboo and Rattan", which was approved by the Senate on June 25, 2019, pending a Royal Decree. King to officially launch.
This law aims to improve the lives of people, communities, companies by encouraging and motivating them through the mechanism of cultivation, maintenance, processing and use to promote the value of raw materials of economic and social value.
Recently, a local company is planning to plant bamboo on 10,000 hectares and set up a factory to process bamboo into materials and furniture to supply local needs and export in Pratheat commune, Oreang O district, Tbong Khmum province.
This investment project is responding to the agricultural development policy 2019-2023 and especially actively participates in the implementation of the law on "Establishment of the International Network for Bamboo and Rattan". On the other hand, this project will contribute to the sustainable development of bamboo resources, benefit society, economy, brotherhood, green environment and create forest cover. Ministry announces seniority remuneration for textile, garment and footwear enterprises
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on July 08, 2019 issued a notification on the opening of the remuneration of seniority pay before 2019 and the payment of new seniority allowance from 2019 onwards. Go for textile, garment and footwear enterprises.
1. Seniority allowance as stated in the new Article 89 of the Labor Law applies only to workers with an indefinite employment contract (UDC).
2. Separately, workers who have a fixed-term employment contract receive a contract severance pay that is proportional to the salary as well as the contract duration, and this compensation is limited by the collective agreement. Unless otherwise specified in the collective agreement, this indemnity shall be at least 5% of the wages paid by the worker during the contract period.
3: Workers who are using the type of employment contract with a duration that exceeds the maximum period prescribed by law and who have already received the severance pay (5%) in the past, can not ask the employer to pay the seniority reminder. The new Article 89 of the Labor Law.
5: Existing seniority pay before 2019 and new seniority allowance in each year from 2019 are tax-exempt.
6. Workers do not receive seniority pay in case workers resign on their own or commit serious mistakes.
(Kampong Speu): The humanitarian work of Mr. Hun Many, a team of volunteer doctors, was appreciated by the people in the capitals and provinces after this tireless team continued to treat people. People often live in towns and remote areas for the sole reason that they want to see everyone in good health in accordance with the wishes as well as the strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
In fact, on July 7, 2019, the team of 425 volunteer doctors, Mr. HUN Many, led by Mr. Leang Phaly, the leader of the volunteer doctors, Mr. HUN Many continued to visit and treat and provide medicine by Free for 2,545 people at Ang Stok Pagoda (Ang Stok Secondary School), Milav Village, Toul Ampil Commune, Bor Seth District, Kampong Speu Province.
After the inspection and treatment, more than 2,000 authorities and residents of Bor Seth district, Kampong Speu province also thanked Mr. Hun Many for sending a team of doctors with enough experience and many years of treatment. Give them without fear of fatigue.
Mr. Tun Nop, 83 years old, living in Prey Khla Village, Toul Ampil Commune, Bor Seth District, Kampong Speu Province, with heart failure and high blood pressure, expressed his happiness to see Mr. Hun Many's team of volunteer doctors go to treat people He is free.
He also thanked Mr. Hun Many for sending a team of doctors to treat people living in Tuol Ampil commune, Bor Seth district, Kampong Speu province.
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, said that students must take a real skill to study for the future of the family and society, especially to take the skills they know will contribute to the development of the country. Prosper and continue to be peaceful.
Speaking at the graduation ceremony for students at Lim Kok Wing University in Phnom Penh recently, Dr. Hang Chuon Naron said that he would like to ask Cambodian students to embrace a real skill to study for the future of the family and society.
The Minister said that the study of a real skill does not require each student to study at an expensive university, because the study of a specific skill requires each student to be determined and set a clear goal that What do you want to do, what do you want to become an expert and how to study?
Minister Hang Chuon Naron said that setting a specific goal can make each student spend less time and get more results, but if each student does not set a goal and learn from memory is not able to achieve this goal. No.
In addition, a real skill is not related to the student is the child of the rich or the child of the poor, it is important to study that skill clearly, which means that if you study agriculture, it is agriculture, if you study a foreign language. Be clear about the language, be able to achieve goals and be able to advance the future of family and society.
In addition, the Minister of Education stated that according to the new goal of the Ministry of Education, the Ministry has set a young person to have at least one life skills.
Professor Moniroul Islam, Rector of Lim Kok Wing University, said that the university will encourage students to study a major according to the recommendation of the Minister of Education so that each student can quickly achieve the future goals of family and society. Also.
