The Director General confirmed that tomorrow he will visit the outbreak site in Svay Rieng and tomorrow he will visit Takeo to announce the outbreak and advise people how to prevent the spread.
To prevent the spread of African swine fever, Agriculture Minister Veng Sakhon has sent a letter to the governors of the two provinces requesting action to curb the movement of pigs, pork and pig-derived products from the blast site. Disease.
In the letter, the Minister stated, "Please, His Excellency the Governor of the Provincial Board of Governors and local authorities at all levels, cooperate to implement the veterinary measures of professional officials to strengthen the prevention of the movement of pigs, pigs and other products. "Birth of pigs from the outbreak area within a radius of 3 (three) kilometers to implement effective veterinary measures as appropriate."
African swine fever is not contagious to humans, but it is a vicious disease that spreads from region to region, causing up to 100% disease and death in pigs. High for pig farmers.
