(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Fitness has organized the second quarterly meeting of 2019 to strengthen the cooperation between the members of this group effectively and discuss the results of the challenges that have been implemented with us. Find a solution.
Of course, we know that human trafficking is a complex global issue that requires all ministries, agencies and NGOs to work together to address it. This was stated by Mr. Nhek Vannara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, representing Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Fitness.
Mr. Nhek Vannara added that today's meeting aims to strengthen and enhance the effectiveness of protecting and assisting victims in all forms, law enforcement, prosecuting perpetrators of human trafficking and sexual exploitation, justice and the provision of services. Quality and appropriateness with the common goal of addressing and eliminating all forms of human trafficking, as well as sexual exploitation and all forms of exploitation that occur in Cambodia.
The department will have three main goals: 1. Repatriation, receipt and transmission 2. Rehabilitation 3. Integration, which is the priority work of the Ministry. The Royal Government has established the Anti-Human Trafficking Committee (NEC), chaired by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, with 21 relevant ministries and five specialized bodies.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Social Affairs said that the Anti-Human Trafficking Committee has divided into six inter-ministerial working groups, including the Victims Protection Working Group led by the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, which has decided on the appointment of members. Victim protection work, dated September 29, 2015.
Mr. Nhek Vannara hopes that the national and international legal documents are being actively implemented and this effect must be continued widely for the benefit of the victims.
