(Phnom Penh): Police from the Office of Anti-Human Trafficking and Protection of Minors this morning, July 8, 2019, sent 40-year-old Nguyen Thi Nguy Thi, the owner of a massage parlor, to court for investigation. Legal charges related to the sexual exploitation of minors.
The operation, led by Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner General and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, was coordinated by Ms. Sivanny, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, and led by Lt. Gen. Chan Kittikhom, Deputy Commissioner. Anti-Trafficking and Protection of Minors of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police.
According to the police, the owner of the place is Nguyen Thi Ngouty, who lives at the massage place at 22B, Street 288, Sangkat Boeung Keng Kang II, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, Phnom Penh.
According to the police force, the 10,000 Riel scratch massage massage parlor is open from 9 am until late at night, with six young women, two suspected minors, waiting for guests to come for a massage. Normally, it costs 10,000 riel for an hour and sex costs from $ 15 to $ 20 per session.
