(Phnom Penh): The Prince Holding Multipurpose Building, located in Phnom Penh, was officially inaugurated with a press conference on the development strategy of Prince Real Estate Group held in front of the Prince Holding Multipurpose Building. Group in Phnom Penh under the theme "Building Dreams and the Future".
The inauguration ceremony of Prince Holding Multipurpose Building together with this press conference was held on the morning of July 6, 2019 with the participation of Mr. Pen Sophal, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, and Mr. Oknha Pung Kheav Se, President of the Association. The Khmer-Chinese Coalition in Cambodia, along with many other dignitaries.
Mr. Pen Sophal expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the achievements of Prince Real Estate Group in recent years and congratulated the opening of Prince Holding Multipurpose Building. Under China's One Belt One Road framework, Chinese investment in Cambodia and Chinese foreign visitors to Cambodia rank first, and hopefully in the future more Chinese companies will come to invest in Cambodia.
Mr. Pen Sophal stated that for the past four years, Prince Real Estate Group Charitable Foundation has been committed to providing assistance in the field of charity to enhance the company's responsibility by focusing on supporting children who are unable to continue their education. Disability, the elderly, urban development, Chinese language education, environmental protection and many other areas, with a total budget of more than 6 million US dollars and helping more than 150,000 people.
QIU GUOXING, Chief Executive Officer of Prince Real Estate Group, said that Prince Holding Group is a high-standard office building in Cambodia with a total investment of about $ 70 million, with a total investment of $ 24.8 million. 00 square meters. As a new symbol of the city, the Prince Holding Multifunctional Building combines functions such as hospitality, meeting hall, sales office and more.
