(Phnom Penh): Eleven foreigners, mostly Asians, were allowed to enter the oath of office to take the oath of allegiance as Cambodian citizens. The swearing-in ceremony took place after the 11 foreigners had properly met the requirements of Cambodian law.
The swearing-in ceremony for Cambodian citizenship took place on the afternoon of July 8, 2019 in the Supreme Court of the Kingdom of Cambodia, presided over by Dr. Chiv Keng, Chairman of the Oath Council and Vice President of the Supreme Court after the death of the King. His Majesty the King granted the Royal Decree to all 11 foreigners to become Cambodian citizens from today onwards.
Major General Ok Samnang, Deputy Director of the Nationality Department of the Ministry of Interior, told Fresh News that 11 foreigners who have already become Cambodian citizens after the King of Cambodia issued a Royal Decree to take the oath. Before the Supreme Court to fulfill the legal status of a Cambodian citizen in accordance with the principles and procedures of the Nationality Law.
Lt. Gen. Ok Samnang further stated that the naturalization of these 11 nationalities is based on Article 16, Article 27 of the Law on the Nationality of All Foreigners who have already acquired Khmer nationality through a Royal Decree must take an oath before the court. Top. The Royal Decree granting Khmer nationality must be handed over to the person concerned after taking the oath.
