More than 1,000 hectares of state-owned forest reserves in Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province are being cleared to belong to traders, the provincial governor immediately sent officers to prevent
(Kampong Chhnang): Often, a small number of corrupt land traders often cause rainstorms, trying to find all possible means to encroach on state land for resale. Local people appealed to Mr. Chhour Chandoeun, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province to help monitor and prevent in time.
Reports from local residents tell Fresh News that the recent encroachment on state-owned land has been on the rise. In order to avoid criticism and cheating, the governor of Kampong Chhnang province and the director of the provincial agriculture department should investigate and find the perpetrators and punish them according to the law.
The provincial governor confirmed that after receiving the information, he sent officers and authorities to prevent and stop the clearing of those lands. According to the governor of Kampong Chhnang province, this case started from the local authority, which allowed the traders to clear the road, but the provincial level did not know.
In fact, on the morning of July 7, 2019, a group of journalists found a machine that was clearing and encroaching on community forest land in Prasnup commune, Rolea Bier district. According to reports from residents, the land clearing group is a state-owned permanent forest reserve of more than 1,000 hectares, with land traders using images and pretexts to build roads.
As for the legal action, Mr. Chhour Chandoeun is not sure yet, waiting to discuss with the relevant officials and authorities whether to send the case to court or not, while the traders are already known to the authorities.
According to the report, the community forest land at that point is more than 1,000 hectares in 3 villages, Trapeang Pil village, Prasnip village, Sam village, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province, and is also the land that is the stronghold of a handful of crooks.
