Cambodia to Send 39 Natural Science Research Candidates to International Competition in China
(Phnom Penh): Under the auspices of the Royal Government of Cambodia, on July 17, 2019, 39 middle and high school students in the field of natural science research will compete in the international competition in China. With the participation of many countries, while in 2018, Cambodia received 16 components.
On July 07, 2019, a pilot project to participate in the research project to participate in the "Global Natural History Day 2019" was held at CKCC with the participation of Mr. Nith Bunlong, Chairman of the Commission on World Natural History Day 2018 In Cambodia, along with 36 candidates, equivalent to 26 teams, there will be a presentation on their topics before going to the upcoming competition in China.
"Global Natural History Day 2019" is a theme for the international competition will be held from July 18 to 21, 2019, hosted by the People's Republic of China.
According to Mr. Nith Bunlong, the candidates are students from Phnom Penh, Battambang and Siem Reap, of which a total of 39 candidates will leave on July 17, 2019 to compete in Shanghai. China, July 18-21, 2019, with the participation of many countries in Asia, Africa, and especially in China, which requires only 16 regions.
He added that in order to compete in this international program, all students who do natural science projects must be eliminated in Cambodia first to have the right to continue to compete for medals at all levels. China.
Mr. Nith Bunlong further stated that "The results in 2015, 2016 and 2017 were not very successful, they won a lot of silver and bronze medals, but the gold medals were few, but in 2018, Cambodia won the gold medal." "16 out of 40 candidates and 18 silver medals, 4 bronze medals in the last period, we have achieved good results."
Please be informed that "World Natural History Day" is a program that was established in 2012, while Cambodia sent students to compete in 2015, and this is the fifth time that Cambodia continues to participate in such international programs. And a total of more than 100 people have been sent by the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Meanwhile, Mey Roeun, the guardian of Mey Monisana, who studied at Rolous Secondary School in Siem Reap, was very happy to see her son qualify for the Cambodian qualifiers and to be ready to continue competing in China. In the near future, he also hopes that his son will win a gold medal from the competition in China.
