Cambodia went through decades of civil war, beginning with the coup d'état overthrowing Norodom Sihanouk in 1970 and then falling under the Khmer Rouge regime of 1975-1979. The Khmer Rouge regime collapsed on January 7, 1979, and the people were liberated from the regime, but gun battles continued until the Paris Agreement.
Under the victorious policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in 1998, Cambodia was restored to full peace, and this full and stable peace brought Cambodia to a state of development with economic growth of around 7% annually.
However, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia has often called on all people to join in maintaining Cambodia's peace and to join against any group that attempts to destroy this peace, wanting to bring Cambodia back to war.
