After receiving the report, the local police force and the criminal police force led by Colonel Nop Sarak, Inspector of the Siem Reap City Police Inspectorate, went to the scene and disseminated the report on the motorcycle through the radio, ID and telephone system.
Immediately after receiving the report, Siem Reap Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Tith Narong issued a stern order to all inspectors, especially the district inspectorate based on National Road 6, to lead a joint operation. To find the lost motorcycle, return it to the victim and catch the perpetrator and punish him.
After that, the criminal force led by Lieutenant Colonel Nuon Sakdey Chamroeunrith, Deputy Inspector in charge of Siem Reap City Criminal Division, cooperated with the Sotnikum District Police Force to search the suspect's car and found 5 motorcycle license plates and vehicle identification card (credit card). Motorcycle) 05 sheets, including tools for locking the motorcycle, as well as some license plate accessories.
After checking that the suspect and the evidence were found to be criminal, Brigadier General Pheng Chendareth instructed the Sotnikum District Police Inspector to hand over the suspect and the evidence of transportation to the Siem Reap City Police Inspectorate as the case builder. Procedures.
The suspect, after being interrogated at the Siem Reap City Police Inspectorate, admitted that the two motorcycles were stolen by his accomplices and handed over to another accomplice in Phnom Penh to be sold for a profit. From shipping per unit costs $ 150.
According to the confessions and evidence of the suspects, the Siem Reap City Criminal Police prepared a case to be sent to court for legal punishment, while the remaining suspects were identified by the police force and continue to search for arrest.
Two motorcycle exhibits confiscated with the approval of Major General Tit Narong, Siem Reap Provincial Police Commissioner, have already been returned to the victims, Ke Chhon and Seng Sopheak, by the Siem Reap City Police. . Donald Trump "because of the British ambassador to Washington" after the message was leaked criticizing him from behind ...
