Kampong Speu provincial authorities summon a group of people to instruct and stop activities immediately after destroying houses without a proper order in Phnom Sruoch district
(Kampong Speu): According to local reports, there was a case of demolition of a family house in Chrey Sen Chey village, Taing Samrong commune, Phnom Sruoch district, Kampong Speu province, caused by many people on July 6, 2019. According to the report of the local authority, this case is suspected to have started from the land dispute between the citizens on both sides.
The deputy district governor confirmed that the move to dismantle his house was illegal because it was an act of abuse to others and the other party did not buy or sell anything, as the land has a protection order. . He added that if any citizens do not agree or have any questions, they must go to the authorities to solve, should not commit such actions.
According to the Deputy District Governor, after the incident on the afternoon of July 7, 2019, the authorities also called both parties to interrogate and educate at the commune hall to stop activities and wait for the authorities to resolve the procedure.
Dr. Leang Taing Leang, director of the Baray-Santuk Referral Hospital, said: "There is no care in eradicating tiger mosquitoes, which is one of the causes of dengue fever outbreaks this year."
In addition, Mr. Hourn Bunna, a pediatrician at Baray-Santuk Referral Hospital, said that the tiger mosquito, which is a transmitting agent of dengue fever, likes to bite and suck blood during the day, from 6 am to 7 pm. Dengue occurs in both adults and children, but is present in 85% of children under 15 years of age.
He also urged all residents to take care to clean the environment around the house, especially to prevent water in the house, which can allow tiger mosquitoes to breed there, because tiger mosquitoes are agents. The most deadly form of dengue fever.
Dengue fever is caused by tiger mosquitoes and usually occurs during the rainy season from June to October. The disease can be fatal if the patient is not treated within a week.
If you see a child or we have any of the above symptoms, we should hurry to the hospital to get a blood test for viruses immediately.
Meanwhile, the Minister of Health, Mr. Mam Bunheng, called on private doctors and pharmacists in all pharmacies not to sell drugs without the right doctor and mix drugs because this dengue is different from other diseases. Others need to be clearly monitored.
