The world would be in serious danger if Iran had nuclear weapons, the US Secretary of State warned.
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo has repeatedly warned that the world would be in serious danger if Iran had nuclear weapons and that resumption of uranium enrichment would make it more isolated as well as face sanctions. . This is according to the press release from Sputnik on Monday, July 08, 2019.
Iran on Sunday announced the start of a short-term increase in enrichment of uranium to 3.6 percent, a level restricted under the 2015 Iran Nuclear Agreement.
In addition, Tehran will reduce or cancel its commitment to the nuclear deal every 60 days.
