By: Chao Chak Smok On July 7, 2019, General Kun Kim presented medals to the police and staff of Sihanoukville Autonomous Port who participated in the search and rescue operation for the victims of the collapse of a seven-story building.
(Preah Sihanouk): After awarding medals to the military, General Kun Kim presented medals to the police force involved in the search and rescue operation for the victims of the collapse of a seven-story building in Preah Sihanouk province.
Addressing the Medal Ceremony for Police and Workers of Sihanoukville Autonomous Port Workers who Helped to Rescue Workers Victims of the Collapse of a 7-Storey Building in Preah Sihanouk Province on the afternoon of July 7, 2019, Senior General Kun Kim The first vice-chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management called the collapse a "tragic incident" that killed 28 workers and injured 26 others.
General Kun Kim emphasized that this is a bitter lesson for all that needs to be considered and closely monitored for construction sites in terms of technical characteristics and quality of construction to avoid as destructive as we have encountered. Found on June 22, 2019.
He said that Sihanoukville, especially Sihanoukville is developing rapidly, in which many small and large buildings have been under construction. Therefore, it requires regular inspections of safety at the construction site as well as the quality of the construction to ensure that no building can collapse like another seven-story building.
On behalf of Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, Senior Minister Kun Kim thanked the forces from all over 1,700 people who participated in the two-and-a-half-day operation to find the victims. Under the rubble of a 7-storey building that collapsed at 4:30 am on June 22, 2019, 28 people were killed (4 females) and 26 injured (2 females). People).
On this occasion, Major General Chuon Narin, Sihanoukville Provincial Police Commissioner, expressed regret over the incident and that as a police force need to join the Royal Government to protect and save the people. Nationwide drug crackdown for July 7: 32 cases cracked, 66 arrested
