Drug arrest and trafficking case in Kampong Siem district, police arrested 2 suspects
(Kampong Cham): Pursuant to the Royal Government's 4th plan to fight against illegal drugs and the order of General Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police, which urges measures to crack down on drug activities nationwide on the 6th. In July 2019, Kampong Cham provincial police arrested two suspects in Kampong Siem district.
Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Em Kosal said that after receiving information from the people, he sent a force to search and launch an operation to crack down on illegal drug trafficking in Trapeang Char village, Krala commune, Kampong Siem district. Kampong Cham Province.
The operation was carried out by the Kampong Cham Provincial Anti-Drug Office in collaboration with the Kampong Siem District Police Inspectorate, led by Lieutenant Colonel Chiv Sengros, Director of the Office for the Suppression of Illegal Drug Trafficking.
The first suspect is Snguon Chandy, 29 years old, living in Trapeang Char village, Krala commune, Kampong Siem district, Kampong Cham province, and the second suspect is Met Sokheng, 24 years old, living in Beng Chas village, Ampil commune, Kampong Siem district, Kampong Cham province. Police confiscated 14 packages of white gram powder (3 large packages), 2 mobile phones, 1 motorbike, 2 electronic scales, some packing materials and 2 accessories.
Currently, the above suspects have been sent to the specialized office to proceed with the procedure. Preah Vihear Province Celebrates 11th Anniversary of Preah Vihear Temple Registration as a World Heritage Site
(Preah Vihear): The National Authority of Preah Vihear this morning, July 7, 2019, celebrated the 11th anniversary of the registration of the Temple of Preah Vihear as a World Heritage Site 2008-2019.
The ceremony was held at Moradok Techo Borey Svara pagoda in Thom Cheat village, Sra Em commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province, presided over by Mr. Chuch Phoeun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, and attended by Mr. Kim Setara, President of Preah Vihear National Authority. And Ms. Chak Heng, Deputy Provincial Governor, representing Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province.
Mr. Chuch Phoeun stated that it is not only the temple of Preah Vihear that has outstanding value that we need to add to the World Heritage List, but also the temple of Koh Ker in Srayong commune, Kulen district, Preah Vihear province and the temple of Preah Khan in Kampong Svay district. New society. If the Koh Ker temple documents are made before January 2020 and submitted to the World Heritage List and will be managed by the Preah Vihear authorities.
Mr. Chuch Phoeun continued, "Before agreeing to register the temple as a World Heritage Site, it was very difficult to go through a meeting with more than 100 countries participating, more than 90 countries have analyzed all aspects. Decided to let us in. If we go in and we do not try to take care of ourselves, they will ask to withdraw.
Mr. Kim Setara said, "For the past 11 years, we have all been working to preserve and develop the Temple of Preah Vihear with great success in both the national and international framework."
He said that from year to year, the protection, conservation and development of the Temple of Preah Vihear has improved steadily under the good cooperation between the National Authority of Preah Vihear and the Preah Vihear Provincial Authority, local authorities, national institutions and international partners under the shadow of peace. The wise and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Requests Monks to Disseminate the Dangers of Drugs While Sermon
