On the occasion, General Kun Kim considered the past building collapse as a great sorrow for the nation, which needs to be careful about the quality of construction to avoid any eventual danger again.
General Kun Kim also warned that in Sihanoukville, in the future there may be 50-storey buildings, so it is better to be prepared with rescue forces and rescue equipment based in Sihanoukville directly than to wait. Remember the mobility of forces or equipment from afar, which can slow down the rescue operation.
The senior minister confirmed that he would ask Samdech Techo Prime Minister, who is the chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, to arrange this work.
