Report: Only 2 months! 544 civilians killed in Russian, Syrian army operation
(Syria): At least 544 civilians have been killed and more than 2,000 wounded since Russia and the Syrian army launched an air strike operation against the last rebel base in the country's northwest. Syria in the past two months. This is according to the Syrian human rights organization quoted by Reuters on Sunday, July 7, 2019.
Russian warplanes have joined Syrian government forces in leading large-scale offensive operations since April 26 on the last Syrian rebel bases in Idlib and Hama provinces. The Syrian Network for Human Rights (SNHR) also said that 544 civilians, including 130 children, had been killed and 2,117 wounded in the joint military operation.
Idlib and Hama are the latest major battlefields between Russian-backed Syrian government forces and US-backed Syrian rebels. Most of Syria is currently under the control of the government of Syrian President Bashar al-Assad. Cambodia Airways announces the appointment of Mr. Ly Vahet and Ms. Sok Somavathy as Goodwill Ambassadors
