Mr. Sun Chanthol instructed the people to provide information to the team in case they face difficulties in their daily lives, and he and the team, especially the Cambodian People's Party, stay with you at all times under all circumstances. To serve you as servants of the people, the people as our masters, not us as masters of the people.
On that occasion, the youth representatives who are members of Ang Mit Ting congratulated Ang Mit Ting, celebrated the 68th anniversary of the founding of the Cambodian People's Party and expressed their deep gratitude for saving the Cambodian people from the genocidal regime. The Pol Pot race and the leadership of the society for peace and prosperity.
After that, Mr. Sun Chanthol distributed the prizes of the best students at the provincial level to the students of Koh Thom district, 9th and 12th grade who passed the subjects of Khmer literature, mathematics and physics and encouraged the teachers to have good achievements in Teach outstanding students.
Finally, he also inspected the progress of the construction of the swimming pool in Koh Thom District Stadium and encouraged young people, students as well as swimmers to participate in swimming training for health and be ready to Participate in the upcoming SEA Games in 2023, which Cambodia will host. Senior Minister Kun Kim urges officials to hold on to natural disaster information to help victims in a timely manner
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kun Kim, Senior Minister in charge of Special Missions and First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, urged all his officials to be aware of the situation and information related to natural disasters, both natural and accidental. Other to rescue the victims in time.
Senior Minister Kun Kim's speech was made on July 6, 2019, on the occasion of the Senior Minister's meeting to pass the report on "Disaster Management in the First Half of 2019 and Other Issues". . The meeting was held at the headquarters of the National Committee for Disaster Management, with the participation of the Vice President and many leaders.
Senior Minister Kun Kim said at the meeting that all officials must do their job, not just wait for orders from superiors. Must grasp the news report, both national and international news, briefly inform the leadership to find ways to solve and respond in a timely manner.
At the same time, Senior Minister Kun Kim also urged all officials to cooperate with relevant ministries and institutions to be prepared to prevent and participate in solving all problems in a timely and highly effective manner.
Mr. Kun Kim also told the officials of the National Committee for Disaster Management to work together to fulfill their duties effectively to contribute to reducing the government's difficulties as an institution and subordinate to the Royal Government. Not only that, you have to overcome all the obstacles in front of you to achieve the plan of your superiors.
In addition, Senior Minister Kun Kim also urged all officials to work in unity and clear division of labor, remembering their respective roles that they play an important role in helping people to prevent or assist during Disasters happen. All officials must continue to maintain a stronger internal unity to develop the unit to respond to the actual working situation.
The report added that in the first six months of this year, Cambodia has experienced some problems from natural disasters as well as some diseases. There were 13,843 cases of dengue fever and 24 deaths nationwide. Dengue provinces include Ratanakiri, Mondulkiri, Kratie, Kampong Cham, Siem Reap, Phnom Penh, Banteay Meanchey, Prey Veng, Oddar Meanchey, Koh Kong and Sihanoukville.
Most of the patients were treated at all five Kantha Bopha hospitals, including the National Children's Hospital. Institute for Success organizes discussions to find solutions to inconsistencies between employers and employees
(Phnom Penh): Institutions, no matter how small or large, always hear complaints about inconsistencies between bosses and employees, always hear that this boss is good, that boss is bad, or this employee is good, that staff is bad in management. . Inconsistency between bosses, managers and employees is also a factor that leads to institutional failure.
On Friday, July 5, 2019, yesterday, the Institute for Success organized a forum to discuss "great boss attitude and great staff" to find solutions to all these problems. The forum was attended by leaders, management and staff from various institutions to share their experiences.
In response to this sensitive issue, Kem Oeun, director of the Institute for the Study of Success, stated that when people have weak leadership, they solve problems by blaming each other, and blame does not provide progress.
Learning for Success Institute is an organization that conducts educational and training activities to help students, youth, employees, employers to have high knowledge, skills, ethics, personal discipline, self-confidence and clear goals in life, as well as contribute to the vision and The goal of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the political program of the Royal Government of Cambodia's Rectangular Strategy to increase human resources with real capacity and quality.
