(Siem Reap): The ASEAN Veterans Federation at the end of 2019 will hold the 32nd Executive Committee Meeting and the 19th General Assembly in Cambodia at the end of 2019.
During the meeting, Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association and President of the ASEAN Veterans Federation, took turns to meet and make some recommendations to the members who participated in this discussion meeting.
After discussing and exchanging opinions, the Working Committee agreed on the principles, content and agenda for inclusion in the Executive Committee Meeting and the General Assembly for future approval.
The ASEAN Veterans Association (VECONAC) was established in 1980 and currently has 10 member countries, including: Brunei Veterans Association, Cambodian Veterans Association, Indonesian Veterans Federation, Lao Veterans Federation, Malaysian Army Veterans, Myanmar War Veterans Organization, Philippine Veterans Federation, Singapore Army Veterans Federation, Thai War Veterans Organization and Vietnam Veterans Association.
The federation was established to promote and enhance the luxury of life, the impact of age and the impact of war on the social health of war victims, and to raise awareness among the people to achieve cooperation. Towards harmony, social justice and peace.
The federation also has a mission to promote a global understanding of the views, values, praises and interests of the countries of the region and to promote the legitimacy of the interests of war veterans and war victims with the legal recognition of ex-associations. Member fighters.
