(Phnom Penh): The Central Market building, which is almost 30 years old, was built in 1990 and is in a very dilapidated condition, which will collapse at any time if no action is taken on repair and improvement. Again, no.
The site of the building, called the Stone Market of Central Market, currently has more than 500 vendors selling it, but on closer inspection, the building needs to be renovated immediately.
When asking vendors from one stall to another, Mr. Sok Penh Vuth explained the plans for the urgent renovation of the stone market building, fearing that the lease would collapse during heavy rains or that would cause accidents such as Occurs in Sihanoukville.
The district governor raised concerns that if the building collapses at night, it could avoid danger to people, but if it happened during the day, it would be very serious.
A pork trader added that she agreed to the renovation, but had to find a temporary location, arguing that for a clothing seller, it was not a big deal, but for her, pork was a regular supply. The day can not be missed.
On the other hand, the opinion of another trader who agreed to the wishes of the authorities, he asked for notice before the repair for a long time to avoid him ordering more items for the sale.
In front of the vendors, Mr. Sok Penh Vuth also confirmed that the renovation of the market building does not require vendors to pay money, the state is responsible for all, and the size of the stalls, the location of the stalls remain the same. All do not worry.
Examination of the pillars of the market building and the explanation of the officers and engineers who accompanied them showed great concern due to cracks and corroded steel wires due to the long life of the building.
In addition to their confidence, all traders through the Daun Penh district governor request to meet directly with Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh to discuss this issue before the official repair.
So far, the authorities have not been able to determine how many days it will take to repair, and the location of the temporary store is still unknown, pending the decision of the Governor of Phnom Penh, just today. Come to study and check the condition of the building and the opinions of the traders only.
