Police crack down on 4 robbers in Ang Snoul district, Kandal province
(Central): The specialized police force of Ang Snoul District Police Inspectorate launched an operation to crack down on six robbers while the other two were fleeing. These thieves robbed people and took property, causing injuries.
Mr. Thach Sovanna, Chief of Criminal Police of Ang Snoul District, said on July 6, 2019 that these thieves acted on July 4, 2019 at the intersection of National Road 51, Trapeang Kak Village, Samrong Leu Commune, Ang Snoul District. Central.
The forensic officer confirmed that before the incident, the victim left the chicken coop in Sre Kach village, Tuol Prech commune to go home. The leg caused the motorcycle to fall and one of the suspects ran down and cut the victim with a knife to the left forearm, then the victim escaped and the suspect picked up the victim's motorcycle and fled.
After the victim complained to the police, the force immediately chased and hid until they reached Snoul Khpos village, Sangkat Kambol, Khan Kambol, Phnom Penh, and arrested a suspect named Phat Tola, alias Thai. It was not until July 5, 2019 that the search and arrest force arrested 3 more people named Yong Puthea Chamnan alias Chhe, Yan Serey alias Soch alias Moch alias Sich and Pheak Pros Mao.
According to the suspect's confession, 6 of his accomplices acted 5 times, including Ang Snoul district on National Road 51 2 times, the first time: on June 28, 2019 at the village Trapeang Trach, Damnak Ampil Commune, Ang Snoul District, Kandal Province, 2nd time: On July 4, 2019, at the point of National Road No. 51, Trapeang Kak Village, Samrong Leu Commune, Ang Snoul District, Kandal Province and west of Thnal Toteung Market in Kampong Speu Province, 3 more times. Days.
