(Phnom Penh): In response to the concerns of citizens who are focusing on construction safety issues and the Royal Government's actions in managing and maintaining safety in the construction sector for the people, as well as measures to encourage builders. Construction in accordance with environmental standards, the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit organized a press conference on "Principles of Construction Technical Management in Cambodia."
Through the press conference held this morning, July 5, 2019, Mr. Bin Sambath Tharoth, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Compensation, was assigned by Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management to be a speaker. The photo also represents the parties of the Ministry.
Speaking on the occasion, the expert described in detail the obligations of the construction owner from the time of applying for a building permit to the completion of completion in order to obtain legitimacy for investment in its construction sector.
Mr. Bin Sambath Tharoth claimed that all construction work requires a construction permit, so both the compensation owner and the construction business designer must ensure that their construction project has received a permit from the Ministry of Land Management or Only from the provincial and municipal authorities can the construction process begin.
The construction permit must be accompanied by the architectural plan, and after obtaining the construction permit, the investor who owns the compensation must apply for the groundbreaking certificate, which must be accompanied by the construction plan, construction contract, insurance contract, construction contract and Employment contract with workers.
If necessary, can come with a certificate of environmental impact assessment, after receiving the permit to open the site, we can do the construction. This is according to Mr. Bin Sambath Tharoth.
During the construction phase, professional officers will inspect all stages, including underground work, then ground work, all floor work, for all construction components, all concrete pouring work, it is necessary to inspect. The builder needs to make an invitation letter to the competent provincial, municipal or ministry authority for the ministry to send an expert to inspect.
After the completion of the construction, the compensation owner must apply for the closing letter after closing the construction site and must confirm the correctness (specified in Sub-Decree No. 86 on the construction permit) in order to be able to occupy and use the building, but in practice, the Royal Government Ministry Territories The provincial / municipal authorities are still soft on not yet implementing the certification to facilitate construction investors in Cambodia.
After demarcation, the builder must build within the boundary, it is strictly forbidden to build beyond this demarcation, and in the case of construction beyond the boundary and construction permit means illegal. At the same time, the team continues to monitor and control the quality of construction until the end.
It should be informed that until now, the construction sector in Cambodia seems to be growing rapidly, which is because Cambodia maintains peace and political stability under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, head of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
