To begin with, the Acting Minister warmly welcomed the ADB Vice President's visit to Cambodia and expressed his appreciation for the good cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the ADB in the past.
He added that ADB is a loyal partner and plays an important role in the development of Cambodia. In fact, under the cooperation between Cambodia and ADB, the Strategic Partnership for Development of Cambodia (CPS) 2019-2023 has set out a joint strategic framework for the next five years under the larger ADB co-financing. $ 300 million per year.
In order to meet the needs of Cambodia's development as stated in the National Strategic Plan of Cambodia, especially the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4, which is the socio-economic policy agenda of the political program of the Royal Government of the 6th legislature of the National Assembly for Cambodia. Achieve the goal of becoming a high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050.
The Acting Minister also briefed the ADB Vice President on the overall state of the Cambodian economy, which has been achieving strong macroeconomic stability with high economic growth despite the external challenges and risks. To some extent, this is a proof that Cambodia is on the right track.
The ADB Vice President also praised the Royal Government's efforts and praised Cambodia's success in achieving high economic growth and poverty reduction. He also stressed that the ADB will continue to support Cambodia and would like to assist Cambodia in setting up a legal framework related to public-private partnership mechanisms.
The Acting Minister and ADB Vice President also exchanged views on regional issues, development policies, and diversification of funding sources.
The Acting Minister requested the ADB to continue to assist Cambodia in five important areas: First: Diversification of the economic base to promote Cambodia's competitiveness, Second: Development of human resources and skills, Third: Development of the financial sector Objective: 4: Urban planning based on the sector's master plan and investment plan, and 5: Development of the energy sector in Cambodia, focusing on network connectivity, reliability and affordability.
He also informed the ADB Vice President that Cambodia plans to explore the possibility of issuing state bonds in the near future, which will not only help Cambodia diversify its sources of financing and mobilize domestic savings, but also Help develop and train the capacity of relevant ministries and institutions of the Royal Government to be ready to enter the capital market.
These co-financing funds are used to invest in areas such as agriculture and natural resources, water supply and urban infrastructure, transportation and information technology, industry and commerce, finance, public administration, Technical and vocational education and training, health, energy and multidisciplinary.
