Sihanoukville Buddhist University organizes "Understanding of Asal Bochea" program to spread awareness to Buddhists
(Phnom Penh): The Buddhist University of Sihanoukville on the afternoon of July 5, 2019 organized a program "Understanding the festival of Asal Bochea" to spread the understanding of Buddhists in the field of Buddhism. The event was held at the Chaktomuk Conference Hall with the participation of many monks as well as Buddhist and imperial experts.
The Asal Bochea festival, which will be held in 2019 to commemorate the 2643rd anniversary of the founding of the Buddha, the 2614th anniversary of the founding of the Buddha, the first sermon and the birth of the monks, as well as the 2608th performance Years.
Usually on the 15th day of the month of Asat, Buddhists often go to their favorite pagoda to participate in the celebration, there will be a procession around the temple, offering flowers, worshiping the Preah Ratanatray, listening to sermons and bringing Sada skirts and other gifts to give to monks on the occasion of the rainy season.
According to the order of Preah Samuh, librarian Oeun Sam Ath, Deputy Dean of Sihanoukville Buddhist University, said that Asalha is a major Buddhist festival that is celebrated every year by Buddhist countries, especially Cambodia. However, this festival has not been celebrated as big as other religious festivals such as Meak Bochea, Pisak Bochea, Preah Vossa and Vesa festivals, etc.
Oeun Sam Ath, the librarian, said that the Asal Bochea festival that will be celebrated in 2019 is to commemorate five important events: first: the birth of the Buddha, second: the departure to build the Buddha, Third: Performing the first sermon or giving the first sermon to the world and healing the five monks, fourth: the birthday of the monk and fifth: Performing the miracle.
The celebration of Asal Bochea will be held in Phnom Penh, Siem Reap and Kampong Thom provinces to bring together this important concept and will be included in other religious festivals in the future. Because the content of Asal Bochea is important for Buddhists to know more about the religion of the Buddha.
