Ministry of Foreign Affairs issues press release on the results of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's participation in the WTO meeting and other events in Geneva, Switzerland
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on July 05, 2019 issued a press release on the results of the participation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia in the Global Review Meeting. Seventh, on "Aid for Trade" at the World Trade Organization (WTO) and other events from July 3 to 5, 2019 in Geneva, Switzerland.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Successfully Participates in the 7th Global Review Meeting on "Aid for Trade" at the WTO Headquarters under the theme "Supporting Diversification and Economic Promotion for Sustainable and environmental development through trade assistance ”and participation in a number of key events.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a keynote address, sharing Cambodia's experience in formulating trade policies and strategies and the success of socio-economic development after Cambodia became a member of the WTO last year. 2004, as well as Cambodia's current and future role in supporting the multilateral trading system and maintaining the path to global liberalization.
