(Phnom Penh): In June 2019, Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit as Founder and Honorary President, received donations from philanthropists totaling 169,213,300 Riels and 98, $ 986. This is according to the press release of Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia, which was received by Fresh News on July 6, 2019.
According to a press release from the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia, in addition, the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia has just received a donation of 913,086 US dollars, which is a deduction from the ticket price to visit the Angkor resort area in the second quarter of 2019 from Angkor Institute and the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia will transfer this money to Kantha Bopha Hospital to be used for free examination and treatment.
The Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia would like to thank all the donors who have always supported and donated funds to support and ensure the sustainable, efficient and quality operation of the five Kantha Bopha Hospitals in order to improve the well-being of children and infants. In Cambodia.
