After the outbreak of dengue fever, Tbong Khmum Red Cross Branch donated 10,000 tablets of serum to the provincial health department to supply hospitals and health centers
(Tbong Khmu): In order to participate in humanitarian activities in the field of health, Tbong Khmum Red Cross Branch has opened a branch fund to buy 10,000 serums to provide to the Provincial Health Department to supply to the referral centers in 6 districts and health centers throughout Tbong Khmum.
The handing over ceremony was held at Tbong Khmum Provincial Red Cross Branch on July 05, 2019, presided over by Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Tbong Khmum Provincial Governor and Ms. Leng Sokha, President of Tbong Khmum Provincial Red Cross Branch. Ros Sokhon, Director of the Red Cross Branch and Mr. Keo Vann: Director of the Provincial Health Department and many other stakeholders.
Ms. Leng Sokha said that it is necessary to treat dengue fever, which is on the rise in referral hospitals in Tbong Khmum province, so the provincial Red Cross branch bought and donated 10,000 serums to the health department. The province is now supplying hospitals.
Mr. Keo Vann: Director of Tbong Khmum Provincial Health Department thanked the Provincial Red Cross Branch for meeting the need by providing a lot of serum. He distributed to the seven operating districts, referral hospitals, six districts and all health centers in the province that are in need because the rate of children with dengue fever is increasing alarmingly.
Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, on behalf of all the people in the province, thanked for the large number of serum offerings now, which is a time to unite and provide warmth to the people, especially in the field of humanitarian and health. People are needed, especially young children who are suffering from dengue fever in hospitals and health centers.
He also instructed the directors of the seven executive districts to increase their attention to provide better health services to the people and called on all citizens to work together to eliminate tiger mosquito breeding grounds, especially parents to take care of their children. Small, wearing long sleeves, long legs and sleeping in the mosquito net to avoid dengue fever all together.
Next week, the Senate will convene a meeting of the Standing Committee to review and decide on four proposals.
(Phnom Penh): The Senate of Cambodia will hold a meeting of the Standing Committee to review and decide on four proposals on July 8, 2019 next week. This is according to the announcement of the Senate on July 5, 2019, which was received by Fresh News.
According to this announcement, the General Secretariat of the Senate informed the public that on Monday, July 08, 2019 at 8:00 AM, the Senate of Cambodia will hold a meeting of the Standing Committee with the following agenda:
1. Examine and decide on the request of the Ninth Committee of the Senate to submit the draft law on the approval of the payment guarantee of the Royal Government of Cambodia to SPHP (Cambodia) Co., Ltd. in the agenda of the third session Senate, 4th legislature.
2. Examine and decide on the request of the Ninth Committee of the Senate to submit the draft law on the approval of the payment guarantee of the Royal Government of Cambodia to the company requesting Thek or New Bill Ek to be on the agenda of the third session of the Senate. Fourth.
3. Examine and decide on the request of the Ninth Committee of the Senate to submit the draft law on the approval of the payment guarantee of the Royal Government of Cambodia to Sme Open Co., Ltd. in the agenda of the third session of the Senate for the fourth term.
4. Examine and decide on the request of the Third Committee of the Senate to submit the draft law on the approval of Cambodia to be a member of the Agreement on Port Ownership Measures to Prevent and Eliminate Illegal and Unauthorized Fishing Into the agenda of the third session of the Senate of the fourth legislature.
