It should be noted that before 1997, two Chinese people came to buy land from the people in Leach village, Orussey commune, Kampong Tralach district, Kampong Chhnang province, with the district authority officials collecting a total of 26 hectares. One named Silemeng owns more than 10 hectares and the other more than 15 hectares.
The Chinese then paid $ 100 per family, with a total of 34 families, and the landlord handed over the documents to the landlord for a fee. Taken to run the title deed, but since then, the above Chinese people have disappeared, even though the title deed has been issued to the above Chinese people as the owner.
Later, the landowners complained to the authorities to get their land back. Suddenly, Hem Vansoeun and Yin Dara Phuong came out and claimed that the land above belonged to them and had 26 hectares of legal titles. Instead. It was only later that Yin Dara Phuong claimed that he was the wife of a Chinese man named Silemeng through a marriage letter dated November 27, 1997, issued by Russey Keo district court.
On May 25, 2019, the police arrested Mr. Hem Vansoeun on a temporary detention order, but he did not confess to his actions and filed for bail, but was denied by the trial judge. Go to the Court of Appeal to ask for bail, which the Court of Appeal plans to clear on July 9, 2019.
