Confirmation of the law does not apply to these trucks was made during the meeting between Senior Minister Sun Chanthol and a total of 179 transport companies (passengers and goods across the border) at the Ministry of Public Works and Transport on July 05, 2019. The meeting was held to discuss a number of measures to tighten law enforcement on large trucks to help prevent and reduce traffic accidents.
The meeting between the Minister of Public Works and Transport and the transport company took place after some transport companies refused to participate in complying with Cambodia's road traffic laws. In particular, refused to cooperate with officials of the National Road Safety Committee, who inspected the technical vehicles and driver's licenses at the Phnom Penh Autonomous Port and Sihanoukville.
In the operation to enforce the traffic rules of the trucks entering and exiting the Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville Autonomous Ports, which took place from June 15, 2019, most of the trucks obeyed the law. About 11% of cars do not obey the law properly. In addition, some companies' vehicles tried to evade inspection at the port, leading to congestion in the transport of goods.
In front of the management and representatives of the transport company, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol claimed that even if the trucks try to avoid entering the port, must be checked, no exceptions.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said, "Not all vehicles must enter the port to be inspected for technical specifications, but all vehicles running on public roads in Cambodia must obey the law." The Ministry can not catch only when the car enters the port, it wants to catch at any time as long as the car runs on the road and it is illegal, so even if all the container trucks parked on the road, the Ministry can catch The same.
In addition to confirming the law enforcement position on these trucks, Mr. Sun Chanthol also urged all transport companies to comply with all traffic laws. He said that when there is a serious traffic accident on the road, the company loses its national economic interests and national honor.
"For carriers to reduce the enforcement of the law on the inspection of heavy vehicles, how to reduce? Because the law is the law, we must all obey the law. "The Road Safety Committee can not allow and absolutely reduce what is done in violation of the road traffic law." Mr. Sun Chanthol addressed the management and representatives of the company who attended this morning's meeting.
This evening, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will leave Geneva for Cambodia after completing his work there.
