(Phnom Penh): The posting that "Cambodia rejects US assistance in repairing a building at Ream Naval Base" is untrue. This was confirmed by General Chhum Socheat after many journalists asked him about this issue.
"The allegations that" the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia has denied US assistance to repair the training and storage facilities of the Cambodian Naval Base "are completely untrue because the Ministry "The defense has never asked the United States to repair the building."
General Chhum Socheat confirmed that the training and storage building of the accused is not under the control of the Ream Naval Base, but the building of the National Committee for Maritime Security, which is temporarily located at the Ream Naval Base, which will be relocated. Hold a new place in the near future and there is no need for repairs yet.
"Regarding the letter from the Deputy Assistant Secretary of Defense of the United States, the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia also invited the Deputy Chief of Staff at the US Embassy to hear why Cambodia is not yet in need of US assistance," he said. The United States to repair the building as well.
A spokesman for the Ministry of National Defense urged all media outlets not to continue to comment on false information that could lead to confusion on the Cambodian Ministry of National Defense.
