The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, expressed his feelings at the 41st session of the UN Human Rights Council in Geneva, Switzerland on July 4, 2019. It is very unfortunate today that the human rights order has become a political tool for some powerful countries as an excuse to interfere in the sovereignty and independence of a weak country.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that some groups or institutions are not afraid to apply two standards to the assessment of the implementation of human rights in Cambodia to hinder development as well as destroy the honor of the Cambodian nation.
Samdech Techo said that it was strange that Cambodia was asked to strengthen democracy, respect for human rights and the rule of law, but when law enforcement authorities, some groups or institutions accused Cambodia of restricting freedom of expression. Worse, some countries and institutions have taken human rights hostage in connection with the provision of aid or economic benefits to Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "We are deeply saddened by the fact that human rights have now become a political tool for some powerful countries, or rather their new executive norms." "They are an excuse for interfering in the sovereignty and independence of a weak country."
On behalf of the people, the senior UN human rights official and member states stressed that Cambodia remains committed to strengthening close cooperation in a constructive partnership with the UN human rights mechanism. Nation and all stakeholders to better promote and protect human rights.
(Switzerland): "Cambodia in the pages of newspapers and reports compared to Cambodia is very different or sometimes very different." This is the original statement made by Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the 41st session of the UN Human Rights Council on July 4, 2019 in Geneva, Switzerland.
