Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated: "This is the reason why I put forward a" win-win policy "that brought to Cambodia a complete end to the war and the attainment of peace, national reunification. And complete national unity throughout the country for the first time at the end of 1998 in the history of Cambodia for the last several decades.
He emphasized that this was a peace achieved by Cambodia itself, without bloodshed, without the use of weapons or ammunition, and without outside orders or support. Peace has opened up opportunities for development in all areas.
Cambodia was formerly plagued and devastated by chronic war, national division, territorial division and insecurity everywhere, now a country of complete peace, national unity and territorial integrity, strong security and an attractive tourist destination. In the region and in the world, people live in peace and harmony, both in their families, in their communities, and in society as a whole.
Cambodia, once a killing field dominated by dictatorships and the most heinous crimes of the genocidal regime, has now become a land of freedom with a firm adherence to the principles of liberal multiparty democracy through the holding of elections. Regular, free, fair and just and a state that obeys the rule of law and all citizens have equal rights before the law.
Cambodia, formerly despised, besieged, and politically and economically isolated, is now an independent state with full sovereignty and territorial integrity, and is actively expanding its integration into the region's structure and structure. And the world, as well as playing an active, equal and equal role in all regional and international affairs.
"The Cambodian people have the right to receive information from all sources and to have the right to express their views on all topics," Hun Sen said. "I personally have a Facebook page, a forum for people from all walks of life to comment on my leadership on issues of local development, the misconduct of officials and authorities, and more."
As a government, we just ask that all expressions be made responsibly and that there is a separation between the right to express an opinion on an issue and insults, baseless accusations, and a window of reputation. "Name spreading false information, calling for the overthrow of a legitimate government that could lead to social unrest and division."
