(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chheang Vun, Chairman of the National Assembly Committee on Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation, Propaganda and Information, confirmed that the National Assembly will summon some other senior officials in the Royal Government to comment on the implementation of their work in the future. Coming soon after the parliament rejoins.
Speaking to Fresh News after the oral response of Mr. Ang Vong Vathana, Minister of Justice in the National Assembly on July 4, 2019, Mr. Chheang Vun confirmed: "Oh, come on. "Now, we will continue to rejoin the army, summon the ministers one after another, week after week, week after week, and the debate will be even deeper until the election."
Mr. Chheang Vun claimed that the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, had opened the way for the National Assembly to summon any minister or official of the Royal Government to comment on their actual performance, just to request the Minister of Justice to enter. To clarify in front of the National Assembly, Samdech immediately signed the agreement.
Mr. Chheang Vun added that the reason why the National Assembly summoned any minister or official to clarify is to prevent any minister or head of unit from doing his job loosely on any part of its jurisdiction assigned by the government. Give. Therefore, in the name of the National Assembly, the highest institution of the nation has the role of strengthening the rule of law, strengthening democracy, especially strengthening the well-being of the people as a whole.
At the same time, Mr. Chheang Vun revealed that after joining the army, the issue that the National Assembly wants to know is related to the management of banking and microfinance, which many people suffer from interest, false information, and some other issues. .
It should be informed that on July 4, the National Assembly summoned the Minister of Justice to address the National Assembly session regarding law enforcement. The summoning of the Minister of Justice was made at the request of the Sixth Committee of the National Assembly, chaired by Mr. Pen Panha.
This is the first time that the National Assembly of the 6th legislature has summoned the Minister of the Royal Government to comment on the performance of work since taking office for the new term one year ago. In the past, the summoning of ministers for clarification was often seen as active, but only the Supreme Advisory Council.
Ms. Michelle Bachelet made the remarks during a courtesy call and discussion on human rights issues with Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen on July 4, 2019 in Geneva, Switzerland. The meeting took place after Samdech Techo and the High Commissioner attended the 41st regular meeting of the UN Human Rights Council.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Ms. Michelle Bachelet, discussed many human rights issues in Cambodia, as well as some of Cambodia's efforts to improve human rights issues in Cambodia. The Prime Minister also highlighted that in the past, there has been a lot of painting on human rights issues in Cambodia, but Cambodia still strives to develop the country, adhere to democracy, protect and promote human rights.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that talking about human rights in Cambodia, especially during the Khmer Rouge era, had no rights at all. On the contrary, for now, Cambodia is full of rights.
The Prime Minister further stated that Samdech has done a lot of work to promote the development and promotion of human rights in Cambodia. Recently, Samdech has taken action to help women with grievances in the judiciary by setting up a group of volunteer lawyers to defend them for free. In addition, Samdech also increased the national budget for the Ministry of Women's Affairs as well as the Ministry of Justice to work on the case of women who lack lawyers.
The Prime Minister also stated that in the past, Samdech has given a lot of rights to women and in the past also set out a number of policies for social protection.
The UN High Commissioner for Human Rights, Michelle Bachelet, said at the meeting that much work needs to be done, including the empowerment of women. Especially related to economic issues that Cambodia has done a lot in the past.
In front of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the UN High Commissioner for Human Rights also thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia for always accepting recommendations to improve the human rights situation. She added that the High Commissioner for Human Rights is always ready to provide cooperation to improve human rights issues in Cambodia.
However, Ms. Michelle Bachelet confirmed to Samdech Techo Hun Sen that the High Commissioner for Human Rights recognizes that Samdech Techo's leadership has greatly improved, especially the economic and social rights of the people.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Prime Minister confirmed to the UN High Commissioner for Human Rights that he always welcomes the discussion on human rights issues in Cambodia. In this meeting, Samdech Techo also decided to sign an agreement every two years on the renewal of the Office of Human Rights of human rights organizations in Cambodia to avoid any worries.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo also invited the UN High Commissioner for Human Rights to visit Cambodia at an appropriate time. The High Commissioner has accepted the request and will visit at any convenient time.
