Preah Sihanouk Provincial Governor Asks Officials to Release Machinery to Restore Streams and Canals to Relieve Floods After Heavy Rain
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, continued to order the provincial officials and local authorities to continue the machinery to restore streams and canals at the corner of LV Bridge in Sangkat 4, Sihanoukville to relieve flooding after heavy rains. These days, one side of Sihanoukville was submerged.
According to the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration Officer in charge of the drainage and canal system, every day in Sihanoukville, there is flooding when there is heavy rain.
The official said that today's flooding was not the first time in Sihanoukville and that the floods were caused by the size of streams and canals, which were mostly narrowed due to the construction of houses. And other structures of some people have illegally encroached on the mouths of streams and canals.
Preah Sihanouk provincial administration officials continued that every day in Sihanoukville, there are some buildings built without underground drainage system and flooded with soil.
In addition, there is some rubbish floating around the mouth of the sewer, so the current does not lead to flooding, flooding of people's houses and some roads.
Officials said that currently, the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration has been working to solve the flood by using technical measures to bring machinery to open the waterway and take legal action against those who encroach on the mouth of the stream. And illegally owned canals to relieve flooding during heavy rains.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration officials believe that the activities of bringing machinery to dig canals, canals and the construction of underground drainage systems to release rainwater by the technical team of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration will be able to lead to flood relief in the city. Sihanouk will be successful in the near future.
