Tripoli: A UN official has considered an air strike on an immigration detention center that killed 44 people on the outskirts of Tripoli, Libya, a possible war crime. This was released by the BBC on Wednesday, July 3, 2019.
At least 44 people have been killed and more than 130 injured in an airstrike on a Tajoura detention center on the outskirts of Tripoli, according to Libyan authorities. Most of the victims were migrants being held in the Tajoura Detention Center, where 600 migrants are being held.
