Court orders detention of a man after causing a traffic accident that caused two deaths and injuries in Sangkat Kbal Koh, Khan Chbar Ampov
(Phnom Penh): Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Mr. Hong Sokonvathana, on July 3, 2019, issued an order to detain a man after causing a traffic accident that caused one death and one serious injury at In front of house No. 089, National Road No. 1, Sangkat Kbal Koh, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh.
The perpetrator, 24-year-old Va Vanny, a resident of Kampong Phnom village, Kampong Po commune, Leuk Dek district, Kandal province, was placed under investigation for "reckless driving, negligence, carelessness, causing death and injury". Articles 83 and 85 of the Law on Road Traffic.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Asks Finland to Increase Investment in Cambodia and Boost Bilateral Trade
At the beginning of the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Wilskin Nary discussed the purchase of generators for power generation in Cambodia. According to Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, in front of the Finnish Minister, thanked the Finnish company for selling the generator, which can generate up to 200 megawatts of electricity and emit less toxic fumes to solve the problem. Lack of energy in Cambodia.
The two counterparts also discussed strengthening ties and cooperation between the two countries. Regarding the strengthening of relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Finland, the Minister of Finland emphasized that Finland is seeking an honorary consul to help promote the relationship between Finland and Cambodia in the future.
In addition to strengthening relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Finland, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also focused on investing and expanding trade between the two countries.
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn stated that in this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested Mr. Wilskin Nary to visit Cambodia as well as advise Finnish investors to visit Cambodia to study and find investment opportunities in Cambodia.
In front of the Finnish Minister, Samdech Techo emphasized that at present, Cambodia buys and imports more products from Finland than Finland buys or imports Cambodian products to Finland. Samdech Techo told the Finnish Minister that he would like to see the trade volume between Cambodia and Finland increase in the future.
The Prime Minister said that Cambodia has natural resources, so Finland participates in investment and processing for export.
In this meeting, the Finnish Minister expressed his desire to invest in waste management in Cambodia. Regarding waste, Samdech Techo claimed that it is a sensitive issue in Cambodia, Samdech asked Finland to consider investing if there is interest. But Samdech Techo also reminded that the policy and position of the Royal Government of Cambodia is not to import waste from abroad and domestic waste to be produced into energy or paper.
During the meeting, the Prime Minister emphasized that he had visited Finland in 2006 as part of the Asia-Europe Meeting hosted by Finland. Through the Prime Minister, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his expectation that the Finnish leader will attend the Asia-Europe Summit 2020 in Phnom Penh.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also mentioned about Cambodia's rice exports to the EU market. Samdech asked Finland to support Cambodia's position in selling rice because Cambodia is the number one rice exporter to Europe. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also mentioned that the tax on Cambodian rice. Samdech Techo stated that this tax is not fair for Cambodia to compete in this free market.
The Prime Minister emphasized that ASEAN and the European Union are strategic partners together. It is important for these two areas to work together in the past as well as in the future. Samdech Techo confirmed to the Finnish Minister that the two sides are now negotiating to find ways to promote free trade between the two regions.
