Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Deputy Chief of Tbong Khmum Provincial Assistance Team and Chairman of Oreang District Assistance Team, accompanied by Deputy Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, led the team to meet with pig farmers in Mean commune after receiving Received information on the outbreak of African swine fever in Kampoul Serey village and Soy village in Mean commune, Oreang Leu district, Tbong Khmum province to check the actual situation and help solve problems for the people.
On this occasion, Mr. Eang Sophalleth also chaired a meeting to promote the implementation of the instructions of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and ready to cooperate with professional officials of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, who will visit tomorrow or not tomorrow.
In order to promote the effective implementation of the Prakas on the identification of African swine fever outbreaks and as a rule to prevent the spread of the disease to other areas, the Governor of Tbong Khmum Provincial Board of Governors and the Chairman of Tbong Khmum Provincial Administrative Unity Command Issue some necessary and urgent instructions as follows:
2: Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries shall appoint veterinary officers in cooperation with commune councils, village chiefs, village animal health agencies to compile statistics on the number of pig farming families, the number of pigs present in cages and the health status of both animals. In the outbreak area and within 3 km and 10 km radius.
3: O'Raing Ov District Administrative Unity Command, commune chiefs of all communes, administrative police officers, and village chiefs must support and cooperate with veterinary officers to educate and disseminate the Prakas on the identification of African swine fever outbreaks and the consequences of African swine fever. Animal health conditions in the breeding grounds and prevention of trade, transportation of animals in and out of the outbreak area.
4. All Unity Committees of Districts shall widely disseminate the consequences of African swine fever to the farmers' economy as well as the national economy within their jurisdiction and immediately report to the Tbong Khmum Provincial Veterinary Officer in case of sick pigs or Die to take timely and effective action.
5. All units stationed at the border with Vietnam must strengthen the ban and prevent the movement of pigs and all kinds of pig products across the border without a permit.
6: The owner of the slaughterhouse must cooperate with the veterinary officer to prevent the import of live pigs without a certificate of animal hygiene from the veterinary authority into the slaughterhouse and to advise the slaughter of pigs to buy pigs that come from areas without infectious diseases. Properly allowed and not allowed to kill pigs outside the slaughterhouse.
