JICA seeks to establish four Cambodian villages in Japan
(Phnom Penh): Japan is looking to establish four Cambodian villages in Japan so that Cambodians living and working in Japan can meet, communicate and live in the same environment as in their homeland. This statement was made during a working meeting between the representative of JICA Japan in Southeast Asia and Mr. Yeon, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, representing Mr. Vong Soth, Minister on July 3, 2019.
Mr. Yeon expressed his gratitude and appreciation for Japan's intention to establish a Cambodian village in Japan and to strengthen the skills of caring for the elderly. He considered that this is a great intention and that Cambodia will cooperate happily.
