However, Reuters, based on a source obtained from a senior US official at the Department of Commerce and Industry under the auspices of the US Department of Commerce, claimed that Huawei would remain on Washington's blacklist. The agency will also monitor the licenses of US companies planning to sell their products to Huawei.
(Battambang): The National Election Committee (NEC) held a meeting on the afternoon of July 3, 2019 to review the work of the third mandate council election in 2019 and to review the voter list and voter registration. 2019.
The ceremony was held in Battambang province under the presidency of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, and Mr. Sik Bun Hok, Chairman of the National Election Committee, as well as many other stakeholders.
The number of Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Council seats for the third mandate in 2019 is 4,114 seats, of which 559 are Capital / Provincial Council seats and 3,555 are Municipal / District / Khan Council seats. The constituencies are 11,572 commune / sangkat councilors.
Central Working Group Visits Sihanoukville to Hold Meeting to Discuss and Solve Some Necessary Challenges
(Preah Sihanouk): The Central Working Group for Sihanoukville, chaired by Mr. Tek Reth Samrech, this morning, July 3, 2019, organized a meeting of the Standing Committee of the Central Working Group for Sihanoukville to discuss and Find urgent solutions to some of the major challenges such as garbage, sewage and drainage canals, security, security, trademarks, illegal construction, road repairs and construction of Sihanoukville.
Regarding security and order, the President instructed the relevant parties to follow the recommendations and in-depth of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, during the inauguration ceremony of Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province on June 28, 2019. .
Regarding the issue of garbage and drainage canals and sewers, the meeting accepted the advice of Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, urging the signing of a contract with the garbage collection company as soon as possible and determine the company's plan and capacity for garbage collection. Clearly included in the contract to monitor the implementation of the company, both household waste and garbage from construction sites.
In addition, the Department of Environment is cooperating with local authorities to locate garbage containers in the four districts of Sihanoukville, which will facilitate garbage collection in the entire city. On the other hand, the Ministry of Environment has provided a 5-hectare location on the outskirts of the city to store garbage collected from the city before transporting it to a remote incinerator.
Drainage canals and sewers will be rehabilitated, garbage will be removed, and border posts will be erected to the canal's standard level to prevent encroachment, and drainage systems will be set up to facilitate sewage flow, avoid congestion and flooding. . Both jobs will be implemented soon.
Mr. Tek Reth Samrech also urged the authorities to instruct and order the construction site to close the fence and store garbage properly. Legal constructions must have a permit attached to the wall of the construction site, and illegal constructions will be dealt with severely in the future.
