Senior Mongolian official: Cambodia's disability sector has grown significantly, setting a good example for the Asia-Pacific region
(Phnom Penh): Mongolian Deputy Minister of Labor and Social Protection Un Bayat Gambosorin praised Cambodia's disability sector for its remarkable progress, which is a good example for the Asia-Pacific region.
This statement was made during a separate meeting of the 4th Asia-Pacific Conference on Environmental Development with Mr. Nhek Vannara, Secretary of State for the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, representing Minister Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation. On Tuesday, July 2, 2019 in Mongolia.
During the meeting, Mr. Nhek Vannara confirmed to Mr. Unobayat Gambo Sorin that Cambodia, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister, has taken great care of people with disabilities and has made rapid progress in this field. For the past 20 years, especially employment opportunities for people with disabilities in public institutions recruited 2% and the private sector recruited 1%.
Mr. Nhek Vannara praised the attention of the Cambodian delegation from the leaders and officials in charge of organizing the 4th Asia-Pacific Conference on Environmental Development and Community-Based Infrastructure Development. Disability, the elderly and pregnant women are also good examples for Cambodia.
At the same time, the Deputy Minister of Labor and Social Protection of Mongolia also commended and thanked Cambodia for sending a high-level delegation to the 4th Asia-Pacific Conference on Community-Based Development on this special occasion.
In addition, representatives of the two countries' leaders agreed to further strengthen ties on employment and disability as part of the promotion of respect for rights and sustainable development based on the principles of the Convention on the Rights of the Child. Disability and the Law on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities.
