Ministry of Economy and IMF hold 2-day workshop on "‹ Public Investment Management "
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of July 2, 2019, Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Acting Minister of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, presided over a workshop on "Public Investment Management" co-organized by the Ministry of Economy and Finance and International Monetary Fund (IMF).
The acting minister said that after the end of the civil war, all kinds of physical infrastructure was almost completely destroyed throughout the country. Public investment has served as an important means of building rural infrastructure, connectivity and other socio-economic infrastructure, which are essential foundations for the rehabilitation, construction, and development of the country.
This remarkable achievement is the result of the Royal Government's efforts to mobilize its own resources and invest itself. The size of this investment has been growing year by year. "As the demand for investment grows and the government is able to invest more, the key is to focus on efficiency," he said.
"It is true that although we do not yet have a comprehensive framework for managing public investment, in the past due to the Royal Government's efforts to regulate public investment, especially the Ministry of Economy and Finance," he said. "As a staff, our public investment, although small, has played an important role in sustaining economic growth and reducing poverty, as well as the development of the country as a whole."
In fact, we have seen that Cambodia's economic growth over the past 20 years has grown by an average of 7.7% per year, of which national investment, including foreign direct investment, is less than 30%. Prove that our use of resources is efficient. If we look at other countries, they invest about 40% -50% as national resources to achieve 7% economic growth, and sometimes even can not achieve this goal.
However, we are not yet happy with the results, and we still think that we are still lacking in terms of mechanisms, institutions, laws and human resources, as the demand for investment is growing and evolving more complex. Especially large investment projects. Therefore, public investment management is very important to ensure efficient use, efficient and transparent allocation of resources, transparency and sustainability.
1: Free training for about 70 unlicensed drivers at Phnom Penh Autonomous Port from Monday to Friday and driving test on Saturday. The next step will be implemented at Sihanoukville Autonomous Port.
2. Place two mobile technical inspection vehicles (checks) near the Phnom Penh Autonomous Port to check for vehicles that have not been inspected.
3: Car parking in Phnom Penh, all 5 locations will extend the service time until 10 pm to facilitate the technical inspection of vehicles in a timely manner.
It should be noted that the National Committee for Road Safety on June 15, 2019 decided to inspect the technical characteristics of vehicles and driver's licenses directly at the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port and Phnom Penh Autonomous Port. During the 15 days (June 15-30) of the operation, 1,954 vehicles were inspected at both ports and 224 illegal vehicles, or 11 percent, were found.
The operation to inspect the technical specifications of vehicles and driver's licenses to the two autonomous ports is a hot rule to prevent road accidents caused by large trucks after seeing that the accident rate of about 20% Caused by large trucks. The accident was caused by a technical problem with the vehicle and the negligence of the driver.
The operation, despite widespread acclaim from the public, has also created some challenges for investors and business people. That is, the inspection of vehicles that are not technically correct and the driver's license makes the car not technically sufficient or the driver without a driver's license, etc. do not dare to enter the port and lead to obstruction of the transport of goods.
