The meeting between Trump and Kim at the inter-Korean demilitarized zone on Sunday made Donald Trump the first incumbent US president to enter North Korean territory. The meeting was considered by the media, including North Korea, a historic one, with some experts expecting Kim to respond positively by considering Trump's visit to the United States.
North Korea, meanwhile, is well aware that only with nuclear weapons is it safe to talk to the United States. Moreover, Pyongyang could not trust Donald Trump 100 percent, with tens of thousands of US troops stationed in South Korea and Japan.
Simply put, the United States is unlikely to be able to withdraw troops from South Korea and Japan, as their military presence is also being monitored by both China and Russia, while North Korea will still have to keep nuclear weapons. Together to protect themselves.
