(Phnom Penh): The Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia (GMAC) has reminded all its members to use the services of transport companies to use trucks in full compliance with the Road Traffic Law to avoid congestion caused by goods. From vehicle technical inspection.
GMAC's call comes as the National Road Safety Committee is taking action to inspect vehicles and driver's licenses at the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port and the Phnom Penh Autonomous Port. The operation took place on June 15, 2019.
During the last 15 days of operation, the National Road Safety Committee inspected 1,954 vehicles at both ports and found 224 illegal vehicles, accounting for 11 percent.
In its open letter on July 2, 2019, the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia expressed 100% support for the implementation of the law of the National Road Safety Commission in order to prevent and reduce traffic accidents to a minimum. Max.
However, the Garment Manufacturers Association has requested Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, to take interim measures to restrict the implementation of the law on road traffic.
The association also requested the Royal Government of Cambodia to have a temporary solution with the Cambodian Transport Association regarding the enforcement of traffic laws of the National Road Safety Commission. In this open letter, the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia stated that its members have been unknowingly becoming victims of this problem.
At a press conference on vehicle and driver's license inspection operations on July 2, 2019, Mr. Seng Chhuon, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, claimed that the congestion at the port was caused by vehicles not obeying the law. The team also found that most of the illegal vehicles belonged to carriers with multiple vehicles.
General Him Yan, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police and a member of the National Road Safety Committee, also claimed that the inspection of vehicles at the port takes only one to two minutes if the vehicles have sufficient documents and technical specifications. Do not delay.
