(Svay Rieng): A deputy commander of the Chantrea District Gendarmerie, while riding a motorbike, suddenly a dog ran over and hit him, causing his immediate death on the spot. This unfortunate incident happened at 14:50 pm on July 1, 2019 along National Road No. 1 between km 142/143 in Doeum Po village, Svay Tayan commune, Kampong Ror district, Svay Rieng province.
Sources from the scene said that before the incident, a man was seen riding a motorcycle from west to east. When he arrived at the scene, suddenly a dog ran across the road and collided with a motorcycle, causing the man The driver fell head over heels on the road and died instantly on the spot.
According to the local police, the victim was named Kong Chhel, male, 53 years old, occupation: Gendarmerie, Deputy Commander, living in Po village, Mes Thnak commune, Chantrea district. The victim was driving a black 2016 Honda C125 with license plate number Svay Rieng 1H 6670 when he crashed into a dog and died at the scene, while the motorcycle was slightly damaged. The body was handed over to the family for traditional rites.
According to the source, the victim came to a meeting in the province while returning to the district and was killed in a traffic accident. The means of transportation were kept at the Svay Teap District Police Inspectorate.
