This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a high-level Cambodian delegation to attend the World Trade Summit in Switzerland.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, July 2, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, led a high-level delegation to attend a meeting on "Inspection". Global Review of Trade Assistance 2019 "will take place from 3 to 5 July 2019 at the World Trade Organization (WTO) in Geneva, Switzerland.
Accompanying Samdech Techo Prime Minister to Switzerland now include: Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and other senior government officials. According to a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, find out about Cambodia's activities at the World Trade Organization (WTO).
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will lead a high-level delegation to attend the "Global Review of Aid for Trade 2019" meeting to be held from 3 to 5 July 2019 at the World Trade Organization (WTO) in Geneva, Switzerland.
Cambodia applied for WTO membership on December 8, 1994. On December 21, 1994, the Working Group on Cambodia's Accession to the WTO was established. On 08 May 1999, the Memorandum of Understanding on Cambodia's Trade Policy was submitted to the WTO Secretariat. On October 13, 2004, Cambodia officially became a member of the WTO.
After becoming a member of the WTO, Cambodia has successfully reviewed its trade policy twice, the first on November 1-3, 2011 and the second on November 3, 2011. November 21-23, 2017 in accordance with the obligations. Cambodia was elected chair of the Coordinating Group of Least Developed Countries from early 2017 to early 2018.
Becoming a member of the World Trade Organization, Cambodia has gained many benefits, such as: Strengthening local policies and institutions through the reform of documents, regulations, laws and work programs after becoming a member of the WTO, creating an attractive environment. Investment and trade, as well as expanding export markets to many major markets.
As a member of the WTO, Cambodia has received special treatment and favors as a member of the Least Developed States. Cambodia also receives technical and financial assistance from the Integrated Framework (EIF) program under the WTO and international development partners, such as the World Bank, the Asian Development Bank and other international donors.
In fact, the first and second phase of the EIF program is helping Cambodia promote three priority tasks: trade facilitation, export diversification and competition. Due to this assistance, Cambodia conducted a series of Business Strategic Analysis (DTIS) studies in 2001, 2007, 2014 and updated the third Cambodia Integration Strategy Document 2019-2023 in line with the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4.
Cambodia is currently receiving technical assistance from the WTO and other donors to fully implement the Trade Facilitation Agreement (TFA) under the One-Stop-Shop Development Project led by the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
The WTO also assisted Cambodia in establishing an information center, which was inaugurated on March 13, 2017 as a training and research center for WTO-related information and international trade for government officials, the private sector, educational institutions and the public. General.
In order to increase efficiency and expand trade diplomacy with WTO members, with the request of the Ministry of Commerce and the approval of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia Permanent mission of the WTO and international organizations related to the economic and trade sector in Geneva on February 21, 2017.
The mission not only works with the 164-member WTO, but also with key trade-related organizations such as the 191-member International Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO), the United Nations Conference on Trade and Development. (UNCTAD) has 195 member countries, the International Trade Center (ITC), the United Nations Industrial Development Organization (UNIDO) and other international trade-related organizations.
Cambodia is the sixth of 10 ASEAN countries to have two ambassadors / ambassadors, one from the United Nations and other international organizations, and the other from the WTO and trade-related economic organizations.
Cambodia is currently continuing to play a key role as a member of the TROIKA, assisting the Central African Republic and the Chadian Republic in successfully coordinating a group of 36 least developed countries on WTO negotiations. More.
The mission coordinated with the World Intellectual Property Organization to bring Cambodia into membership in a number of treaties and agreements, as well as facilitated the registration of international brands under the Madrid system, with Cambodia receiving an annual budget of about $ 200,000.
Cambodia is participating in negotiations to take advantage of the preferential tariffs on the source of goods in the service sector and export duty-free and 100% non-quota on Cambodian products, in addition to the already provided by China, Japan in the amount of 97%. Of all items. Iran increases refining and reserves of uranium in retaliation for US sanctions
