(Phnom Penh): Yesterday, when I saw the news about the signing of a free trade agreement between the EU and Vietnam, I was overwhelmed and immediately raised the question of where to go to EU standards?
According to the agreement, both sides can trade freely, with no tariff barriers. As a Cambodian citizen, I would like to sincerely congratulate Vietnam, our neighbor, for reaching this agreement. But what I want to note now is just to find out and analyze the real elements of the so-called EU standards.
In fact, in this world, there is no justice, no standard, no friend, no right, there is only benefit. This is a well-known theory of international relations.
But what is happening in Cambodia and in Vietnam now is a lesson that Cambodian children must learn and remember:
Therefore, Cambodian politicians who like to take the issue of democracy and human rights to the situation in their country should wake up and should stop doing politics to destroy the nation and destroy the kitchen of their own people as they are doing today. This.
Therefore, those who strive for the Phnom Penh government to comply with European or American standards are only foolish demands, because where to go to European standards, where to go to American standards, because in reality, if they apply to other Cambodia and apply to other countries. Others like this? Being a politician who dances without knowing the rhythm is nothing but dragging the nation backwards or making it difficult to move forward.
All in all, going through the actual situation as mentioned above, I really understand the firm stance of Prime Minister Hun Sen, who has repeatedly stated that "do not trade national sovereignty for aid." On the other hand, the Phnom Penh government strives to attract and accept investment or assistance from all directions, without discrimination, communist or liberal bloc, that is, as long as it is beneficial to the national economy and the Cambodian family economy, it is acceptable to all.
