Free from studying! "Youth for Society" Continues to Develop a Buddhist Moral Education Program at Sok An Phnom High School, Kirivong District
(Takeo): In order to promote the field of Buddhism and to contribute to the promotion of knowledge for the Cambodian people to understand the virtues of parents, a group of students called "Youth for Society" continued to organize a moral education program in the Buddhist style to connect with society at Sok High School An Phnom, Kampeng commune, Kirivong district, Takeo province.
This program was held on Sunday 13 Roch Khe Ches Chhnang Kor Eksak BE 2563 on June 30, 2019 with the participation of partners in collaboration with the Organization of Children and Youth Education, Wat Varin Prek Leap Youth Group and Education, local authorities, philanthropists and a large number of young volunteers as well.
On behalf of the entire organizing committee, Venerable Hoy Mengteang said that Buddhism is an important part of active participation in education. He added that many monks are imparting knowledge, morals and ethics to the students, Buddhist education for peace, both physically and mentally, so that they can better understand the values of the Khmer nation, as well as Strive to obey your parents as well.
The monk, who represents the "Youth for Society" group, said that teaching children in the Buddhist way is part of the Buddhist path, which makes the path of the empire more prosperous. Progress in a country depends on the understanding of the children who are the next generation, when all children understand the value of family clearly, they will begin to become good citizens, which is the hope for the nation.
Venerable Hoy Mengteang added that Cambodian student volunteers really want to participate in the development of this society for the better, so this activity shows that young people do not remain silent or ignore society. That no. "Sacrifice, loyalty and redemption are the most important things we can do for all, for the community, for education," he said.
The Venerable also thanked and thanked all the monks and all the participants who were invited to participate in this event, as well as the philanthropists who donated both money and materials.
