Ms. Kim Nhor, Representative of Mr. Yon Min, Meets and Eats Solidarity Noodles with About 600 Mlup Tapang Children
(Preah Sihanouk): Ms. Kim Nhor, representative of Mr. Yon Min, former Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, this morning, July 1, 2019, met with about 600 children of Mlup Tapang in Sangkat 4, Preah Krong. Sihanouk. The event was also attended by the Red Cross branch and the Sihanoukville Women's Association.
According to Prak Chan Sokha, president of the Provincial Women's Association, the solidarity noodle gathering with staff and youth groups at the Mlup Tapang NGO Center was initiated by former Sihanoukville Governor Yon Min.
She said that in the past, Mr. Yon Min always took care to mobilize philanthropists to support the children in the center of Mlup Tapang. In addition to a solidarity meal with more than 600 children, a ton of rice and some drinks were donated by the Provincial Women's Association and the Sihanoukville Red Cross.
Mrs. Rath Chanpun, Director of Mlup Tapang Organization, thanked Mr. Yon Min, former Governor of Sihanoukville Province, for always supporting the mission of Mlup Tapang Organization in rescuing street children and vulnerable drug addicts to educate them. Get new opportunities for the future.
She stated that Mlup Tapang has a mission to help poor children and vulnerable youth throughout Sihanoukville without discrimination. The organization has collected and adapted them better. The director stated that for the children of Mlup Tapang, there is a curriculum for kindergarten and primary school.
Regarding these issues, she asked the provincial leaders and philanthropists to provide appropriate support and requested the Governor of Sihanoukville, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun to facilitate 1: improve the access road to the center, 2: Please facilitate the network Water and electricity to use enough and third: Ask for funding as possible. Khan 7 Makara authorities announced the search for relatives of a woman who died in a traffic accident (the body is kept at Wat Teuk Thla)
