An unidentified 68-year-old female passenger with no real address and address was hit by a motorbike and seriously injured. She was taken by ambulance to Calmette Hospital with serious injuries and died in an ambulance. In the hospital. The body is currently being taken to Wat Teuk Thla for a traditional ceremony.
"We would like to inquire about the relatives and family of the deceased, who has the following features: height about 1 meter 40, white, right finger, wearing a red, yellow, yellow and black striped shirt," he said. Etc.
If you have seen and know the above, please contact the Police Inspectorate of Khan 7 Makara, Tel: 012 988 018. International financial institutions and European countries increase support for the Royal Government's efforts to develop Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): While many developing countries are facing challenges in boosting economic growth to achieve their development goals, Cambodia has proudly attracted a significant amount of support from financial institutions. International and European countries.
On 18 June 2019, a representative of the Royal Government of Cambodia signed a second US $ 60 million Concessional Loan Agreement with a representative of the European Investment Bank (EIB) for the implementation of the “Water Treatment Plant Construction Project”. Saat Bak Kheng ”to complete its $ 100 million loan package, its first concessional loan to Cambodia through the Royal Government.
In late May, the World Bank Board also approved the Cambodia Partnership Framework, a program to support the Royal Government in achieving its development goals over the next five years with a credit package. More than $ 1 billion and more technical assistance.
The approval comes after a period of disruption in its operations in Cambodia, but was restored amidst the World Bank's vision, correct leadership, and practical achievements of the World Bank. He considered it a record to achieve high economic growth and environmentally friendly development.
The most interesting thing is that when approved, the US Representative spoke first and expressed full optimism and support for the government's efforts. The unanimous decision was made after a delegation from the World Bank Board of Directors visited in person to find out the facts and examine the progress of Cambodia.
The Asian Development Bank (ADB) has also completed its Country Partnership Strategy for the next five years, increasing its financing package to Cambodia by more than $ 300 million per year. Official approval of the document in August.
In addition, Germany, France, Sweden and several EU countries are in talks with the government to provide credit, grants, and additional technical support for new development projects that the government is You indicate the order of priority.
He added that it is difficult to find AI technology, which is a new technology for today. What he and his team consider and continue to research is that speaking, especially the Khmer language is still limited, so in the future his team will develop robots as smart as humans.
The Khmer Kids Robotics Group also thanked the Ministry of Labor as well as all stakeholders for their support and assistance in the process of building the robot and requested the Ministry and other stakeholders to continue to provide support in order to be able to Can continue to study, research and find new technologies.
