Driving by car owner named Deng Van, Male, 38 years old, Nationality Khmer, Nationality Khmer, Occupation: Trader "Lok Do", Residence: Sos Village, Sdao Commune, Sangkum Thmei District, Preah Vihear Province.
Colonel Lahn Ly Sivleng, Kulen District Police Inspector, said that before the incident, the victim was driving a fuel truck as usual, intended to sell in Sangkum Thmey district, but due to a tire accident, the victim drove to pump air. When the air pump is pumped, the spare car is turned on and the power cable passes from the battery head, causing a fire.
He said that after the incident, the police took a fire truck to intervene, spraying water, but could not help extinguish the fire because of the power of gasoline and diesel on the car too much.
He said that in this incident, caused the fire of 1 car, 25 barrels of diesel, 1 barrel of 30 liters equal to 750 liters, 2 cans of gasoline equal to 440 liters, 30 cases of beer, 20 cases of fruit juice and car related documents.
Takeo Provincial Commissioner issues additional orders to police throughout the province to increase security, order and safety for the people
(Takeo): On the morning of July 1, 2019, Major General Sok Samnang, Takeo Provincial Police Commissioner, held a meeting to review the situation and the results of cooperation in maintaining security and social order in June and the direction of implementation in July 2019 at Takeo Provincial Police Hall.
During the meeting, Mr. Snarngkar mentioned the results, achieved the challenges and set the direction to continue the work of strengthening the discipline of the forces, as well as disseminated the recommendations of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and the new regulations of General Santibandit Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner.
Finally, the Major General advised the Inspector, Deputy Inspector, the Post Chief to fulfill the tasks assigned by his superiors to be more successful and more effective. Phnom Penh Governor Urges Monks and Buddhists to Work Together for Peace to Ensure Cambodia's Further Development
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, urged monks and Buddhists to work together to maintain peace in order to ensure that Cambodia is more developed and prosperous, so that people can live in warmth, prosperity and without any disturbance. Obey religious beliefs.
Mr. Khuong Sreng's encouragement in the Buddhist moral education program to baptize more than 560 children at Wat Phneat Samplei with the participation of hundreds of government officials and Buddhists on the afternoon of June 30, 2019 .
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has been building peace for Cambodia so far with great difficulty. Therefore, we must work together to maintain this peace in any form, so that no unscrupulous person can forget to destroy this peace.
At the same time, Mr. Khuong Sreng urged all monks to play a stronger role in educating society for peace, non-violence, while the field of Buddhism is flourishing and the country is peaceful and politically stable. Good.
He added that the Royal Government considers monks to play an important role in contributing to a peaceful and non-violent society. He added that the Royal Government has encouraged monks to educate society through Buddhist programs linked to society, which are broadcast on all radio and television stations.
Samdech Preah Moha Sometheathipadei Kitti Utstes, Dr. Non Nget, said that now all monks have obeyed the Dharma, Discipline and study to have a deeper knowledge, both secular and moral, to help educate the minds of the people to live. In a peaceful society, there is no resentment and love for each other and the use of vices against social law.
