Senior Minister Ly Thuch told Korea that Samdech Techo Hun Sen highly valued and considered the education sector in Cambodia as a bridge towards building a prosperous future nation.
(Phnom Penh): On July 1, 2019, Senior Minister Ly Thuch presided over the handing over ceremony of a five-room school building in Trapeang Prasat Primary School, Sangkat Trapeang Krasaing, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh. JEJU of the Republic of Korea via live.
The Senior Minister also thanked the leaders and members of the YMCA-JEJU for joining the Humanitarian Solidarity Force to promote education in Cambodia.
On behalf of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the Senior Minister expressed his deep gratitude to all teachers who have contributed to building the society through the education and training of human resources in Cambodia, especially teachers. And taking care to teach students to become good children, good friends and good students to become bamboo shoots for the next generation of Cambodian children.
The Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo, highly appreciated and strongly supported the education sector, considering the education sector as a bridge towards building a prosperous future nation, in which the lives of teachers were also improved. Resolve well.
The Spokesperson welcomed and applauded the principle agreement reached by the President of the People's Republic of China Xi Jinping and US President Donald Trump on the sidelines of the formal meeting in the resumption of talks aimed at strengthening Bilateral free trade.
The Spokesperson also noted that the participation of the United Nations, as well as the World Trade Organization and the leaders of key industrialized countries in the G20 Summit from 28 to 29 June 2019 in Osaka, Japan, has shown a growing interest in contributing to sustainable global development.
The Spokesperson praised the achievements of the G20 Summit, covering a number of key agendas, such as free trade, climate change, technology for development, as well as environmental considerations and other topics.
The Spokesperson for the Korean Peninsula Evolution Unit highly appreciated the meeting between South Korean President Moon Jae-in and US President Donald Trump this weekend, also highlighting the contribution for the benefit of The Korean Peninsula, as well as world security.
The Spokesperson also reminded that Cambodia under the strong and skillful leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has successfully transformed the Cambodian border from a battlefield into a border of peace, cooperation and common development.
