Samdech Techo Hun Sen has expressed his determination that Cambodia will not bow to the teachings of others on human rights issues, because in some places, people are being killed by bombs and shells fired from planes almost every day, but they do not. Considered human rights issues. Senior health official: Counterfeit and substandard medicines as hidden weapons can kill and hurt the economy
(Siem Reap): Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, said that counterfeit and substandard medicines are hidden weapons that can kill people silently and seriously affect the family economy and society.
At the same time, to ensure the quality, safety and effectiveness of medicines, all ASEAN drug authorities need to work together to combat counterfeit and substandard medicines.
This statement was made by the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health during a meeting on "Strengthening Regional Cooperation in Combating Counterfeit and Substandard Medicines" on July 1-2, 2019 in Siem Reap.
In addition, the Ministry of Health of Cambodia, in its capacity as chair of the ASEAN Senior Officials Meeting on Health (SOMHD), has partnered with the World Health Organization (WHO) to review the existing legal framework. ASEAN member states seek joint mechanisms to increase operational capacity against counterfeit and substandard drugs and strengthen existing governance mechanisms to address complex issues related to drug quality.
"Counterfeit and substandard medicines are hidden weapons that can quietly kill people and seriously damage the family economy and society," she said. "Therefore, in order to ensure the quality, safety and effectiveness of medicines, all ASEAN drug authorities need to work together to combat counterfeit and substandard medicines."
