It should be noted that at present, Krousar Thmey School for the Blind and Deaf is divided into two parts: Special Education High School and National Institute of Special Education, and this school has 5 locations with a total management board of 890 teachers and students. There are 702 students, 286 females, 162 blind students, 61 females and a total of 540 deaf students, 225 females.
The school was first established in 1991, and over the past 20 years, the program for educating blind and deaf children has been active and constantly evolving thanks to the Royal Government of Cambodia. In particular, Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Samdech Kittipritthbandit have always provided a lot of valuable support to Krousar Thmey for running the program forever.
Samdech continued, "At least when all the ammunition fell on Hang Chuon Naron, all of a sudden they withdrew?" No, ”he said. Inter-ministerial to tighten measures to encourage tourism ferry operators to implement tax payments
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism and relevant ministries and institutions have agreed to establish an inter-ministerial commission to strengthen the implementation of the law on tourism ferry operators, promote the payment of taxes to the state and strengthen security for tourists properly.
Mr. Chea Bora said that the components that will join the inter-ministerial committee include: Ministry of Tourism, Ministry of Public Works and Transport, Ministry of Economy and Finance, General Department of Taxation, General Commissioner of National Police, General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia and relevant departments and units. Some more.
After the meeting, Mr. Chhun Makara, Director of the Department of Agency Management and Tourism of the Ministry of Tourism, said that there are currently 124 tourist boats across the country (Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville), including 16 business licenses and licenses. Thirty-five temporary vessels, but all of those cruise ships have not yet been taxed.
He said that the temporary license is given to businesses that do not have enough legal documents, leaving only 90 days, but if there are still not enough documents, the Ministry will not renew.
Mr. Chhun Makara said that the tax payment to the state will apply to all types of tourist ferries doing business in the country, while Mr. Chea Bora also mentioned in the meeting that this time there will be restrictions on those traders must come. Pay import tax on their vehicles because there have been many soft compromises in the past, but the dealers still refuse to follow the law.
Mr. Chhun Makara also informed that for the tourist ferry business that wants to create new or old traders who want to expand their business, they must have the correct tax payment documents from the Customs and Excise Department and have the vehicle technical inspection certificate from the Ministry of Public Works provided by the Ministry of Tourism. Provide tourism licenses and standard evaluation services for tourism services, which means allowing traders to conduct their business.
In the face of this important work, the inter-ministerial working group also agreed to include indicators related to the management of port standards and the improvement of the aesthetics of the environment, sanitation, garbage and so on.
On the other hand, since there has been a case of a tourist ferry sinking in Sihanoukville in the past, the inter-ministerial working group will also promote safety for guests. The case of the sinking of a tourist ferry in Sihanoukville did not cause any harm to tourists, as the tourists had already disembarked before the incident.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Se, Prime Minister of Cambodia, this morning, July 1, 18,725 pregnant women, midwives and women under 2 years of age received social protection policies. The duration of this funding program.
This statement was made by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the meeting with the management, teachers and students of the School for the Blind and Deaf of Krousar Thmey and the transfer of the school to the Ministry of Education. Youth and sports.
Through the social protection policy of the program, financial support for women from poor families from pregnancy to children under the age of two will help reduce the number of children with intellectual disabilities. Acne, too.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasizes that the implementation of the program to support women from poor families from pregnancy to child under two years of age is not a coincidence, but a serious consideration to want people Our citizens are healthy.
According to a joint statement from the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Ministry of Health, the 760,000 Riel program is divided into three phases. The first stage is during pregnancy is to pay 4 times 40,000 Riel, the second stage is to give 200,000 Riel at birth and the third stage is after childbirth until the child under two. The year is to pay 10 times 40,000 riels at a time.
In case of pregnancy and miscarriage, support is also provided. In that, if the unborn child is 12 weeks old, he / she will receive a subsidy of 40,000 Riels at a time. If the miscarried child is between 12 weeks and 24 weeks old, he / she will receive a subsidy of 40,000 Riels twice.
The Royal Government will also support cases where a baby is born but dies. In this case, receive 200,000 Riels during childbirth and 40,000 Riels three times during the medical examination.
In the case of postpartum mother death, the money is donated to the legal guardian. The budget is to provide 200,000 Riels at the time of delivery and to be given 10 times 40,000 Riels at a time when taking the child to receive health care services until the child is 2 years old.
