Later, the police arrested him and brought him to the Daun Penh district police inspector for questioning. When the police questioned the suspect, he confessed that he took the drugs from a motodup driver and distributed them in a small package worth 15,000,000 Riel. Large package worth 25,000,000 Riels.
At present, the above suspects, together with the exhibits, are in charge of building the case and proceeding according to the legal procedure. Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association (TYDA) Participates in Raising Awareness on Drug Dangers to Vulnerable Communities
(Phnom Penh): This weekend, the community team of Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association (TYDA) in collaboration with the Department of Mental Health and Drug Abuse and Tuol Kork District Authority launched a campaign to raise awareness about the dangers of drugs. Addicted to vulnerable communities along the railway line of Sangkat Boeung Kak 1, Boeung Kak 2 and Teuk Laak 2, and also sent 3 drug victims to continue treatment.
In this campaign, a team of 45 doctors and volunteers conducted health education and drug awareness to the community of women victims and distributed 630 packs of medicine for diarrhea, headache, fever, 310 books and pens. 240 trees.
