Korea Wants to Establish National Center for Aesthetic Science in Cambodia to Provide Quality and Safe Aesthetic Education
(Phnom Penh): A large association of the Republic of Korea has expressed its intention to establish a "National Standards Center for Aesthetic Sciences" in Cambodia to provide quality and effective education, training, beauty skills to young people, especially safety for clients in Cambodia and in the region. Well.
This statement was made during a working meeting between Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training and a delegation from the International Association of Education in the field of beauty education of South Korea led by Mr. Harry Hwang on the morning of July 1. 2019 at the office of the Ministry of Labor.
On that occasion, Mr. Lee Sung Yeob, Representative of the International Association for Education in the field of beauty of South Korea, said that his visit to Cambodia is to show the intention to invest in the establishment of the "National Center for Aesthetic Science". Because he saw the potential of the beauty sector in Cambodia is reviving, which can establish international cooperation in this field.
Mr. Lee claimed that his association has been successfully operating in the field of beauty around the world, with many member institutions in countries such as South Korea, Japan, Hong Kong, Australia, New Zealand, Canada and the United States. And so on.
Lee sought the permission of the Minister of Labor and Vocational Training to set up the investment project, promising that if the investment project were to work, Cambodians and locals would benefit. High quality, efficient and safe beauty services through education and training of beauty service providers from Korean experts and experts from partner institutions.
In response, Mr. Ith Sam Heng fully welcomed and supported the project of establishing this center, especially HE Dr. Minister ensured the issuance of a license to the center to operate legally.
The Minister encouraged that the opening of the National Center for Aesthetic Sciences in Cambodia will receive attention as well as respond to the current market for beauty services, as the Cambodian economy is still growing and people's livelihoods are still growing. Seeking beauty services is also in constant demand.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng stated that if this investment project can work, Cambodia and South Korea will achieve a new cooperation to contribute to strengthening the relationship between the Royal Government and the government, people and people. Kratie Military Commander Distributes School Supplies to Over 400 Students at Kratie City Orussey 1 Primary School
