"Reach Sey" Company Restores the Siem Reap River Without Legal Laws and Korean Projects Destroy the River Bank and Trees, Mr. Tea Seiha Takes Strict Action Against the Company
(Siem Reap): On the afternoon of Sunday, June 30, 2019, the Joint Provincial Committee led by Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap Province, inspected the condition of the river restoration of "Reach Sey" Company, which carried out the technical rehabilitation of the river. And projects of the Republic of Korea. In fact, this project will start to open the restoration site in late 2019 or early 2020.
The inspection was also attended by the Director of Administration, Provincial Hall, Inter-sectoral management, leaders of relevant departments, specialized units, municipal authorities and commune chiefs.
Mr. May Samet, Chief of Siem Reap Commune, said that according to the monitoring of the Siem Reap River Restoration Activity in the second phase of the company, there were irregular activities that were technically wrong from the Korean project by the company digging the soil from the riverbank. Put it somewhere else by the river or sell it for a plot of land to make an apartment. These are the problems that the commune hall reports to the city hall to take measures to prevent this activity.
According to a city official, who asked not to be named, the rehabilitation of the river is a project of the provincial Department of Economy and Finance to solve the flood problem in this rainy season, which will have to rehabilitate parts of the Siem Reap River. The water flows quickly to avoid water blockage that can cause flooding in Siem Reap. But the company has not received any plans to restore the river.
Mr. Tea Seiha also confirmed that the project will start in late 2019 or early 2020, but for the project that Reachsey company is implementing, the province does not know. On the other hand, the company's excavation along the river bank, according to the inspection that there is no project documents to restore the river.
In that, he also asked the company, does the company understand the technique of digging to restore the river? But what the company is doing now is digging the ground for business, as well as destroying trees, which are important to prevent runoff, erode riverbanks and prevent runoff during the rainy season.
On that occasion, the provincial governor also stressed that the Reachsey Company must re-prepare the land along the river bank in accordance with the project of Chaika.
He also set some measures for the relevant departments to cooperate in the implementation of this project, as well as to store the company's machinery to deal with and find out the source that led to the placement. These machines came to do this work because the provincial authorities have not yet opened the construction site, this seems to be an insult to the provincial authorities.
In that, he also expressed his sorrow for the trees that were dug up and destroyed to fall into the river without any natural resources at all.
According to some residents who live along the river, it is okay to dig the river to build a road along the river, but this is to dig the river to sell to the seller to split the land for sale. They also asked the authorities to take strict and responsible measures against the company that dares to violate the law and destroy the environment of the trees that grow along the river.
