(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, July 14, 2019, tomorrow, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cross. The Cambodian Red Cross will hold talks with the management, teachers and students of Krousar Thmey School for the Blind and Deaf and transfer the management of the school to the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
Krousar Thmey School for the Blind and Deaf was first established in 1991 as the "National Center for Education for the Blind and Deaf". The center is also a training center for teachers for the blind and deaf, as well as a place to publish and produce educational materials for the blind and deaf.
In 1993, Krousar Thmey initiated the first educational process for blind children in Cambodia, with Ms. Phalla as the management team at Chbar Ampov School for the Deaf.
Later, due to the large number of students with disabilities in the provinces and the need for education for blind and deaf children, Krousar Thmey opened a series of schools such as schools for the blind and deaf children in Battambang in 1996. Chbar Ampov School for the Deaf in 1997, Siem Reap School for the Deaf and Blind in 2001 and Kampong Cham School for the Blind and Deaf in 2002.
Ros Sovacha, spokesman for the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, told Fresh News that Krousar Thmey's School for the Blind and Deaf is currently divided into two sections: the Special Education High School and the National Institute of Special Education. The five schools have a management team, teachers and a total of 890 students. There are 702 students, 286 females, 162 blind students, 61 females and a total of 540 deaf students, 225 females.
Over the past 20 years, educational programs for blind and deaf children have been active and constantly evolving due to the high attention paid by the Royal Government of Cambodia. In particular, Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Samdech Kittipritthbandit have always provided a lot of valuable support to Krousar Thmey for running the program forever.
Every year, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit always invite or send representatives to meet and prepare food for blind and deaf children in these schools.
