(Phnom Penh): West View Cambodia International School, an extension to the secondary school from Learning Jungle International School, has officially launched on the same day with a graduation ceremony and student performances to raise funds for the hospital. Kantha Bopha presided over by Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports.
According to the press release of WestView Cambodia International School, which was received by Fresh News on July 1, 2019, WestView Cambodia International School stands on the standard of quality education and sharpens students to be able to compete in District and on the international stage.
In addition, WestView Cambodia International School has a curriculum director and a team of teachers with more than 10 years of teaching licenses and more than 10 years of secondary school teaching experience from the United States and abroad.
In early June, the school received a license from the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports for an international curriculum, and now WestView Cambodia International School is a candidate for accreditation from an international school quality assessment body to provide opportunities for students. West View School attends world famous universities.
Currently, WestView International School of Cambodia is located next to Learning Jungle International School, Primary Branch, located at 254AK, Street 598, Sangkat Toul Sangke, Khan Russey Keo. WestView Cambodia International School students will start school in early August 2019.
The school is also building its second new location on an area of more than 10,000 square meters, just 5 minutes from Aeon Mall Sen Sok. The new facility will be equipped with state-of-the-art facilities in line with international study standards and can accommodate more than 1,000 students, as well as a swimming pool, gymnasium, meeting room for up to 300 people, staff accommodation and Students as well.
In addition, on that occasion, the school celebrated the great achievements of the students who successfully completed the kindergarten level at Learning Jungle International School. This successful result was achieved due to the good support and cooperation from all parents and the hard work commitment of the staff at the school.
Learning Jungle International School also initiated a fundraising program, with a total of $ 5,000 from ticket sales, student performances, and funding from the management of WestView Cambodia International School and four Learning Jungle International Schools. Thousands of dollars, a total of 9,000 dollars to be donated to Kantha Bopha Hospital.
Mr. Ly Virak, Chairman of the Board of Directors of both schools and on behalf of all staff, would like to thank all the parents and guardians for their strong trust in both schools and for giving them the opportunity to Take care of and teach your children from the beginning until today and in the future. The Russian S-400 missile system will arrive in Turkey in the next 10 days, according to Erdogan.
