Samdech Picheay Sena Tea Banh: Golf in Cambodia is developing remarkably in order to build its capacity and quality of sports to be better and stronger
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Defense and President of the Golf Federation of Cambodia, on June 30, 2019, confirmed that currently, Cambodian golf is developing remarkably. Mark in the goal of preparing to build their ability and quality of sports to be better and stronger.
This statement was made by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh on the occasion of Samdech Pich Sena's participation in a friendly golf tournament to celebrate the 60th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Indonesia, which was held at the tennis court. Koulgen Phnom Penh, Phnom Penh, this morning, June 30, 2019.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh stated that "Currently, Cambodian golf has been developing remarkably in order to build its capacity and quality of sports to be stronger in accordance with the strategic plan of the Royal Government. "Towards hosting the 2023 SEA Games."
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh also said that this year 2019 is the 60th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the two countries, Cambodia - Indonesia.
Samdech Pich Sena continued that in the past 60 years, Indonesia has been actively involved at both the regional and global levels, especially contributing to the search for peace in Cambodia by sending Blue Hat troops to protect peace during the election. UNTAC, co-chair of the Paris Peace Talks in 1993, assisted in training and developing human resources in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
At the same time, the Minister of National Defense said that the relations between the two countries are constantly developing in all fields, in which the two countries' defense fields have continuously strengthened close cooperation in training and capacity building. People.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh emphasized, "In recent years, the trade between the two countries has increased steadily, in 2017, the size of the economy increased to 539 million US dollars, and in 2018 increased. Up to 558 million US dollars.
At the same time, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh strongly believes that after today's friendly golf tournament, the cooperation between Cambodia and Indonesia will grow in all fields, including economy, defense, education, etc.
