A local company plans to plant 10,000 hectares of bamboo and set up a factory to process bamboo into materials and furniture to supply local needs and export
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, this morning, June 30, 2019, accompanied by his colleagues, visited Pratheat commune, Oreang O district, Tbong Khmum province to plant bamboo as a symbol with An Madi Group.
The Minister's symbolic bamboo planting activity is to reassure the public that the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, with the Forestry Administration as its staff, has begun implementing the Law on the Establishment of the International Network for Bamboo and Rattan. Approved by the Senate on June 25, 2019.
Mr. Oknha An Madi informed the Minister that, realizing the potential of bamboo production and to participate in the development of bamboo production in accordance with the content of the above law, the company planted bamboo on 25 hectares for seed, then planned to plant as production. 10,000 hectares of land and set up a factory to process various materials and furniture to supply domestic demand and export.
On this occasion, the Minister highly appreciated the willingness of the President of the company to participate in the development of bamboo production through industrial bamboo cultivation to complete the production chain of bamboo from seed production, processing and export.
This investment project is responding to the agricultural development policy 2019-2023 and especially actively participates in the implementation of the law on "Establishment of the International Network for Bamboo and Rattan". On the other hand, this project will contribute to the sustainable development of bamboo resources, benefit society, economy, brotherhood, green environment and create forest cover.
