(Ottawa): The 69 container ships that Canada chartered late last month to bring its garbage back from the Philippines have finally returned to Canada, ending the problem. The garbage dispute that has been raging since 2013 and has made the two countries look at each other in recent months. This is according to a quote from Reuters on Sunday morning, June 30, 2019.
The scam began in 2013 and 2014, when a Canadian company shipped several containers of counterfeit plastic labels to the Philippines.
