During the meeting held on June 26, 2019, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon expressed his satisfaction with the relationship between Cambodia and Germany over the past four years, which is reflected in the strong trade relationship. Strongest among European countries, high-level exchanges of visits and regular consultations, especially for development cooperation.
The Deputy Prime Minister thanked the German government and people for their assistance to Cambodia in areas such as agriculture, health, demining, decentralization and rural development. He also thanked the Ambassador for his personal efforts in the past term.
In response, the Ambassador expressed his satisfaction with the work in Cambodia, from the beginning of his term. He witnessed Cambodia's progress in the economic and social spheres, and Germany is a long-term partner of Cambodia.
He noted the success of the consultations, and Germany increased its development assistance to Cambodia. At the same time, more and more German companies are interested in investing in Cambodia, such as in the electricity sector, which is a sign of the need for development. Germany has also provided scholarships for the training of young diplomats in Cambodia, bringing the total to 13 so far.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon says Germany has provided forty-eight million six hundred thousand euros in grants and concessional loans for poverty reduction projects in Cambodia from 2019-2020. The trade volume between the two countries is estimated at $ 1 billion, with German tourists receiving more than 100,000 a year.
Regarding the EBA issue, the Deputy Prime Minister informed the Ambassador that the Royal Government is working with the European Commission to maintain the EBA for Cambodia by arranging for a European Commission mission to Cambodia earlier this month.
In this regard, the Ambassador was pleased to note that the Royal Government has worked hard to increase workers' salaries and maternity leave as part of social protection.
The Deputy Prime Minister said that the Royal Government is committed to strengthening democracy, freedom of the press and civil society unions, which so far have pardoned union leaders and established a forum for consultation with civil society.
At the same time, the German ambassador was impressed by Samdech Techo Prime Minister's statement that he always discussed with the opposition.
In regional cooperation, the Ambassador said that the European Union is very interested in ASEAN and wants to expand relations with ASEAN beyond the economic sector to politics and security.
The Deputy Prime Minister and the Ambassador agreed to continue discussions to reach a Memorandum of Understanding between the two Ministries of Foreign Affairs and to continue to support each other in multilateral mechanisms such as the United Nations. And UNESCO.
