(Phnom Penh): Female tiger mosquitoes are commonly known as carriers of dengue fever and have been causing great concern for 2019 because it is the year of the tiger mosquito breeding cycle and lead to dengue fever. Bleeding also occurs in many cases. In the first six months of 2019, there were about 13,000 cases of dengue fever caused by leopard mosquitoes and about 24 cases.
In addition to causing dengue fever, leopard mosquitoes also cause Zika and rheumatoid arthritis. This was confirmed by Dr. Huy Rekul, President of the National Center for Malaria Control, Parasitology and Anthropology.
To prevent the spread of dengue fever, measures to prevent the spread of tiger mosquitoes and how to prevent tiger tiger bites are one of the most important measures. To prevent and get rid of tiger mosquitoes, we should first learn about the origin and lifestyle of tiger mosquitoes.
At a recent press conference on dengue fever organized by the Royal Government Spokesperson, Dr. Huy Rekul, President of the National Center for Malaria Control, Parasitology and Botany, shared his knowledge about the tiger mosquito as follows:
Climate factors are also a common cause of tiger mosquitoes. If the temperature rises by one degree, the chance of developing dengue fever is 20%. One millimeter of rainfall increases the incidence of dengue fever by 30 percent. In the rainy season, dengue fever occurs twice as much as in the dry season, that is, the presence of tiger mosquitoes is the dengue virus.
Participating in the prevention of tiger mosquitoes is an effective way to prevent dengue fever. Dr. Huy Rekul also suggested some ways to prevent the formation of tiger mosquitoes.
Dr. Hul Rekul advised that in order to prevent the presence of tiger mosquitoes, business owners involved in the tires of motorcycles, motorcycles must be stacked properly, cover the board to ensure that no water can go into the shell. Or find a mosquito net to cover the tires.
In people's homes, all sources that lead to flooding must be collected and buried. The forest around the house must be cut down, the house must be tidy so that it does not become a mosquito shelter, and the windows of the house should be opened with enough light.
Putting abattoirs and BTIs in water bottles is also a way to get rid of tiger mosquitoes. In the first six months of 2019, about 184 tons of medicine have been distributed to the people, and in 2019, the Ministry is preparing up to 300 tons of medicine to be distributed to the people.
Spraying is also a way to get rid of tiger mosquitoes. But this way, the Ministry does not encourage because spraying it also affects the health of the people.
Dr. Huy Rekol also advised that parents or relatives should immediately send their children or relatives to a public hospital if there is a suspicion of dengue fever. Rekul claimed that if there was a delay or delay for several days, doctors could not save.
