Mr. Te Sophal also revealed that Angkor Coffee is unique in that it is a coffee grown locally, not imported, that is, coffee grown in Mondulkiri province. Angkor coffee is grown and refined in a natural way and is imported from one of the world's top quality coffee producing countries.
He also revealed that there are four factors that make the coffee grown in Mondulkiri province is not inferior to coffee imported from abroad:
* 1. Topography: The topography of Mondulkiri is a kind of red soil and the most favorable topography for coffee. Even more special is the type of soil that is naturally fertile and conducive to coffee.
* Second. Rainfall: Mondulkiri is a province covered by most of the forest, which is a factor that can attract a lot of rain in that area. The fact that this area has more rainfall than other areas and makes this area really favorable for coffee cultivation.
* Fourth. Climate: Due to the high altitude, this province is famous as a province with cool weather almost all year round.
Mr. Te Sophal It is important to help buy and use Cambodian products, and it is even more important if Cambodian products can compete with foreign products or be superior to neighboring countries. In the mission to promote local products, Angkor Coffee has been preparing to launch new product packages that can be purchased at major supermarkets in Phnom Penh soon.
