Mr. Vong Soth led nearly 2,000 party members to celebrate the 68th anniversary of the founding of the CPP in Ponhea Krek district, Tbong Khmum province, nearly two thousand new party members were announced
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Vong Soth, Chairman of the Central Working Group visited Ponhea Krek District, Tbong Khmum Province, and she led nearly 2,000 party members to celebrate the 68th anniversary of the founding of the Cambodian People's Party (June 28, 1951 - June 28, 2019) in the district. Ponhea Krek, Tbong Khmum Province, held on June 29, 2019 at the party headquarters of Ponhea Krek district. On that occasion, nearly 2,000 members of the Cambodian People's Party were also recognized.
Addressing nearly 2,000 members, Mr. Vong Soth, Chairman of the Working Group, gave a brief history of the founding of the Cambodian People's Party on June 28, 1951, under the original name "Revolutionary People's Party". "Khmer" then in 1991 changed its name to the "Cambodian People's Party."
He added that Cambodia has now adopted a free market economy, stabilizing national economic growth and, through this growth, equitable distribution of resources and transparency. Encourage and support the development of the private sector because it is the engine of national economic growth, create jobs, create jobs, increase income for farming families.
Mr. Vong Soth confirmed to the members that the Cambodian People's Party under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen is committed to continue to build, protect and develop the nation for continuous progress to meet the needs of the people in the 2018-2023 mandate. And achieve development goals in all areas with efficiency, equity and sustainability.
In addition, Mr. Vong Soth called on all members to continue to strengthen and expand social services for the vulnerable, improve the living conditions of the people and continue to promote Cambodia's integration with the international community in the regional and global framework. . Continue to stand firm in maintaining the great and invaluable achievements of the society, especially peace and political stability.
Unusual! Three young Cambodian children from former workers in Korea become the owners of Borey in Kampong Thom province
(Kampong Thom): Three young Cambodian children who were former workers in South Korea a few years ago have now developed into owners of modern housing, a potential real estate business and Popular in Kampong Thom province.
Son Sokea said he had worked in Korea for two years and eight months.
"Breaking down from earning thousands of dollars to starting your own business is not easy," he said. "We have to face a lot of problems, but we have to overcome them: family factors, social factors, challenges with people and business people in the same field that are around us, and especially ourselves."
Mr. Chan Khin also revealed that he had worked as a laborer in Korea for three years and six months.
At the same time, Mr. Phon Samean said that he was also a former worker in Korea for 2 years and 10 months, but now he has changed his life from being a worker to a businessman.
"We should know how to value our personal time and manage our income and expenses well, otherwise our time in Korea may not improve or return to Cambodia with nothing left," he said. "Therefore, we should start to set clear goals and time to be able to increase personal possibilities and achievements when we return to the country."
