(Kratie): Kratie provincial officials claim that the director of the Kratie Provincial Department of Agriculture and forest chief conspired to provide timber stockpiles for sale and distribution near the border, giving traders the opportunity to import illegal timber. Cross-border to sell in Vietnam.
Pursuant to the law issued by Mr. Try Sopheak, Director of Kratie Provincial Department of Agriculture, dated 3 June 2019, signed by Mr. Nuon Pov Ratana, Deputy Director in Charge of Kratie Forestry Administration and at the request of Chhlong Forestry State has allowed Tea Keo Mony to set up a non-timber forest products distribution warehouse located in Trapeang Sre village, 2 Thnou commune, Snuol district, Kratie province.
According to Mr. Try Sopheak, the above storage location was issued by the Ministry of Agriculture and the location where he issued the permit did not have any timber to transport, only in the same village Trapeang Sre, so he would like to confirm that there is no timber. Confusion.
According to officials and timber traders, the timber storage location of the traders that Mr. Sopheak allowed was not a convenient strategy for stockpiling timber for sale and distribution in the country, but a convenient storage location for timber smuggling through the border corridor. Many are sold in Vietnam because the location is near the border corridor only a few kilometers.
