The President, as well as all the members, expressed their pleasure to be invited to participate in the celebration of the 68th anniversary of the birth of the Cambodian People's Party, which is now history.
Taking this opportunity, the chairman of the working group announced to accept 807 new party members, including 415 women who came from the seven communes of Tambor district. Mr. Chhum Socheat and Mr. Ouk Kong lead the working group to celebrate the 68th anniversary of the Cambodian People's Day in Samlot district
(Battambang): Mr. Chhum Socheat, Chairman of the National Working Group for Samlot District and Mr. Ouk Kong, Chairman of the Working Group of the Cambodian People's Party for Samlot District this morning, June 29, 2019, led the working group to celebrate the 68th anniversary. Year of birth of the Cambodian People's Party in Samlot district.
The event was held at the CPP headquarters in Samlot district with the participation of 200 CPP leaders and members in Samlot district.
Mr. Chhum Socheat, Chairman of the National Working Group for Samlot District, read out the speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian People's Party to the participating members.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, paid a courtesy call on Mr. Minuroki Uchi, Deputy Minister of Environment of Japan, to discuss work related to waste management, transportation, drainage and sewerage, and environmental conservation. Environment and development in Phnom Penh.
The meeting was also attended by Mr. Horino Uchihi Hidehisa, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Japan to Cambodia, Mr. Sokano Yuichi, President of JICA Cambodia, Mr. Kushia Masato, Director of the Kitakyushu Department of Environment, and other relevant officials. More. The meeting was held on the afternoon of June 29, 2019.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that in cooperation to promote development in Phnom Penh, the city side has been supporting the development of a strategic plan to support climate change, focusing on six priority tasks, including: waste management, energy, Transportation, drainage and sewerage, environmental conservation and green products.
(Pailin): Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province and Chairman of the Provincial Party Committee, said that through four decades of the process of struggling to save the life of the country, the restoration and defense of the motherland from the victory of January 7 to Cambodia. Some valuable lessons that are most important for the future of Cambodia.
He said that nearly 40 years after the January 7 victory under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister has made great achievements in all areas. To preserve and protect all the achievements of the society and to achieve great success in building, developing the motherland and improving the living standard of the people.
Mr. Phan Chanthul continued that the main goals of the Cambodian People's Party to continue to strengthen peace, stability, security and social order to be strong and promote the development of the country in all areas in a sustainable manner, which is a strong pillar in achieving the goal. Of the Cambodian People's Party in the next 5 years in the development of serving the country in response to the will of the electorate.
Through the glorious victory of the Cambodian People's Party, it shows that the Cambodian people need and believe in the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party to ensure peace, strengthen democracy and the rule of law, socio-economic development, improve people's lives and continue to improve. Forms in all areas going forward.
Construction in Sihanoukville has seen tremendous growth in recent years. Most of those constructions are invested by Chinese investors. Mr. Yon Min, former Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, said that there are currently 194 construction projects in Preah Sihanouk Province with a height of 5 to 40 floors.
On June 22, a nearly seven-storey building collapsed, crushing workers, killing 28 and injuring 26. The collapse of the building was claimed to be of poor quality and illegal.
On the occasion of presiding over the transfer of the post of Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province from Mr. Yon Min to Mr. Kouch Chamroeun this morning, June 29, 2019, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated that the construction issues in Preah Sihanouk Province were of interest to Samdech and Worried about problems since the early stages of investment growth.
The collapse of buildings in Sihanoukville, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng said that the impact on investment and tourism as well. The Minister of Interior said that the building was of poor quality and no one wanted to stay there.
In order to avoid possible accidents related to construction as well as to restore confidence, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng warned Mr. Kouch Chamroeun and government officials in Sihanoukville to carefully examine all construction. Samdech Krala Hom reminded that all constructions must have rules, must have quality and safety.
During his inauguration as Governor of Sihanoukville this morning, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun also announced his commitment to improve the quality of construction in Sihanoukville.
It should be noted that in order to improve the quality of construction in Sihanoukville after the collapse of the building, the Royal Government of Cambodia has established a special committee with a mixed composition from the relevant ministries and institutions to inspect all construction in Sihanoukville.
