After searching, it was discovered that there was a fishing game embedded in it, and in the meantime, the force confiscated all the equipment in that location, while the owner was not arrested because he was not in that location. .
Authorities said that the owner of this illegal gambling place was Hun Kimcheat, a 39-year-old man, and when the force arrived, they did not see the owner in that location, only one person in charge, Prum Nareach. Only. The force then confiscated all the exhibits, including 27 computers, 29 chairs and 7 fishing games, and stored them at Por Sen Chey District Hall, waiting for the owner to be summoned for questioning.
