Cambodian Red Cross in Kampong Thom Province Brings Samdech Kittipritthbandit's Donation and Condolences to the Families of Lightning Victims
(Kampong Thom): Kampong Thom Provincial Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross Led by Ms. Khieu Sina Chea Chanto, Honorary Vice President of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch of Kampong Thom Province The body of Mrs. Bun Samien, who died due to lightning.
Please be informed that Ms. Bun Samien died in a lightning strike on June 26, 2019 while she and her family were visiting the plantation. Mrs. Bun Samien, 44 years old, has 3 children and her husband is a farmer living in Tipor Village, Tipor Commune, Santuk District, Kampong Thom Province. In that incident, one of her daughters was injured but not life threatening.
On that occasion, Ms. Khieu Sina Chea Chanto, on behalf of the Honorary Prince, expressed her deepest sympathy and condolences to the family of the deceased with the deepest regret for this tragedy.
She stressed that all the difficulties that people face are the concerns of the leaders, especially the Cambodian Red Cross, which must be addressed immediately. In fact, upon receiving this news, the team immediately came down to meet and distribute some gifts, although not much and could not solve the shortage completely, but confirmed the compassion of the leaders, especially the Red Cross. In Cambodia, when people face difficulties, especially during natural disasters.
