Please be informed that on June 24, 2019, Mr. Ros Piseth, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, issued a detention order for Mr. Oknha Sok Bun and 5 other Koh Rong Sangkat authorities after the Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU) detained It is involved in illegal land grabbing in Koh Rong commune, Koh Rong city, Sihanoukville province. Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign, June 28: 1,536 illegal vehicles found and 1,161 fined
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for June 28, 2019, the traffic police force inspected 5,242 vehicles and found 1,536 vehicles (75% motorcycles), 375 education vehicles and park 1,161 fines, according to the official report of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 2,962 helmets and goggles were inspected on June 28, 184 education helmets and 945 helmets were fined.
Representatives of educational institutions and universities from Australia will travel to Phnom Penh to participate in the Australian Scholarship and Study Fair, which will be held at Sofitel Phnom Penh from 1pm to 6pm on the 11th. July. This program is organized annually by the IDP in Cambodia and is open to the public.
The Education Fair program is organized by IDP, a leading international educational institution, and sends students to study abroad in Australia, New Zealand, Canada, the United States, the United Kingdom, and Ireland.
Students and parents are invited to meet with representatives from well-known schools, universities and educational institutions from around Australia, where they will provide advice and suggestions on study options, tuition fees, accommodation fees and the visa application process to Australia. Live. Institutions that will be present in this program include from secondary and short courses to doctoral degrees.
Officials from the IELTS test center in Cambodia will also be available to provide advice on IELTS test registration, IELTS test preparation, and free IELTS computer testing. The Australian Center for Training (ACE) will also be present at the event to provide information related to learning English in preparation for qualifying for an Australian educational institution.
Mao Sreng, director of IDP Education in Cambodia, said: “This is a rare opportunity for Cambodian students who wish to study abroad. The exhibition will provide an educational platform that brings together the resources and information that students need to make a decision to study in Australia.
In Cambodia, students and parents can find IDP Study Abroad Information Offices at all branches of the Australian Center for Training (ACE) in Phnom Penh and Siem Reap for a free consultation.
