Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng presents five challenges facing Sihanoukville and urges immediate resolution (Video inside) (Preah Sihanouk): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, at the inauguration ceremony of Kouch Chamroeun As the Governor of Sihanoukville, he pointed out the five challenges facing the economy and demanded immediate joint action.
The five challenges that Prince Sar Kheng raised this morning, June 29, 2019 include:
* First: Land Dispute Land Management: At this point, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng noted that in the past, when Sihanoukville was not very developed, land prices have not risen, this problem does not occur, but now Land disputes seem to be on the rise, so they must be resolved peacefully together to avoid the use of violence.
* Second: Construction quality: Check the construction is under construction and running business because we have recent experience is the collapse of the building, so requires careful inspection. In addition, the safety of the building must also be examined, focusing on fire issues.
* Third: Security in Koh Rong and the islands under Sihanoukville: Currently, the number of tourists in the islands seems to be increasing, so to ensure the safety of tourists, the relevant authorities need to strengthen this work. Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stressed that the police force must have three islands to guard and also have to have an auxiliary intervention force to intervene in time when any incident occurs.
* Fourth: Road infrastructure: While this province is developing the traffic situation is more busy, so the existing roads seem to be narrow and some places are also damaged, but this point Prince Krala Hom Sar Kheng Confirm that it is also in the consideration of the head of the Royal Government.
* Fifth: Together to solve the problem of sewage, sewage, rain: Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that this issue has four ministries involved, including the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, the Ministry of Environment and the Ministry Water resources and meteorology, so those involved must work together.
