Therefore, after the consideration of the Royal Government, it was decided to transfer Mr. Kouch Chamroeun from Kampong Cham province to the position of Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province after Mr. Yon Min, former Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, resigned. From a recent building collapse accident. And Kampong Cham Province replaced by Mr. Un Chanda, former Governor of Preah Vihear Province.
After listening to the report of Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Samdech Krala Hom saw that Mr. Un Chanda, the new Governor of Kampong Cham, also committed to continue the work of Mr. Kouch Chamroeun to make Kampong Cham more successful.
The Cambodian Federation of Investors Association is committed to curbing the illegal sale of cosmetics online to protect the well-being of the people.
(Phnom Penh): While the sale of beauty products as well as health supplements is widely available online, the Royal Government and the public are very concerned about some products that are sold without a license and without certification, while some counterfeit products. Many have also been found and destroyed.
In order to join the Royal Government in preventing this problem, the Federation of Investors Federation of Cambodia (FYC) is committed to participating in this campaign and also intends to help orient the business of selling cosmetics as well as nutritional products. This health is for all business owners as well.
This is the expression of the will of Dr. Samohak Ley Sopheap, Executive Director of the Federation of Investors of Cambodia on behalf of this association, which took place after the 6th Ordinary Meeting of the Board of Directors of the Federation of Investors of Cambodia (FFC) in High Sky Hotel on June 28, 2019.
Mr. Ley Sopheap said that now the world has been evolving to the Industrial Revolution 4.0, and in Cambodia is also reviving this development, in which he saw the problem of the business of selling cosmetics. Also online, especially on Facebook, means that most of their business ventures are not yet properly licensed, without quality certification from the relevant ministries and institutions, and also have little care and use properly. .
He said that this point has directly and indirectly affected the health of consumers or consumers, which is causing concern for the government and the general public.
Mr. Ley Sopheap stated that the Association of Federation of Investors of Cambodia is committed to prevent the above problems with the Royal Government. Engaged in the business of selling cosmetics as well as other health supplements.
He added that if these traders join the Cambodian investment community and follow the relevant legal procedures and regulations, the association will encourage them to facilitate all kinds of issues for them to get a legitimate business. There is a guarantee of trust and help increase customers through the reputation of its products as well.
But if the trader is a natural person or a legal entity does not participate in the proper implementation of the law, they will certainly face the law and be responsible to their customers.
He said that the Cambodian Investors Association always welcomes traders or companies who want to become members of the association, which will be open after the membership status is officially decided in the near future. This is why the association will support and facilitate all means for its members.
Please be informed that in the 6th Ordinary Meeting of the Board of Directors of the Federation of Cambodian Investors Association, the meeting decided to issue internal regulations for the members to conduct their work in accordance with the policies of the Royal Government. In addition, the meeting reviewed the statute of membership of this new association to reach a formal decision at the next meeting.
