Cambodia, Hong Kong sign agreement on avoidance of double taxation and prevention of tax evasion related to income tax
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China have signed an agreement on the avoidance of double taxation and the prevention of tax evasion related to income tax. This is according to the press release of the General Department of Taxation of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, which was received by Fresh News on the night of June 28, 2019.
The agreement provides benefits to the signatories on strengthening bilateral cooperation, ensuring the right to taxation, the growth of the tax base through the attraction of direct investment, capital flows, technology transfer and expertise. From abroad, protection of residents from tax-related misconduct, and protection of domestic tax revenue through cooperation in the fight against tax evasion between the two jurisdictions.
The agreement will enter into force once the two jurisdictions have completed their respective domestic proceedings. This agreement is another of the many important achievements that the Royal Government of the 5th legislature of the National Assembly under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has achieved, especially in the context of ASEAN economic integration.
At the same time, Cambodia has been negotiating this agreement with some other partner countries such as Malaysia, the Philippines, Korea and Japan.
Duke Pung Kheav Se: Khmer-Chinese Alliance Association Established to Attract Investment to Develop Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Duke Pung Kheav Se, President of the Khmer-Chinese Association in Cambodia, said on June 28, 2019 that the Khmer-Chinese Association in Cambodia was established to serve the Chinese people and attract investment to develop the country. Cambodia.
This statement was made by Duke Pung Kheav Se during a friendly dinner with representatives of market vendors in Phnom Penh, which was held at Koh Pich Center on the evening of June 28, 2019.
Duke Pung Kheav Se stated, “The Khmer-Chinese Association in Cambodia is a large civil society organization with a nationwide network established by Cambodian-Chinese people who are legally registered in Cambodia to serve and attract Chinese people. Invest to develop Cambodia.
"On the other hand, the Khmer-Chinese Association is also a bridge to connect and strengthen the relationship between the Chinese people to be closer and to reach cooperation in trade and other fields." This is the additional emphasis of Duke Pung Kheav Se.
Duke Pung Kheav Se continued that based on the principles of the Association as mentioned above, the Association Association initiated this friendly dinner so that all market traders know each other more, strengthen the relationship and the Association We are happy to provide feedback in various fields and to coordinate on all business issues.
Please be informed that this is the third time that the Khmer-Chinese Association in Cambodia has organized a friendly dinner to meet with market vendors in Phnom Penh.
