(Preah Vihear): On June 27, 2019, the Red Cross Youth and Kampong Sralou High School students raised a total of 1,656,200 Riels to support Mr. Touch Phalla, a secondary school teacher. Kampong Sralao is located in Kampong Sralao village, Kampong Sralao commune, Cheb district, Preah Vihear province, after being completely engulfed by fire on June 26, 2019.
In addition, immediately after the house caught fire, Mr. Sok Santara, Governor of Chhep District and Honorary President of the Cambodian Red Cross Sub-Branch, also brought the Red Cross donations to visit and expressed regret over the fire that caused Burn this house. He also advised the victims not to despair on behalf of the local authorities and the team promised to help rebuild the house soon.
Mr. Sok Santara continued that the Cambodian Red Cross, headed by Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, always pays attention to the victims without any discrimination on the basis of political affiliation or race. Complexion. Donations given at this time include: 2 million Riels and many other materials.
