(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Yun Min will be removed from the position of Governor of the Board of Governors of Preah Sihanouk Province on June 29, 2019 tomorrow, after he has ruled this province for about 4 years. Before announcing his resignation, Mr. Yun Min urged relevant officials in Sihanoukville to serve the people faithfully and to abide by the law.
Mr. Yon Min's remarks were made during the meeting to review the work results for June 2019 and work directions for July on the afternoon of June 27, 2019.
During the meeting, Mr. Yon Min thanked the civil servants in various departments and units of Sihanoukville Provincial Administration for their hard work and support for his leadership for almost 4 years to promote Sihanoukville. The development of people's lives has improved as it is today.
The provincial governor, who is nearing the end of this role, also asked the officials to continue to inspect the treatment bases at all construction sites, strengthen public services to the people to be good, fast, quality, transparent and accountable so that people can trust, take care Pay attention to resolving land disputes for the people, strengthen administrative documents to be accurate and clear, and the implementation of the work must be based on the law.
Please be informed that Mr. Yon Min on June 24, 2019 decided to resign as the Governor of Sihanoukville. This request is made to apologize to the victims who suffered in the building collapse at more than 4 am on June 22, 2019. The building collapsed, killing 28 people and injuring 26 others.
