Ministry of Commerce organizes election for rice federation for new mandate
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Commerce has issued guidelines on the election of the Chairman and Board Member of the Rice Federation of Cambodia, which will start accepting applications for the position of Chairman and Board Member from July 4 to 18, 2019.
For the election of the composition of the Board of Directors of the Rice Federation of Cambodia, which includes: 1 Chairman, 5 Vice-Chairmen, and 13 members, of which 6 members are appointed by the Minister or Chairman of the relevant unit and Must have the approval of the Royal Government without the need to vote.
Fisheries Administration in collaboration with International Wildlife and Wildlife Organization and Wildlife and Nature Alliance organized a study tour of coastal fishing communities
(Kampot): The Fisheries Administration, in collaboration with the International Wildlife and Fauna (FFI) and the Wildlife and Nature Coalition (WEA), organized a study tour for a total of 40 fisheries community committees from coastal areas on the 24th. June 27, 2019 in Trapeang Sangke fishing community, Trapeang commune, Teuk Chhou district, Kampot province, which is a model fishing community in the area in its community management process.
Cambodia's coastal fishing communities play an important role in contributing to the effective protection of the local fisheries resources of each fishing community and ensuring the sustainability of fisheries resources for future generations.
Through this study tour, the participants had the opportunity to learn from each other's good experiences, especially the experience of defending fisheries, raising funds from various sources, including community-based ecotourism services for the sustainability of the community. The future of the fishing community. In particular, all communities participated in planting mangrove trees as a symbol under the slogan "Mangroves protect us - we protect mangroves" and put up educational labels.
Coastal fishing communities, local authorities and relevant departments are strongly committed to strengthening the protection of fishery resources.
