District Inspector Por Sen Chey leads his own force to implement and educate traffic law on National Road 4
(Phnom Penh): This morning, June 28, 2019, at the intersection of National Road 4 in front of Borey Sen Monorom, Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, Colonel
Ek Yim Saran, Police Inspector of Por Senchey District, led a force to educate and disseminate the road traffic law on driving in violation of the law, reversing driving without a helmet, and driving over heavy traffic.
Mr. Yim Saran said, "I have enforced the traffic law and instructed the traffic police on National Road 4 around Borey Sen Monorom Odim, as well as the intervention unit to help solve and facilitate traffic congestion on a regular basis. Especially in the morning and evening, please respect the law and have understanding while driving.
Mr. Yim Saran said, "In order to reduce traffic accidents and traffic violations, we must implement, disseminate, restrict and widely educate the drivers of vehicles or motorcycles on the road must comply with the law. "Travel all the time, but a small number of drivers and motorcycles continue to drive illegally, causing congestion and accidents."
Drivers without helmets, glass, cement pipes, recycled vehicles, vehicles with black spots on the glass, curtains without proper documents are prohibited from being educated or fined in accordance with the law.
