(Phnom Penh): The book "Understanding Community Health Care" which provides basic health education messages to prevent and care for the health of people of all ages living in urban or rural areas was officially launched on June 27, 2019 at Presided over by Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health.
In the workshop on the official launch of the book "Understanding Community Health Care" in Kampong Cham, Ms. O Vandin said that this book is divided into 5 chapters, including: Chapter 1: Health Services And healthy living, prevention and care related to non-communicable diseases, Chapter 2: Child health, Chapter 3: Women's health and pregnancy, Chapter 4: Adult health and Chapter 5: Consumption Medication properly.
She said that the Ministry of Health, under the leadership of Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, has always taken care to raise people's awareness of health and the search for appropriate health services, considering health education and behavior change as A priority strategy to promote health and have a National Center for Health Promotion as a monitoring and coordination staff.
At the same time, she also thanked all health officials and the World Health Organization for their efforts to develop this book for the benefit of the Cambodian people. 134 Families Affected by Typhoon in Khsach Kandal District Receive Donations from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen
(Kandal): The Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Kandal Province, including Khsach Kandal District Branch, this morning, June 28, 2019, brought the donation of the Cambodian Red Cross distributed by Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross. 134 families in Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province.
All the vulnerable people expressed their gratitude for the noble and noble spirit of Samdech Bun Rany Hun Sen, who always thought and associated with the well-being of the people with compassion and without any discrimination. Donations distributed to each family include: 50 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 10 cans of fish, 1 can of soy sauce, 1 can of fish sauce and some other budget.
