Government and private sector officials express views on Cambodia's readiness for the arrival of the Fourth Industrial Revolution
The discussion on "Cambodia Industry 4.0" aims to provide a forum for raising the awareness of the Cambodian people, especially students about Industry 4.0, and contribute to the development of Cambodia's policy towards a new era of Advances in technology.
Please be informed that the 4th Industrial Revolution is coming, there will be crossings in the 1st, 2nd and 3rd Industrial Revolution. The first industrial revolution took place between 1760 and 1840, and mechanical production first appeared through the development of steam engines combined with the use of railways.
The Second Industrial Revolution appeared in the late 19th century through the discovery of electricity and the creation of factory production chains, and the Third Industrial Revolution was based on the development of Internet technology, information technology (IT), semiconductors and so on. Computerization.
During the discussion, the four speakers jointly expressed their views on Cambodia's readiness for the arrival of the Fourth Industrial Revolution.
Ms. Cham Nimol said that within the framework of the Ministry of Commerce is also ready to accept the 4.0 industry, as well as two major goals, in which the first direction has already been implemented and the second. : Implementing soon.
The second part is to set up an online system within the Ministry itself, a system for checking reports for the development of each unit under the whole commercial institution, such as the report of the General Department of the General Department of Foreign Trade in the country. How far has he progressed or evolved?
Mr. Chi Sela said, "For my opinion. I think this Industrial Revolution 4.0 will be very easy to say, not to mention people can only think, can also provide, but for convenience, this also has a slight negative effect, is easier. "It makes people lazy."
Mr. Ung Luy Na said that the entry of Industry 4.0 will help the national economy. Obviously, as in agriculture, there can be opportunities to increase our productivity, for example, we used to farm with low yields, but when Industry 4.0 comes in, agricultural products will be better.
He added that the management of the Royal Government is also easier, with the Royal Government managing and allocating resources more effectively.
