This afternoon, the Anti-Corruption Unit will hold a press conference on the land case on Koh Rong after the arrest of Duke Sok Bun and five local officials
(Phnom Penh): The Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU) will hold a press conference on the afternoon of June 28, 2019 to cover the land case in Sangkat Koh Rong, Koh Rong City, Preah Sihanouk Province after the arrest and detention of Tycoon Sok. Bun and five other officials were involved in a case of forgery in the area.
It should be informed that on June 24, 2019, Mr. Ros Piseth, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, issued a detention order for Mr. Oknha Sok Bun and 5 other Koh Rong Sangkat authorities in connection with the illegal land grabbing in Sangkat Koh Rong. Rong, Koh Rong City, Preah Sihanouk Province. This decision was made after the Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Mr. Kuch Kimlong, decided to charge.
The six suspects are: Ung Nith, Chairman of Koh Rong City Council, Sihanoukville Province; Seng Huang Leang, Chief of Koh Rong Commune, Koh Rong City, Sihanoukville Province; Member of Sangkat Koh Rong, Koh Rong Municipality, Preah Sihanouk Province, 4th: Ke Som, Second Deputy Chief of Koh Rong Commune, Preah Sihanouk Province 6. Name: Sok Bun, General Director of Sok Bun Group.
As for Oknha Sok Bun, he was charged with "forgery of public documents, use of forged public documents and instigating acts of intentional destruction and malicious acts committed in Koh Rong commune, Koh Rong district, Preah Sihanouk province during 2016 to 2019 under Article 629 , 630 and 28 (601) of the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
It should be noted that Oknha Sok Bun, along with 5 other authorities in Sangkat Koh Rong, Koh Rong City, Preah Sihanouk Province, was arrested by the Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU) and sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on the morning of the 24th. This June 2019 involves the encroachment of state land and the forgery of other people's land in Koh Rong commune between 2016-2019.
