I would like to reply and explain to the public that these days my 80-year-old mother is seriously ill and is being treated at the hospital. My biggest duty as a grateful child is to take care of my mother almost every night after taking a break from administrative work.
Coincidentally, on the night of June 25, I went to take care of my elderly mother who was very sick until more than 2 o'clock at midnight on June 26, only to rest for a few hours on the same day at 5 o'clock. In the morning, I have to get up early to lead the masses to participate in the program at Koh Pich.
I would like to apologize to the public all over the country, especially I would like to sincerely apologize to the leaders at all levels for the inappropriate gestures in yesterday's ceremony unintentionally due to my personal health problems. Thank you for the constructive reminder.
