Mr. Chea Bora organized a meeting to review the work and divide the national working group in each commune in Kampong Ror district, Svay Rieng province.
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Chea Bora, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism and Chairman of the National Working Group for Kampong Ror District, held a meeting on June 27, 2019 to review the implementation of the political program and the Rectangular Strategy. The fourth phase of the Royal Government and to divide the work in each commune in Kampong Ror district.
He requested the Vice-Chairman and members of the national working group to visit localities in Kampong Ror district, as well as staff and relevant professional units around the administration of Kampong Ror district, to comment on the challenges encountered and suggestions to gather input. Develop action plans at the commune level to implement the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 more effectively.
In this regard, in order to support the implementation of the Royal Government's Rectangular Policy and Strategy Program, Phase 4, a national working group in Kampong Ror district was established to accept the problems and requests of the people in the local communes. Kampong Ror based on the action plan of each working group.
Mr. Chea Bora also requested the Chairman of the Working Group, the Deputy Chairman of the Working Group and the members of the commune in Kampong Ror district to implement the following:
* To increase trust, warmth and closeness with local people through local visits, organizing public forums and good deeds of the authorities, officials and relevant authorities at all levels.
* Consider and solve challenges and requests related to people's livelihood, especially irrigation system, crop production, construction of important infrastructure in villages, communes, districts, electricity supply, clean water, sanitation, public order, market organization. Clean town model, clean village and clean house.
* Promote the implementation of good public service competition from the village, commune to district level.
* Link the relationship between the Royal Government and the people through the widespread dissemination of the Rectangular Strategic Political Program, Phase 4, National Strategic Development Plan, Safe Village and Commune Policy, sectoral policy program and the overall situation of the country in connection with the situation in Local and promote implementation at all levels, all sectors and citizen participation.
* Increase the responsibility of each working group by monitoring and supporting the implementation of programs, projects and action plans at the local level.
* Plan work activities in each commune, especially pay attention to the organization of public forums at least once a month, and for communes with challenges to organize public forums according to the actual situation of each commune can be more than 1 Once a month to grasp the opinions and suggestions of the people and report to the national working group in Kampong Ror district.
* Mobilize resources from various sources to participate in solving people's livelihoods as well as local development.
* Cooperate to promote and enhance the accountability of the commune administration in providing public services to the people.
The President of the Royal Academy added that the difference between the statue of Princess Indra Devi and the statue of Princess Chey Reach Devi, who were all the wives of King Jayavarman VII, was also clearly demonstrated through in-depth consideration. . Through the composition of speakers, facilitators and participants from major professional institutions, all of whom are senior researchers and experts with experience and knowledge.
According to Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, in response to the research results of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, the Royal Government of Cambodia has supported the construction of two buildings to the Royal Academy of Cambodia, one of which was named "Indra Devi Building" by the Princess. Author, professor and wife of Jayavarman VII, the emperor of the Khmer Empire during the glorious Mohanakor era.
Dr. Yong Pov added that in the past, national and international researchers have studied the field of sculpture and have revealed many statues in the history of Khmer art, especially from the 9th to the 12th century, where statues were found. The ones that people worship. In the fourth part of the 12th century, the successor statues were identified by researchers, especially the statue of Jayavarman VII.
Deputy Prosecutor Markny decides to send a man with a luxury car drunk and drugs, chases police, throws passengers and reporters to the Opportunity Center
(Phnom Penh): According to the police, after the interrogation, Ms. Markny, the Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, decided to send Chuon Chandary to the Opportunity Drug Treatment Center for my treatment. Despite a complaint from the victim, the man was immediately taken to the police station on charges of threatening to insult the public.
In connection with the decision to send the suspect to the Opportunity Center, I was attacked by a group of journalists and victims who were known to have lodged a complaint with the Meanchey district police, and the prosecution did not act on their complaint.
Please be informed that the suspect named Chuon Chandary, male, 34 years old, living at house No. 5C, National Road No. 4 in Sangkat Choam Chao, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, was arrested by the police on the morning of June 23, 2019 at the pig's nose at the head of the road. 271 Sangkat Chak Angre Leu, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh, after he threw metal, stone and shoes at the traffic police and journalists.
After getting out of the car, the suspect shouted at the lamp and picked up the metal, stone and leather, chased the police and journalists ran wild on the public road.
