Ministry of Environment Recognizes 19 Protected Area Communities in Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary in Kampong Thom, Preah Vihear, Stung Treng and Kratie Provinces
(Phnom Penh): 19 protected area communities in the Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary in the four provinces of Stung Treng, Kampong Thom, Preah Vihear and Kratie have been officially recognized by the Ministry of Environment. This is the statement of Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State
On June 27, 2019, the official recognition ceremony of the Ministry of Environment was held with the participation of senior officials of the Ministry of Environment and representatives of provincial authorities and representatives of the community. June 26 in Thala Parivat district, Stung Treng province and on June 27, 2019 in Preah Vihear province.
Please note that Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary covers an area of more than 430,000 hectares in four provinces: Stung Treng, Preah Vihear, Kampong Thom and Kratie. Currently, about 100 park rangers have been stationed to protect and preserve the Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary.
Outgoing German ambassador reveals that many German companies are interested in doing business in Cambodia in the energy sector
(Phnom Penh): Outgoing German Ambassador to Cambodia Ingo Karsten told Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, that many German companies are interested in doing business in Cambodia, especially in the field. Power. This is according to Mr. Ket Sophan, spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
"He (the ambassador) stated that he was one of the leaders in the growth and development of Cambodia, and his economy and society, he also confirmed that Germany is a long-term cooperation partner with Cambodia," Mr. Sophan. . "Observing Cambodia's growth, many German companies are interested in investing in Cambodia, especially in the energy sector," he said.
A senior foreign ministry official said that within the framework of the Development Cooperation Consultation, Germany had provided concessional financing of about 48 million euros (approximately 66 million US dollars) in the reduction plan. Poverty in Cambodia for 2019 to 2020. He added that the Cambodian head of diplomacy thanked Germany for the loan.
