(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of assuming the position of President of the Khmer Cycling Federation in the 2018-2022 mandate, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, pledged to strengthen cooperation with the Executive Committee and all coaches to continue to lead and develop sports. This one to grow towards the victory in the 32nd SEA Games (2023 SEA Games).
The Minister's commitment was made at the Extraordinary General Assembly of the Khmer Cycling Federation, which was held on the afternoon of June 27, 2019 at the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia under the chairmanship of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and President of the National Olympic Committee, senior government officials, coaches and more than 100 athletes.
On that occasion, Minister Pan Sosak praised the achievements of the old Executive Committee and the dedication of Cambodian and foreign coaches, as well as all athletes who have participated in the development of Cambodian cycling until success. In the past, the nation has won 1 gold medal, 1 silver medal and many honorary awards.
The Minister highlighted the need for cycling and requested the views and support of all members of the Executive Committee, federal officials and coaches to address all of the sport's key challenges to build and develop. Ability of Cambodian athletes towards high quality sports both regionally and globally.
"Currently, cycling requires a very high level of professionalism and skill. Not only high-performance athletes, even cyclists must be manufactured and equipped with modern technology to win the race. "The more modern and convenient the bike, the more expensive it is." Mr. Pan Sosak emphasized.
Speaking at a press conference on dengue fever organized by the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit on June 27, 2019, Mr. Huy Rekul, President of the National Center for Combating Dengue Fever, estimated that dengue fever in 2019 could last forever. Up to 50,000 cases, an increase of about 5 times compared to 2018.
The director of the National Center for Dengue Fever pointed out that the increase in dengue fever in 2019 is due to the cycle of the disease, which lasts every 5 to 6 years or every 10 to 12 years. Like this. The increase in dengue fever for 2019 is not unique to Cambodia, but also to Asia-Pacific and ASEAN countries.
In addition, the Ministry of Health has prepared nearly 10,000 liters of tiger mosquito repellent for spraying in people's villages. But the mechanism of using this drug is not encouraged by the Ministry because it also affects the health of the people. At the same time, the Ministry of Health has also prepared about 70,000 serums to help people with dengue fever.
In this morning's press conference, Mr. Huy Rekol also gave some advice to people with dengue fever. Mr. Rekul reminded parents or relatives to send their children or relatives to a government hospital immediately if there is a suspicion of dengue fever.
23 companies interested in special students in French
(Phnom Penh): About 150 young people of the French language special training program of the Royal University of Law and Economics participated in the inauguration of the PEPITE project and the establishment of a private sector consultation committee of the Royal University of Law and Economics on June 26, 2019 Yesterday.
On that occasion, 23 companies presented, advertised and recruited staff and provided job counseling in various positions. The job orientation program was also organized with a presentation and sharing of good experiences of alumni of the Royal University of Law and Economics.
PEPITE is a new structure created to provide higher education institutions with the opportunity to consult directly with the private sector in order to understand the needs of the labor market, provide opportunities for companies to better collaborate with training and recruitment institutions, as well as Provide opportunities for students to get jobs and internships at companies as well.
The project is a product of the Polar Innovation and Entrepreneurship, which the French Higher Education Agency (AUF) in the Asia-Pacific region selects and offers to the Royal University of Law and Economics for the purpose of improving the quality of education and providing employment to graduates. Study as well as create a new role of higher education institutions in exchange and better cooperation with the private sector.
The PEPITE Advisory Committee is made up of representatives from higher education agencies using the French language, representatives from companies from the French and European Chambers of Commerce, representatives from the French Embassy, special education program project director, and the head of the Francophone office of the Royal University. Law and Economics.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Po, President of the National Blood Transfusion Center of Cambodia, stated that from January 1 to the end of June, there were 29,000 blood donors to the center, but the demand for blood is still increasing. .
This statement was made by the President of the National Blood Transfusion Center of Cambodia on the morning of June 27, 2019 at Cho Ray Hospital, Phnom Penh, on the occasion of his participation in the blood donation program of Cho Ray Hospital in Phnom Penh with the participation of company staff. Sokimex and Sokha Hotel under the slogan "Humanitarian spirit together to donate blood to save lives".
"So far, the National Blood Transfusion Center of Cambodia has received nearly 30,000 units of blood, and every year the demand for blood continues to increase, despite the large number of donors," said Dr. Sok Po.
The president of the National Blood Transfusion Center also expressed concern to the people who do not yet have a high awareness of the benefits of donating blood to patients, he said, "Donation not only shows a humane spirit. However, he showed his dedication to helping the victims as well as to their own health. "Blood donation can also reduce absorption, weight gain and iron overload."
The President of the National Blood Transfusion Center of Cambodia also thanked Choray Phnom Penh Hospital for always encouraging its staff to donate blood twice a year and at least 100 units at a time. .
Please be informed that throughout 2018, the National Blood Transfusion Center of Cambodia received 83,984 units of blood nationwide, including 58,397 blocks in Phnom Penh.
The doctor also saw that donating blood is a good charity work that requires each citizen to help each other to save the lives of all patients who need blood, especially this offer Is extremely helpful for patients with severe dementia.
Dr. Sok Po, President of the National Blood Transfusion Center of Cambodia, added that in terms of figures, about 25 percent of the population throughout Cambodia donated blood voluntarily. Senior official of the Ministry of Public Works: Due to the increase in vehicles, traffic congestion and accidents
