According to preliminary information from residents living near the scene, the man who committed suicide by burning gasoline named Sok had just returned from working in Thailand and was a suspected drug user. From cracking drugs.
Speaking on the International Day against Drug Abuse on the morning of June 26, Sar Kheng explained that the reason why Cambodia does not have the death penalty is because the country has a history of suffering from wars, divisions and killings.
At the same time, Samdech also called on the authorities not to take action against drug traffickers, even though Cambodia does not have the death penalty. Samdech warned that, however, if the authorities are still behind the drug activities, it will harm them.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated: “Do not reduce this is the third word. According to the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, due to our history of war and division, massacres, we have abolished the death penalty in Cambodian society, no matter what the crime. "Therefore, drug offenses are not punishable by death."
"If we compare with neighboring countries in the region or next to the village, the fence with us is not the same. This does not mean that we want the death penalty, it is impossible, because the Constitution says so, but it does not mean that without the death penalty, we would risk committing this crime. To ourselves, to our families, to our society as well.
According to Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, the mitigation that he wanted to emphasize was the blink of an eye from the competent authorities who opened up drug trafficking activities without taking any action.
Samdech said, "So how do you reduce this? It could be through intervention or our authority to turn a blind eye to the process and refuse to take action to crack down. "It is considered a mitigation, which is a problem." An officer in Bavet was lucky to win 100 million Riel from Carabao energy drink
(Svay Rieng): In the new season of increasing the grand prize of 100 million Riels to 100 prizes, a man who works as an officer named Sudina, 33 years old, currently living in Bavet Leu village, Bavet commune, Bavet city, Svay Rieng province. Lucky to win a big prize from Carabao energy drink in the amount of 100 million Riels.
Speaking to the team that handed over the prize money of 100 million Riel to the home, Mr. Sudina said that almost every day after tired and exhausted, he always buys a carabao energy drink to eat regularly.
Last weekend, he bought a can of carabao from a vendor near his house to eat. When I ate it, I suddenly saw a prize of 100 million riels. Suddenly, he was so excited that he could hardly believe his eyes and shouted to the seller and people nearby to help check and call the company.
He added that 100 million Riel is very important to his family and after receiving 100 million Riel from Carabao, he will use some to help the family whose father is sick. Save some to build a house and start a family business to support your future.
Please note: For the real prize, only on the can with the Khmer letters as the mark.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Governor Visits a Japanese Family Who Was Destroyed by a 7-Story Building
(Preah Sihanouk): The accident of a 7-storey building in Village 3, Sangkat 4, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province also caused a small Japanese shop called "Kokai" with Tita next to the building to be completely destroyed, but luckily Well, his wife, children and staff staying in another shop, the family survived.
The collapse of the building above, it is noted that a restaurant of a Japanese family, the seven-storey building collapsed, causing complete damage to property.
The Japanese shop owner said that his shop had a fence next to the wall of the collapsed building, and on the morning of June 22, 2019, the day the seven-story building collapsed, his family of three, a couple The children and staff of another family of three, a couple of children, were resting in the shop together during the collapse of the building.
The Japanese man said that on the day of the building collapse, they were not in danger of death, but only minor injuries, because after the building collapsed, there is still a small hole that allows them to crawl or crawl out. Go outside on your own without having to have a rescue team.
Regarding this issue, Major General Chuon Narin, Police Commissioner of Preah Sihanouk Province, confirmed to Fresh News on the afternoon of June 26, 2019 that in the incident of the building collapse, there were Japanese people who had a shop next to the scene, there were a number of members. Three people escaped unharmed, but shops and equipment were completely destroyed.
He said that his shop was also destroyed by a seven-storey building, completely destroying materials and property, and that at the time of the incident, the Japanese man, the owner of the shop, his wife, children and Cambodian staff, a couple, and a small child were asleep. That too, but fortunately survived the incident by crawling out of there in shock.
The Japanese man added that they were also victims, but no one questioned his family and supported them, only the victims in the building, and now his family and staff Has completely lost its livelihood.
At this point, the Japanese man raised his hand to call on the leaders of the administration of Sihanoukville and the leaders of relevant ministries and institutions, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, to facilitate their lives during the meeting. This difficulty is favored.
However, after receiving the news that a Japanese family was affected and homeless by the collapsed building, Mr. Yon Min, Governor of Sihanoukville on the evening of June 26, 2019, led officials Visit a Japanese family and bring them some food and some money.
