83 Cambodian students receive 100% scholarships to study in China for 3 years
(Phnom Penh): 83 Cambodian students left Cambodia on the morning of June 27, 2019 to continue their studies for three years in China.
The study tour came after they received a scholarship from the China Southeast Asian Development Fund Management Committee under the China One Belt One Road project through the Public Welfare Fund Association. Cambodia-China.
Ms. Oknha Keo Mom, Vice President of the Cambodia-China Public Welfare Association and Director of Lily Food Industry Co., Ltd., said that the students who received the third scholarship are from other institutions such as: Ministry Environment, Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Union of Doctors, Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Group 8 Youth Association, Lily Food Industries Co., Ltd. and students from all provinces of Cambodia.
In addition to providing 100% scholarships for the three years, the association also offers Chinese language courses, accommodation, food, 1,000 yuan per month and round-trip airfare.
It should be informed that this is the third time that Cambodian students have received scholarships through the Cambodia-China Public Welfare Foundation Association. Kindergarten teacher.
General Chuon Sovann told the authorities to avoid the four "do not" do not be involved, do not be behind, do not relax and do not intervene in drug cases
(Banteay Meanchey): On June 27, 2019, the International Day Against Drugs, on June 26, under the theme "Health for Justice, Justice for Health" was held in Suon Meanchey under the presidency of General Chuon Sovann, Deputy Chief of Staff. General Ke Kim Yan, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs.
The program was also accompanied by Mr. Ou Rathrey, Governor and Chairman of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Drug Control Committee, and was attended by the leadership of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, representatives of the Provincial Council, Departments and Units of the Provincial and Municipal Control Committees. Around Banteay Meanchey province, all kinds of armed forces, youth, scouts, Red Cross, students and more than 3,000 stakeholders.
Mr. Om Chantha, Deputy Governor, welcomed and presented the joint efforts to fight drugs, prevent drug problems and treat drug addicts in collaboration with the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, Departments, Armed Forces and stakeholders. Around the province.
Russey Keo District Governor to Repair National Road No. 5 and Reinstall Drainage System from Twin Road, Sangkat Kilometer 6
(Phnom Penh): The section of National Road No. 5 and the drainage system from the point of the twin roads in Sangkat Kilometer 6, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh, which was damaged in one area, will have to open the road repair site and replace the drainage system In the near future, using the budget package of Phnom Penh Capital Hall to relieve the flooding caused by the rainy season to facilitate travel for people.
This was announced during the leadership of some relevant public officials to inspect the restoration of the temporary drainage system by Mr. Chea Pisey, District Governor and a member of the Secretariat of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia on June 26. 2019.
Mr. Chea Pisey said that after many inspections on the drainage system, the water was definitely damaged because there was a blockage of water that could not flow quickly when it rained. During the rainy season, damage to National Road No. 5 from the twin roads of Sangkat Kilometer 6.
(Phnom Penh): Permanent Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin, Minister in Charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers, expressed confidence that Senior Minister Kun Kim, who has just been appointed as the First Deputy Chairman of the Disaster Management Committee, will lead this work successfully and effectively. Further growth aims to reduce disasters in Cambodia.
During the inauguration ceremony on the morning of June 27, 2019, Deputy Prime Minister Binh Minh also instructed Senior Minister Kun Kim not to change the structure, especially the current officials and to continue to control their emotions. Well, do not be partisan. But if the officer does not do the job properly as instructed, things can change.
In addition, Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin instructed officials working on the Disaster Management Committee to work hard with the new leadership, headed by Kun Kim, and to adhere to the principles and adhere to the leadership. Of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The Deputy Prime Minister explained that the spirit of leadership is not the same, that all officials must learn to change attitudes and be able to adapt and work hard together to maintain their current role. Better. In addition, do not look at each other.
In his determination to take on the new role, Senior Minister Kun Kim pledged to do his best to fulfill the duties and responsibilities of the Royal Government, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia. Given to serve the motherland.
Senior Minister Kun Kim pledged: "I am deeply committed to working with my colleagues to serve as the Chief of Staff and as an effective and timely facilitator." "Implementing the priority policies of the government of the sixth legislature and the mandate of the National Committee for Disaster Management, we will wait to hear the guidance of His Excellency Dr. Binh Chin to implement effectively."
At the same time, Mr. Kun Kim also called on the Armed Forces of Ministries and Institutions to assist Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management. Well done to Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Please be reminded that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on June 24, 2019, issued a decision to appoint Mr. Kun Kim as the First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, replacing Mr. Nhim Vanda. .
The reason for the removal of Mr. Nhim Vanda was stated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen due to lack of responsibility and lies after the incident of the collapse of a seven-story building, which caused dozens of deaths and injuries.
It should be informed that at present, Senior Minister Kun Kim is the Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the President. In his role as Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, he observed that Mr. Kun Kim worked tirelessly to reach the grassroots in order to understand the lives and daily lives of members of the Cambodian Veterans Association and solve problems. There are some other challenges as well.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, urged his subordinates and professional working groups to prepare lessons for training and dissemination to employers, workers and the general public to understand the risks. Caused by asbestos.
The promotion was made on the occasion of the Minister presiding over the dissemination of the National Asbestos News Series in Cambodia at Tonle Bassac II Restaurant on June 27, 2019.
In his opening remarks, Mr. Ith Sam Heng explained, "Asbestos is very useful for industry because it is durable, but it also has a significant impact on human health through respiration, and most of it causes "Diseases include lung cancer, lung cancer, uterine cancer, lung cancer, pneumonia, pneumonia, bronchitis, respiratory diseases and even esophageal cancer, stomach cancer and intestinal cancer."
By organizing the dissemination of the National Asbestos Bulletin in Cambodia, this is another testament to the attention and high responsibility of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and all stakeholders for development. Occupational health and safety in the workplace in Cambodia.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng suggested that the National Asbestos Awareness Working Group in Cambodia needs to be updated frequently to provide information on policy development, identifying workplace challenges, assisting in planning and prioritizing activities to reduce Affection of asbestos fibers.
He also called on development partners, including the Australian Asbestos Safety and Eradication Agency, Afida, the ILO / Japan and the World Health Organization (WHO) to continue to support Cambodia's ability to prepare for As a plan of action leading to the safe use and prevention of all the risks caused by this asbestos.
