Tomorrow, the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit will hold a press conference on dengue fever in Cambodia
According to a statement from the Royal Government Spokesperson 'Unit, the press conference will be held at 10 am at the National Children's Hospital. Speakers who will address the issue of dengue fever include: representatives of the Ministry of Health, representatives of the National Children's Hospital and Ms. Hun Mana.
The press release also states that the current press conference will highlight the current situation of dengue fever, dengue response rules and measures (patient storage and medicine), challenges, experiences. Of the National Children's Hospital to provide dengue treatment services and additional needs.
The Ministry of Health claims that 2019 is the year that dengue fever broke out in Cambodia. The Minister of Health, Professor Mam Bunheng, has stated that from the beginning of 2019 to June 20, there were 12,000 cases of dengue fever nationwide and 21 deaths.
The National Children's Hospital receives an average of more than 300 dengue patients per day. From the beginning of 2019 to June 20, the National Children's Hospital received 3,000 cases of dengue fever, of which 4 died.
In response to the outbreak of dengue fever in 2019, the Ministry of Health has also introduced a number of measures to prevent and control the disease. The Ministry of Health has set out a number of rules, such as educating people on prevention in some way, spraying mosquito nets in people's homes, distributing mosquito nets, dipping drugs, and preparing equipment and providing diagnostic training.
At the same time, the Ministry of Health also encouraged the medical team to make more efforts with high attention to save patients effectively and quickly.
