Authorities are searching for the body of a missing fisherman in Koh Kong province
(Koh Kong): Police and the owner of a fishing boat off the coast of Koh Kong province are searching for the body of a boat worker who went missing on June 25, 2019. According to the Mondul Seima District Inspector, the exact reason for the disappearance of the fishing boat worker is not yet known.
Chea Sarin, police inspector of Mondul Seima district, said this morning, June 26, 2019 that the police have not found the body of a fishing boat that fell into the water at 12:50 pm on June 25. No.
After a 26-year-old man named Lonh Pet, resident of Village 3, Pak Klang Commune, Mondul Seima District, Koh Kong Province, reported on the missing incident, a 31-year-old male worker named Nget fell into the water at Krasa Island, Phny Meas Commune, Koh Kong District. Kirisakor.
Mondul Seima District Police Inspector confirmed that he still does not know the exact cause of the disappearance of the fishermen, whether due to natural disasters, rainstorms or homicides, killing water habits as of now. Authorities and fishing boat owners continue to search for victims' bodies. In case the body is found, the authorities will examine the forensic examination and ask the relevant people later.
It should be informed that every rainy season, people living in Koh Kong province who are fishermen often experience missing or sinking boats while going fishing in the middle of the sea.
At the same time, the authorities and experts also call on fishermen to be very careful when going out fishing if they receive information on climate change to avoid any natural disasters.
According to a statement issued by the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology on June 26, the weather in Cambodia changes from June 26 to July 2, causing low pressure valleys. The southwest monsoon increased the effect.
The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has advised residents, fishermen or water travelers to be extra vigilant in coastal provinces, including Koh Kong and Sihanoukville, with moderate to heavy rainfall combined with strong winds. Strong and high waves. Court Sentences Victims to Two Years and Fines 35 Million Riel to Victims of Rath Rathmony's Video Production
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of June 26, 2019, the Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court held a hearing to announce the verdict of the accused, Rat Rathmony, to 2 years imprisonment and to order to pay 35 million in compensation. Riel to two victims, relatives who are plaintiffs.
Please be reminded that during the hearing on the afternoon of June 12, 2019, one of the key witnesses, Mr. Nak Sothea, Principal of Indratevi High School, confirmed to the court that Mr. Rath Rathmony had requested the location of his school to record a video about the lives of Cambodians after the regime. Pol Pot.
Contrary to the request, Mr. Rath Mony produced a video related to the mother selling her child for sex, which was detrimental to the school's reputation until the authorities called him in for questioning and reprimanding the characters and victims of the case. The story also claims that before filming the video, Rat Rathmony promised to help them start a business through the help of the video.
Mr. Koy Sao was the trial judge and Mr. Vong Bunvisoth was the representative of the prosecution.
In the same case, Mr. Seng Bothy, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on December 13, 2018, issued a detention order for a person named Rath Rathmony working as a Russian Today (RT) news agency. Thai authorities arrested and deported Cambodia at the request of the Cambodian side in connection with the production of the video "My Mother Sells Me", a form of misrepresentation that brought disgrace to Cambodia.
According to Long Kim Heang, the wife of Rat Rat Mony, her husband, Rat Rat Mony, a Russian Today Today (RT) news agency, was arrested by Thai authorities and handed over to the Cambodian government. At her request, her husband was arrested in connection with the production of a documentary entitled "My Mother Sold Me" by Russian Today (RT).
Please note that the video with the content "My mother sells me" is about a Cambodian woman who sells her daughter due to lack of livelihood and describes the situation of sex work in Cambodia. This video has been seen by the Royal Government as a distortion of the prestige, honor and dignity of Cambodian women and hurts the honor of Cambodia.
