(Phnom Penh): An Indian company that has been successful in developing vocational education for more than 7 years has expressed its intention to establish cooperation with the Royal Government of Cambodia in vocational training for young people studying in Secondary level and young people who drop out of school so that they get a clear skill and a decent job.
Mr. Rachanisha said that his company intends to establish cooperation with the Royal Government of Cambodia in developing vocational training development projects for young Cambodians who are studying at the lower secondary level (secondary school) and young people who have dropped out. Study up to 9th grade so that they can get any professional skills and get a decent job, including skills in technology, tourism, health, finance and so on.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng expressed his strong support for the purpose of establishing this cooperation, with the Minister pointing out and assigning the expert team of the General Department of Technical and Vocational Education (TVET) to discuss the relevant work in order to The above cooperation emerges and bears fruit for development in Cambodia.
He added that there are currently more than 10 million workers in Cambodia, and the rate of labor entering the labor market each year is less than half a million, but even so, Cambodia still can not provide. Training them all yet, which requires both national and international partners to help develop this sector even more.
The Minister of Labor further stated that the purpose of establishing this cooperation is in line with the situation that Cambodia is in need of more partners, and the Minister informed Mr. Rajinee Shakanotra that the Royal Government always welcomes this cooperation.
