Iran warns of retaliation, while US threatens to retaliate if Iran dares to strike first
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Iranian President Hassan Rouhani has warned that the Iranian military will retaliate strongly against any renewed US encroachment on the Iranian border, while Donald Trump has just announced that the United States will Retaliate without mercy if Iran dares to launch any attack. This was released by Sputnik on Wednesday afternoon, June 26, 2019.
Rohani made the warning in a telephone conversation with French President Emmanuel Macron this week. "If the United States violates its airspace and airspace again, the Iranian military will retaliate with the utmost force," he said.
Tensions between the United States and Iran have escalated into an armed conflict after Iran shot down a US spy plane. Donald Trump also ordered US troops to launch an attack on Iran, but canceled the order just 10 seconds later.
The United States has accused Iran of shooting down its drones in international airspace over the Strait of Hormuz, but Tehran has denied any wrongdoing. The wreckage of the drone was extracted from Iran in its waters.
Siem Reap Provincial Administration Holds the First Ordinary Meeting of Provincial Council to Discuss and Report on the Performance Report of Provincial Administration
(Siem Reap): This morning, June 26, 2019, the Siem Reap Provincial Administration held the first ordinary meeting of the Provincial Council of the third mandate to discuss and discuss the work report of the Provincial Administration of the second mandate. Remaining 3 months approved by the provincial council.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Ung Hoeun, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap. The meeting also disseminated Instruction No. 015 of the Ministry of Interior on the preparation of internal rules and regulations of the council, and discussed the preparation of the draft calendar of the meeting of the provincial council for 12 months and other affairs. .
During the meeting, the members of the meeting discussed and approved the agenda of the meeting and allowed to review the report on the results and implementation activities of the Siem Reap Provincial Administration approved by the Provincial Council and the remaining 3 periods. Month 2019.
Mr. Sok Thol, Director of Administration of the Provincial Hall, read the report on the results of work and the direction to be implemented by the Siem Reap Provincial Administration remaining in the second mandate of the Provincial Council and read the instructions of the Ministry of Interior on the preparation of internal regulations. And the Council's internal rules of procedure.
Mr. Tea Seiha also clarified to the meeting about the hierarchy of the roles and responsibilities of the Provincial Council, Provincial Board of Governors in the legislation and executive. He said that focusing on the work of mineral resources and construction, the department must pay high attention to construction issues in the city / district, both old and new, about construction technical standards during construction in accordance with technical standards and laws. Permitted to build or not.
He said that if all constructions are illegal or in violation of technical standards, construction must be stopped immediately or dismantled to ensure public safety and security, to avoid such incidents in Sihanoukville.
The Siem Reap provincial governor added that the issue of transportation of mineral resources and excavation of the land, the Department must immediately check on the site of the permit and the excavation is in accordance with the instructions of the Department. However, if there is no construction site, it must be suspended or closed at once.
The governor also stressed that "the competent forces of the relevant departments must work together to implement the problem of land trucks that cause crashes on the city streets."
Mr. Ung Hoeun also requested the provincial councilors who have not yet declared their assets to act immediately and reminded the leaders of departments, institutions and units around the province to provide reports on activities and results implemented by the relevant departments, institutions and units. Each month according to the schedule of the provincial hall administration and must be present at the meeting of the provincial council in all departments, institutions and units.
He said that on the other hand, the remaining work of the Provincial Board of Governors must take all the work mentioned in this meeting to implement the work to achieve high results and improve the lives of the people. Participate in local development of communes for future development. The Ministry of Tourism is committed to reforming the application for tourism licenses to facilitate access for tour operators.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism has pledged to carry out in-depth reforms, especially on facilitating the conditions of applying for a tourism license and incorporating technology to facilitate and expedite access to the services of tour operators, and also called on tour operators And all tourism businesses need to be modernized by applying for a license online.
To introduce this reform to national and sub-national civil servants and tour operators across the country, the Ministry of Tourism has organized a dissemination workshop on the new reform of tourism license applications chaired by Mr. Song Tonghap, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Tourism; Deputy Chairman of the Financial Management Reform Working Group of the Ministry of Tourism on June 26, 2019 at the Phnom Penh Hotel.
On that occasion, Mr. Song Tonghap said that the Ministry of Tourism has set up a number of mechanisms to increase the efficiency and transparency of the Ministry of Tourism's public services, including:
2. The Ministry of Tourism has launched a one-stop shop to facilitate the application for tourism licenses and the transparency of the payment of public services by the Ministry of Tourism. Tour operators can easily apply for and pay public service fees without worrying about overdue public service fees.
3. Adjusting the conditions of applying for a tourism license in accordance with the current situation and reducing the documents required to facilitate the application for a tourism license quickly.
In order to expedite the Ministry of Tourism's financial reform work quickly and efficiently, Mr. Song Tonghap made the following recommendations:
1: Request the General Department of Tourism Industry Management to strengthen the mechanism to encourage tourism service business owners to use the online licensing application system by organizing training courses or visiting business locations.
2. Request tourism service business owners to join the reform of the Ministry of Tourism to increase efficiency and transparency in the provision of public services.
3. Request the Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism to actively participate in the reform work of the Ministry of Tourism, especially on the work of applying for tourism licenses through the online system.
4. To request the General Department of Tourism Industry to organize a meeting with tourism business owners to facilitate the conditions for applying for a tourism license, based on the principle of improving the quality of tourism services and making it easier for tour operators.
The Ministry of Tourism has implemented an online tourism license application reform program, which was implemented in early 2016. As of 2018, there are a total of 177 tourism licenses applied for online licenses. However, as of the first five months of 2019, the Ministry of Tourism observed that 90 businesses had applied, an increase of four times compared to the same period in 2018.
Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara announces the composition of the Construction Quality Inspection Commission in Preah Sihanouk Province (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, chaired a meeting on About construction management in Sihanoukville.
The meeting was held on June 25, 2019 at Sihanoukville Provincial Hall with the participation of Mr. Kun Kim, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, Mr. Yon. Mine Governor of Sihanoukville to be replaced and other relevant units.
The meeting announced the composition of the Sihanoukville Provincial Construction Quality Control Committee and the technical working group, approved and submitted a check list to inspect the construction to be based on the evaluation of construction quality, and requested the committee and the technical working group to start implementation. Work one week in the first step, to be executed on time, accurately and respect professional ethics.
The Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction will summarize and consult with Samdech Krala Hom, Deputy Prime Minister of the Ministry of Interior to report and request a high decision from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and immediately suspend the construction site. No rules and no technical standards.
The Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction has also set up two fire trucks for Sihanoukville with a capacity of 57 floors to increase rescue capacity in the event of an accident.
Please note that in addition to the above meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara also had a meeting with construction owners and construction contractors of about 165 companies.
During the meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara also requested that the company be willing to increase investment in cooperation with the inspection team, which is responsible for supporting them to respect the law in construction and improve the quality of construction to bring personal and economic benefits. National.
The Ministry of Land Management has confirmed that illegal constructions do not allow people to stay, do not allow them to do business without water and electricity. Red Cross Donations Distributed to 1291 Families in Romeas Hek District
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng Province and Chairman of the CRC Branch Committee of Svay Rieng Province, this morning, June 26, 2019, led a working group to visit and distribute CRC humanitarian donations to the families. Accident due to strong winds in Romeas Hek district, Svay Rieng province on June 21, 2019.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Se Vuthy, Provincial Gendarmerie Commander, Mr. Sou Mol, Acting Governor of Romeas Hek District, Mr. and Mrs. Member of Branch Committee, Sub-Branch, Provincial Branch of Cambodian Red Cross Village, commune chief, district and commune councils, many more.
The donations were distributed in two places: first: Svay Tontum pagoda in Trapeang Sdao commune and Ang Prasre commune, a total of 794 families, and second: Andong Po pagoda, in Andong Po commune and Doung commune, a total of 497 families. Of these, 48 families were severely affected, 785 families were average and 458 families were slightly affected.
The Provincial Governor conveyed the greetings and memories from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to the people, who are always concerned about the well-being and urges to solve the problems of People all the time and everywhere. He also expressed regret over the damage to property as well as the homes of relatives affected by the strong winds.
Please note that the donations distributed include: Each family received 30 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 6 bottles of soy sauce, 10 cans of fish, 1 folding mat, 1 rubber sheet, 1 kit (mosquito net, blanket, sarong, krama) ) And a budget of 200,000 riels.
The average victim family received 30 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 6 bottles of soy sauce, 10 cans of fish, 1 folding mat, 1 kit (mosquito net, blanket, sarong, krama) and 50,000 Riels. The least affected families received 50,000 Riels per family. Mr. Sao Sokha, Chairman of Romeas Hek District Assistance Team, also donated 10,000 Riels to each family.
(Prey Veng): Mr. Chea Somethy, Governor of Prey Veng Province and Deputy Governor of Prey Veng Province, led their colleagues to visit the workers who were injured by the building collapse on June 22, 2019. Treated at Sihanoukville Referral Hospital.
On that occasion, the Governor of Prey Veng Province visited 3 victims living in Prey Veng Province and 10 other injured people from other provinces on the morning of June 26, 2109 at Sihanoukville Provincial Referral Hospital.
Mr. Chea Somethy said that on behalf of the provincial leadership, I would like to wish the three injured victims and their relatives from other provinces who are being treated at the Sihanoukville Referral Hospital a speedy recovery. Do not miss to get back to business as usual.
With this, the Governor of Prey Veng Province and lower officials distributed some money to 3 injured people living in Prey Veng Province and 10 other injured people in other provinces.
It should be noted that Prey Veng province had 6 dead and 5 injured in the collapse of a 7-storey building in Sihanoukville out of a total of 54 victims (28 dead and 26 injured).
Sihanoukville CamControl Officers Continue to Investigate Defective Products at Tumnup Rolok Market and Mart Market
(Preah Sihanouk): Officials of Camkotrol Branch, Preah Sihanouk Province, on June 26, 2019, in cooperation with the local authorities, continued to disseminate food quality, safety, inspection of food products and pre-packaged goods at Tumnup Rolok Market, Seafood Distribution Depot. Sros and Phsar Mart around Meteorology in Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province.
According to the CamControl official in Sihanoukville, the purpose of the inspection was to prevent the traffic of defective goods, counterfeit labels, expiration dates and the presence of banned chemicals that could harm people's health.
According to CamControl officials, during the inspection, some food samples were taken for preliminary testing, including fresh shrimp, squid, oysters, dried fish, pickled fish, cabbage, and navy beans to find banned chemicals that can cause harm. To the health of the people.
At the same time, professional officers inspected for non-compliance on the packaging of food products. As a result, officials did not find the presence of banned chemicals in the above food products and there was no display of expired food packaging.
At the same time, officials have advised other traders to understand and follow the law on quality control, safety of products and services to avoid affecting the health of people will be able to face the law.
