It should be noted that after providing financial support to 1,487 rescue teams in the case of the collapse of a seven-story building in Sihanoukville, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, also announced to equip them with more gold medals in response to All their efforts, including the private sector.
Announcing the new Director of Battambang Provincial Department of Women's Affairs, Ms. Phok Sopheak, replacing Ms. Ou Ieng, who has retired
(Battambang): Mrs. Khim Chamroeun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, Mr. Uy Ry, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Nguon Rattan: Battambang Provincial Governor on the morning of June 26, 2019, presided over the inauguration of the Deputy Director of the Provincial Department of Women's Affairs. New Battambang by Ms. Phok Sopheak has been appointed as the new Director of the Battambang Provincial Department of Women's Affairs, replacing Ms. Oe Ieng, who has retired.
The inauguration ceremony was also attended by the leaders of the forces, departments around the province, officials of the Department of Women's Affairs.
Mr. Nguon Rattan: Congratulations and support to the newly appointed Director of the Department of Women's Affairs, who has one director and two deputy directors now, and also thanked the former director of the Department of Retirement for her hard work. Has done its professional work well so far related to women's work, having played many roles at the sub-national level, especially working well with the provincial administration and relevant authorities in the past.
