(Prey Veng): Police in Prey Veng province launched a series of drug crackdown operations, leading to the arrest of 51 suspects, confiscating nearly 50 packages of drugs and other items.
The General Commissioner considered that the above drug crackdown to contribute to the implementation of the Royal Government's safe village-commune policy.
According to the Commissioner, in 5 cases of illegal storage, transportation or trafficking of drugs, 10 suspects were arrested, 2 females, in 3 cases of illegal use of drugs, 41 suspects were arrested. Three women and 47 small packages of methamphetamine (ice cubes) and some smoking materials.
(Svay Rieng): The position of Governor of Chantrea District, Svay Rieng Province has been revealed to be changed in early July 2019, but the people in this district want to see the current District Governor, Mr. Nguon Ram, continue to hold the same position until Request to Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior to intervene in this case.
The insistence of the above people is because they see that his leadership with the local people and local authorities has cooperated well and developed.
She requested the provincial leadership and called on Samdech Sar Kheng to keep Mr. Nguon Ram as the governor of Chantrea district because he has worked hard to develop the district and the people respect him and all the authorities and civil society organizations in Also domestic.
As for Mr. Chea Sam An, a resident of Trapeang Bon village, Prey Koki commune, Chantrea district, he also said that the governor of Chantrea district, Mr. Nguon Ram, is a good official, he knows how to help people who are in need and needy, as in any village in the commune. Dead and destitute, he always brought money and bought a coffin for cremation, as well as help solve many problems.
As a citizen, I would like to request the provincial leadership to keep Mr. Nguon Ram as the district governor in order to provide the opportunity to lead Chantrea district to grow continuously because the people like him a lot.
As for some commune authorities in Chantrea district, Svay Rieng province, they said that if there was a change in Mr. Nguon Ram, it was a decision of their superiors, they did not dare to object, but in the mandate under the current district governor, he did not lead Having no prejudices with the people or with the village or commune authorities, he always cooperates smoothly and gives good recommendations to promote local development work as well.
However, Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng Province, told the members of Svay Rieng City Council recently announced on June 19, 2019 that in the future, there will be a change of three district governors, including The change of deputy governors of some districts and cities, and young people will be able to become leaders in some districts to strengthen the work more smoothly.
According to Chantrea district officials, the change of governor of Chantrea district will be announced on July 4, 2019.
