A group of volunteer doctors and students from the United States came to treat people at Ream Naval Base
(Preah Sihanouk): Through the coordination of Mr. Thong Khong, Minister of Tourism, on June 26, 2019, a group of doctors and student volunteers from the United States, along with Cambodian volunteer doctors, visited to treat patients. Free for troops, families, troops and people living around Ream Naval Base, Sihanoukville.
In addition to medical check-ups, the team of doctors and volunteer students also educated on health issues, provided prostheses, treated teeth and distributed glasses to the army, families, the army and the people.
This is the 10th time to visit Cambodia and the third time to do face-to-face treatment at Ream Naval Hospital, Sihanoukville in collaboration with Ream Naval Base, Cambodian Sailing Federation and with the participation of teachers. Doctors at Ream Navy Hospital as well.
ADB decides to provide $ 60 million in low-interest loans to Cambodia to help increase skills and workforce competition
"Having a highly skilled workforce is very important for a fast-growing economy and a growing workforce like Cambodia," said Yumikoyama Makawa, ADB's education specialist for Southeast Asia.
"ADB Concessional Loans will focus on improving the skills of employees working in high-growth sectors to help drive the country's development," she said. "We will make sure that all stakeholders, especially the government and the private sector, work together to improve the skills of employees."
The skills development project for the competition will help produce 18,000 qualified technicians, 28% of whom are women with higher access to employment and skills, the statement added. Techniques in four priority areas: manufacturing, construction, electricity and electronics.
The five technology training institutes selected for this project are: Battambang Institute of Technology, Institute of Technology of Cambodia, Angkor National Polytechnic Institute, National Institute for Technical Training for TVET Park and Techo Sen Svay Rieng Regional Polytechnic Institute.
In addition, the project will provide opportunities for skills development and skills remediation for existing employees to address skills gaps and skills shortages in the industry through job-based learning programs. Eighteen job-based concessional lending programs will be implemented in partnership with industry players, which will help improve the capacity of about 360 employees.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng: Capital-Provincial Drug Control Committee Must Completely Eliminate Drug Trafficking and Use Offenses
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, said on June 26, 2019 that from now on, the Capital-Provincial Drug Control Committee must take care to completely eliminate All crimes of drug trafficking and use in clubs and entertainment venues within its jurisdiction before the end of 2019.
This statement was made on the occasion that Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the International Day Against Drug Abuse under the theme "Health for Justice, Justice for Health" at Koh Pich Center, Phnom Penh. Phnom Penh this morning, June 26, 2019.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated, "From now on, the Capital-Provincial Drug Control Committee must pay attention to completely eliminate all drug trafficking and use crimes in clubs and venues. "Fun places in its jurisdiction before the end of 2019."
At the same time, Samdech Krala Hom emphasized that all types of law enforcement officers at all levels must absolutely avoid the 4 do not be involved, do not be behind, be a reference, do not relax and do not intervene in drug cases.
Samdech Krala Hom added that for border provinces, all police, army and relevant authorities stationed in the border areas must be organized as members of the local anti-drug commission to prevent drug trafficking. Enter the country and participate in the implementation of drug-free villages, communes / sangkats in their target areas, cooperating effectively with neighboring countries.
Samdech Krala Hom also called on the private sector, investors or traders with related businesses and places that are prone to be involved in drug offenses, absolutely must not be involved in drugs, do not take legal business to take advantage of Drug offenders must respect the business law and investment law and participate in preventing drug offenses by reporting or requesting intervention from the authorities when there is a suspicion of non-hidden crime.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng asks the Minister of Justice to freeze the assets of drug traffickers and human traffickers (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, requested Mr. Ang Vong Vathana, Minister of Justice Together, they freeze the property of those who are drug traffickers and those who are human traffickers.
The remarks of the Minister of Interior to the Minister of Justice were made on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the International Anti-Drug Day this morning, June 26, 2019, at the Koh Pich Center in Phnom Penh.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng said that the effects of drugs, in his opinion, are very bad. First, it destroys human resources because drugs invade the young people who are studying, ruining the future of the country. Second, this drug is related to all kinds of crimes, drug users can become terrorists, can become thieves, robbers, which is a crime.
According to Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, another case in which Samdech asked the Minister of Justice to freeze his property was to freeze anyone who engaged in human trafficking cases. Samdech stated that the reason why Samdech proposed to freeze the assets of human traffickers was because the money from the human trafficking activities could become financing, causing terrorism and it was a serious violation of human rights.
The Royal Government of Cambodia is considering developing and turning Sihanoukville into a multi-purpose model special economic zone.
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has been studying to develop and transform Sihanoukville into a multi-purpose special economic zone in line with Cambodia's industrial development policy.
The intention to transform Sihanoukville into a multi-purpose model special economic zone was presented at a meeting of the Economic and Financial Policy Committee (SEC) on June 25, 2019 at the Ministry. Economy and Finance Presided over by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy. This is according to the press release received by Fresh News on June 26, 2019.
The above meeting of the Economic and Financial Policy Committee to discuss the results of the preliminary study on the preparation of the master plan for the development and transformation of Sihanoukville into a multi-purpose special economic zone in line with the policy of industrial development in Cambodia. (IDP) 2015-2025.
According to the press release, the meeting discussed the results of the working group's preliminary study and identified challenges, including recommendations as policy measures to address both current and future issues, and asked the working group to study and consider. Comprehensive for the inclusion of specific implementation action plans in the master plan to develop and transform Sihanoukville into a multi-purpose model special economic zone.
The master plan must include a long-term vision based on key principles such as:
Five Chinese, Taiwanese and Cambodian kidnappers sent to court in connection with the kidnapping of a construction boss in Chamkarmon district (Video inside) (Phnom Penh) Four Chinese Taiwanese and a Cambodian man, reportedly a military police officer, came to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court in connection with a case of kidnapping, extortion and possession of a weapon without permission.
It should be reminded that after receiving the complaint by phone on the night of June 22, 2019, the specialized police force of Chamkar Mon district launched a search and arrested the above five suspects immediately at the New Building. Thams Location 724, Norodom Street, Village 10, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
During the operation, the police rescued four Taiwanese Chinese victims. During the arrest of the suspects, the police found exhibits including a pistol No. 1556, 3 pistols, 20 bullets and 1 handcuff.
Kampong Thom Provincial Governor instructs all newly appointed officials to continue their work, maintain unity and respect the leadership
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, instructed all newly appointed officials to continue their work, maintain unity and respect the assignments of the leadership.
He said this on the occasion that he and Mr. Chhun Chhon, Chairman of the Provincial Council, presided over the inauguration ceremony of 33 provincial halls and departments around the province this morning, June 25, 2019. There were about 300 participants.
On this occasion, Mr. Chhun Chhon instructed all newly appointed officials to pay attention to perform their duties well and to study to understand their roles and responsibilities and to understand the rules and regulations. Make the rules clear, because the leadership of the public administration does not follow the imagination.
It should be noted that the 33 civil servants who will be announced to take office this morning are from 23 provincial halls, 3 provincial departments of education, youth and sports, 6 provincial departments of social affairs, veterans and youth rehabilitation and 6 provincial public works departments. 1 person.
US Secretary of State arrives in Kabul unannounced
Kabul: US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo on Tuesday paid an unannounced visit to Kabul, Afghanistan, to meet with Afghan President Ashraf Ghani. Peace talks with Taliban This was released by the Chinese News Agency on Wednesday morning, June 26, 2019.
In a meeting with Ghani, Pompeo said he hoped Afghanistan would seek peace to end the current protracted conflict ahead of the September 28 presidential election. In addition, Pompeo and Ghani also agreed that finding peace is a priority to be achieved.
According to Pompeo, the United States is ready to withdraw its troops from Afghanistan indefinitely. The US Secretary of State's visit comes ahead of the seventh meeting between US and Taliban representatives soon to end the long-running conflict in the United States. The United States invaded Afghanistan in 2001.
Phnom Penh Capital Administration: The 14 district governors will be subject to administrative discipline and legal responsibility if there is illegal construction in their jurisdiction (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Phnom Penh Capital Administration has issued a letter of instruction to the 14 district governors Claiming that they may be subject to administrative discipline and legal liability if any unlicensed structures are built within their jurisdiction.
In his letter, Mr. KHOURN Sreng noted that in the past, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has regularly advised the Khan Administration to take care to prevent all constructions that do not have a construction permit and the construction that violates the construction permit in Phnom Penh.
(Phnom Penh): 35 families living in Prey Tea village, Sangkat Choam Chao 3, Khan Por Sen Chey, representing 145 families who have been in a long-running land dispute with the 91st Airborne Division, protested this morning, June 26, 2019. In front of the Por Sen Chey district hall to seek the intervention of the district governor to help solve the problem while military officers at the Air Force base have been encroaching on their land.
The trip to the district court came after they erupted in protest yesterday, accusing the military of lying.
They allege that the military officers not only encroached on their land, but also against the remarks made by the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who decided to hand over their land. Residents said that military officials misrepresented the truth, leading to the misconception that the dispute had been resolved and that all villagers had received land, but in fact nearly 10 hectares of land had been sold by the military. And.
The villagers went to protest the disputed land next to the Air Force base in Prey Tea village, Sangkat Choam Chao 3, Khan Por Sen Chey at 1:30 on June 25, 2019.
In addition, after the agreement was reached, in just two days, it was time to hand it over, but suddenly the team stopped solving it, and the reason for not resolving it is still a mystery until now.
The military then violated the disputed land at will, and they continued to protest, and the matter, although not resolved, remained quiet for some time. The lot was split and they protested again.
