Poll results: More people in US and Europe are skeptical of democracy
(Brussels): More than half of the world's population thinks their country is a democracy, while some Western Europeans see a surge in social media, a poll released on Tuesday. As a threat to democracy. This was released by CNA on Tuesday evening, June 25, 2019.
In fact, in the United States, which is holding presidential elections in 2020, Americans themselves are skeptical of their democracy, with 46 percent saying the United States is democratic and 40 percent saying it is not enough. In Europe, as many as 52% of the population think that the EU is not acting in the interests of Europe as a whole, and such criticisms are most prevalent among Italians, French and Greeks.
According to the survey, more than 40 percent of those surveyed in Canada, the United States and Austria, as well as others, had similar views on social media, such as Facebook and Twitter. Etc. have been negatively impacting democracy. Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign, June 25: 1,135 Illegal Vehicles Found and 683 Fineed
