(Phnom Penh): Ms. Keo Sok Pisey, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, on behalf of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, on June 25, 2019, led the campaign to put up abbots and educate people about the elimination of tiger mosquito sanctuary in Prey Chisak village, Prey Preung Khang. 1.2 feet in Sangkat Choam Chao III to help prevent the spread of dengue fever in Phnom Penh.
On that occasion, Ms. Keo Sok Pisey said, "There is no tiger mosquito sanctuary, no dengue fever, so visiting Abet and educating people to understand the elimination of tiger mosquito sanctuary as a dengue agent is the most important factor. . "When his house is without water, the environment is clean, there is no tiger mosquito sanctuary and there is no agent to transmit dengue to his children and his family."
"The Phnom Penh administration, as well as the Ministry of Health, has encouraged people to get rid of tiger mosquito shelters around their homes in their villages, which is key to preventing the spread of dengue fever," he said. "Dengue transmission depends on the dengue transmission agent, the tiger mosquito, which transmits dengue fever. If the tiger mosquito sanctuary can be eradicated and the tiger mosquitoes are not present in our city, there will be no dengue transmission."
