The following is the announcement of Phnom Penh Capital Administration: Chip Mong planted 3,200 rosewood trees in Samaki Phnom Oral Nature Conservation Community, Kampong Speu Province
(Phnom Penh): 65 employees of Chip Mong Company successfully cooperated with members of Samaki Natural Protection Community in Oral District, Kampong Speu Province to plant 3,200 rosewood seedlings on June 22, 2019.
Chip Mong is the first company to plant rosewood in the Samaki Phnom Oral Nature Conservation Community for two consecutive years, and in 2018, Chip Mong staff planted 1,000 mixed saplings in the community.
Mr. Nget Raya, an employee of Chip Mong Company, who participated in the tree planting program in Samaki Natural Protection Community, stated that in addition to contributing directly to the community, the team has strengthened the relationship between them because of Chip Mong Company. When meeting like this, the program allows the team to get to know each other and the community more.
Mr. Nget Raya added, "Apart from planting 3,200,000 rosewood trees, all of our staff have volunteered to raise a small amount of money to buy school supplies to distribute to nearly 300 students at Sre Kin Knong Primary School." The community is also united. ”
As of mid-2019, Chip Mong has led about 130 employees to plant trees in two communities, planting 3,200 rosewood trees, planting 3,000 mangrove trees and planting 500 mangrove seedlings. Distributed fruit juice, jams, homemade cakes, as well as school supplies and sports equipment to nearly 600 community school students.
Every year, Chip Mong Company organizes four tree planting programs in various communities. In early April 2019, Chip Mong Company organized mangrove planting program and mangrove nursery in Trapeang Sangker ecotourism community in Kampot province. Concrete bridge, a project of the Royal Government in Sambo district, Kratie province, will be completed by the end of 2019
