(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has launched a training course to strengthen the capacity of gender facilitators, accompanied by the launch of the Strategic Plan for Gender Mainstreaming in the Employment and Vocational Training Phase 4, 2019-2023, chaired by Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister Employment and Vocational Training at the Ministry of Labor.
She said the German government is committed to supporting the Cambodian government in contributing to the achievement of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).
Mr. Ith Sam Heng said that the Strategic Plan for Gender Mainstreaming in the field of employment and vocational training, Phase 4, 2019-2023, is to include all issues and needs of women in the preparation, implementation, monitoring and evaluation of Policies, programs and projects to ensure that men and women are equally involved in decision-making in prioritizing and allocating budgets at both the national and sub-national levels.
The Minister said that the Strategic Plan for Gender Mainstreaming in the field of employment and vocational training, Phase 4, 2019-2023, was compiled through:
* Review of the implementation of the Gender Mainstreaming Strategy of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training 2014-2018 and the collection of opinions as well as good experiences on gender issues in the field of employment and vocational training from the Department of Labor and the Department of Labor and Capital-provincial vocational training.
* Analysis of the current situation of men and women in the labor market in Cambodia.
Gender identification and prioritization at both national and sub-national levels for the strategic planning of gender mainstreaming in the field of employment and vocational training, Phase 4, 2019-2023.
In order to successfully implement the expected goals, Mr. Ith Sam Heng gave the following recommendations to all stakeholders:
* First, gender mainstreaming is a relevant task in both the field of employment and vocational training, so all units under the Ministry must work closely with the Ministry's gender team to promote the successful implementation of this strategic plan. .
* Second, request the Ministry of Gender Working Group to increase its activities by striving to unleash its full potential and turn its will and participation into effective practical activities.
* Third: Increase closer cooperation with the Ministry of Women's Affairs and relevant ministries and institutions, national and international organizations to mobilize support for technical and financial assistance cooperation to promote the implementation of the Gender Mainstreaming Strategic Plan in the field of employment. And vocational training, the fourth phase of 2019-2023 was successful.
Kampong Speu Customs and Military Officers Crack Down on 5 Luxury Cars That Failed to Implement Customs Duties
(Kampong Speu): At least 5 luxury cars were searched by the Kampong Speu Provincial Customs and Excise in cooperation with the Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie until the crackdown at Chbar Morn, Kampong Speu on the afternoon of June 24. 2019.
Although all five vehicles were equipped with license plates, a search by the Kampong Speu Provincial Customs and Excise Department found that the vehicles had not fulfilled their import duties and taxes properly.
In addition, the Customs Branch requested the citizens to participate in fulfilling the duties of the Customs and Excise properly, and every purchase or sale of vehicles must verify all clear customs documents.
Please note that the case of customs crime requires customs officers to conduct research, collect information clearly, professionally and legally. Currently, the Kampong Speu Provincial Customs and Excise Branch is making a record of the customs offense and sending it to the General Department of Customs and Excise for a decision.
