Draft Law on the Management of Petroleum and Petroleum Products Passes the Senate (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Senate unanimously approved the draft Law on the Management of Petroleum and Petroleum Products by 53 out of 53 votes in plenary session. This morning, June 25, 2019. The meeting was chaired by Samdech Say Chhum, President of the Senate, with the participation of 53 senators.
The draft law on the management of oil and petroleum products was approved by the National Assembly in the morning of June 17, 2019.
Please note that the Draft Law on the Management of Petroleum and Petroleum Products is the most necessary law for the management and development of petroleum resources in Cambodia. This draft law has 9 chapters and 72 articles.
This draft law covers all activities in the oil sector in the territorial integrity and sovereignty of the Kingdom of Cambodia, including the seabed and subsoil of the exclusive economic zone and the plateau, as well as other areas where The Kingdom of Cambodia has sovereign rights.
The statement said that the management of the oil sector must be based on the principles of transparency, accountability, equity in social progress and public welfare, security and safety and environmental responsibility.
