(Ratanakkiri): The Ministry of Economy and Finance has announced the appointment of Mr. Duch Bunna to the post of Director of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Department of Economy and Finance, replacing Mr. Ton Sotharoth, the retired director.
The above ceremony took place on the morning of June 25, 2019 at Ratanakkiri Provincial Hall, presided over by Mr. Vong Sandab, Undersecretary of State, Representative of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Nab Bunheng, Chairman of the Provincial Council, Mr. Moung Pang, Acting Provincial Governor, as well as the Director of the Kratie, Mondulkiri, Stung Treng and Preah Vihear Provincial Departments of Economy and Finance.
After Mr. Tun Sotharoth made a brief report on the past work, Mr. Vong Sandab handed over the appointment of Mr. Duch Bunna as the Director of the Department of Economy and Finance from now on.
Mr. Vong Sandab stated that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has decided to strictly implement the slogan "Reform is life, if not reform is death." In this sense, the reform work is a priority for the Royal Government to lead Cambodia to achieve a high middle income country by 2030.
At the same time, the Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance also instructed Mr. Douch Bunna, the new Director of the Department, to work hard to fulfill the roles and responsibilities assigned by the unit to improve the financial work of the province and to cooperate well with all departments. Administrative skills of municipalities, districts, communes, sangkats and policies to improve the public financial management of the Ministry of Finance.
Mr. Vong Sandab added that in addition, he must strive to fulfill his duties by adhering to the work approach, leading and managing the unit in accordance with the principles of advance work, team work to be transparent, efficient and responsible with high professionalism. .
