Phillip Bank announces temporary suspension of ATM service from June 28
(Phnom Penh): According to the announcement of Phillip Bank received by Fresh News on June 21, 2019, all of its ATMs and mobile banking services will be temporarily suspended from 6 pm. Friday, June 28 to 8 am, Monday, July 1, 2019 and will install the core banking system to organize the integration with KREDIT Microfinance Institution in the future.
Due to the installation of the above banking system, your old ATM card can no longer be used by customers. Therefore, all Phillip Bank customers go to the branch nearest to you to exchange for a new ATM card from July 1, 2019, just bring your ID card or passport along with your old ATM card.
Meanwhile, the Bank apologizes for the inconvenience and for the above reasons, the Bank will extend the working hours until 6:30 pm in the first week of July and Saturday, July 6, 2019 from 9:00 AM Until 5 pm for the new ATM card offer.
For more information, please contact customer service or contact the staff of each branch of Phillip Bank: 0869300000.
