215-meter wooden bridge at Beng Mealea temple completed
(Siem Reap): The construction of a 215-meter-long maze of wooden bridges in Beng Mealea Temple (including stairs) built to replace the old wooden bridges by experts of APSARA Authority in collaboration with Kham Someth Company has been completed. It is very attractive to tourists to capture the beautiful view of the temple and make it easy to visit this huge Khmer architecture.
The project was completed in May 2019.
Mr. Chhean Ratha, Acting Director of the Department of Preservation of Temples Outside Angkor Park, said that the attraction of Beng Mealea Temple is the great architectural structure, highlighted by rich design and harmony between the temple and nature, which preserves the originality of the temple. The presence of a long wooden bridge facilitates the visit of guests.
The history of this wooden bridge was built in 2002 by an international film company authorized by the Apsara Authority to film in the Beng Mealea temple to facilitate the transport of heavy film equipment. After the filming, the APSARA Authority has maintained and repaired this bridge continuously until today to make it easier for tourists to visit the temple.
Recently, due to the deterioration of the old bridge due to the age, quality of wood, weather, causing the bridge to rot and cause danger to visitors, especially the bridge is too small to accommodate the growth of the APSARA Authority in collaboration with Kham Someth decided to dismantle And new construction of 215 meters on the total length and planned to take three months to build, but due to the slow supply of wood, it was postponed until 7 months (October 2018 to May 2019).
The bridge costs 83 cubic meters of wood, made of koki wood, rattan, and rattan. It has a clean, strong design that can withstand up to more than 10 years, and has been expanded from 80 cm to 1.50 meters to make it easier for tourists to visit. Come and go.
Regarding the technique of building a new wooden bridge to replace the old bridge, Mr. Puth Soth, Technical Officer of the Department of Preservation of Temples Outside Angkor Park, said that the team has carefully calculated the thickness and size of the wood to ensure the safety of guests, strengthen the bridge structure by preparing equipment We construct according to technical standards.
The wood connection uses bolts for the fasteners, which ensures a longer quality than special nails, easy to repair later. In order to protect the bridge construction for a long time, the team also used pesticides to paint the wood.
The technical official added that in addition to the beauty of the temple and the safety of tourists, experts also consider the preservation of the temple is to follow the layout and technical standards that have already been studied.
If you touch the rock, you have to move the rock out with the previous plan and change the position, but if you can not move the rock, use the tires of the motorcycle to prevent the wood from pressing on the rock and instead of digging the ground down. To maintain the balance of the bridge, experts used concrete supports to support the pillars and support the bridge. These works are to maintain the beauty, quality of construction and sustainable preservation of archeological sites.
