(Taiwan): A Taiwanese F-16V fighter jet recently successfully landed on a highway in a rural area of Taiwan. The exercise is claimed by the Taiwanese military to increase the pilot's ability to land fighter jets in all road conditions in the event that all airports on Taiwan are controlled and destroyed by any attack by Beijing.
* If war breaks out, China will take a short time to attack Taiwan
The landing of the Taiwan F-16V fighter jet came after Chinese Defense Minister Wei Fenghe confirmed at a regional meeting in early June that Beijing would use military force to attack Taiwan if Someone, especially the United States, wants to separate Taiwan from China.
Taiwan has been separated from China since 1949, but China has not abandoned plans to reunite. But for decades, China has been reluctant to launch an attack on Taiwan for a variety of political reasons, especially fear of war, pushing itself to face the United States directly, while still not 100 percent convinced that Washington Will help Taiwan.
