Authorities and experts hold an emergency meeting after leaking a picture of the abbot of Pochentong pagoda in bed with his mistress
(Phnom Penh): Authorities and officials on the morning of June 24, 2019, held an emergency meeting after an unusual image was leaked on Facebook related to the abbot of Pochentong pagoda and Srey Sneh.
The meeting was chaired by Preah Dhammapanha Monisem Sophea, Acting Sub-Khan of Por Senchey District, and invited officials, monks and stakeholders at the Sub-District Hall of Por Senchey.
During the meeting, Preah Dhammapanha Monisem Sophea said that the opening of the meeting was due to an unusual image posted on Facebook about a photo of Bhikkhu Van Vanle, the chief abbot of Pursatram pagoda (called Pochentong) and a woman who Happened yesterday until today.
Preah Silvo Brahmatsaphy Preah Dhammathorn Anukon said that both parties should explain the incident that happened, is it true? Please provide true and honest answers to make it easier for the sub-school to resolve.
Bhikkhu Van Vanny described that the picture posted on Facebook was not real, but was cut for the window of his honor and Buddhist values.
Lop Thida, the owner of the photo that was posted on Facebook, said that she had nothing to do with the monk and that the photos were not true. The person who posted them intended to defame her. Me and my family. I totally reject all these fake photos.
Then, Vipassana Nun Phal Sna continued: "Regarding the statements made by the two parties above, it is confirmed that the photos posted on Facebook are not true, but some people or groups intended to post them. Destroying only Buddhist values.
Preah Krou Ratavinyo Choeur Chenda Preah Samuh Anukon Khan has said that if the two people have nothing to do with each other, please post a message in response to the fact that they have never really known each other on Facebook. The public knows and should not be confused.
Mr. Prak Pin, Director of Cult and Religion Office of Po Sen Chey District, fully agreed with the above opinion.
