South Korea helps Cambodia continue project to develop public employment service system
The agreement was signed by Mr. Hai Hun Leng, Director of the National Employment Agency (NEA) and Mr. Yang Seung-jun, Director of the Development Cooperation Department of the Ministry of Labor and Employment of the Republic of Korea. The signing ceremony was presided over by Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training at the Ministry of Labor on the afternoon of June 24, 2019.
Prior to the signing ceremony, Mr. Ith Sam Heng met with Mr. Yan Song Chun, focusing on labor cooperation and vocational training between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea.
On that occasion, the Minister said that in the past, Cambodia and South Korea have had good relations with each other and are close cooperation partners, with the Korean side having received Cambodian workers to work there continuously until now. The number of Cambodian workers going to work in the Republic of Korea has risen to nearly 60,000.
Regarding this project to develop the public employment service system, Minister Ith Sam Heng fully supported and encouraged the technical working groups of both sides to work closely to achieve success for both countries, Cambodia and Korea. .
In connection with the public service system development project, Yang expressed the expectation that it will achieve better results for the assets of both nations.
The representative of the Ministry of Labor of Korea is committed to continue good cooperation in the field of employment and vocational training with Cambodia, especially to continue the project to develop this public employment service system to be better.
After the signing ceremony, Mr. Hay Hun Leng told reporters that the National Employment Agency (NEA) now has its own website for providing public employment services through the Internet, but the ability The transmission of information to job seekers is still limited.
That is why the Ministry of Labor and Employment of the Republic of Korea has collaborated to provide more comprehensive and better website development to the existing NEA.
In this sense, the IT team will develop a database system to collect information of job seekers, information of employers, factories, enterprises and all sources of job information stored in a cellular interface. Together and easy to find information.
