(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on Monday afternoon, June 24, 2019, received a delegation from the company. CP Vietnam, led by Mr. Le Sung Vuoy and his colleagues, paid a courtesy call on Cambodia and discussed cooperation in pig production between the two countries.
Along with the success of CP Vietnam, the Minister requested the company to consider expanding investment in Cambodia by cooperating with CP Cambodia to increase domestic pork production, ensure sufficient supply, ensure quality and safety of disease-free meat. On the other hand, this investment can help create jobs for people and especially use local raw materials to the fullest.
At today's meeting, the two sides agreed to pay an official visit to CP Vietnam to exchange experiences and learn more about breeding techniques, feed production and especially disease prevention and control mechanisms. The African swine fever that the company has implemented in the past has been successful. Samdech Heng Samrin Sends Condolences to Families of Victims of 7-Storey Building Collapse in Preah Sihanouk Province
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, and his wife and family sent a message of condolences to the families of the victims of the collapse of a seven-storey building in Village 3, Sangkat 4, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province.
The following is a message from Samdech Heng Samrin: Kdei Karuna organized a mobile exhibition of the Flower Project on Sexual Violence and Gender during the Khmer Rouge Regime in Ratanakkiri Province.
The Mobile Exhibition of the Flower Project and the Intergenerational Discussion was held in the presence of Mr. Muong Pang, Acting Provincial Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, and was attended by Mr. Tim Menea, Director of Kdei Karuna and Mr. and Mrs. Deputy Director of Departments around the main province. Village chiefs, commune chiefs, school principals, students, and many people.
Mr. Muong Pang continued that after the liberation on January 7, 1979, the Cambodian government worked hard to restore and build the country from zero until the current situation, building roads, bridges, schools, hospitals and helping to create social equity because in that period there were many Go by widows, widows, orphans, and so on.
Mr. Tim Menea stated that the organization of a mobile exhibition program, the Flower Project and the Intergenerational Dialogue on Sexual Violence and Gender in the Khmer Rouge Regime, as a Compensation Project in Case 002/02, focused on marriage during the Khmer Rouge regime. Red submitted to the Khmer Rouge Tribunal and organized by Kdei Karuna in Banlung City, Ratanakkiri Province now.
In addition, Mr. Tim Menea stated that Kdei Karuna is a local NGO registered with the Ministry of Interior and has been working since 2005 in a total of 21 provinces, focusing on peacebuilding and peace building. Disseminate the history of the Khmer Rouge based on three main points: reconciliation, equality and dignity.
In fact, Kdei Karuna has been implementing two major programs: the dissemination of the history of the Khmer Rouge and justice, and the intergenerational dialogue with the international community, with four projects for intergenerational dialogue in the family on sexual violence. And gender during the Khmer Rouge regime and the healing and reconciliation of victims of torture during the Khmer Rouge regime.
Senior Minister Osman Hassan Leads a Meeting of Companies Doing Business on Hajj Pilgrimage and Tourism to Saudi Arabia
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of June 24, 2019, at the Peace Palace, Mr. Oknha Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission, led a delegation to meet with representatives of companies doing business in the field of tourism, pilgrimage to Saudi Arabia.
The meeting focused on the management of the Hajj program to be transparent, safe and accurate to those who travel to perform the Hajj and Om Roh, with the participation of Mr. and Mrs. representatives of some ministries and companies.
Senior Minister Osman Hassan told the entire meeting that without an embassy in Saudi Arabia, the association was having difficulty communicating through the governments of the two countries, causing a number of problems. Brothers and sisters who travel there.
Therefore, following the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister has always helped to resolve this issue in the past, so he will make a request from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government, to be the Honorary Consul General or Ambassador. Cambodia based in Saudi Arabia to facilitate communication.
He said that having studied some countries in Asia, such as Malaysia, Indonesia, Singapore, Thailand, he will also ask the Samdech again in principle to establish an institution to select and manage Hajj, which these countries have full experience. In managing Haji affairs, especially Singapore, it was established 50 years ago.
It should be reminded that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as he always has solved many problems, especially in the past regarding the number of pilgrims quota, which the Saudi government has set for Cambodia only 500 to 600 people.
Due to this quota factor, in 2015, about 500 of our brothers and sisters failed to attend and hundreds of registered people did not receive visas. Therefore, Samdech Techo immediately assigned Mr. Osman Hassan, the Secretary General, to liaise with the Ministry of Hajj in Saudi Arabia.
After examining the fact that Cambodia had experienced war after failing to participate in the Hajj more than 20 years later, Samdech Techo Hun Sen brought peace and religious harmony, and the Ministry of Hajj in Saudi Arabia decided to waive the ban. Quota level to date.
