Mr. Lou Kimchhun expressed his regret and apology for taking a photo of a smile at the collapse of a building in Sihanoukville
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Lou Kimchhun, Delegate of the Royal Government of Cambodia in charge of the Director General of the Autonomous Port, who participated in the rescue operation for the victims of the building collapse in Preah Sihanouk Province, expressed his regret and apology to the public, especially the families of the victims. One wrong gesture while taking a picture of a smile with Lt. Gen. Non Sokha at the scene.
At the same time, Mr. Lou Kimchhun also expressed his deepest feelings after receiving the sad news about the collapse of a building in Group 11, Village 3, Sangkat 4, Sihanoukville, which caused many deaths and injuries. This morning, June 22, 2019.
However, during the rescue operation, it was observed that Mr. Lou Kimchhun sent his officers and some relief supplies to help rescue the victims who were trapped in the rubble of the seven-story building.
The latest toll from the collapse caused 50 deaths and injuries, including 26 deaths (four females) and 24 injuries (two females). Rescuers are still searching for people suspected of being in the rubble.
Chinese delegation in Zhejiang wants to invest in tourism in Cambodia and will launch direct flights to Cambodia this year
(Phnom Penh): After mentioning investment opportunities in the tourism sector in Cambodia, the Chinese delegation from Zhejiang Province expressed its intention to invest in establishing tourism areas in Cambodia, especially for older tourists, while connecting direct flights. This province has been confirmed to be officially launched in 2019.
The remarks were made during a working meeting between Minister of Tourism Thong Khon and a Chinese delegation from Zhejiang Province led by Zhang Zexi, Vice Chairman of the Zhejiang Provincial Advisory Council, at the Ministry of Tourism this morning. June 24, 2019.
During the meeting, the Chinese delegation was very interested in investment opportunities to create tourist destinations for elderly tourists in Cambodia. There are 2.8 million people abroad, of which about 80,000 are from Cambodia.
Zhang means that more and more Chinese tourists from his province will visit Cambodia, and every winter they like to stay in their leisure zone in southern China, which has a mild climate. Hotter than Zhejiang Province.
That is why he and the delegation came to discuss with the Cambodian side to express their desire to invest in building leisure accommodation for Chinese tourists from there.
Minister Thong Khon welcomed the Chinese side's intentions and introduced investment opportunities in the tourism sector, especially in the coastal areas of Cambodia and along the Mekong River. Cambodia more than 400 km has beautiful scenery and favorable for long stays and sightseeing of tourists.
At the same time, Mr. Thong Khon requested the Chinese side in Zhejiang Province to promote Chinese language training for Chinese-speaking tourism professionals and tour guides through the establishment of a tourism vocational school in Cambodia to achieve the number of professional staff. And tour guides respond to the growing number of tourists, especially Chinese tourists.
The minister also asked the Chinese side to help speed up the connection of direct flights from Zhejiang to Cambodia to boost tourism from the province. At this point, Mr. Zhang Xuxi replied that his Zhejiang Province also made efforts to promote this work, and during 2019, direct flights from Zhejiang Province to Cambodia will be officially launched.
Regarding the investment opportunities and requests from the Cambodian side, Mr. Zhang's delegation will inform the Chinese government and continue discussions with relevant ministries and institutions to help Cambodian friends.
