Minister of Agriculture Leads a Delegation to Defend the Draft Law on the Approval of Cambodia as a Member of the Agreement "Port Ownership Measures to Prevent and Eliminate Illegal Fishing" in front of the National Assembly Committee
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, this morning, June 24, 2019, led a delegation of the Ministry to defend the draft law on the approval of Cambodia as a member of the Agreement on "State Measures". Port owners to prevent and eliminate illegal fishing without report and without permission "with the Third Committee and the Fifth Committee of the National Assembly.
The meeting was co-chaired by Mr. Chea Vandeth, Chairman of the Third Committee, Mr. Chheang Vun, Chairman of the Fifth Commission, and Ms. Chea, Vice-Chairman, and many other members and members of the National Assembly.
First of all, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia and on behalf of the Ministry, the Minister expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Kittipritthbandit Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, for allowing the submission of the 3rd and 5th Committees of the National Assembly. The above law now.
Statement to the Co-Chair and members of the Ministerial Meeting briefed on the brief history and main contents of the draft law as follows: This agreement was approved by the FAO Conference on 22 November 2009. Currently, 60 countries, including the European Union, are parties to the agreement, including five in Southeast Asia.
Objective: First, to fight and eliminate IUU through the effective implementation of port owners' measures to ensure the sustainable development and conservation of fishery resources and marine ecosystems. Second, prevent IUU fisheries from entering the international market.
This agreement consists of 10 sections and 37 articles and was approved by the Council of Ministers in the plenary session of the Council of Ministers on June 7, 2019.
