(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Association of Travel Agents (CATA), Ministry of Tourism, Phnom Penh Capital Hall, the Cyclo Conservation Association and the Informal Business have jointly organized the 2019 Cyclo Tourism Race to encourage cyclo riders and promote the use of cyclo in tourism. Attract national and international tourists.
This cyclo-tourism event was held under the theme "Conservation of cyclo for tourism" at Preah Neang Prachha Barami Park in Sangkat Chroy Changva, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh on the morning of June 23, 2019 under the chairmanship of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh.
Speaking at the ceremony, Mr. Thong Khon stated that the cyclo not only acts as a means of transportation that does not harm the environment and serve the lives of the Cambodian people, but can also act as a tourism product that contributes significantly. To attract tourists and provide new experiences of city tourism by providing cyclo tour services in the tour package.
The president of CATA stated that looking at this challenge, he pushed for the organization of the 2019 Cyclo Tour in order to increase the popularity, increase the use of cyclo and the income of cyclo riders to protect the cyclo business not to lose. Through the use of cyclos in tourism.
For the cyclo that participated in the 2019 cyclo tour race, there are a total of 136 units. After 1 km, the first place winner went to Mr. Ron Chak from Prey Veng province with a cyclo with license plate number 117, while the second place went to Mr. Do Saroeun from Svay Rieng province and the third place went to Mr. Mr. Sim Choeun from Prey Veng province.
Please note that the first place winner received 400,000 Riels, the second place winner received 320,000 Riels and the third place winner received 240,000 Riels. Separately, the participants who did not win also received an incentive of 100,000 Riels each.
