Ministry of Commerce considers US embassy official statement that Chinese companies use Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone to ship tax evaded goods to the United States without clear basis
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Ministry of Commerce has dismissed allegations by US Embassy officials that some Chinese companies use the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone to send goods from China to the United States to avoid paying taxes or lower taxes. Lift without a clear basis. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Commerce, which was received by Fresh News on the afternoon of June 23, 2019.
The Ministry of Commerce stated that "in connection with this case, after assigning a professional officer to investigate, the Ministry of Commerce would like to confirm that the statement of the US Embassy official has no clear basis, which is contrary to the actual practice because in the economic zone In particular, Sihanoukville does not have a manufacturer of flour made from grain and steel pipes.
According to the Ministry of Commerce, Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone is a multi-purpose economic and trade zone with Chinese, Cambodian, American, Japanese, French, South Korean, Irish, Vietnamese and Thai enterprises. It also produces a wide range of goods such as textiles, clothing, bags and leather products and accessories.
It should be noted that Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone is located in Bit Trang Commune, Prey Nob District, Preah Sihanouk Province was established on March 17, 2008 on an area of 1,113 hectares. Currently, Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone has nearly 200 companies, factories and enterprises and is investing, providing employment to more than 20,000 Cambodians. Kampong Thom Provincial Governor Instructs Stung Sen City Council of the Third Mandate to Do a Good Work for the People
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, advised the Stung Sen City Council of the third mandate to be an executive member to develop the local people well and effectively, which is the desire of the people. On the occasion of his participation in announcing the inauguration of Stung Sen City Council for the third mandate on the afternoon of June 22, 2019.
The provincial governor instructed the 17 newly appointed municipal councilors, with Mr. Hok Rin as the chairman of the third-mandate municipal council, to work hard to serve the interests and needs of the local people fairly, fairly and without discrimination. Must adhere to political tendencies to participate in building and developing more prosperous localities.
He said that the promotion of responsibility and ownership in fulfilling its roles and responsibilities to develop the base to meet the needs and improve the lives of people with transparency and accountability.
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen will return to Cambodia at 3 pm on June 23, 2019 after attending the 34th ASEAN Summit in Phnom Penh. Bangkok, Thailand for 2 days.
The 34th ASEAN Summit for two days on 22 and 23 June 2019 is held under the theme "Promoting Partnership for Sustainability". The meeting focused on enhancing cooperation and strengthening consensus among ASEAN members to address new global challenges.
The summit will also explore ways to take ASEAN to the next level, sustainably and seamlessly.
Simultaneously with the 34th ASEAN Summit, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also attended the following meetings and programs: * Summit between the Heads of State / ASEAN Government with representatives of the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly * Summit between Heads of State / ASEAN Government with the ASEAN Business Advisory Council and * ASEAN Heads of State / Government Summit with ASEAN Youth Representatives.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that the banking sector is continuing to grow in both size and scope, safely and environmentally, leading to assets in the banking system to increase to 173% of GDP. Consumer deposits and loans to the private sector increased by 102% and 92%, respectively.
The remarks were made by the Governor-General on the occasion of the celebration of the 10th anniversary of Sacombank (Cambodia) Plc. Of Vietnam on June 22, 2019.
Chea Chanto said the growth of the banking sector was due to the maintenance of economic growth of around 7%, mainly supported by the continued inflow of foreign direct investment, high export growth coupled with strong demand. Domestic. In fact, the high growth rate over the past two decades has improved the living standards of the people and reduced poverty in Cambodia at a rate of at least 1% per year.
He said that while the inflation rate remained low, it was manageable while the exchange rate was stable. Improved macroeconomic stability has also contributed to the steady growth of the banking sector.
He said that with this growth, the network of banks and microfinance institutions have expanded throughout the capital-province, new financial products have been developed, while the financial infrastructure has been actively developed, which has resulted in the expansion of capabilities. Use and access the financial services of the people to expand their economic activities, especially the people living in rural areas.
"Payment systems have been steadily evolving in line with advances in financial technology and responding to the needs of ASEAN integration, and the financial environment has continued to grow, with 69% of adults now Use official financial services.
Mr. Chea Chanto stated that Sacombank (Cambodia) Plc. Is one of the five Vietnamese commercial banks established in Cambodia. At the same time, the Bank has continuously increased its capital to meet the new requests of customers, comply with the regulations of the National Bank of Cambodia and expand its branch network up to 9, in line with the continuous development of the banking system.
He said that the presence of Vietnam Bank, Sacombank (Cambodia) Plc. Has shown the confidence of Vietnamese investors in Cambodia and shows the closer trade ties, friendship and cooperation between Vietnam and Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): Everyone is born with the right to life, liberty and security of person without the right to be subjected to arbitrary interference with his privacy, family, home or correspondence.
Violation of the rights and freedoms of others by the detention and detention of ordinary persons outside the legal authorities and without the permission of the law is illegal. However, in the case of actual crimes and misdemeanors, the law allows any individual to arrest the perpetrator and bring him or her to a judicial police officer.
To better understand how "illegal detention and detention" is punishable by law? Fresh News' Legal Awareness Program in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation will present the following students:
In order to prevent and reduce this crime, Article 253 of the 2009 Penal Code provides for the illegal detention of detainees, which stipulates that a person who is in custody or in custody of another person without a legal order or outside the law Conviction:
The aggravating circumstance of the above offenses is punishable by imprisonment from 15 (fifteen) to 30 (thirty) years in the case of torture or cruelty or causing death without intent to cause death or misconduct. For the purpose of extorting property or demanding certain conditions.
To make it easier to understand the charges of illegal detention and detention, we would like to cite the following examples: Mr. Sok and Mr. Sao are very angry with thieves who often come to steal their belongings when they He is not at home.
One day, they arrived and saw a thief stealing items from their home. They caught the thief, held him in their kitchen for a week, and tortured the thief. That too.
Based on the above facts, we can conclude that Mr. Sok and Mr. Sao are indeed the victims of the theft, but they do not have the right to detain the suspects beyond the legal period, they can only catch the thief. Handed over to a nearby judicial police officer only.
Their actions above are illegal and may be prosecuted and punished in accordance with the provisions of the above article. For the above offenses, additional penalties may be imposed as provided in Article 255 of the Penal Code.
In summary, unlawful detention or detention without the authority of the law and without the permission of the law is criminalized by the Penal Code and the person who commits the crime shall be severely punished. Protect the rights, freedoms, honor and dignity of the people.
Mr. Vong Pisen Visits and Distributes Gifts to People Affected by Typhoon in Pearang District, Prey Veng Province
(Prey Veng): This morning, June 23, 2019, the National Team to Pearang District led by Mr. Vong Pisen saw the damage to people's houses due to the natural disaster on June 21, 2019. A total of 63 houses, of which 17 were severely damaged and 46 were slightly damaged.
Meanwhile, the chairman of the working group prayed that natural disasters do not occur, causing further damage to people's homes.
