Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign on June 23: 789 illegal vehicles found and 457 fines
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for June 23, 2019, the traffic police force inspected 3,989 vehicles, found 457 vehicles violating the law (59% motorcycles), 332 education vehicles and 457 fines. Units, according to the official report of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 2,101 helmets and goggles were inspected on June 23, 139 education helmets and 254 helmets were fined.
Khmer Breweries Hosts Beer and Beverage Technology Training Workshop
(Phnom Penh): Khmer Breweries has held a nationwide educational workshop on Khmer Breweries technology to share knowledge with its product distributors.
This educational workshop was first held in 53 different locations in Phnom Penh, starting from June 21 and continuing to travel to many other provinces in Cambodia.
Ms. Kong Kosal, Marketing Director of Khmer Breweries, said that the purpose of this workshop was "to share information related to the modern technology used in the production of high quality beer and beverages of Khmer Breweries. "Everyone will understand more about the ingredients from the machines and the technology of brewing beer and beverages they are distributing."
She added that the company also takes this valuable opportunity to meet with wholesale and retail customers to establish a close relationship with each other.
It should also be noted that all workshops will be taught by experienced technicians with many years of experience in the production of beer and beverages, both Khmer and foreign, trained from Germany.
