During the breakfast meeting before the ASEAN Summit, the Prime Ministers of the three countries exchanged views and views on promoting bilateral, multilateral, regional and international cooperation. Especially related to the development in the triangle area, which borders the three countries.
The Prime Ministers of the three countries praised and appreciated the positive results of the Triangle Development Zone Working Group, which has contributed to mobilizing resources from all directions to develop the triangle to a new face and progress. Order. In particular, it has transformed from an area where people live in poverty into an area that is connected in terms of infrastructure, people-to-people communication.
The three heads of government also pledged to work together to transform the development triangle into a new economic pole for the three countries, especially to improve the living standards of the people in the three countries. Improving from day to day.
Tehran: Iranian lawmakers shouted insults at the United States in a plenary session on Sunday after a deputy speaker accused Washington of being a "global terrorist mastermind". This was released by Reuters on Sunday, June 23, 2019.
US President Donald Trump on Friday acknowledged that he had ordered the US military to launch air strikes against Iran, but decided to withdraw immediately because the attack could have killed 150 people. But Iran has also warned that it will take strong action against any threat to its territorial integrity.
Donald Trump on Saturday announced that additional economic sanctions against Iran would take effect Monday (Washington time) to prevent the Islamic Republic from acquiring nuclear weapons. He also stated that the option of using military force against Tehran would always be on his desk. 28 Colombian soldiers train for demining skills in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): After successfully completing the training of 27 Iraqi officials and receiving praise from the trainees less than a week ago, now a group of 28 Colombian trainees came to Cambodia for training. Demining and UXO Clearance Skills at the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC).
CMAC International Relations and Cooperation Officer told Fresh News on the afternoon of June 23, 2019 that Colombian troops arrived in Cambodia on the evening of June 22, 2019 and the training will start on the 24th. June 2019.
The same official confirmed that from the end of June to August 2019, CMAC will receive 3 groups of trainees who come to train in demining skills, the use of demining equipment maintenance and personnel and human resource management skills, including:
Group 1: Twenty Colombian soldiers will undergo more than two weeks of training from June 24 to July 4, 2019, learning how to clear landmines. And Unexploded Ordnance (BAC),
Group 2: Eight Colombian soldiers train for nearly two months from June 27 to August 20, 2019, using and maintaining demining equipment.
Group 3: 7 participants from Laos who came to study staff management and human resources for 4 weeks, studying in Cambodia for 2 weeks and in Laos for 2 weeks.
